\s1 Ezekiel’s Vision by the River Kebar
\r (\ref Psalm 137:1–9|PSA 137:1-9\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb In the thirtieth|בִּשְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֗ה\rb*, \rb on the fifth|בַּחֲמִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb day|לַחֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the fourth month|בָּֽרְבִיעִי֙\rb*, \rb while I|וַאֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb was among|בְתֽוֹךְ־\rb* \rb the exiles|הַגּוֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the River|נְהַר־\rb* \rb Kebar|כְּבָ֑ר\rb*, \rb the heavens|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb* \rb opened|נִפְתְּחוּ֙\rb* \rb and I saw|וָאֶרְאֶ֖ה\rb* \rb visions|מַרְא֥וֹת\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 1:1 \ft Or \fqa from God\f*
\p \v 2 \rb On the fifth|בַּחֲמִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb day of the month|לַחֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb*— \rb it|הִ֚יא\rb* \rb was the fifth|הַחֲמִישִׁ֔ית\rb* \rb year|הַשָּׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb of the exile|לְגָל֖וּת\rb* \rb of King|הַמֶּ֥לֶךְ\rb* \rb Jehoiachin|יוֹיָכִֽין׃\rb*— \v 3 \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְ֠הוָה\rb* \rb came directly|הָיֹ֣ה\rb*\rb |הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Ezekiel|יְחֶזְקֵ֨אל\rb* \rb the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֛ן\rb*, \rb the son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of Buzi|בּוּזִ֧י\rb*, \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans|כַּשְׂדִּ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 1:3 \ft That is, the Babylonians\f* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the River|נְהַר־\rb* \rb Kebar|כְּבָ֑ר\rb*. \rb And there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb the LORD’s|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb hand|יַד־\rb* \rb was|וַתְּהִ֥י\rb* \rb upon him|עָלָ֛יו\rb*.
\s1 The Four Living Creatures
\p \v 4 \rb I looked|וָאֵ֡רֶא\rb* \rb and saw|וְהִנֵּה֩\rb* \rb a whirlwind|ר֨וּחַ\rb*\rb |סְעָרָ֜ה\rb* \rb coming|בָּאָ֣ה\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the north|הַצָּפ֗וֹן\rb*, \rb a great|גָּדוֹל֙\rb* \rb cloud|עָנָ֤ן\rb* \rb with fire|וְאֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb flashing back and forth|מִתְלַקַּ֔חַת\rb* \rb and brilliant light|וְנֹ֥גַֽהּ\rb* \rb all around|סָבִ֑יב\rb* \rb it|ל֖וֹ\rb*. \rb In the center|וּמִ֨תּוֹכָ֔הּ\rb* \rb of the fire|הָאֵֽשׁ׃\rb* \rb was a gleam|כְּעֵ֥ין\rb* \rb like amber|הַחַשְׁמַ֖ל\rb*\rb |מִתּ֥וֹךְ\rb*,\f + \fr 1:4 \ft Or \fqa The center of the fire looked like glowing metal\ft ; similarly in verse 27\f* \v 5 \rb and within it|וּמִ֨תּוֹכָ֔הּ\rb* \rb was the form|דְּמ֖וּת\rb* \rb of four|אַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb living creatures|חַיּ֑וֹת\rb*.
\p \rb And this was|וְזֶה֙\rb* \rb their appearance|מַרְאֵֽיהֶ֔ן\rb*: \rb They had|לָהֵֽנָּה׃\rb* \rb a human|אָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb form|דְּמ֥וּת\rb*, \v 6 \rb but each|לְאֶחָ֑ת\rb* \rb had four|וְאַרְבָּעָ֥ה\rb* \rb faces|פָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb and four|וְאַרְבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb wings|כְּנָפַ֖יִם\rb*\rb |לְאַחַ֥ת\rb*. \v 7 \rb Their legs|וְרַגְלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb were straight|יְשָׁרָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and the soles|וְכַ֣ף\rb* \rb of their feet|רֶ֣גֶל\rb* \rb were like the hooves|כְּכַף֙\rb*\rb |רֶ֣גֶל\rb*\rb |רַגְלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb of a calf|עֵ֔גֶל\rb*, \rb gleaming|וְנֹ֣צְצִ֔ים\rb* \rb like|כְּעֵ֖ין\rb* \rb polished|קָלָֽל׃\rb* \rb bronze|נְחֹ֥שֶׁת\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Under|מִתַּ֙חַת֙\rb* \rb their wings|כַּנְפֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb their four|אַרְבַּ֣עַת\rb* \rb sides|רִבְעֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb they had human|אָדָ֗ם\rb* \rb hands|וְיָדוֹ\rb*. \rb All four living creatures|לְאַרְבַּעְתָּֽם׃\rb* \rb had faces|וּפְנֵיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb and wings|וְכַנְפֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*, \v 9 \rb and their wings|כַּנְפֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb were touching|חֹֽבְרֹ֛ת\rb* \rb one|אֶל־\rb* \rb another|אֲחוֹתָ֖הּ\rb*.\rb |אִשָּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb They did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb turn|יִסַּ֣בּוּ\rb* \rb as they moved|בְלֶכְתָּ֔ן\rb*; \rb each|אִ֛ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb one went|יֵלֵֽכוּ׃\rb* \rb straight|עֵ֥בֶר\rb* \rb ahead|פָּנָ֖יו\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb The form|וּדְמ֣וּת\rb* \rb of their faces|פְּנֵיהֶם֮\rb* \rb was that|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of a man|אָדָם֒\rb*, \rb and each of the four|לְאַרְבַּעְתָּ֔ם\rb* \rb had the face|וּפְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of a lion|אַרְיֵ֤ה\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the right side|הַיָּמִין֙\rb*, \rb the face|וּפְנֵי־\rb* \rb of an ox|שׁ֥וֹר\rb* \rb on the left side|מֵֽהַשְּׂמֹ֖אול\rb*, \rb and also|לְאַרְבַּעְתָּ֑ן\rb* \rb the face|וּפְנֵי־\rb* \rb of an eagle|נֶ֖שֶׁר\rb*\rb |לְאַרְבַּעְתָּֽן׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb Such were their faces|וּפְנֵיהֶ֕ם\rb*.
\p \rb Their wings|וְכַנְפֵיהֶ֥ם\rb* \rb were spread|פְּרֻד֖וֹת\rb* \rb upward|מִלְמָ֑עְלָה\rb*; \rb each had|לְאִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb two wings|שְׁ֚תַּיִם\rb* \rb touching|חֹבְר֣וֹת\rb* \rb the wings of the creature on either side|אִ֔ישׁ\rb*, \rb and two|וּשְׁתַּ֣יִם\rb* \rb wings covering|מְכַסּ֔וֹת\rb* \rb its|אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb body|גְּוִיֹתֵיהֶֽנָה׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb Each|וְאִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb creature went|יֵלֵ֑כוּ\rb* \rb straight ahead|אֶל־\rb*\rb |עֵ֥בֶר\rb*\rb |פָּנָ֖יו\rb*. \rb Wherever|אֶ֣ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb*\rb |יִֽהְיֶה־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֨מָּה\rb* \rb the spirit|הָר֤וּחַ\rb* \rb would go|לָלֶ֙כֶת֙\rb*, \rb they would go|יֵלֵ֔כוּ\rb*, \rb without|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb turning|יִסַּ֖בּוּ\rb* \rb as they moved|בְּלֶכְתָּֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb In the midst|וּדְמ֨וּת\rb* \rb of the living creatures|הַחַיּ֜וֹת\rb* \rb was the appearance|מַרְאֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb of glowing|אֵ֗שׁ\rb* \rb coals|כְּגַחֲלֵי־\rb* \rb of fire|בֹּֽעֲרוֹת֙\rb*, \rb or|כְּמַרְאֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of torches|הַלַּפִּדִ֔ים\rb*.\rb |הִ֕יא\rb* \rb Fire|לָאֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb moved back and forth|מִתְהַלֶּ֖כֶת\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb the living creatures|הַחַיּ֑וֹת\rb*; \rb it was bright|וְנֹ֣גַהּ\rb*, \rb and lightning|בָרָֽק׃\rb* \rb flashed|יוֹצֵ֥א\rb* \rb out of|וּמִן־\rb* \rb it|הָאֵ֖שׁ\rb*. \v 14 \rb The creatures|וְהַחַיּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb were darting back and forth|רָצ֣וֹא\rb*\rb |וָשׁ֑וֹב\rb* \rb as quickly as|כְּמַרְאֵ֖ה\rb* \rb flashes of lightning|הַבָּזָֽק׃\rb*.
\s1 The Four Wheels
\p \v 15 \rb When I looked|וָאֵ֖רֶא\rb* \rb at the living creatures|הַחַיּ֑וֹת\rb*, \rb I saw|וְהִנֵּה֩\rb* \rb a|אֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb wheel|אוֹפַ֨ן\rb* \rb on the ground|בָּאָ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb beside|אֵ֥צֶל\rb* \rb each creature|הַחַיּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb with its four|לְאַרְבַּ֥עַת\rb* \rb faces|פָּנָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb The workmanship|וּמַעֲשֵׂיהֶם֙\rb* \rb of the wheels|הָאוֹפַנִּ֤ים\rb* \rb looked like|מַרְאֵ֨ה\rb* \rb the gleam|כְּעֵ֣ין\rb* \rb of beryl|תַּרְשִׁ֔ישׁ\rb*, \rb and all four|לְאַרְבַּעְתָּ֑ן\rb* \rb had the same|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb likeness|וּדְמ֥וּת\rb*. \rb Their workmanship|וּמַ֣עֲשֵׂיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb looked|וּמַרְאֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb like|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a wheel|הָאוֹפַ֖ן\rb* \rb within|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb a wheel|הָאוֹפָֽן׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb As they moved|בְּלֶכְתָּ֣ם\rb*, \rb they went|יֵלֵ֑כוּ\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb any of the four|אַרְבַּ֥עַת\rb* \rb directions|רִבְעֵיהֶ֖ן\rb*, \rb without|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb pivoting|יִסַּ֖בּוּ\rb* \rb as they moved|בְּלֶכְתָּֽן׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb Their rims|וְגַ֨בֵּיהֶ֔ן\rb* \rb were high|וְגֹ֥בַהּ\rb* \rb and awesome|וְיִרְאָ֣ה\rb*,\rb |לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and all four|לְאַרְבַּעְתָּֽן׃\rb* \rb rims|וְגַבֹּתָ֗ם\rb* \rb were full of|מְלֵאֹ֥ת\rb* \rb eyes|עֵינַ֛יִם\rb* \rb all around|סָבִ֖יב\rb*. \v 19 \rb So as the living creatures|הַֽחַיּ֔וֹת\rb* \rb moved|וּבְלֶ֙כֶת֙\rb*, \rb the wheels|הָאוֹפַנִּ֖ים\rb* \rb moved|יֵלְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb beside them|אֶצְלָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and when the creatures|הַֽחַיּוֹת֙\rb* \rb rose|וּבְהִנָּשֵׂ֤א\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the ground|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb the wheels|הָאוֹפַנִּֽים׃\rb* \rb also rose|יִנָּשְׂא֖וּ\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb Wherever|עַ֣ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb*\rb |יִֽהְיֶה־\rb*\rb |שָּׁ֨ם\rb* \rb the spirit|הָר֤וּחַ\rb* \rb would go|לָלֶ֙כֶת֙\rb*, \rb they would go|יֵלֵ֔כוּ\rb*\rb |שָׁ֥מָּה\rb*\rb |הָר֖וּחַ\rb*\rb |לָלֶ֑כֶת\rb*, \rb and the wheels|וְהָאוֹפַנִּ֗ים\rb* \rb would rise|יִנָּשְׂאוּ֙\rb* \rb alongside them|לְעֻמָּתָ֔ם\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb the spirit|ר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb of the living creatures|הַחַיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb was in the wheels|בָּאוֹפַנִּֽים׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb When the creatures moved|בְּלֶכְתָּ֣ם\rb*, \rb the wheels moved|יֵלֵ֔כוּ\rb*; \rb when the creatures stood still|וּבְעָמְדָ֖ם\rb*, \rb the wheels stood still|יַֽעֲמֹ֑דוּ\rb*; \rb and when the creatures rose|וּֽבְהִנָּשְׂאָ֞ם\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the ground|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb*, \rb the wheels|הָאֽוֹפַנִּים֙\rb* \rb rose|יִנָּשְׂא֤וּ\rb* \rb alongside them|לְעֻמָּתָ֔ם\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb the spirit|ר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb of the living creatures|הַחַיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb was in the wheels|בָּאוֹפַנִּֽים׃\rb*.
\s1 The Divine Glory
\p \v 22 \rb Spread out|נָט֥וּי\rb* \rb above|עַל־\rb*\rb |מִלְמָֽעְלָה׃\rb* \rb the heads|רָאשֵׁיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb of the living creatures|הַחַיָּה֙\rb* \rb was the likeness|וּדְמ֞וּת\rb* \rb of an awesome|הַנּוֹרָ֑א\rb* \rb expanse|רָקִ֔יעַ\rb*, \rb gleaming|כְּעֵ֖ין\rb* \rb like crystal|הַקֶּ֣רַח\rb*. \v 23 \rb And under|וְתַ֙חַת֙\rb* \rb the expanse|הָרָקִ֔יעַ\rb*, \rb their wings|כַּנְפֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb stretched out|יְשָׁר֔וֹת\rb* \rb toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|אִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb another|אֲחוֹתָ֑הּ\rb*. \rb Each one|וּלְאִ֗ישׁ\rb* \rb also had two wings|שְׁתַּ֤יִם\rb* \rb covering|מְכַסּוֹת֙\rb* \rb its body|גְּוִיֹּתֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb When the creatures moved|בְּלֶכְתָּ֔ם\rb*, \rb I heard|וָאֶשְׁמַ֣ע\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sound|ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of their wings|כַּנְפֵיהֶ֡ם\rb* \rb like the roar|כְּקוֹל֩\rb* \rb of many|רַבִּ֤ים\rb* \rb waters|מַ֨יִם\rb*, \rb like the voice|כְּקוֹל־\rb* \rb of the Almighty|שַׁדַּי֙\rb*,\f + \fr 1:24 \ft Hebrew \fqa Shaddai\f* \rb like|ק֥וֹל\rb* \rb the tumult|הֲמֻלָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |כְּק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of an army|מַחֲנֶ֑ה\rb*.
\p \rb When they stood still|בְּעָמְדָ֖ם\rb*, \rb they lowered|תְּרַפֶּ֥ינָה\rb* \rb their wings|כַנְפֵיהֶֽן׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb And there came|וַיְהִי־\rb* \rb a voice|ק֕וֹל\rb* \rb from above|מֵעַ֕ל\rb* \rb the expanse|לָרָקִ֖יעַ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb their heads|רֹאשָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb as they stood still|בְּעָמְדָ֖ם\rb* \rb with their wings|כַנְפֵיהֶֽן׃\rb* \rb lowered|תְּרַפֶּ֥ינָה\rb*.
\p \v 26 \rb Above|וּמִמַּ֗עַל\rb* \rb the expanse|לָרָקִ֙יעַ֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb their heads|רֹאשָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb was|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the likeness|דְּמ֣וּת\rb* \rb of a throne|כִּסֵּ֑א\rb*\rb |וְעַל֙\rb* \rb with the appearance|כְּמַרְאֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of sapphire|סַפִּ֖יר\rb*\rb |אֶֽבֶן־\rb*, \rb and on the throne|הַכִּסֵּ֔א\rb* \rb high above|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb was a figure|דְּמ֣וּת\rb* \rb like that|כְּמַרְאֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of a man|אָדָ֛ם\rb*\rb |דְּמ֞וּת\rb*\rb |מִלְמָֽעְלָה׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb From what seemed|מִמַּרְאֵ֥ה\rb* \rb to be His waist|מָתְנָ֖יו\rb* \rb up|וּלְמָ֑עְלָה\rb*, \rb I saw|וָאֵ֣רֶא׀\rb* \rb a gleam|כְּעֵ֣ין\rb* \rb like amber|חַשְׁמַ֗ל\rb*, \rb with what looked|כְּמַרְאֵה־\rb* \rb like fire|אֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb within|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb it|לָהּ֙\rb* \rb all around|סָבִ֔יב\rb*. \rb And from what seemed|וּמִמַּרְאֵ֤ה\rb* \rb to be His waist|מָתְנָיו֙\rb* \rb down|וּלְמַ֔טָּה\rb*, \rb I saw|רָאִ֙יתִי֙\rb* \rb what looked|כְּמַרְאֵה־\rb* \rb like fire|אֵ֔שׁ\rb*; \rb and brilliant light|וְנֹ֥גַֽהּ\rb* \rb surrounded Him|סָבִֽיב׃\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb The appearance|כְּמַרְאֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of the brilliant light|הַנֹּ֙גַהּ֙\rb* \rb all around Him|סָבִ֔יב\rb* \rb was like that|מַרְאֵ֤ה\rb* \rb of a rainbow|הַקֶּ֡שֶׁת\rb* \rb in a cloud|בֶעָנָ֜ן\rb* \rb on a rainy|הַגֶּ֗שֶׁם\rb* \rb day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb*. \rb This|ה֕וּא\rb* \rb was the appearance|מַרְאֵ֖ה\rb* \rb of the likeness|דְּמ֣וּת\rb* \rb of the glory|כְּבוֹד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb And when I saw it|וָֽאֶרְאֶה֙\rb*, \rb I fell|וָאֶפֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb facedown|עַל־\rb*\rb |פָּנַ֔י\rb* \rb and heard|וָאֶשְׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb a voice|ק֥וֹל\rb* \rb speaking|מְדַבֵּֽר׃ס\rb*.
\c 2
\s1 Ezekiel’s Call
\p \v 1 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָם֙\rb*,\f + \fr 2:1 \ft Or \fqa Son of Adam\ft ; here and throughout Ezekiel\f*” \rb He said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָ֑י\rb*, “\rb stand up|עֲמֹ֣ד\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb your feet|רַגְלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and I will speak|וַאֲדַבֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb to you|אֹתָֽךְ׃\rb*.” \v 2 \rb And as|כַּֽאֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb He spoke|דִּבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*, \rb the Spirit|ר֗וּחַ\rb* \rb entered|וַתָּ֧בֹא\rb* \rb me|בִ֣י\rb* \rb and set me|וַתַּעֲמִדֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb my feet|רַגְלָ֑י\rb*, \rb and I heard|וָאֶשְׁמַ֕ע\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb Him speaking|מִדַּבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָֽי׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 3 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָם֙\rb*,” \rb He said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֗י\rb*, “\rb I|אֲנִ֤י\rb*\rb |אֽוֹתְךָ֙\rb* \rb am sending|שׁוֹלֵ֨חַ\rb* \rb you to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a rebellious|הַמּוֹרְדִ֖ים\rb* \rb nation|גּוֹיִ֥ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb has rebelled|מָרְדוּ־\rb* \rb against Me|בִ֑י\rb*. \rb To|עַד־\rb*\rb |עֶ֖צֶם\rb* \rb this very|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb they|הֵ֤מָּה\rb* \rb and their fathers|וַאֲבוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb have rebelled|פָּ֣שְׁעוּ\rb* \rb against Me|בִ֔י\rb*. \v 4 \rb They are obstinate|קְשֵׁ֤י\rb*\rb |פָנִים֙\rb* \rb and stubborn|וְחִזְקֵי־\rb*\rb |לֵ֔ב\rb* \rb children|וְהַבָּנִ֗ים\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb am sending|שׁוֹלֵ֥חַ\rb*\rb |אוֹתְךָ֖\rb* \rb you to them|אֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and you are to say|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, ‘\rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהֹוִֽה׃\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*.’
\p \v 5 \rb And whether|אִם־\rb* \rb they|וְהֵ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb listen|יִשְׁמְע֣וּ\rb* \rb or|וְאִם־\rb* \rb refuse to listen|יֶחְדָּ֔לוּ\rb*— \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb they|הֵ֑מָּה\rb* \rb are a rebellious|מְרִ֖י\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb*— \rb they will know|וְיָ֣דְע֔וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb a prophet|נָבִ֖יא\rb* \rb has been|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb among them|בְתוֹכָֽם׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb But you|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָ֠דָם\rb*, \rb do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָ֨א\rb* \rb of them|מֵהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb or their words|וּמִדִּבְרֵיהֶ֣ם\rb*. \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָ֗א\rb*, \rb though|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb briers|סָרָבִ֤ים\rb* \rb and thorns|וְסַלּוֹנִים֙\rb* \rb surround|אוֹתָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb and you dwell|יוֹשֵׁ֑ב\rb* \rb among|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb scorpions|עַקְרַבִּ֖ים\rb*. \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִּירָא֙\rb* \rb of their words|מִדִּבְרֵיהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb or dismayed|תֵּחָ֔ת\rb* \rb by their presence|וּמִפְּנֵיהֶ֣ם\rb*,\rb |אַל־\rb* \rb though|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb they are a rebellious|מְרִ֖י\rb*\rb |הֵֽמָּה׃\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb*. \v 7 \rb But speak|וְדִבַּרְתָּ֤\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My words|דְּבָרַי֙\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb whether|אִֽם־\rb* \rb they listen|יִשְׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb or|וְאִם־\rb* \rb refuse|יֶחְדָּ֑לוּ\rb* \rb to listen|כִּ֥י\rb*, \rb for they|הֵֽמָּה׃פ\rb* \rb are rebellious|מְרִ֖י\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb And you|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb listen|שְׁמַע֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֤ת\rb* \rb to what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb tell you|מְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb*.\rb |אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb be|תְּהִי־\rb* \rb rebellious|מֶ֖רִי\rb* \rb like that rebellious|הַמֶּ֑רִי\rb* \rb house|כְּבֵ֣ית\rb*. \rb Open|פְּצֵ֣ה\rb* \rb your mouth|פִ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and eat|וֶאֱכֹ֕ל\rb*\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb give|נֹתֵ֥ן\rb* \rb you|אֵלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 9 \rb Then I looked|וָאֶרְאֶ֕ה\rb* \rb and saw|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb a hand|יָ֖ד\rb* \rb reaching out|שְׁלוּחָ֣ה\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָ֑י\rb*, \rb and|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb in it|ב֖וֹ\rb* \rb was a scroll|מְגִלַּת־\rb*\rb |סֵֽפֶר׃\rb*, \v 10 \rb which He unrolled|וַיִּפְרֹ֤שׂ\rb*\rb |אוֹתָהּ֙\rb* \rb before me|לְפָנַ֔י\rb*.\rb |וְהִ֥יא\rb* \rb And written|כְתוּבָ֖ה\rb* \rb on the front|פָּנִ֣ים\rb* \rb and back|וְאָח֑וֹר\rb*\rb |וְכָת֣וּב\rb* \rb of it|אֵלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb were words of lamentation|קִנִ֥ים\rb*, \rb mourning|וָהֶ֖גֶה\rb*, \rb and woe|וָהִֽי׃ס\rb*.
\c 3
\s1 Ezekiel Eats the Scroll
\r (\ref Revelation 10:1–11|REV 10:1-11\ref*)
\p \v 1 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*,” \rb He said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*,\rb |אֵ֥ת\rb* “\rb eat|אֱכ֑וֹל\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you find here|תִּמְצָ֖א\rb*. \rb Eat|אֱכוֹל֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb* \rb scroll|הַמְּגִלָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb then go|וְלֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb and speak|דַּבֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 2 \rb So I opened|וָאֶפְתַּ֖ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my mouth|פִּ֑י\rb*, \rb and He fed|וַיַּ֣אֲכִלֵ֔נִי\rb* \rb me|אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the scroll|הַמְּגִלָּ֥ה\rb*\rb |הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָם֙\rb*,”\rb |בִּטְנְךָ֤\rb* \rb He said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֗י\rb*, “\rb eat|תַֽאֲכֵל֙\rb* \rb and fill|תְמַלֵּ֔א\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb your stomach|וּמֵעֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb with this|הַזֹּ֔את\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb scroll|הַמְּגִלָּ֣ה\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am giving you|נֹתֵ֣ן\rb*.”\rb |אֵלֶ֑יךָ\rb*
\p \rb So I ate|וָאֹ֣כְלָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and it was|וַתְּהִ֥י\rb* \rb as sweet|לְמָתֽוֹק׃פ\rb* \rb as honey|כִּדְבַ֥שׁ\rb* \rb in my mouth|בְּפִ֖י\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Then He said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָ֑י\rb*, “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb go now|לֶךְ־\rb*\rb |בֹּא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and speak|וְדִבַּרְתָּ֥\rb* \rb My words|בִדְבָרַ֖י\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb For|כִּ֡י\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb are not|לֹא֩\rb* \rb being sent|שָׁל֑וּחַ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb a people|עַ֨ם\rb* \rb of unfamiliar|עִמְקֵ֥י\rb* \rb speech|שָׂפָ֛ה\rb* \rb or difficult|וְכִבְדֵ֥י\rb* \rb language|לָשׁ֖וֹן\rb*, \rb but to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֖ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* — \v 6 \rb not|לֹ֣א׀\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the many|רַבִּ֗ים\rb* \rb peoples|עַמִּ֣ים\rb* \rb of unfamiliar|עִמְקֵ֤י\rb* \rb speech|שָׂפָה֙\rb* \rb and difficult|וְכִבְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb language|לָשׁ֔וֹן\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb words|דִּבְרֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb you cannot|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb understand|תִשְׁמַ֖ע\rb*. \rb Surely|אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹ֤א\rb* \rb if I had sent you|שְׁלַחְתִּ֔יךָ\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb*, \rb they|הֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb would have listened|יִשְׁמְע֥וּ\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb But the house|וּבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*\rb |לֹ֤א\rb* \rb will be unwilling|יֹאבוּ֙\rb* \rb to listen|לִשְׁמֹ֣עַ\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb*\rb |אֵינָ֥ם\rb* \rb they are unwilling|אֹבִ֖ים\rb* \rb to listen|לִשְׁמֹ֣עַ\rb* \rb to Me|אֵלָ֑י\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb is hard-headed|חִזְקֵי־\rb*\rb |מֵ֥צַח\rb* \rb and hard-hearted|וּקְשֵׁי־\rb*\rb |לֵ֖ב\rb*\rb |הֵֽמָּה׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Behold|הִנֵּ֨ה\rb*, \rb I will make|נָתַ֧תִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your face|פָּנֶ֛יךָ\rb* \rb as hard|חֲזָקִ֖ים\rb* \rb as|לְעֻמַּ֣ת\rb* \rb their faces|פְּנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*,\rb |וְאֶֽת־\rb* \rb and your forehead|מִצְחֲךָ֥\rb* \rb as hard|חָזָ֖ק\rb* \rb as|לְעֻמַּ֥ת\rb* \rb their foreheads|מִצְחָֽם׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb I will make|נָתַ֣תִּי\rb* \rb your forehead|מִצְחֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb like a diamond|כְּשָׁמִ֛יר\rb*, \rb harder|חָזָ֥ק\rb* \rb than flint|מִצֹּ֖ר\rb*. \rb Do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb be afraid|תִירָ֤א\rb* \rb of them|אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb or|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb dismayed|תֵחַ֣ת\rb* \rb at their presence|מִפְּנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb even though|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb they|הֵֽמָּה׃פ\rb* \rb are a rebellious|מְרִ֖י\rb* \rb house|בֵּֽית־\rb*.”
\p \v 10 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*,” \rb He added|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלָ֑י\rb*, “\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb listen carefully|וּבְאָזְנֶ֥יךָ\rb*\rb |שְׁמָֽע׃\rb* \rb to all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the words|דְּבָרַי֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I speak|אֲדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb and take them|קַ֥ח\rb* \rb to heart|בִּֽלְבָבְךָ֖\rb*. \v 11 \rb |וְלֵ֨ךְ\rb* \rb Go|בֹּ֤א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your people|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמֶּ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb the exiles|הַגּוֹלָה֙\rb*; \rb speak|וְדִבַּרְתָּ֤\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb to them|אֶל־\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, ‘\rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהֹוִ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*,’ \rb whether|אִֽם־\rb* \rb they listen|יִשְׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb or|וְאִם־\rb* \rb refuse to listen|יֶחְדָּֽלוּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 12 \rb Then the Spirit|ר֔וּחַ\rb*\f + \fr 3:12 \ft Or \fqa the wind\ft ; also in verse 14\f* \rb lifted me up|וַתִּשָּׂאֵ֣נִי\rb*, \rb and I heard|וָאֶשְׁמַ֣ע\rb* \rb a great|גָּד֑וֹל\rb* \rb rumbling|רַ֣עַשׁ\rb* \rb sound|ק֖וֹל\rb* \rb behind me|אַחֲרַ֔י\rb*: “\rb Blessed be|בָּר֥וּךְ\rb* \rb the glory|כְּבוֹד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb in His dwelling place|מִמְּקוֹמֽוֹ׃\rb*!”\f + \fr 3:12 \ft Or \fqa sound behind me as the glory of the LORD rose from its place!\f* \v 13 \rb It was the sound|וְק֣וֹל׀\rb* \rb of the wings|כַּנְפֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the living creatures|הַחַיּ֗וֹת\rb* \rb brushing|מַשִּׁיקוֹת֙\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb one|אִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb another|אֲחוֹתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb and the sound|וְק֥וֹל\rb* \rb of the wheels|הָאוֹפַנִּ֖ים\rb* \rb beside them|לְעֻמָּתָ֑ם\rb*, \rb a great|גָּדֽוֹל׃\rb* \rb rumbling|רַ֥עַשׁ\rb* \rb sound|וְק֖וֹל\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb So the Spirit|וְר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb lifted me up|נְשָׂאַ֖תְנִי\rb* \rb and took me away|וַתִּקָּחֵ֑נִי\rb*, \rb and I went|וָאֵלֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb in bitterness|מַר֙\rb* \rb and in the anger|בַּחֲמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of my spirit|רוּחִ֔י\rb*, \rb with the strong|חָזָֽקָה׃\rb* \rb hand|וְיַד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb upon me|עָלַ֖י\rb*. \v 15 \rb I came|וָאָב֨וֹא\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the exiles|הַגּוֹלָ֜ה\rb*\rb |תֵּ֣ל\rb* \rb at Tel-abib|אָ֠בִיב\rb* \rb who dwelt|הַיֹּשְׁבִ֤ים\rb* \rb by|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb the River|נְהַר־\rb* \rb Kebar|כְּבָר֙\rb*. \rb And for seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb I sat|וָאֲשֶׁר\rb* \rb where|שָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb they|הֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb sat|יוֹשְׁבִ֣ים\rb* \rb and remained|וָאֵשֵׁ֥ב\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֛ם\rb* \rb among them|בְּתוֹכָֽם׃\rb*, \rb overwhelmed|מַשְׁמִ֥ים\rb*.
\s1 A Watchman for Israel
\p \v 16 \rb At the end|מִקְצֵ֖ה\rb* \rb of seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֑ים פ\rb*\rb |וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֕י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 17 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*, \rb I have made|נְתַתִּ֖יךָ\rb* \rb you a watchman|צֹפֶ֥ה\rb* \rb for the house|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb Whenever you hear|וְשָׁמַעְתָּ֤\rb* \rb a word|דָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb from|מִמֶּֽנִּי׃\rb* \rb My mouth|מִפִּי֙\rb*, \rb give them a warning|וְהִזְהַרְתָּ֥\rb* \rb from Me|אוֹתָ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb If I say|בְּאָמְרִ֤י\rb* \rb to the wicked man|לָֽרָשָׁע֙\rb*, ‘\rb You will surely die|מ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |תָּמ֔וּת\rb*,’ \rb but you do not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb warn him|הִזְהַרְתּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb speak out|דִבַּ֛רְתָּ\rb* \rb to warn|לְהַזְהִ֥יר\rb* \rb him|רָשָׁ֛ע\rb* \rb from his wicked|הָרְשָׁעָ֖ה\rb* \rb way|מִדַּרְכּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb to save his life|לְחַיֹּת֑וֹ\rb*, \rb that|ה֤וּא\rb* \rb wicked man|רָשָׁע֙\rb* \rb will die|יָמ֔וּת\rb* \rb in his iniquity|בַּעֲוֺנ֣וֹ\rb*,\f + \fr 3:18 \ft Or \fqa for his iniquity\ft ; also in verse 19\f* \rb and I will hold you|מִיָּדְךָ֥\rb* \rb responsible for|אֲבַקֵּֽשׁ׃\rb* \rb his blood|וְדָמ֖וֹ\rb*. \v 19 \rb But if|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you|וְאַתָּה֙\rb* \rb warn|הִזְהַ֣רְתָּ\rb* \rb a wicked man|רָשָׁ֔ע\rb* \rb and he does not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb turn|שָׁב֙\rb* \rb from his wickedness|מֵֽרִשְׁע֔וֹ\rb* \rb and his wicked|הָרְשָׁעָ֑ה\rb* \rb way|וּמִדַּרְכּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb he|ה֚וּא\rb* \rb will die|יָמ֔וּת\rb* \rb in his iniquity|בַּעֲוֺנ֣וֹ\rb*, \rb but you|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb will have saved|הִצַּֽלְתָּ׃ס\rb* \rb yourself|נַפְשְׁךָ֥\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb Now if a righteous man|צַדִּ֤יק\rb* \rb turns|וּבְשׁ֨וּב\rb* \rb from his righteousness|מִצִּדְקוֹ֙\rb* \rb and commits|וְעָ֣שָׂה\rb* \rb iniquity|עָ֔וֶל\rb*, \rb and I put|וְנָתַתִּ֥י\rb* \rb a stumbling block|מִכְשׁ֛וֹל\rb* \rb before him|לְפָנָ֖יו\rb*, \rb he|ה֣וּא\rb* \rb will die|יָמ֑וּת\rb*. \rb If|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb you did not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb warn him|הִזְהַרְתּוֹ֙\rb*, \rb he will die|יָמ֔וּת\rb* \rb in his sin|בְּחַטָּאת֣וֹ\rb*,\f + \fr 3:20 \ft Or \fqa for his sin\f* \rb and the righteous acts|צִדְקֹתָו֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he did|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb be remembered|תִזָּכַ֗רְןָ\rb*. \rb And I will hold you|מִיָּדְךָ֥\rb* \rb responsible for|אֲבַקֵּֽשׁ׃\rb* \rb his blood|וְדָמ֖וֹ\rb*. \v 21 \rb But if|כִּ֧י\rb* \rb you|וְאַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb warn|הִזְהַרְתּ֣וֹ\rb* \rb the righteous man|צַדִּ֗יק\rb*\rb |צַדִּ֖יק\rb* \rb not|לְבִלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb to sin|חֲטֹ֛א\rb*, \rb and he|וְה֣וּא\rb* \rb does not|לֹא־\rb* \rb sin|חָטָ֑א\rb*, \rb he will indeed live|חָי֤וֹ\rb*\rb |יִֽחְיֶה֙\rb* \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb he heeded your warning|נִזְהָ֔ר\rb*, \rb and you|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb will have saved|הִצַּֽלְתָּ׃ס\rb* \rb yourself|נַפְשְׁךָ֥\rb*.”
\p \v 22 \rb And there|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb the hand|יַד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb was|וַתְּהִ֥י\rb* \rb upon me|עָלַ֛י\rb*, \rb and He said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֗י\rb*, “\rb Get up|ק֥וּם\rb*, \rb go out|צֵא֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the plain|הַבִּקְעָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and there|וְשָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb I will speak|אֲדַבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb with you|אוֹתָֽךְ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 23 \rb So I got up|וָאָקוּם֮\rb* \rb and went out|וָאֵצֵ֣א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the plain|הַבִּקְעָה֒\rb*, \rb and behold|וְהִנֵּה־\rb*, \rb the glory|כְּבוֹד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb was present|עֹמֵ֔ד\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֤ם\rb*, \rb like the glory|כַּכָּב֕וֹד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I had seen|רָאִ֖יתִי\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the River|נְהַר־\rb* \rb Kebar|כְּבָ֑ר\rb*, \rb and I fell|וָאֶפֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb facedown|עַל־\rb*\rb |פָּנָֽי׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb Then the Spirit|ר֔וּחַ\rb* \rb entered|וַתָּבֹא־\rb* \rb me|בִ֣י\rb* \rb and set me|וַתַּעֲמִדֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb my feet|רַגְלָ֑י\rb*. \rb He spoke|וַיְדַבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb with me|אֹתִי֙\rb* \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֔י\rb*, “\rb Go|בֹּ֥א\rb*, \rb shut yourself|הִסָּגֵ֖ר\rb* \rb inside|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb your house|בֵּיתֶֽךָ׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb And you|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*,\rb |הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb they will tie|נָתְנ֤וּ\rb* \rb with ropes|עֲבוֹתִ֔ים\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*, \rb and you will be bound|וַאֲסָר֖וּךָ\rb* \rb so that you cannot|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb go out|תֵצֵ֖א\rb* \rb among the people|בְּתוֹכָֽם׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb I will make your tongue|וּלְשֽׁוֹנְךָ֙\rb* \rb stick|אַדְבִּ֣יק\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the roof of your mouth|חִכֶּ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb and you will be silent|וְנֶֽאֱלַ֔מְתָּ\rb* \rb and unable|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |תִֽהְיֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |לְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb to rebuke them|מוֹכִ֑יחַ\rb*, \rb though|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb they|הֵֽמָּה׃\rb* \rb are a rebellious|מְרִ֖י\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb But when I speak|וּֽבְדַבְּרִ֤י\rb* \rb with you|אֽוֹתְךָ֙\rb*, \rb I will open|אֶפְתַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your mouth|פִּ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb and you are to tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, ‘\rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהֹוִ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*.’ \rb Whoever listens|יִשְׁמָע֙\rb*, \rb let him listen|הַשֹּׁמֵ֤עַ׀\rb*; \rb and whoever refuses|יֶחְדָּ֔ל\rb*, \rb let him refuse|וְהֶחָדֵ֣ל׀\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb they|הֵֽמָּה׃ס\rb* \rb are a rebellious|מְרִ֖י\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb*.[’’]
\c 4
\s1 A Sign of Jerusalem’s Siege
\p \v 1 “\rb Now you|וְאַתָּ֤ה\rb*, \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָם֙\rb*, \rb take|קַח־\rb* \rb a brick|לְבֵנָ֔ה\rb*, \rb place|וְנָתַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb it|אוֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb before you|לְפָנֶ֑יךָ\rb*, \rb and draw|וְחַקּוֹתָ֥\rb* \rb on it|עָלֶ֛יהָ\rb* \rb the city|עִ֖יר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb Then lay|וְנָתַתָּ֨ה\rb* \rb siege|מָצ֗וֹר\rb* \rb against it|עָלֶ֜יהָ\rb*: \rb Construct|וּבָנִ֤יתָ\rb* \rb a siege wall|דָּיֵ֔ק\rb*, \rb build|וְשָׁפַכְתָּ֥\rb* \rb a ramp|סֹֽלְלָ֑ה\rb* \rb to it|עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb*, \rb set up|וְנָתַתָּ֨ה\rb* \rb camps|מַחֲנ֛וֹת\rb* \rb against it|עָלֶ֧יהָ\rb*, \rb and place|וְשִׂים־\rb* \rb battering rams|כָּרִ֖ים\rb* \rb around it|עָלֶ֥יהָ\rb* \rb on all sides|סָבִֽיב׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb Then|וְאַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb take|קַח־\rb* \rb an iron|בַּרְזֶ֔ל\rb* \rb plate|מַחֲבַ֣ת\rb* \rb and set it up|וְנָתַתָּ֤ה\rb*\rb |אוֹתָהּ֙\rb* \rb as an iron|בַּרְזֶ֔ל\rb* \rb wall|קִ֣יר\rb* \rb between yourself|בֵּינְךָ֖\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb and the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb*. \rb Turn|וַהֲכִינֹתָה֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your face|פָּנֶ֨יךָ\rb* \rb toward it|אֵלֶ֜יהָ\rb* \rb so that it is|וְהָיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb under siege|בַמָּצוֹר֙\rb*, \rb and besiege it|וְצַרְתָּ֣\rb*.\rb |עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb This|הִ֖יא\rb* \rb will be a sign|א֥וֹת\rb* \rb to the house|לְבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Then|וְאַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb lie down|שְׁכַב֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb your left|הַשְּׂמָאלִ֔י\rb* \rb side|צִדְּךָ֣\rb* \rb and place|וְשַׂמְתָּ֛\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the iniquity|עֲוֺ֥ן\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb upon yourself|עָלָ֑יו\rb*. \rb You are to bear|תִּשָּׂ֖א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their iniquity|עֲוֺנָֽם׃\rb* \rb for the number|מִסְפַּ֤ר\rb* \rb of days|הַיָּמִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you lie on your side|תִּשְׁכַּ֣ב\rb*\rb |עָלָ֔יו\rb*. \v 5 \rb For I|וַאֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb have assigned|נָתַ֤תִּֽי\rb* \rb to you|לְךָ֙\rb*\rb |יָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb 390|שְׁלֹשׁ־\rb*\rb |מֵא֥וֹת\rb*\rb |וְתִשְׁעִ֖ים\rb* \rb days|י֑וֹם\rb*, \rb according to the number|לְמִסְפַּ֣ר\rb* \rb of years|שְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of their iniquity|עֲוֺנָ֔ם\rb*. \rb So you shall bear|וְנָשָׂ֖אתָ\rb* \rb the iniquity|עֲוֺ֥ן\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb When you have completed|וְכִלִּיתָ֣\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb these days|אֵ֗לֶּה\rb*, \rb lie down|וְשָׁ֨כַבְתָּ֜\rb* \rb again|שֵׁנִ֔ית\rb*, \rb but on|עַל־\rb* \rb your right|הַיְמוֹנִי\rb* \rb side|צִדְּךָ֤\rb*, \rb and bear|וְנָשָׂ֖אתָ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the iniquity|עֲוֺ֣ן\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*. \rb I have assigned|נְתַתִּ֥יו\rb* \rb to you|לָֽךְ׃\rb* \rb 40|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb days|י֔וֹם\rb*, \rb a day|י֧וֹם\rb*\rb |י֥וֹם\rb* \rb for each year|לַשָּׁנָ֛ה\rb*\rb |לַשָּׁנָ֖ה\rb*. \v 7 \rb You must turn|תָּכִ֣ין\rb* \rb your face|פָּנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb toward|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the siege|מְצ֤וֹר\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb with your arm|וּֽזְרֹעֲךָ֖\rb* \rb bared|חֲשׂוּפָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and prophesy|וְנִבֵּאתָ֖\rb* \rb against it|עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Now behold|וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb*, \rb I will tie you up|נָתַ֥תִּי\rb* \rb with ropes|עֲבוֹתִ֑ים\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb so you cannot|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb turn|תֵהָפֵ֤ךְ\rb* \rb from side|מִֽצִּדְּךָ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb side|צִדֶּ֔ךָ\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb you have finished|כַּלּוֹתְךָ֖\rb* \rb the days|יְמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of your siege|מְצוּרֶֽךָ׃\rb*.
\s1 The Defiled Bread
\p \v 9 \rb |וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb But take|קַח־\rb* \rb wheat|חִטִּ֡ין\rb*, \rb barley|וּ֠שְׂעֹרִים\rb*, \rb beans|וּפ֨וֹל\rb*, \rb lentils|וַעֲדָשִׁ֜ים\rb*, \rb millet|וְדֹ֣חַן\rb*, \rb and spelt|וְכֻסְּמִ֗ים\rb*; \rb put|וְנָתַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb in a single|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb container|בִּכְלִ֣י\rb* \rb and make|וְעָשִׂ֧יתָ\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb into bread|לְלָ֑חֶם\rb* \rb for yourself|לְךָ֖\rb*. \rb This is what you are to eat|תֹּאכֲלֶֽנּוּ׃\rb* \rb during the|מִסְפַּ֨ר\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֜ים\rb* \rb 390|שְׁלֹשׁ־\rb*\rb |מֵא֧וֹת\rb*\rb |וְתִשְׁעִ֛ים\rb* \rb days|י֖וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |אַתָּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb you lie|שׁוֹכֵ֣ב\rb* \rb on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb your side|צִדְּךָ֗\rb*. \v 10 \rb You are to weigh out|בְּמִשְׁק֕וֹל\rb* \rb twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb shekels|שֶׁ֖קֶל\rb* \rb of food|וּמַאֲכָֽלְךָ֙\rb*\f + \fr 4:10 \fqa 20 shekels \ft is approximately 8 ounces or 228 grams of food.\f*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb to eat|תֹּאכֲלֶ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb each day|לַיּ֑וֹם\rb*, \rb and you are to eat it|תֹּאכֲלֶֽנּוּ׃\rb* \rb at set times|מֵעֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb*\rb |עֵ֖ת\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb You are also to measure out|בִּמְשׂוּרָ֥ה\rb* \rb a sixth|שִׁשִּׁ֣ית\rb* \rb of a hin|הַהִ֑ין\rb* \rb of water|וּמַ֛יִם\rb*\f + \fr 4:11 \fqa A sixth of a hin \ft is approximately 0.65 quarts or 0.61 liters of water.\f* \rb to drink|תִשְׁתֶּ֖ה\rb*, \rb and you are to drink it|תִּשְׁתֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb at set times|מֵעֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb*\rb |עֵ֖ת\rb*. \v 12 \rb And you shall eat|תֹּֽאכֲלֶ֑נָּה\rb* \rb the food|וְהִ֗יא\rb* \rb as you would a barley|שְׂעֹרִ֖ים\rb* \rb cake|וְעֻגַ֥ת\rb*, \rb after you bake|תְּעֻגֶ֖נָה\rb* \rb it over dried human|הָֽאָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb excrement|בְּגֶֽלְלֵי֙\rb*\rb |צֵאַ֣ת\rb* \rb in the sight of the people|לְעֵינֵיהֶֽם׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 13 \rb Then the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*, “\rb This is how|כָּ֣כָה\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will eat|יֹאכְל֧וּ\rb* \rb their defiled|טָמֵ֑א\rb* \rb bread|לַחְמָ֖ם\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֕ם\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I will banish them|אַדִּיחֵ֖ם\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 14 “\rb Ah|אֲהָהּ֙\rb*, \rb Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb*,” \rb I said|וָאֹמַ֗ר\rb*, “\rb |הִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb I|נַפְשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb have never|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb defiled myself|מְטֻמָּאָ֑ה\rb*.\f + \fr 4:14 \ft Hebrew \fqa “Ah, Lord GOD,” I said, “Behold, my soul has never been made unclean.\f* \rb From my youth|מִנְּעוּרַ֣י\rb* \rb until|וְעַד־\rb* \rb now|עַ֔תָּה\rb* \rb I have not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb eaten|אָכַ֙לְתִּי֙\rb* \rb anything found dead|וּנְבֵלָ֨ה\rb* \rb or mauled by wild beasts|וּטְרֵפָ֤ה\rb*. \rb No|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb unclean|פִּגּֽוּל׃ס\rb* \rb meat|בְּשַׂ֥ר\rb* \rb has ever entered|בָ֥א\rb* \rb my mouth|בְּפִ֖י\rb*.”
\p \v 15 “\rb Look|רְאֵ֗ה\rb*,” \rb He replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֔י\rb*, “\rb I will let|נָתַ֤תִּֽי\rb* \rb you|לְךָ֙\rb* \rb use cow|הַבָּקָ֔ר\rb* \rb dung|צְפוּעֵי\rb* \rb instead of|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb human|הָֽאָדָ֑ם\rb* \rb excrement|גֶּלְלֵ֣י\rb*, \rb and you may bake|וְעָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb*\rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb your bread|לַחְמְךָ֖\rb* \rb over that|עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃ס\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb Then He told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb me|אֵלַ֗י\rb*, “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָם֙\rb*,\rb |הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb I am going to cut off|שֹׁבֵ֤ר\rb* \rb the supply|מַטֵּה־\rb*\f + \fr 4:16 \ft Hebrew \fqa staff\f* \rb of food|לֶ֙חֶם֙\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*. \rb They will anxiously|וּבִדְאָגָ֑ה\rb* \rb eat|וְאָכְלוּ־\rb* \rb bread|לֶ֥חֶם\rb* \rb rationed by weight|בְּמִשְׁקָ֖ל\rb*, \rb and in despair|וּבְשִׁמָּמ֖וֹן\rb* \rb they will drink|יִשְׁתּֽוּ׃\rb* \rb water|וּמַ֕יִם\rb* \rb by measure|בִּמְשׂוּרָ֥ה\rb*. \v 17 \rb So|לְמַ֥עַן\rb* \rb they will lack|יַחְסְר֖וּ\rb* \rb food|לֶ֣חֶם\rb* \rb and water|וָמָ֑יִם\rb*; \rb they will be appalled|וְנָשַׁ֙מּוּ֙\rb* \rb at the sight of one|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb another|וְאָחִ֔יו\rb* \rb wasting away|וְנָמַ֖קּוּ\rb* \rb in their iniquity|בַּעֲוֺנָֽם׃פ\rb*.[’’]
\c 5
\s1 The Razor of Judgment
\p \v 1 “\rb As for you|וְאַתָּ֨ה\rb*, \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֜ם\rb*, \rb take|קַח־\rb* \rb a sharp|חַדָּ֗ה\rb* \rb sword|חֶ֣רֶב\rb*, \rb use it|תִּקָּחֶ֣נָּה\rb* \rb as a barber’s|הַגַּלָּבִים֙\rb* \rb razor|תַּ֤עַר\rb*, \rb and shave|וְהַעֲבַרְתָּ֥\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb your head|רֹאשְׁךָ֖\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and beard|זְקָנֶ֑ךָ\rb*. \rb Then take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֥\rb* \rb a set of scales|מֹאזְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |מִשְׁקָ֖ל\rb* \rb and divide the hair|וְחִלַּקְתָּֽם׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb When the days|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the siege|הַמָּצ֑וֹר\rb* \rb have ended|כִּמְלֹ֖את\rb*, \rb you are to burn up|תַּבְעִיר֙\rb* \rb a third of the hair|שְׁלִשִׁ֗ית\rb*\rb |בָּא֤וּר\rb* \rb inside|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb*; \rb you are also to take|וְלָֽקַחְתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb a third|הַשְּׁלִשִׁ֗ית\rb* \rb and slash|תַּכֶּ֤ה\rb* \rb it with the sword|בַחֶ֙רֶב֙\rb* \rb all around the city|סְבִ֣יבוֹתֶ֔יהָ\rb*; \rb and you are to scatter|תִּזְרֶ֣ה\rb* \rb a third|וְהַשְּׁלִשִׁית֙\rb* \rb to the wind|לָר֔וּחַ\rb*. \rb For I will unleash|אָרִ֥יק\rb* \rb a sword|וְחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb behind them|אַחֲרֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb But you are to take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֥\rb*\rb |מִשָּׁ֖ם\rb* \rb a few|מְעַ֣ט\rb* \rb strands of hair|בְּמִסְפָּ֑ר\rb* \rb and secure|וְצַרְתָּ֥\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb in the folds of your garment|בִּכְנָפֶֽיךָ׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb Again|ע֣וֹד\rb*, \rb take|תִּקָּ֔ח\rb* \rb a few of these|וּמֵהֶם֙\rb*, \rb throw|וְהִשְׁלַכְתָּ֤\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb*\rb |תּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the fire|הָאֵ֔שׁ\rb*, \rb and burn|וְשָׂרַפְתָּ֥\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb*\rb |בָּאֵ֑שׁ\rb*. \rb From there|מִמֶּ֥נּוּ\rb* \rb a fire|אֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb will spread|תֵצֵא־\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהֹוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: ‘\rb This is|זֹ֚את\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*, \rb which I have set|שַׂמְתִּ֑יהָ\rb* \rb in the center|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb*, \rb with countries|אֲרָצֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb all around her|וּסְבִיבוֹתֶ֖יהָ\rb*. \v 6 \rb But she has rebelled|וַתֶּ֨מֶר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb against My ordinances|מִשְׁפָּטַ֤י\rb* \rb more wickedly|לְרִשְׁעָה֙\rb* \rb than|מִן־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶ֨ת־\rb* \rb against My statutes|חֻקּוֹתַ֔י\rb* \rb worse than|מִן־\rb* \rb the countries|הָאֲרָצ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb around her|סְבִיבוֹתֶ֑יהָ\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb her people have rejected|מָאָ֔סוּ\rb* \rb My ordinances|בְמִשְׁפָּטַי֙\rb* \rb and have not|לֹא־\rb* \rb walked|הָלְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb in|בָהֶֽם׃ס\rb* \rb My statutes|וְחֻקּוֹתַ֖י\rb*.’
\p \v 7 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֞ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר׀\rb*: ‘\rb |יַ֤עַן\rb* \rb You have been more insubordinate|הֲמָנְכֶם֙\rb* \rb than|מִן־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb around you|סְבִיבֽוֹתֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*; \rb you have not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb walked|הֲלַכְתֶּ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb in My statutes|בְּחֻקּוֹתַי֙\rb* \rb or|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb kept|עֲשִׂיתֶ֑ם\rb* \rb My ordinances|מִשְׁפָּטַ֖י\rb*, \rb nor|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb have you even conformed|עֲשִׂיתֶֽם׃ס\rb*\f + \fr 5:7 \ft Some Hebrew manuscripts and Syriac \fqa My ordinances; you have even conformed\f* \rb to the ordinances|וּֽכְמִשְׁפְּטֵ֧י\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb around you|סְבִיבוֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*.’
\p \v 8 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: ‘\rb Behold|הִנְנִ֥י\rb*, \rb I Myself am|אָ֑נִי\rb*\rb |גַּם־\rb* \rb against you, Jerusalem|עָלַ֖יִךְ\rb*, \rb and I will execute|וְעָשִׂ֧יתִי\rb* \rb judgments|מִשְׁפָּטִ֖ים\rb* \rb among you|בְתוֹכֵ֛ךְ\rb* \rb in the sight|לְעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִֽם׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Because of|יַ֖עַן\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your abominations|תּוֹעֲבֹתָֽיִךְ׃ס\rb*, \rb I will do|וְעָשִׂ֣יתִי\rb* \rb to you|בָ֗ךְ\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have never|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb done before|עָשִׂ֔יתִי\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֛ת\rb* \rb and|אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb will never|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb do|אֶעֱשֶׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |כָמֹ֖הוּ\rb* \rb again|ע֑וֹד\rb*. \v 10 \rb As a result|לָכֵ֗ן\rb*, \rb fathers|אָב֞וֹת\rb* \rb among you|בְּתוֹכֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb will eat|יֹאכְל֤וּ\rb* \rb their sons|בָנִים֙\rb*, \rb and sons|וּבָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb will eat|יֹאכְל֣וּ\rb* \rb their fathers|אֲבוֹתָ֑ם\rb*. \rb I will execute|וְעָשִׂ֤יתִי\rb* \rb judgments|שְׁפָטִ֔ים\rb* \rb against you|בָךְ֙\rb* \rb and scatter|וְזֵרִיתִ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your remnant|שְׁאֵרִיתֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb to every|לְכָל־\rb* \rb wind|רֽוּחַ׃פ\rb*.’
\s1 Famine, Sword, and Dispersion
\p \v 11 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֣ן\rb* \rb as surely as I|אָ֗נִי\rb* \rb live|חַי־\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם֮\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִה֒\rb*,\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb because|יַ֚עַן\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb you have defiled|טִמֵּ֔את\rb* \rb My sanctuary|מִקְדָּשִׁ֣י\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your detestable idols|שִׁקּוּצַ֖יִךְ\rb*\rb |וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb and abominations|תּוֹעֲבֹתָ֑יִךְ\rb*,\rb |וְגַם־\rb* \rb I Myself|אֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb will withdraw My favor|אֶגְרַע֙\rb*; \rb I will not look upon you|עֵינִ֔י\rb*\rb |וְלֹא־\rb* \rb with pity|תָח֣וֹס\rb*, \rb nor|וְגַם־\rb* \rb will I|אֲנִ֖י\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb spare you|אֶחְמֽוֹל׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb A third|שְׁלִשִׁתֵ֞יךְ\rb* \rb of your people will die|יָמ֗וּתוּ\rb* \rb by plague|בַּדֶּ֣בֶר\rb* \rb or be consumed|יִכְל֣וּ\rb* \rb by famine|וּבָֽרָעָב֙\rb* \rb within you|בְתוֹכֵ֔ךְ\rb*, \rb a third|וְהַ֨שְּׁלִשִׁ֔ית\rb* \rb will fall|יִפְּל֣וּ\rb* \rb by the sword|בַּחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb outside your walls|סְבִיבוֹתָ֑יִךְ\rb*, \rb and a third|וְהַשְּׁלִישִׁית֙\rb* \rb I will scatter|אֱזָרֶ֔ה\rb* \rb to every|לְכָל־\rb* \rb wind|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb and unleash|אָרִ֥יק\rb* \rb a sword|וְחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb behind them|אַחֲרֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb And when My anger|אַפִּ֗י\rb* \rb is spent|וְכָלָ֣ה\rb* \rb and I have vented|וַהֲנִחוֹתִ֧י\rb* \rb My wrath|חֲמָתִ֛י\rb* \rb against them|בָּ֖ם\rb*, \rb I will be appeased|וְהִנֶּחָ֑מְתִּי\rb*. \rb And when I have spent|בְּכַלּוֹתִ֥י\rb* \rb My wrath|חֲמָתִ֖י\rb* \rb on them|בָּֽם׃\rb*, \rb they will know|וְֽיָדְע֞וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb in My zeal|בְּקִנְאָתִ֔י\rb* \rb have spoken|דִּבַּ֙רְתִּי֙\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb I will make|וְאֶתְּנֵךְ֙\rb* \rb you a ruin|לְחָרְבָּ֣ה\rb* \rb and a disgrace|וּלְחֶרְפָּ֔ה\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb around you|סְבִיבוֹתָ֑יִךְ\rb*, \rb in the sight|לְעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who pass by|עוֹבֵֽר׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb So you will be|וְֽהָ֨יְתָ֜ה\rb*\f + \fr 5:15 \ft DSS, LXX, Syriac, and Vulgate; MT \fqa So it will be\f* \rb a reproach|חֶרְפָּ֤ה\rb* \rb and a taunt|וּגְדוּפָה֙\rb*, \rb a warning|מוּסָ֣ר\rb* \rb and a horror|וּמְשַׁמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb to the nations|לַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb around you|סְבִיבוֹתָ֑יִךְ\rb*, \rb when I execute|בַּעֲשׂוֹתִי֩\rb* \rb judgments|שְׁפָטִ֜ים\rb* \rb against you|בָ֨ךְ\rb* \rb in anger|בְּאַ֤ף\rb*, \rb wrath|וּבְחֵמָה֙\rb*, \rb and raging|חֵמָ֔ה\rb* \rb fury|וּבְתֹכְח֣וֹת\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb have spoken|דִּבַּֽרְתִּי׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb When I shower|בְּֽשַׁלְּחִ֡י\rb* \rb you|בָּהֶם֙\rb*\f + \fr 5:16 \ft Hebrew \fqa them \f*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb with the deadly|הָרָעִ֤ים\rb* \rb arrows|חִצֵּי֩\rb* \rb of famine|הָרָעָ֨ב\rb* \rb and|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |הָי֣וּ\rb* \rb destruction|לְמַשְׁחִ֔ית\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I will send|אֲשַׁלַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb to destroy you|לְשַֽׁחֶתְכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb I will intensify|אֹסֵ֣ף\rb* \rb the famine|וְרָעָב֙\rb* \rb against you|עֲלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and cut off|וְשָׁבַרְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb supply|מַטֵּה־\rb*\f + \fr 5:16 \ft Hebrew \fqa staff\f* \rb of food|לָֽחֶם׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb I will send|וְשִׁלַּחְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb famine|רָעָ֞ב\rb* \rb and wild|רָעָה֙\rb* \rb beasts|וְחַיָּ֤ה\rb* \rb against you|עֲ֠לֵיכֶם\rb*, \rb and they will leave you childless|וְשִׁכְּלֻ֔ךְ\rb*. \rb Plague|וְדֶ֥בֶר\rb* \rb and bloodshed|וָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb will sweep|יַעֲבָר־\rb* \rb through you|בָּ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb and I will bring|אָבִ֣יא\rb* \rb a sword|וְחֶ֙רֶב֙\rb* \rb against you|עָלַ֔יִךְ\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb have spoken|דִּבַּֽרְתִּי׃פ\rb*.”
\c 6
\s1 Judgment against Idolatry
\r (\ref Deuteronomy 4:15–31|DEU 4:15-31\ref*; \ref Deuteronomy 12:29–32|DEU 12:29-32\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb And the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*, \rb set|שִׂ֥ים\rb* \rb your face|פָּנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the mountains|הָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and prophesy|וְהִנָּבֵ֖א\rb* \rb against them|אֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb You are to say|וְאָ֣מַרְתָּ֔\rb*: ‘\rb O mountains|הָרֵי֙\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb hear|שִׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb*! \rb This is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְ֠הוִה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to the mountains|לֶהָרִ֨ים\rb* \rb and hills|וְלַגְּבָע֜וֹת\rb*, \rb to the ravines|לָאֲפִיקִ֣ים\rb* \rb and valleys|וְלַגֵּאָיֹת\rb*:\rb |הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֜י\rb* \rb am about to bring|מֵבִ֤יא\rb* \rb a sword|חֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb against you|עֲלֵיכֶם֙\rb*, \rb and I will destroy|וְאִבַּדְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb your high places|בָּמֽוֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb Your altars|מִזְבְּח֣וֹתֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb will be demolished|וְנָשַׁ֙מּוּ֙\rb* \rb and your incense altars|חַמָּֽנֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb will be smashed|וְנִשְׁבְּר֖וּ\rb*; \rb and I will cast down|וְהִפַּלְתִּי֙\rb* \rb your slain|חַלְלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb your idols|גִּלּוּלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb I will lay|וְנָתַתִּ֗י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the corpses|פִּגְרֵי֙\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the Israelites|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb their idols|גִּלּֽוּלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and scatter|וְזֵרִיתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your bones|עַצְמ֣וֹתֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb around|סְבִיב֖וֹת\rb* \rb your altars|מִזְבְּחוֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Wherever|בְּכֹל֙\rb* \rb you live|מוֹשְׁב֣וֹתֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb the cities|הֶעָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb will be laid waste|תֶּחֱרַ֔בְנָה\rb* \rb and the high places|וְהַבָּמ֖וֹת\rb* \rb will be demolished|תִּישָׁ֑מְנָה\rb*, \rb so that|לְמַעַן֩\rb* \rb your altars|מִזְבְּחֽוֹתֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb will be laid waste|יֶחֶרְב֨וּ\rb* \rb and desecrated|וְיֶאְשְׁמ֜וּ\rb*, \rb your idols|גִּלּ֣וּלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb smashed|וְנִשְׁבְּר֤וּ\rb* \rb and obliterated|וְנִשְׁבְּתוּ֙\rb*, \rb your incense altars|חַמָּ֣נֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb cut down|וְנִגְדְּעוּ֙\rb*, \rb and your works|מַעֲשֵׂיכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb blotted out|וְנִמְח֖וּ\rb*. \v 7 \rb The slain|חָלָ֖ל\rb* \rb will fall|וְנָפַ֥ל\rb* \rb among you|בְּתֽוֹכְכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb and you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\s1 A Remnant to Be Blessed
\p \v 8 \rb Yet I will leave a remnant|וְהוֹתַרְתִּ֗י\rb*, \rb for|בִּהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb some of you|לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb will escape|פְּלִ֥יטֵי\rb* \rb the sword|חֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb when you are scattered|בְּהִזָּרֽוֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb* \rb and throughout the lands|בָּאֲרָצֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Then in the nations|בַּגּוֹיִם֮\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they have been carried captive|נִשְׁבּוּ־\rb*, \rb your survivors|פְלִֽיטֵיכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb will remember|וְזָכְר֨וּ\rb* \rb Me|אוֹתִ֗י\rb* —\rb |שָׁם֒\rb* \rb how|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I have been grieved|נִשְׁבַּ֜רְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb by their adulterous|הַזּוֹנֶ֗ה\rb* \rb hearts|לִבָּ֣ם\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb turned away|סָר֙\rb* \rb from Me|מֵֽעָלַ֔י\rb*, \rb and by|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb their eyes|עֵֽינֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb that lusted|הַזֹּנ֕וֹת\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb idols|גִּלּֽוּלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb So they will loathe|וְנָקֹ֙טּוּ֙\rb* \rb themselves|בִּפְנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb the evil|הָֽרָעוֹת֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they have done|עָשׂ֔וּ\rb* \rb and for all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb their abominations|תּוֹעֲבֹתֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb And they will know|וְיָדְע֖וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*; \rb I did not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb declare|דִּבַּ֔רְתִּי\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb vain|חִנָּם֙\rb* \rb that I would bring|לַעֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּֽאת׃פ\rb* \rb calamity|הָרָעָ֥ה\rb* \rb upon them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֞ר\rb*: \rb Clap|הַכֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb your hands|בְכַפְּךָ֜\rb*, \rb stomp|וּרְקַ֤ע\rb* \rb your feet|בְּרַגְלְךָ֙\rb*, \rb and cry out|וֶֽאֱמָר־\rb* “\rb Alas|אָ֔ח\rb*!” \rb because of|אֶ֛ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the wicked|רָע֖וֹת\rb* \rb abominations|תּוֹעֲב֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֗ר\rb* \rb will fall|יִפֹּֽלוּ׃\rb* \rb by sword|בַּחֶ֛רֶב\rb* \rb and famine|בָּרָעָ֥ב\rb* \rb and plague|וּבַדֶּ֖בֶר\rb*. \v 12 \rb He who is far off|הָרָח֞וֹק\rb* \rb will die|יָמ֗וּת\rb* \rb by the plague|בַּדֶּ֣בֶר\rb*, \rb he who is near|וְהַקָּרוֹב֙\rb* \rb will fall|יִפּ֔וֹל\rb* \rb by the sword|בַּחֶ֣רֶב\rb*, \rb and he who remains|וְהַנִּשְׁאָר֙\rb*\rb |וְהַנָּצ֔וּר\rb* \rb will die|יָמ֑וּת\rb* \rb by famine|בָּרָעָ֖ב\rb*. \rb So I will vent|וְכִלֵּיתִ֥י\rb* \rb My fury|חֲמָתִ֖י\rb* \rb upon them|בָּֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Then you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb when their slain|חַלְלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb lie|בִּֽהְי֣וֹת\rb* \rb among|בְּתוֹךְ֙\rb* \rb their idols|גִּלּ֣וּלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb around|סְבִיב֖וֹת\rb* \rb their altars|מִזְבְּחֽוֹתֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb on|אֶל֩\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb high|רָמָ֜ה\rb* \rb hill|גִּבְעָ֨ה\rb*, \rb on all|בְּכֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the mountaintops|רָאשֵׁ֣י\rb*\rb |הֶהָרִ֗ים\rb*, \rb and under|וְתַ֨חַת\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb green|רַֽעֲנָן֙\rb*\rb |וְתַ֙חַת֙\rb* \rb tree|עֵ֤ץ\rb* \rb and|כָּל־\rb* \rb leafy|עֲבֻתָּ֔ה\rb* \rb oak|אֵלָ֣ה\rb*— \rb the places|מְק֗וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb they offered|נָֽתְנוּ־\rb*\rb |שָׁם֙\rb* \rb fragrant|נִיחֹ֔חַ\rb* \rb incense|רֵ֣יחַ\rb* \rb to all|לְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb their idols|גִּלּוּלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb I will stretch out|וְנָטִ֤יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My hand|יָדִי֙\rb* \rb against them|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and wherever|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb they live|מוֹשְׁבֽוֹתֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb I will make|וְנָתַתִּ֨י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֜רֶץ\rb* \rb a desolate|שְׁמָמָ֤ה\rb* \rb waste|וּמְשַׁמָּה֙\rb*, \rb from the wilderness|מִמִּדְבַּ֣ר\rb* \rb to Diblah|דִּבְלָ֔תָה\rb*.\f + \fr 6:14 \ft Most Hebrew manuscripts; Vulgate and a few Hebrew manuscripts \fqa Riblah\f* \rb Then they will know|וְיָדְע֖וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.’”
\c 7
\s1 The Hour of Doom
\p \v 1 \rb And the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb O|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb this is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֧י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֛ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֞ר\rb* \rb to the land|לְאַדְמַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\rb The end|קֵ֑ץ\rb*! \rb The end|הַקֵּ֔ץ\rb* \rb has come|בָּ֣א\rb*
\q2 \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the four|אַרְבַּעַת\rb* \rb corners|כַּנְפ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb The end|הַקֵּ֣ץ\rb* \rb is now|עַתָּה֙\rb* \rb upon you|עָלַ֔יִךְ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and I will unleash|וְשִׁלַּחְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb My anger|אַפִּי֙\rb* \rb against you|בָּ֔ךְ\rb*.
\q1 \rb I will judge you|וּשְׁפַטְתִּ֖יךְ\rb* \rb according to your ways|כִּדְרָכָ֑יִךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb and repay|וְנָתַתִּ֣י\rb* \rb you|עָלַ֔יִךְ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb for all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your abominations|תּוֹעֲבֹתָֽיִךְ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb I will not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb look on you|עָלַ֖יִךְ\rb*\rb |עֵינִ֛י\rb* \rb with pity|תָח֥וֹס\rb*,
\q2 \rb nor|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb will I spare you|אֶחְמ֑וֹל\rb*,
\q1 \rb but I will punish you for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb your ways|דְרָכַ֜יִךְ\rb*\rb |עָלַ֣יִךְ\rb*\rb |אֶתֵּ֗ן\rb*
\q2 \rb and for the abominations|וְתוֹעֲבוֹתַ֙יִךְ֙\rb* \rb among you|בְּתוֹכֵ֣ךְ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \rb |תִּֽהְיֶ֔יןָ\rb* \rb Then you will know|וִידַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.’
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\rb Disaster|רָעָ֛ה\rb*! \rb An unprecedented|אַחַ֥ת\rb* \rb disaster|רָעָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 7:5 \ft Or \fqa A unique disaster\ft , as in most Hebrew manuscripts; some Hebrew manuscripts and Syriac \fqa Disaster after disaster\f* —
\q2 \rb behold|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb it is coming|בָאָֽה׃\rb*!
\q1 \v 6 \rb The end|קֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb has come|בָּ֔א\rb*!
\q2 \rb The end|הַקֵּ֖ץ\rb* \rb has come|בָּ֥א\rb*!
\q1 \rb It has roused itself|הֵקִ֣יץ\rb* \rb against you|אֵלָ֑יִךְ\rb*.
\q2 \rb Behold|הִנֵּ֖ה\rb*, \rb it has come|בָּאָֽה׃\rb*!
\q1 \v 7 \rb Doom|הַצְּפִירָ֛ה\rb* \rb has come|בָּ֧אָה\rb* \rb to you|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb O inhabitants|יוֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*.
\q1 \rb The time|הָעֵ֗ת\rb* \rb has come|בָּ֣א\rb*;
\q2 \rb the day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb is near|קָר֛וֹב\rb*;
\q1 \rb there is panic|מְהוּמָ֖ה\rb* \rb on the mountains|הָרִֽים׃\rb*
\q2 \rb instead of shouts of joy|וְלֹא־\rb*\rb |הֵ֥ד\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb |עַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb Very soon|מִקָּר֗וֹב\rb* \rb I will pour out|אֶשְׁפּ֤וֹךְ\rb* \rb My wrath|חֲמָתִי֙\rb* \rb upon you|עָלַ֔יִךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb and vent|וְכִלֵּיתִ֤י\rb* \rb My anger|אַפִּי֙\rb* \rb against you|בָּ֔ךְ\rb*;
\q1 \rb I will judge you|וּשְׁפַטְתִּ֖יךְ\rb* \rb according to your ways|כִּדְרָכָ֑יִךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb and repay you|וְנָתַתִּ֣י\rb*\rb |עָלַ֔יִךְ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb for all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your abominations|תּוֹעֲבוֹתָֽיִךְ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb I will not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb look on you with pity|תָח֥וֹס\rb*\rb |עֵינִ֖י\rb*,
\q2 \rb nor|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb will I spare you|אֶחְמ֑וֹל\rb*,
\q1 \rb but I will punish you|אֶתֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb for your ways|כִּדְרָכַ֜יִךְ\rb*\rb |עָלַ֣יִךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb and for the abominations|וְתוֹעֲבוֹתַ֙יִךְ֙\rb* \rb among you|בְּתוֹכֵ֣ךְ\rb*\rb |תִּֽהְיֶ֔יןָ\rb*.
\q1 \rb Then you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֕ם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb it is I|אֲנִ֥י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb who strikes the blow|מַכֶּֽה׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb Behold|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb the day|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb is here|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb*!
\q2 \rb It has come|בָאָ֑ה\rb*!
\q1 \rb Doom|הַצְּפִרָ֔ה\rb* \rb has gone out|יָֽצְאָה֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb the rod|הַמַּטֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb has budded|פָּרַ֖ח\rb*,
\q2 \rb arrogance|הַזָּדֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb has bloomed|צָ֚ץ\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb Their violence|הֶחָמָ֥ס׀\rb* \rb has grown|קָ֖ם\rb* \rb into a rod|לְמַטֵּה־\rb*
\q2 \rb to punish their wickedness|רֶ֑שַׁע\rb*.\f + \fr 7:11 \ft Literally \fqa The violence has grown into a rod of wickedness\f*
\q1 \rb None|לֹא־\rb* \rb of them will remain|מֵהֶ֞ם\rb*:
\q2 \rb none|וְלֹ֧א\rb* \rb of their multitude|מֵהֲמוֹנָ֛ם\rb*,
\q1 \rb none|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb of their wealth|מֶהֱמֵהֶ֖ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and nothing|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb of value|נֹ֥הַּ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 12 \rb The time|הָעֵת֙\rb* \rb has come|בָּ֤א\rb*;
\q2 \rb the day|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb* \rb has arrived|הִגִּ֣יעַ\rb*.
\q1 \rb Let the buyer|הַקּוֹנֶה֙\rb* \rb not|אַל־\rb* \rb rejoice|יִשְׂמָ֔ח\rb*
\q2 \rb and the seller|וְהַמּוֹכֵ֖ר\rb* \rb not|אַל־\rb* \rb mourn|יִתְאַבָּ֑ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb wrath|חָר֖וֹן\rb* \rb is upon|אֶל־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb multitude|הֲמוֹנָֽהּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb The seller|הַמּוֹכֵ֗ר\rb* \rb will surely|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb recover|יָשׁ֔וּב\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb what he sold|הַמִּמְכָּר֙\rb*
\q2 \rb while|וְע֥וֹד\rb* \rb both remain alive|בַּחַיִּ֖ים\rb*\rb |חַיָּתָ֑ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the vision|חָז֤וֹן\rb* \rb concerning|אֶל־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb multitude|הֲמוֹנָהּ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be revoked|יָשׁ֔וּב\rb*,
\q1 \rb and because of their iniquity|בַּעֲוֺנ֛וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb not one of them|וְאִ֧ישׁ\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb will preserve|יִתְחַזָּֽקוּ׃\rb* \rb his life|חַיָּת֖וֹ\rb*.
\s1 The Desolation of Israel
\q1 \v 14 \rb They have blown|תָּקְע֤וּ\rb* \rb the trumpet|בַתָּק֙וֹעַ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and made|וְהָכִ֣ין\rb* \rb everything ready|הַכֹּ֔ל\rb*,
\q1 \rb but no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb one goes|הֹלֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb to war|לַמִּלְחָמָ֑ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb My wrath|חֲרוֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb is upon|אֶל־\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb multitude|הֲמוֹנָֽהּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb The sword|הַחֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb is outside|בַּח֔וּץ\rb*;
\q2 \rb plague|וְהַדֶּ֥בֶר\rb* \rb and famine|וְהָרָעָ֖ב\rb* \rb are within|מִבָּ֑יִת\rb*.
\q1 \rb Those|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb in the country|בַּשָּׂדֶה֙\rb* \rb will die|יָמ֔וּת\rb* \rb by the sword|בַּחֶ֣רֶב\rb*,
\q2 \rb and those|וַאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in the city|בָּעִ֔יר\rb* \rb will be devoured|יֹאכֲלֶֽנּוּ׃\rb*
\q2 \rb by famine|רָעָ֥ב\rb* \rb and plague|וָדֶ֖בֶר\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 16 \rb The survivors|פְּלִ֣יטֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְהָי֣וּ\rb* \rb will escape|וּפָֽלְטוּ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and live in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the mountains|הֶהָרִ֗ים\rb*,
\q1 \rb |כֻּלָּ֖ם\rb* \rb moaning|הֹמ֑וֹת\rb* \rb like doves|כְּיוֹנֵ֧י\rb* \rb of the valley|הַגֵּאָי֛וֹת\rb*,
\q2 \rb each|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb for his own iniquity|בַּעֲוֺנֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 \rb Every|כָּל־\rb* \rb hand|הַיָּדַ֖יִם\rb* \rb will go limp|תִּרְפֶּ֑ינָה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb knee|בִּרְכַּ֖יִם\rb* \rb will turn to|תֵּלַ֥כְנָה\rb* \rb water|מָּֽיִם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 18 \rb They will put on|וְחָגְר֣וּ\rb* \rb sackcloth|שַׂקִּ֔ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb and terror|פַּלָּצ֑וּת\rb*\rb |וְאֶ֤ל\rb* \rb will overwhelm them|וְכִסְּתָ֥ה\rb*.\rb |אוֹתָ֖ם\rb*
\q1 \rb Shame|בּוּשָׁ֔ה\rb* \rb will cover all|כָּל־\rb* \rb their faces|פָּנִים֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb and all|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb their heads|רָאשֵׁיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb will be shaved|קָרְחָֽה׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 19 \rb They will throw|יַשְׁלִ֗יכוּ\rb* \rb their silver|כַּסְפָּ֞ם\rb* \rb into the streets|בַּחוּצ֣וֹת\rb*,
\q2 \rb and their gold|וּזְהָבָם֮\rb* \rb will seem|יִֽהְיֶה֒\rb* \rb unclean|לְנִדָּ֣ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb Their silver|כַּסְפָּ֨ם\rb* \rb and gold|וּזְהָבָ֜ם\rb* \rb cannot|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |יוּכַ֣ל\rb* \rb save them|לְהַצִּילָ֗ם\rb*
\q2 \rb in the day|בְּיוֹם֙\rb* \rb of the wrath|עֶבְרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb They cannot|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb satisfy|יְשַׂבֵּ֔עוּ\rb* \rb their appetites|נַפְשָׁם֙\rb*
\q2 \rb or fill|יְמַלֵּ֑אוּ\rb* \rb their stomachs with wealth|וּמֵעֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*,\rb |לֹ֣א\rb*
\q1 \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb it became|הָיָֽה׃\rb* \rb the stumbling block|מִכְשׁ֥וֹל\rb*
\q2 \rb that brought their iniquity|עֲוֺנָ֖ם\rb*.
