\c 8
\s1 The Vision of Idolatry in the Temple
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb In the sixth|הַשִּׁשִּׁ֗ית\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָ֣ה\rb*, \rb on the fifth|בַּחֲמִשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb day|לַחֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the sixth month|בַּשִּׁשִּׁי֙\rb*, \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb was sitting|יוֹשֵׁ֣ב\rb* \rb in my house|בְּבֵיתִ֔י\rb*, \rb and the elders|וְזִקְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֖ה\rb* \rb were sitting|יוֹשְׁבִ֣ים\rb* \rb before me|לְפָנָ֑י\rb*; \rb and there|שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb the hand|יַ֖ד\rb* \rb of the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהֹוִֽה׃\rb* \rb fell|וַתִּפֹּ֤ל\rb* \rb upon me|עָלַי֙\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb Then I looked|וָאֶרְאֶ֗ה\rb* \rb and saw|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb a figure|דְמוּת֙\rb* \rb like that of a man|כְּמַרְאֵה־\rb*. \rb From His waist|מָתְנָ֛יו\rb* \rb down|וּלְמַ֖טָּה\rb* \rb His appearance|מִמַּרְאֵ֥ה\rb* \rb was like fire|אֵ֑שׁ\rb*\rb |אֵ֔שׁ\rb*, \rb and from His waist|וּמִמָּתְנָ֣יו\rb* \rb up|וּלְמַ֔עְלָה\rb* \rb He|כְּמַרְאֵה־\rb* \rb was as bright|זֹ֖הַר\rb* \rb as the gleam|כְּעֵ֥ין\rb* \rb of amber|הַחַשְׁמַֽלָה׃\rb*.\f + \fr 8:2 \ft Or \fqa as glowing metal\f* \v 3 \rb He stretched out|וַיִּשְׁלַח֙\rb* \rb what looked like|תַּבְנִ֣ית\rb* \rb a hand|יָ֔ד\rb* \rb and took me|וַיִּקָּחֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb by the hair|בְּצִיצִ֣ת\rb* \rb of my head|רֹאשִׁ֑י\rb*. \rb Then the Spirit|ר֣וּחַ׀\rb* \rb lifted me up|וַתִּשָּׂ֣א\rb*\rb |אֹתִ֣י\rb* \rb between|בֵּֽין־\rb* \rb earth|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb and heaven|הַשָּׁמַ֡יִם\rb* \rb and carried|וַתָּבֵא֩\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֨י\rb* \rb in visions|בְּמַרְא֣וֹת\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֗ים\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלְַ֜מָה\rb*, \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֜תַח\rb*\rb |הַפּוֹנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb of the north|צָפ֔וֹנָה\rb* \rb gate|שַׁ֤עַר\rb* \rb of the inner court|הַפְּנִימִית֙\rb*, \rb where|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb the idol|סֵ֖מֶל\rb* \rb that provokes|הַמַּקְנֶֽה׃\rb* \rb jealousy|הַקִּנְאָ֥ה\rb* \rb was seated|מוֹשַׁ֔ב\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb And there|שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb I saw|וְהִ֨נֵּה־\rb* \rb the glory|כְּב֖וֹד\rb* \rb of the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb like the vision|כַּמַּרְאֶ֕ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I had seen|רָאִ֖יתִי\rb* \rb in the plain|בַּבִּקְעָֽה׃\rb*. \v 5 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*,” \rb He said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*, “\rb now|נָ֥א\rb* \rb lift up|שָׂא־\rb* \rb your eyes|עֵינֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb to|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb the north|צָפ֑וֹנָה\rb*.”
\p \rb So I lifted up|וָאֶשָּׂ֤א\rb* \rb my eyes|עֵינַי֙\rb* \rb to|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb the north|צָפ֔וֹנָה\rb*, \rb and in the entrance|בַּבִּאָֽה׃\rb* \rb north|מִצָּפוֹן֙\rb* \rb of the Altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb Gate|לְשַׁ֣עַר\rb*\f + \fr 8:5 \ft Or \fqa gate of the altar\f* \rb I saw|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb idol|סֵ֛מֶל\rb* \rb of jealousy|הַקִּנְאָ֥ה\rb*.
\p \v 6 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*,” \rb He said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*, “\rb do you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb see|הֲרֹאֶ֥ה\rb* \rb what|מֵהֶם\rb* \rb they are doing|עֹשִׂ֑ים\rb* — \rb the great|גְּדֹל֜וֹת\rb* \rb abominations|תּוֹעֵב֨וֹת\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb the house|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֣ל׀\rb* \rb is committing|עֹשִׂ֣ים\rb* —\rb |פֹּ֗ה\rb* \rb to drive Me far|לְרָֽחֳקָה֙\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb My sanctuary|מִקְדָּשִׁ֔י\rb*? \rb Yet|וְעוֹד֙\rb*\rb |תָּשׁ֣וּב\rb* \rb you will see|תִּרְאֶ֔ה\rb* \rb even greater|גְּדֹלֽוֹת׃ס\rb* \rb abominations|תּוֹעֵב֖וֹת\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb Then He brought|וַיָּבֵ֥א\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֖י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֣תַח\rb* \rb to the court|הֶֽחָצֵ֑ר\rb*, \rb and I looked|וָאֶרְאֶ֕ה\rb* \rb and saw|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb a|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb hole|חֹר־\rb* \rb in the wall|בַּקִּֽיר׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֖ם\rb*,” \rb He told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*, “\rb dig|חֲתָר־\rb*\rb |נָ֣א\rb* \rb through the wall|בַקִּ֑יר\rb*.”
\p \rb So I dug|וָאֶחְתֹּ֣ר\rb* \rb through the wall|בַּקִּ֔יר\rb* \rb and discovered|וְהִנֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb a|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb doorway|פֶּ֥תַח\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Then He said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָ֑י\rb*, “\rb Go in|בֹּ֤א\rb* \rb and see|וּרְאֵה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the wicked|הָרָע֔וֹת\rb* \rb abominations|הַתּוֹעֵב֣וֹת\rb* \rb they|הֵ֥ם\rb* \rb are committing|עֹשִׂ֖ים\rb* \rb here|פֹּֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 10 \rb So I went in|וָאָבוֹא֮\rb* \rb and looked|וָֽאֶרְאֶה֒\rb*, \rb and|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb engraved|מְחֻקֶּ֥ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb all|סָבִ֥יב׀\rb* \rb around|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb the wall|הַקִּ֖יר\rb* \rb was every|כָל־\rb* \rb kind|תַּבְנִ֜ית\rb* \rb of crawling creature|רֶ֤מֶשׂ\rb* \rb and detestable|שֶׁ֔קֶץ\rb* \rb beast|וּבְהֵמָה֙\rb*, \rb along with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the idols|גִּלּוּלֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \v 11 \rb Before them|לִפְנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb stood|עֹמֵ֤ד\rb* \rb seventy|וְשִׁבְעִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb elders|מִזִּקְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the house|בֵֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִ֠שְׂרָאֵל\rb*, \rb with Jaazaniah|וְיַאֲזַנְיָ֨הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Shaphan|שָׁפָ֜ן\rb* \rb standing|עֹמְדִ֣ים\rb* \rb among them|בְּתוֹכָם֙\rb*. \rb Each|וְאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb had a censer|מִקְטַרְתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb in his hand|בְּיָד֑וֹ\rb*, \rb and a fragrant|וַעֲתַ֥ר\rb* \rb cloud|עֲנַֽן־\rb* \rb of incense|הַקְּטֹ֖רֶת\rb* \rb was rising|עֹלֶֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 “\rb Son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָם֒\rb*,” \rb He said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַי֮\rb*, “\rb do you see|הֲרָאִ֣יתָ\rb* \rb what|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the elders|זִקְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of the house|בֵֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb are doing|עֹשִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb in the darkness|בַּחֹ֔שֶׁךְ\rb*, \rb each|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb at the shrine|בְּחַדְרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of his own idol|מַשְׂכִּית֑וֹ\rb*? \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they are saying|אֹמְרִ֗ים\rb*, ‘\rb The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb does not|אֵ֤ין\rb* \rb see|רֹאֶ֣ה\rb* \rb us|אֹתָ֔נוּ\rb*; \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb has forsaken|עָזַ֥ב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 13 \rb Again|ע֣וֹד\rb*,\rb |תָּשׁ֥וּב\rb* \rb He told|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb me|אֵלָ֑י\rb*, “\rb You will see|תִּרְאֶ֛ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb them|הֵ֥מָּה\rb* \rb committing|עֹשִֽׂים׃\rb* \rb even greater|גְּדֹל֖וֹת\rb* \rb abominations|תּוֹעֵב֥וֹת\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb Then He brought|וַיָּבֵ֣א\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֗י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֙תַח֙\rb* \rb of the north|הַצָּפ֑וֹנָה\rb* \rb gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*, \rb and I saw|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb women|הַנָּשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb sitting|יֹֽשְׁב֔וֹת\rb* \rb there|שָׁם֙\rb*, \rb weeping|מְבַכּ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for Tammuz|הַתַּמּֽוּז׃ס\rb*.\f + \fr 8:14 \fqa Tammuz\ft , meaning \fqa Sprout of Life\ft , was a Sumerian god of fertility.\f*
\p \v 15 “\rb Son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֑ם\rb*,” \rb He said|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֖י\rb*, “\rb do you see this|הֲרָאִ֣יתָ\rb*? \rb Yet|ע֣וֹד\rb*\rb |תָּשׁ֥וּב\rb* \rb you will see|תִּרְאֶ֛ה\rb* \rb even greater|גְּדֹל֖וֹת\rb* \rb abominations|תּוֹעֵב֥וֹת\rb* \rb than these|מֵאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 16 \rb So He brought|וַיָּבֵ֣א\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֗י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the inner|הַפְּנִימִית֒\rb* \rb court|חֲצַ֣ר\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb*, \rb and there|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶ֜תַח\rb* \rb to the temple|הֵיכַ֣ל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb between|בֵּ֤ין\rb* \rb the portico|הָֽאוּלָם֙\rb* \rb and|וּבֵ֣ין\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb*, \rb were about twenty-five|כְּעֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb men|אִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb with their backs|אֲחֹ֨רֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the temple|הֵיכַ֤ל\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb and their faces|וּפְנֵיהֶ֣ם\rb* \rb toward the east|קֵ֔דְמָה\rb*; \rb and they|וְהֵ֛מָּה\rb* \rb were bowing to the east|קֵ֖דְמָה\rb* \rb in worship|מִשְׁתַּחֲוִיתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb of the sun|לַשָּֽׁמֶשׁ׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 “\rb Son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָם֒\rb*,” \rb He said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַי֮\rb*, “\rb do you see this|הֲרָאִ֣יתָ\rb*? \rb Is it not enough|הֲנָקֵל֙\rb* \rb for the house|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb to commit|מֵעֲשׂ֕וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the abominations|הַתּוֹעֵב֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they are practicing|עָֽשׂוּ־\rb* \rb here|פֹ֑ה\rb*, \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they must also fill|מָלְא֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֜רֶץ\rb* \rb with violence|חָמָ֗ס\rb* \rb and continually|וַיָּשֻׁ֙בוּ֙\rb* \rb provoke Me to anger|לְהַכְעִיסֵ֔נִי\rb*? \rb Look, they are even|וְהִנָּ֛ם\rb* \rb putting|שֹׁלְחִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the branch|הַזְּמוֹרָ֖ה\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb their nose|אַפָּֽם׃\rb*! \v 18 \rb Therefore|וְגַם־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb will respond|אֶעֱשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb with wrath|בְחֵמָ֔ה\rb*. \rb I will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb look on them|עֵינִ֖י\rb* \rb with pity|תָח֥וֹס\rb*, \rb nor|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb will I spare them|אֶחְמֹ֑ל\rb*. \rb Although they shout|וְקָרְא֤וּ\rb* \rb loudly|גָּד֔וֹל\rb*\rb |ק֣וֹל\rb* \rb in My ears|בְאָזְנַי֙\rb*, \rb I will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb listen to them|אֶשְׁמַ֖ע\rb*.”\rb |אוֹתָֽם׃\rb*
\c 9
\s1 Execution of the Idolaters
\p \v 1 \rb Then I heard Him|בְאָזְנַ֗י\rb* \rb call out|וַיִּקְרָ֣א\rb* \rb in a loud|גָּדוֹל֙\rb* \rb voice|ק֤וֹל\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Draw near|קָרְב֖וּ\rb*, \rb O executioners|פְּקֻדּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb*, \rb each|וְאִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb with a weapon|כְּלִ֥י\rb* \rb of destruction|מַשְׁחֵת֖וֹ\rb* \rb in hand|בְּיָדֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 2 \rb And I saw|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb six|שִׁשָּׁ֣ה\rb* \rb men|אֲנָשִׁ֡ים\rb* \rb coming|בָּאִ֣ים׀\rb* \rb from the direction|מִדֶּרֶךְ־\rb* \rb of the Upper|הָעֶלְי֜וֹן\rb* \rb Gate|שַׁ֨עַר\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר׀\rb* \rb faces|מָפְנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb north|צָפ֗וֹנָה\rb*, \rb each|וְאִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb with a weapon|כְּלִ֤י\rb* \rb of slaughter|מַפָּצוֹ֙\rb* \rb in his hand|בְּיָד֔וֹ\rb*. \rb With them|בְּתוֹכָם֙\rb* \rb was another|אֶחָ֤ד\rb* \rb man|וְאִישׁ־\rb* \rb clothed|לָבֻ֣שׁ\rb* \rb in linen|בַּדִּ֔ים\rb* \rb who had a writing kit|וְקֶ֥סֶת\rb*\rb |הַסֹּפֵ֖ר\rb* \rb at his side|בְּמָתְנָ֑יו\rb*. \rb And they came in|וַיָּבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb and stood|וַיַּ֣עַמְד֔וּ\rb* \rb beside|אֵ֖צֶל\rb* \rb the bronze|הַנְּחֹֽשֶׁת׃\rb* \rb altar|מִזְבַּ֥ח\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Then the glory|וּכְב֣וֹד׀\rb* \rb of the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb rose|נַעֲלָה֙\rb* \rb from above|מֵעַ֤ל\rb* \rb the cherubim|הַכְּרוּב֙\rb*, \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb it had been|הָיָ֣ה\rb*, \rb and moved|עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb to|אֶ֖ל\rb* \rb the threshold|מִפְתַּ֣ן\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb*. \rb And He called|וַיִּקְרָ֗א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the man|הָאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb clothed|הַלָּבֻ֣שׁ\rb* \rb in linen|הַבַּדִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb who had the writing kit|קֶ֥סֶת\rb*\rb |הַסֹּפֵ֖ר\rb* \rb at his side|בְּמָתְנָֽיו׃ס\rb*. \v 4 “\rb Go|עֲבֹר֙\rb* \rb throughout|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb of|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרֽוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb*,” \rb said|וַיֹּ֤אמֶר\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֵלוֹ\rb*, “\rb and put|וְהִתְוִ֨יתָ\rb* \rb a mark|תָּ֜ו\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the foreheads|מִצְח֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb sighing|הַנֶּֽאֱנָחִים֙\rb* \rb and groaning|וְהַנֶּ֣אֱנָקִ֔ים\rb* \rb over|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the abominations|הַתּ֣וֹעֵב֔וֹת\rb* \rb committed|הַֽנַּעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb* \rb there|בְּתוֹכָֽהּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 5 \rb And as I listened|בְּאָזְנַ֔י\rb*, \rb He said|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to the others|וּלְאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb*, “\rb Follow him|עִבְר֥וּ\rb*\rb |אַחֲרָ֖יו\rb* \rb through the city|בָעִ֛יר\rb* \rb and start killing|וְהַכּ֑וּ\rb*;\rb |עַל\rb* \rb do not|תָּחֹ֥ס\rb* \rb show pity|עֵינֵיכֶם\rb*\rb |וְאַל־\rb* \rb or spare anyone|תַּחְמֹֽלוּ׃\rb*! \v 6 \rb Slaughter|תַּהַרְג֣וּ\rb*\rb |לְמַשְׁחִ֗ית\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb the old men|זָקֵ֡ן\rb*, \rb the young men|בָּח֣וּר\rb* \rb and maidens|וּבְתוּלָה֩\rb*, \rb the women|וְנָשִׁ֜ים\rb* \rb and children|וְטַ֨ף\rb*; \rb but do not|אַל־\rb* \rb go near|תִּגַּ֔שׁוּ\rb* \rb anyone|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |עָלָ֤יו\rb* \rb has the mark|הַתָּו֙\rb*. \rb Now begin|תָּחֵ֑לּוּ\rb* \rb at My sanctuary|וּמִמִּקְדָּשִׁ֖י\rb*.”
\p \rb So they began|וַיָּחֵ֙לּוּ֙\rb*\rb |בָּאֲנָשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb with the elders|הַזְּקֵנִ֔ים\rb* \rb who were|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the temple|הַבָּֽיִת׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Then He told|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֜ם\rb*, “\rb Defile|טַמְּא֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the temple|הַבַּ֗יִת\rb* \rb and fill|וּמַלְא֧וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the courts|הַחֲצֵר֛וֹת\rb* \rb with the slain|חֲלָלִ֖ים\rb*. \rb Go forth|צֵ֑אוּ\rb*!”
\p \rb So they went out|וְיָצְא֖וּ\rb* \rb and began killing|וְהִכּ֥וּ\rb* \rb throughout the city|בָעִֽיר׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb |וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb While they were killing|כְּהַכּוֹתָ֔ם\rb*, \rb I|אָ֑נִי\rb* \rb was left alone|וְנֵֽאשֲׁאַ֖ר\rb*. \rb And I fell|וָאֶפְּלָ֨ה\rb* \rb facedown|עַל־\rb*\rb |פָּנַ֜י\rb* \rb and cried out|וָאֶזְעַ֗ק\rb*,\rb |וָֽאֹמַר֙\rb* “\rb Oh|אֲהָהּ֙\rb*, \rb Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb*, \rb when You pour out|בְּשָׁפְכְּךָ֥\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Your wrath|חֲמָתְךָ֖\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*, \rb will You|אַתָּ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֚ת\rb* \rb destroy|הֲמַשְׁחִ֣ית\rb* \rb the entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb remnant|שְׁאֵרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*?”
\p \v 9 \rb He replied|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֗י\rb*, “\rb The iniquity|עֲוֺ֨ן\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֤ל\rb* \rb and Judah|וִֽיהוּדָה֙\rb* \rb is exceedingly|בִּמְאֹ֣ד\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֔ד\rb* \rb great|גָּדוֹל֙\rb*. \rb The land|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb is full of|וַתִּמָּלֵ֤א\rb* \rb bloodshed|דָּמִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and the city|וְהָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb is full of|מָלְאָ֣ה\rb* \rb perversity|מֻטֶּ֑ה\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb they say|אָמְר֗וּ\rb*, ‘\rb The LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has forsaken|עָזַ֤ב\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*; \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb does not|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb see|רֹאֶֽה׃\rb*.’ \v 10 \rb But as for Me|וְגַ֨ם־\rb*, \rb I|אֲנִ֔י\rb* \rb will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb look on them|עֵינִ֖י\rb* \rb with pity|תָח֥וֹס\rb*, \rb nor|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb will I spare them|אֶחְמֹ֑ל\rb*. \rb I will bring their deeds|דַּרְכָּ֖ם\rb* \rb down|נָתָֽתִּי׃\rb* \rb upon their own heads|בְּרֹאשָׁ֥ם\rb*.”
\p \v 11 \rb Then|וְהִנֵּ֞ה\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֣ישׁ׀\rb* \rb clothed|לְבֻ֣שׁ\rb* \rb in linen|הַבַּדִּ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb with the writing kit|הַקֶּ֙סֶת֙\rb* \rb at his side|בְּמָתְנָ֔יו\rb* \rb reported back|מֵשִׁ֥יב\rb*\rb |דָּבָ֖ר\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*, “\rb I have done|עָשִׂ֕יתִי\rb* \rb as|כַאֲשֶׁר\rb* \rb You commanded|צִוִּיתָֽנִי׃ס\rb*.”
\c 10
\s1 God’s Glory Exits the Temple
\p \v 1 \rb And I looked|וָאֶרְאֶ֗ה\rb* \rb and saw|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb above|אֶל־\rb* \rb the expanse|הָרָקִ֙יעַ֙\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb above|עַל־\rb* \rb the heads|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of the cherubim|הַכְּרֻבִ֔ים\rb*, \rb the likeness|דְּמ֣וּת\rb* \rb of a throne|כִּסֵּ֑א\rb* \rb of sapphire|סַפִּ֔יר\rb*\rb |כְּמַרְאֵ֖ה\rb*\rb |כְּאֶ֣בֶן\rb*\rb |נִרְאָ֖ה\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb And the LORD said|וַיֹּ֜אמֶר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֣ישׁ׀\rb* \rb clothed|לְבֻ֣שׁ\rb* \rb in linen|הַבַּדִּ֗ים\rb*\rb |וַיֹּ֡אמֶר\rb*, “\rb Go|בֹּא֩\rb* \rb inside|אֶל־\rb* \rb the wheelwork|לַגַּלְגַּ֜ל\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb beneath|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the cherubim|לַכְּר֗וּב\rb*. \rb Fill|וּמַלֵּ֨א\rb* \rb your hands|חָפְנֶ֤יךָ\rb* \rb with burning coals|גַֽחֲלֵי־\rb*\rb |אֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb from among|מִבֵּינ֣וֹת\rb* \rb the cherubim|לַכְּרֻבִ֔ים\rb* \rb and scatter them|וּזְרֹ֖ק\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb*.” \rb And as I watched|לְעֵינָֽי׃\rb*, \rb he went in|וַיָּבֹ֖א\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Now when the man|הָאִ֑ישׁ\rb* \rb went in|בְּבֹא֣וֹ\rb*, \rb the cherubim|וְהַכְּרֻבִ֗ים\rb* \rb were standing|עֹֽמְדִ֛ים\rb* \rb on the south side|מִימִ֥ין\rb* \rb of the temple|לַבַּ֖יִת\rb*, \rb and a cloud|וְהֶעָנָ֣ן\rb* \rb filled|מָלֵ֔א\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the inner|הַפְּנִימִֽית׃\rb* \rb court|הֶחָצֵ֖ר\rb*. \v 4 \rb Then the glory|כְּבוֹד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb rose|וַיָּ֤רָם\rb* \rb from above|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the cherubim|הַכְּר֔וּב\rb* \rb and stood over|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the threshold|מִפְתַּ֣ן\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb*. \rb The temple|הַבַּ֙יִת֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb was filled|וַיִּמָּלֵ֤א\rb* \rb with the cloud|הֶ֣עָנָ֔ן\rb*, \rb and the court|וְהֶֽחָצֵר֙\rb* \rb was filled|מָֽלְאָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb with the brightness|נֹ֖גַהּ\rb* \rb of the glory|כְּב֥וֹד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb The sound|וְקוֹל֙\rb* \rb of the wings|כַּנְפֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the cherubim|הַכְּרוּבִ֔ים\rb* \rb could be heard|נִשְׁמַ֕ע\rb* \rb as|עַד־\rb* \rb far as the outer|הַחִיצֹנָ֑ה\rb* \rb court|הֶחָצֵ֖ר\rb*, \rb like the voice|כְּק֥וֹל\rb* \rb of God|אֵל־\rb* \rb Almighty|שַׁדַּ֖י\rb*\f + \fr 10:5 \ft Hebrew \fqa El-Shaddai\f* \rb when He speaks|בְּדַבְּרֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb When|וַיְהִ֗י\rb* \rb the LORD commanded|בְּצַוֺּתוֹ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the man|הָאִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb clothed|לְבֻֽשׁ־\rb* \rb in linen|הַבַּדִּים֙\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*, “\rb Take|קַ֥ח\rb* \rb fire|אֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb from within|מִבֵּינ֣וֹת\rb* \rb the wheelwork|לַגַּלְגַּ֔ל\rb*, \rb from among|מִבֵּינ֖וֹת\rb* \rb the cherubim|לַכְּרוּבִ֑ים\rb*,” \rb the man went in|וַיָּבֹא֙\rb* \rb and stood|וַֽיַּעֲמֹ֔ד\rb* \rb beside|אֵ֖צֶל\rb* \rb a wheel|הָאוֹפָֽן׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb Then one of the cherubim|הַכְּר֨וּב\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb reached out|וַיִּשְׁלַח֩\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֜וֹ\rb*\rb |לַכְּרוּבִ֗ים\rb* \rb and took some of|וַיִּשָּׂא֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the fire|הָאֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb was among|בֵּינ֣וֹת\rb* \rb them|הַכְּרֻבִ֔ים\rb*. \rb And he put it|וַיִּתֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the hands|חָפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the man clothed|לְבֻ֣שׁ\rb* \rb in linen|הַבַּדִּ֑ים\rb*, \rb who received it|וַיִּקַּ֖ח\rb* \rb and went out|וַיֵּצֵֽא׃\rb*. \v 8 (\rb The cherubim|לַכְּרֻבִ֑ים\rb* \rb appeared|וַיֵּרָ֖א\rb* \rb to have the form|תַּבְנִית֙\rb* \rb of human|אָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb hands|יַד־\rb* \rb under|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb their wings|כַּנְפֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.)
\p \v 9 \rb Then I looked|וָאֶרְאֶ֗ה\rb* \rb and saw|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb four|אַרְבָּעָ֣ה\rb* \rb wheels|אוֹפַנִּים֮\rb* \rb beside|אֵ֣צֶל\rb* \rb the cherubim|הַכְּרוּבִים֒\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֗ד\rb* \rb wheel|אוֹפַ֣ן\rb* \rb beside|אֵ֚צֶל\rb* \rb each|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb cherub|הַכְּר֣וּב\rb*.\rb |אֶחָ֔ד\rb*\rb |אֵ֖צֶל\rb*\rb |הַכְּר֣וּב\rb*\rb |אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb And the wheels|הָא֣וֹפַנִּ֔ים\rb* \rb gleamed|כְּעֵ֖ין\rb* \rb like a beryl|תַּרְשִֽׁישׁ׃\rb* \rb stone|אֶ֥בֶן\rb*. \v 10 \rb As for their appearance|וּמַ֨רְאֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb all four|לְאַרְבַּעְתָּ֑ם\rb* \rb had the same|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb form|דְּמ֥וּת\rb*, \rb like|כַּאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb a wheel|הָאוֹפַ֖ן\rb* \rb within|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb a wheel|הָאוֹפָֽן׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb When they moved|בְּלֶכְתָּ֗ם\rb*, \rb they would go|יֵלֵ֔כוּ\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb any of the four|אַרְבַּ֤עַת\rb* \rb directions|רִבְעֵיהֶם֙\rb*, \rb without|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb turning|יִסַּ֖בּוּ\rb* \rb as they moved|בְּלֶכְתָּ֑ם\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb wherever|הַמָּק֞וֹם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the head|הָרֹאשׁ֙\rb* \rb faced|יִפְנֶ֤ה\rb*, \rb the cherubim would go|יֵלֵ֔כוּ\rb* \rb in that direction|אַחֲרָ֣יו\rb*, \rb without|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb turning|יִסַּ֖בּוּ\rb* \rb as they moved|בְּלֶכְתָּֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Their entire|וְכָל־\rb* \rb bodies|בְּשָׂרָם֙\rb*, \rb including their backs|וְגַבֵּהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb hands|וִֽידֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb and wings|וְכַנְפֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*,\rb |וְהָאֽוֹפַנִּ֗ים\rb* \rb were full of|מְלֵאִ֤ים\rb* \rb eyes|עֵינַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb all around|סָבִ֔יב\rb*, \rb as were their four|לְאַרְבַּעְתָּ֖ם\rb* \rb wheels|אוֹפַנֵּיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb I heard|בְּאָזְנָֽי׃\rb* \rb the wheels|לָא֖וֹפַנִּ֑ים\rb* \rb being called|קוֹרָ֥א\rb* “\rb the whirling wheels|הַגַּלְגַּ֖ל\rb*.”
\p \v 14 \rb Each of the cherubim|לְאֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb had four|וְאַרְבָּעָ֥ה\rb* \rb faces|פָנִ֖ים\rb*: \rb the first|הָאֶחָ֜ד\rb* \rb face|פְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb was that|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of a cherub|הַכְּר֗וּב\rb*, \rb the second|הַשֵּׁנִי֙\rb* \rb that|וּפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of a man|אָדָ֔ם\rb*, \rb the third|וְהַשְּׁלִישִׁי֙\rb* \rb that|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of a lion|אַרְיֵ֔ה\rb*, \rb and the fourth|וְהָרְבִיעִ֖י\rb*\rb |פְּנֵי־\rb* \rb that|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of an eagle|נָֽשֶׁר׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Then the cherubim|הַכְּרוּבִ֑ים\rb* \rb rose upward|וַיֵּרֹ֖מּוּ\rb*. \rb These|הִ֣יא\rb* \rb were the living creatures|הַחַיָּ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I had seen|רָאִ֖יתִי\rb* \rb by the River|בִּֽנְהַר־\rb* \rb Kebar|כְּבָֽר׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb When the cherubim|הַכְּרוּבִ֔ים\rb* \rb moved|וּבְלֶ֙כֶת֙\rb*, \rb the wheels|הָאוֹפַנִּ֖ים\rb* \rb moved|יֵלְכ֥וּ\rb* \rb beside them|אֶצְלָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and even when they|הַכְּרוּבִ֜ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb spread|וּבִשְׂאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb their wings|כַּנְפֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb to rise|לָרוּם֙\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the ground|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*,\rb |הֵ֖ם\rb* \rb the wheels|הָאוֹפַנִּ֛ים\rb* \rb did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb veer away|יִסַּ֧בּוּ\rb* \rb from their side|מֵאֶצְלָֽם׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb When the cherubim stood still|בְּעָמְדָ֣ם\rb*, \rb the wheels also stood still|יַעֲמֹ֔דוּ\rb*, \rb and when they ascended|וּבְרוֹמָ֖ם\rb*, \rb the wheels ascended|יֵר֣וֹמּוּ\rb* \rb with them|אוֹתָ֑ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb the spirit|ר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb of the living creatures|הַחַיָּ֖ה\rb* \rb was in the wheels|בָּהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Then the glory|כְּב֣וֹד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb moved away|וַיֵּצֵא֙\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb the threshold|מִפְתַּ֣ן\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb* \rb and stood|וַֽיַּעֲמֹ֖ד\rb* \rb above|עַל־\rb* \rb the cherubim|הַכְּרוּבִֽים׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb As I watched|לְעֵינַי֙\rb*, \rb the cherubim|הַכְּרוּבִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb lifted|וַיִּשְׂא֣וּ\rb* \rb their wings|כַּ֠נְפֵיהֶם\rb* \rb and rose up|וַיֵּר֨וֹמּוּ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the ground|הָאָ֤רֶץ\rb*, \rb with the wheels|וְהָאֽוֹפַנִּ֖ים\rb* \rb beside them|לְעֻמָּתָ֑ם\rb* \rb as they went|בְּצֵאתָ֔ם\rb*. \rb And they stopped|וַֽיַּעֲמֹ֗ד\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֣תַח\rb* \rb of the east|הַקַּדְמוֹנִ֔י\rb* \rb gate|שַׁ֤עַר\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb*, \rb with the glory|וּכְב֧וֹד\rb* \rb of the God|אֱלֹהֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb above|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb them|מִלְמָֽעְלָה׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb These|הִ֣יא\rb* \rb were the living creatures|הַחַיָּ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I had seen|רָאִ֛יתִי\rb* \rb beneath|תַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb by the River|בִּֽנְהַר־\rb* \rb Kebar|כְּבָ֑ר\rb*, \rb and I knew|וָאֵדַ֕ע\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they|הֵֽמָּה׃\rb* \rb were cherubim|כְרוּבִ֖ים\rb*. \v 21 \rb Each|לְאֶחָ֔ד\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבַּ֥ע\rb* \rb had four|אַרְבָּעָ֨ה\rb* \rb faces|פָנִים֙\rb* \rb and|לְאֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb four|אַרְבָּעָ֤ה\rb* \rb wings|כְּנָפַ֖יִם\rb*, \rb with what looked like|וּדְמוּת֙\rb* \rb human|אָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb hands|יְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb under|תַּ֖חַת\rb* \rb their wings|כַּנְפֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb Their faces|פְּנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |הֵ֣מָּה\rb* \rb looked like|וּדְמ֣וּת\rb* \rb the faces|הַפָּנִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I had seen|רָאִ֙יתִי֙\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the River|נְהַר־\rb* \rb Kebar|כְּבָ֔ר\rb*\rb |מַרְאֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאוֹתָ֑ם\rb*. \rb Each creature|אִ֛ישׁ\rb* \rb went|יֵלֵֽכוּ׃\rb* \rb straight ahead|אֶל־\rb*\rb |עֵ֥בֶר\rb*\rb |פָּנָ֖יו\rb*.
\c 11
\s1 Evil in High Places
\p \v 1 \rb Then the Spirit|ר֗וּחַ\rb* \rb lifted me up|וַתִּשָּׂ֨א\rb*\rb |אֹתִ֜י\rb* \rb and brought|וַתָּבֵ֣א\rb* \rb me|אֹ֠תִי\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb*\rb |הַקַּדְמוֹנִי֙\rb* \rb the gate|שַׁ֨עַר\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb* \rb that faces|הַפּוֹנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb east|קָדִ֔ימָה\rb*. \rb And there|וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb at the entrance|בְּפֶ֣תַח\rb* \rb of the gate|הַשַּׁ֔עַר\rb* \rb were twenty-five|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשָּׁ֖ה\rb* \rb men|אִ֑ישׁ\rb*. \rb Among|בְתוֹכָ֜ם\rb* \rb them|אֶת־\rb* \rb I saw|וָאֶרְאֶ֨ה\rb* \rb Jaazaniah|יַאֲזַנְיָ֧ה\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Azzur|עַזֻּ֛ר\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and Pelatiah|פְּלַטְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Benaiah|בְּנָיָ֖הוּ\rb*, \rb who were leaders|שָׂרֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָֽם׃פ\rb*. \v 2 \rb And the LORD said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָ֑י\rb*, “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*, \rb these|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb* \rb are the men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֞ים\rb* \rb who plot|הַחֹשְׁבִ֥ים\rb* \rb evil|אָ֛וֶן\rb* \rb and give|וְהַיֹּעֲצִ֥ים\rb* \rb wicked|רָ֖ע\rb* \rb counsel|עֲצַת־\rb* \rb in this|הַזֹּֽאת׃\rb* \rb city|בָּעִ֥יר\rb*. \v 3 \rb They are saying|הָאֹ֣מְרִ֔ים\rb*, ‘\rb Is not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb the time near|בְקָר֖וֹב\rb* \rb to build|בְּנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb houses|בָּתִּ֑ים\rb*? \rb The city|הִ֣יא\rb* \rb is the cooking pot|הַסִּ֔יר\rb*,\f + \fr 11:3 \ft Or \fqa cauldron\f* \rb and we|וַאֲנַ֖חְנוּ\rb* \rb are the meat|הַבָּשָֽׂר׃\rb*.’ \v 4 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֖ן\rb* \rb prophesy|הִנָּבֵ֣א\rb* \rb against them|עֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*; \rb prophesy|הִנָּבֵ֖א\rb*, \rb O son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָֽם׃\rb*!”
\p \v 5 \rb And the Spirit|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֒\rb* \rb fell|וַתִּפֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb upon me|עָלַי֮\rb* \rb and told|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb me|אֵלַ֗י\rb* \rb to declare|אֱמֹר֙\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: “\rb That is what|כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb you are thinking|אֲמַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb*, \rb O house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*; \rb and I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb know|יְדַעְתִּֽיהָ׃\rb* \rb the thoughts|וּמַעֲל֥וֹת\rb* \rb that arise in your minds|רֽוּחֲכֶ֖ם\rb*. \v 6 \rb You have multiplied|הִרְבֵּיתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb those you killed|חַלְלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb city|בָּעִ֣יר\rb* \rb and filled|וּמִלֵּאתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb its streets|חוּצֹתֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb with the dead|חָלָֽל׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִה֒\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֮\rb*: \rb The slain|חַלְלֵיכֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you have laid|שַׂמְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb within|בְּתוֹכָ֔הּ\rb* \rb this city|הֵ֥מָּה\rb* \rb are the meat|הַבָּשָׂ֖ר\rb*, \rb and the city|וְהִ֣יא\rb* \rb is the pot|הַסִּ֑יר\rb*;\rb |וְאֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb but I will remove you|הוֹצִ֥יא\rb* \rb from it|מִתּוֹכָֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb You fear|יְרֵאתֶ֑ם\rb* \rb the sword|חֶ֖רֶב\rb*, \rb so I will bring|אָבִ֣יא\rb* \rb the sword|וְחֶ֙רֶב֙\rb* \rb against you|עֲלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb I will bring you|וְהוֹצֵאתִ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb out of the city|מִתּוֹכָ֔הּ\rb* \rb and deliver|וְנָתַתִּ֥י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb into the hands|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of foreigners|זָרִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and I will execute|וְעָשִׂ֛יתִי\rb* \rb judgments|שְׁפָטִֽים׃\rb* \rb against you|בָכֶ֖ם\rb*. \v 10 \rb You will fall|תִּפֹּ֔לוּ\rb* \rb by the sword|בַּחֶ֣רֶב\rb*, \rb and I will judge|אֶשְׁפּ֣וֹט\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb even|עַל־\rb* \rb to the borders|גְּב֥וּל\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*. \rb Then you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb The city|הִ֗יא\rb* \rb will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb be|תִהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb a pot|לְסִ֔יר\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶם֙\rb*, \rb nor will you|וְאַתֶּ֛ם\rb* \rb be|תִּהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb the meat|לְבָשָׂ֑ר\rb* \rb within it|בְתוֹכָ֖הּ\rb*. \rb I will judge|אֶשְׁפֹּ֥ט\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb even to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the borders|גְּב֥וּל\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*. \v 12 \rb Then you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*. \rb For|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb you have neither|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb followed|הֲלַכְתֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb My statutes|בְּחֻקַּי֙\rb* \rb nor|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb practiced|עֲשִׂיתֶ֑ם\rb* \rb My ordinances|וּמִשְׁפָּטַ֖י\rb*, \rb but you have conformed|עֲשִׂיתֶֽם׃\rb* \rb to the ordinances|וּֽכְמִשְׁפְּטֵ֧י\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb around you|סְבִיבוֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*.”
\s1 A Promise of Restoration
\r (\ref Jeremiah 32:36–44|JER 32:36-44\ref*)
\p \v 13 \rb Now as I was|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb prophesying|כְּהִנָּ֣בְאִ֔י\rb*, \rb Pelatiah|וּפְלַטְיָ֥הוּ\rb* \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of Benaiah|בְּנָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb died|מֵ֑ת\rb*. \rb Then I fell|וָאֶפֹּ֨ל\rb* \rb facedown|עַל־\rb*\rb |פָּנַ֜י\rb* \rb and cried out|וָאֶזְעַ֣ק\rb* \rb in a loud|גָּד֗וֹל\rb*\rb |וָאֹמַר֙\rb* \rb voice|קוֹל־\rb*, “\rb Oh|אֲהָהּ֙\rb*, \rb Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb*, \rb will You|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb bring|עֹשֶׂ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the remnant|שְׁאֵרִ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb* \rb to a complete end|כָּלָה֙\rb*?”
\p \v 14 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 15 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb your brothers|אַחֶ֤יךָ\rb* — \rb your relatives|אַחֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*, \rb your fellow exiles|אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb*\rb |גְאֻלָּתֶ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb and the whole|וְכָל־\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |כֻּלֹּ֑ה\rb* — \rb are those of whom|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb the people|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֗ם\rb* \rb have said|אָמְר֨וּ\rb*, ‘\rb They are far away|רַֽחֲקוּ֙\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*; \rb this|הִ֛יא\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb has been given|נִתְּנָ֥ה\rb* \rb to us|לָ֥נוּ\rb* \rb as a possession|לְמוֹרָשָֽׁה׃ס\rb*.’
\p \v 16 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֣ן\rb* \rb declare|אֱמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִה֒\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֮\rb*: ‘\rb Although|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb I sent them far away|הִרְחַקְתִּים֙\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְכִ֥י\rb* \rb and scattered them|הֲפִֽיצוֹתִ֖ים\rb* \rb among the countries|בָּאֲרָצ֑וֹת\rb*, \rb yet for a little while|מְעַ֔ט\rb* \rb I have been|וָאֱהִ֤י\rb* \rb a sanctuary|לְמִקְדָּ֣שׁ\rb* \rb for them|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb in the countries|בָּאֲרָצ֖וֹת\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they have gone|בָּ֥אוּ\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃ס\rb*.’
\p \v 17 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֣ן\rb* \rb declare|אֱמֹ֗ר\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִה֒\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֮\rb*: ‘\rb I will gather|וְקִבַּצְתִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb you from|מִן־\rb* \rb the peoples|הָ֣עַמִּ֔ים\rb* \rb and assemble|וְאָסַפְתִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb you from|מִן־\rb* \rb the countries|הָ֣אֲרָצ֔וֹת\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have been scattered|נְפֹצוֹתֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb and I will give back|וְנָתַתִּ֥י\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb the land|אַדְמַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.’
\p \v 18 \rb When they return|וּבָ֖אוּ־\rb* \rb to it|שָׁ֑מָּה\rb*, \rb they will remove|וְהֵסִ֜ירוּ\rb*\rb |מִמֶּֽנָּה׃\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its detestable things|שִׁקּוּצֶ֛יהָ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its abominations|תּוֹעֲבוֹתֶ֖יהָ\rb*. \v 19 \rb And I will give|וְנָתַתִּ֤י\rb* \rb them|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb singleness|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb of heart|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb and put|אֶתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb a new|חֲדָשָׁ֖ה\rb* \rb spirit|וְר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb within them|בְּקִרְבְּכֶ֑ם\rb*; \rb I will remove|וַהֲסִ֨רֹתִ֜י\rb* \rb their heart|לֵ֤ב\rb* \rb of stone|הָאֶ֙בֶן֙\rb*\rb |מִבְּשָׂרָ֔ם\rb* \rb and give|וְנָתַתִּ֥י\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb a heart|לֵ֥ב\rb* \rb of flesh|בָּשָֽׂר׃\rb*, \v 20 \rb so that|לְמַ֙עַן֙\rb* \rb they may follow|יֵלֵ֔כוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb My statutes|בְּחֻקֹּתַ֣י\rb*, \rb keep|יִשְׁמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb My ordinances|מִשְׁפָּטַ֥י\rb*, \rb and practice them|וְעָשׂ֣וּ\rb*.\rb |אֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb Then they will be|וְהָיוּ־\rb* \rb My|לִ֣י\rb* \rb people|לְעָ֔ם\rb*, \rb and I|וַאֲנִ֕י\rb* \rb will be|אֶהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb their|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb God|לֵאלֹהִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb But as for|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb those whose hearts|לֵ֧ב\rb* \rb pursue|הֹלֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb detestable things|שִׁקּוּצֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb and abominations|וְתוֹעֲבוֹתֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |לִבָּ֣ם\rb*, \rb I will bring their conduct|דַּרְכָּם֙\rb* \rb down|נָתַ֔תִּי\rb* \rb upon their own heads|בְּרֹאשָׁ֣ם\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*.”
\s1 God’s Glory Leaves Jerusalem
\p \v 22 \rb Then the cherubim|הַכְּרוּבִים֙\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb with the wheels|וְהָאֽוֹפַנִּ֖ים\rb* \rb beside them|לְעֻמָּתָ֑ם\rb*, \rb spread|וַיִּשְׂא֤וּ\rb* \rb their wings|כַּנְפֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and the glory|וּכְב֧וֹד\rb* \rb of the God|אֱלֹהֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb was above|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb them|מִלְמָֽעְלָה׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb And the glory|כְּב֣וֹד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb rose up|וַיַּ֙עַל֙\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb within|תּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb* \rb and stood|וַֽיַּעֲמֹד֙\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb the mountain|הָהָ֔ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb east|מִקֶּ֥דֶם\rb* \rb of the city|לָעִֽיר׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb And the Spirit|וְר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb lifted me up|נְשָׂאַ֗תְנִי\rb* \rb and carried me|וַתְּבִיאֵ֤נִי\rb* \rb back|אֶל־\rb* \rb to Chaldea|כַשְׂדִּ֙ימָה֙\rb*,\f + \fr 11:24 \ft Or \fqa Babylonia\f* \rb to the exiles|הַגּוֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb in the vision given|בַּמַּרְאֶ֖ה\rb* \rb by the Spirit|בְּר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֑ים\rb*. \rb After the vision|הַמַּרְאֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |רָאִֽיתִי׃\rb* \rb had gone up|וַיַּ֙עַל֙\rb* \rb from me|מֵֽעָלַ֔י\rb*, \v 25 \rb I told|וָאֲדַבֵּ֖ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the exiles|הַגּוֹלָ֑ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |דִּבְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb had shown me|הֶרְאָֽנִי׃פ\rb*.
\c 12
\s1 Signs of the Coming Captivity
\p \v 1 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*, \rb you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb are living|יֹשֵׁ֑ב\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb in|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb a rebellious|הַמֶּ֖רִי\rb* \rb house|בֵּית־\rb*. \rb They have eyes|עֵינַיִם֩\rb* \rb to see|לִרְא֜וֹת\rb* \rb but do not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb see|רָא֗וּ\rb*, \rb and ears|אָזְנַ֨יִם\rb* \rb to hear|לִשְׁמֹ֙עַ֙\rb* \rb but do not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb hear|שָׁמֵ֔עוּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb they|הֵֽם׃\rb* \rb are a rebellious|מְרִ֖י\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Therefore|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb pack|עֲשֵׂ֤ה\rb* \rb your bags|כְּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb for exile|גוֹלָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וּגְלֵ֥ה\rb*. \rb In broad daylight|יוֹמָ֖ם\rb*\rb |לְעֵֽינֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb set out from your place|מִמְּקוֹמְךָ֜\rb* \rb and go|וְגָלִ֨יתָ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb another|אַחֵר֙\rb*\rb |מָק֤וֹם\rb* \rb as they watch|לְעֵ֣ינֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb Perhaps|אוּלַ֣י\rb* \rb they will understand|יִרְא֔וּ\rb*, \rb though|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb they|הֵֽמָּה׃\rb* \rb are a rebellious|מְרִ֖י\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb*. \v 4 \rb Bring out|וְהוֹצֵאתָ֨\rb* \rb your baggage|כֵלֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb for exile|גוֹלָ֛ה\rb*\rb |כִּכְלֵ֥י\rb* \rb by day|יוֹמָ֖ם\rb*, \rb as they watch|לְעֵֽינֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*.\rb |וְאַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb Then in the evening|בָעֶ֙רֶב֙\rb*, \rb as they watch|לְעֵ֣ינֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb go out|תֵּצֵ֤א\rb* \rb like those who go|כְּמוֹצָאֵ֖י\rb* \rb into exile|גּוֹלָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb As they watch|לְעֵינֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb dig|חֲתָר־\rb* \rb through the wall|בַקִּ֑יר\rb* \rb and carry your belongings|וְהוֹצֵאתָ֖\rb* \rb out through it|בּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb And as they watch|לְעֵ֨ינֵיהֶ֜ם\rb*, \rb lift|תִּשָּׂא֙\rb* \rb your bags to|עַל־\rb* \rb your shoulder|כָּתֵ֤ף\rb* \rb and take them out|תוֹצִ֔יא\rb* \rb at dusk|בָּעֲלָטָ֣ה\rb*; \rb cover|תְכַסֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb your face|פָּנֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb so that you cannot|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb see|תִרְאֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*. \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I have made you|נְתַתִּ֖יךָ\rb* \rb a sign|מוֹפֵ֥ת\rb* \rb to the house|לְבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.”
\p \v 7 \rb So I did|וָאַ֣עַשׂ\rb*\rb |כֵּן֮\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I was commanded|צֻוֵּיתִי֒\rb*. \rb I brought out|הוֹצֵ֜אתִי\rb* \rb my bags|כֵּ֠לַי\rb* \rb for exile|גוֹלָה֙\rb*\rb |כִּכְלֵ֤י\rb* \rb by day|יוֹמָ֔ם\rb*, \rb and in the evening|וּבָעֶ֛רֶב\rb* \rb I dug|חָתַֽרְתִּי־\rb* \rb through the wall|בַקִּ֖יר\rb* \rb by hand|בְּיָ֑ד\rb*. \rb I took my belongings out|הוֹצֵ֛אתִי\rb* \rb at dusk|בָּעֲלָטָ֥ה\rb*, \rb carrying them|נָשָׂ֖אתִי\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb my shoulder|כָּתֵ֥ף\rb* \rb as they watched|לְעֵינֵיהֶֽם׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb And in the morning|בַּבֹּ֥קֶר\rb* \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֧י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֖י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 9 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*, \rb hasn’t|הֲלֹ֨א\rb* \rb the rebellious|הַמֶּ֑רִי\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb asked|אָמְר֥וּ\rb* \rb you|אֵלֶ֛יךָ\rb*, ‘\rb What|מָ֖ה\rb* \rb are you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb doing|עֹשֶֽׂה׃\rb*?’ \v 10 \rb Tell|אֱמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהֹוִ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*: ‘\rb This|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb burden|הַמַּשָּׂ֤א\rb* \rb concerns the prince|הַנָּשִׂ֞יא\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|בִּיר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb are|הֵ֥מָּה\rb* \rb there|בְתוֹכָֽם׃\rb*.’
\p \v 11 \rb You are to say|אֱמֹ֖ר\rb*, ‘\rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am a sign to you|מֽוֹפֶתְכֶ֑ם\rb*.’ \rb Just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb it happened here|עָשִׂ֗יתִי\rb*,\f + \fr 12:11 \ft Literally \fqa ‘I am a sign to you.’ Just as I have done\ft ; some translators close the quotation at the end of the verse.\f* \rb so|כֵּ֚ן\rb* \rb will it be done|יֵעָשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb*; \rb they will go|יֵלֵֽכוּ׃\rb* \rb into exile|בַּגּוֹלָ֥ה\rb* \rb as captives|בַשְּׁבִ֖י\rb*. \v 12 \rb And at dusk|בָּעֲלָטָ֣ה\rb* \rb the prince|וְהַנָּשִׂ֨יא\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb among them|בְּתוֹכָ֜ם\rb* \rb will lift|יִשָּׂא֙\rb* \rb his bags to|אֶל־\rb* \rb his shoulder|כָּתֵ֤ף\rb* \rb and go out|וְיֵצֵ֔א\rb*. \rb They will dig|יַחְתְּר֖וּ\rb* \rb through the wall|בַּקִּ֥יר\rb* \rb to bring him out|לְה֣וֹצִיא\rb*. \rb He will cover|יְכַסֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb his face|פָּנָ֣יו\rb* \rb so|יַ֗עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb he|ה֖וּא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb cannot|לֹא־\rb* \rb see|יִרְאֶ֥ה\rb* \rb the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*\rb |לַעַ֛יִן\rb*. \v 13 \rb But I will spread|וּפָרַשְׂתִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My net|רִשְׁתִּי֙\rb* \rb over him|עָלָ֔יו\rb*, \rb and he will be caught|וְנִתְפַּ֖שׂ\rb* \rb in My snare|בִּמְצֽוּדָתִ֑י\rb*. \rb I will bring|וְהֵבֵאתִ֨י\rb* \rb him|אֹת֤וֹ\rb* \rb to Babylon|בָבֶ֙לָה֙\rb*, \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the Chaldeans|כַּשְׂדִּ֔ים\rb*;\rb |וְאוֹתָ֥הּ\rb* \rb yet he will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb see it|יִרְאֶ֖ה\rb*, \rb and there|וְשָׁ֥ם\rb* \rb he will die|יָמֽוּת׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb And I will scatter|אֱזָרֶ֣ה\rb* \rb to every|לְכָל־\rb* \rb wind|ר֑וּחַ\rb* \rb all|וְכֹל֩\rb* \rb the attendants|עֶזְרֹה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb around him|סְבִיבֹתָ֥יו\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his troops|אֲגַפָּ֖יו\rb*, \rb and I will draw|אָרִ֥יק\rb* \rb a sword|וְחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb to chase after them|אַחֲרֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb And they will know|וְיָדְע֖וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb when I disperse|בַּהֲפִיצִ֤י\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb and scatter|וְזֵרִיתִ֥י\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb throughout the countries|בָּאֲרָצֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb But I will spare|וְהוֹתַרְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb a few|מִסְפָּ֔ר\rb* \rb of them|מֵהֶם֙\rb*\rb |אַנְשֵׁ֣י\rb* \rb from sword|מֵחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb and famine|מֵרָעָ֣ב\rb* \rb and plague|וּמִדָּ֑בֶר\rb*, \rb so that|לְמַ֨עַן\rb* \rb in the nations|בַּגּוֹיִם֙\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they go|בָּ֣אוּ\rb*, \rb they can recount|יְסַפְּר֜וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb their abominations|תּוֹעֲבֽוֹתֵיהֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |שָׁ֔ם\rb*. \rb Then they will know|וְיָדְע֖וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.”
\p \v 17 \rb Moreover, the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 18 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*, \rb eat|תֹּאכֵ֑ל\rb* \rb your bread|לַחְמְךָ֖\rb* \rb with trembling|בְּרַ֣עַשׁ\rb*, \rb and drink|תִּשְׁתֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb your water|וּמֵימֶ֕יךָ\rb* \rb with quivering|בְּרָגְזָ֥ה\rb* \rb and anxiety|וּבִדְאָגָ֖ה\rb*. \v 19 \rb Then tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֡רֶץ\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֨י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֜ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֩\rb* \rb about those living|לְיוֹשְׁבֵ֤י\rb* \rb in Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb and in|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אַדְמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*: ‘\rb They will eat|יֹאכֵ֔לוּ\rb* \rb their bread|לַחְמָם֙\rb* \rb with anxiety|בִּדְאָגָ֣ה\rb* \rb and drink|יִשְׁתּ֑וּ\rb* \rb their water|וּמֵֽימֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in dread|בְּשִׁמָּמ֣וֹן\rb*, \rb for|לְמַ֜עַן\rb* \rb their land|אַרְצָהּ֙\rb* \rb will be stripped|תֵּשַׁ֤ם\rb* \rb of everything in it|מִמְּלֹאָ֔הּ\rb* \rb because of the violence|מֵחֲמַ֖ס\rb* \rb of all|כָּֽל־\rb* \rb who dwell|הַיֹּשְׁבִ֥ים\rb* \rb in it|בָּֽהּ׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb The inhabited|הַנּֽוֹשָׁבוֹת֙\rb* \rb cities|וְהֶעָרִ֤ים\rb* \rb will be laid waste|תֶּחֱרַ֔בְנָה\rb*, \rb and the land|וְהָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb will become|תִֽהְיֶ֑ה\rb* \rb desolate|שְׁמָמָ֣ה\rb*. \rb Then you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.’”
\s1 The Presumptuous Proverb
\p \v 21 \rb Again the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 22 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb what|מָֽה־\rb* \rb is this|הַזֶּה֙\rb* \rb proverb|הַמָּשָׁ֤ל\rb* \rb that you have in|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|אַדְמַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\rb The days|הַיָּמִ֔ים\rb* \rb go by|יַֽאַרְכוּ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb and every|כָּל־\rb* \rb vision|חָזֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb fails|וְאָבַ֖ד\rb*’?
\p \v 23 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֞ן\rb* \rb tell|אֱמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִה֒\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֮\rb*: ‘\rb I will put an end|הִשְׁבַּ֙תִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to this|הַזֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb proverb|הַמָּשָׁ֣ל\rb*, \rb and in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb they will no longer|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb recite|יִמְשְׁל֥וּ\rb* \rb it|אֹת֛וֹ\rb*.’
\p \rb But|כִּ֚י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb say|דַּבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*: ‘\rb The days|הַיָּמִ֔ים\rb* \rb are at hand|קָֽרְבוּ֙\rb* \rb when every|כָּל־\rb* \rb vision|חָזֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb will be fulfilled|וּדְבַ֖ר\rb*. \v 24 \rb For|כִּ֠י\rb* \rb there will be|יִֽהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb more|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb false|שָׁ֖וְא\rb* \rb visions|חֲז֥וֹן\rb* \rb or flattering|חָלָ֑ק\rb* \rb divinations|וּמִקְסַ֣ם\rb* \rb within|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*, \v 25 \rb because|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb will speak|אֲדַבֵּר֙\rb*\rb |אֵת֩\rb* \rb whatever|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb word|דָּבָר֙\rb* \rb I speak|אֲדַבֵּ֤ר\rb*, \rb and it will be fulfilled|וְיֵ֣עָשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb without|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb delay|תִמָּשֵׁ֖ךְ\rb*. \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb in your days|בִֽימֵיכֶ֞ם\rb*, \rb O rebellious|הַמֶּ֗רִי\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֣ית\rb*, \rb I will speak|אֲדַבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb a message|דָּבָר֙\rb* \rb and bring it to pass|וַעֲשִׂיתִ֔יו\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃פ\rb*.’”
\p \v 26 \rb Furthermore, the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 27 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb take note|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb that the house|בֵֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb is saying|אֹֽמְרִ֔ים\rb*, ‘\rb The vision|הֶחָז֛וֹן\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb sees|חֹזֶ֖ה\rb* \rb is for many|רַבִּ֑ים\rb* \rb years from now|לְיָמִ֣ים\rb*; \rb he|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb prophesies|נִבָּֽא׃\rb* \rb about the distant|רְחוֹק֖וֹת\rb* \rb future|וּלְעִתִּ֥ים\rb*.’
\p \v 28 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֞ן\rb* \rb tell|אֱמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: ‘\rb None|לֹא־\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb of My words|דְּבָרָ֑י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb will be delayed|תִמָּשֵׁ֥ךְ\rb* \rb any longer|ע֖וֹד\rb*. \rb The message|דָּבָר֙\rb* \rb I speak|אֲדַבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb will be fulfilled|וְיֵ֣עָשֶׂ֔ה\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃ס\rb*.’”
\c 13
\s1 Reproof of False Prophets
\r (\ref Micah 2:6–11|MIC 2:6-11\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*, \rb prophesy|הִנָּבֵ֛א\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the prophets|נְבִיאֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb who are now prophesying|הַנִּבָּאִ֑ים\rb*. \rb Tell|וְאָֽמַרְתָּ֙\rb* \rb those who prophesy|לִנְבִיאֵ֣י\rb* \rb out of their own imagination|מִלִּבָּ֔ם\rb*: \rb Hear|שִׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*! \v 3 \rb This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: \rb Woe|ה֖וֹי\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the foolish|הַנְּבָלִ֑ים\rb* \rb prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֣ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb follow|הֹלְכִ֛ים\rb*\rb |אַחַ֥ר\rb* \rb their own spirit|רוּחָ֖ם\rb* \rb yet have seen|רָאֽוּ׃\rb* \rb nothing|וּלְבִלְתִּ֥י\rb*. \v 4 \rb Your prophets|נְבִיאֶ֥יךָ\rb*, \rb O Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb are|הָיֽוּ׃\rb* \rb like foxes|כְּשֻׁעָלִ֖ים\rb* \rb among the ruins|בָּחֳרָב֑וֹת\rb*. \v 5 \rb You did not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb go up|עֲלִיתֶם֙\rb* \rb to the gaps|בַּפְּרָצ֔וֹת\rb* \rb or restore|וַתִּגְדְּר֥וּ\rb* \rb the wall|גָדֵ֖ר\rb* \rb around|עַל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb so that it would stand|לַעֲמֹ֥ד\rb* \rb in the battle|בַּמִּלְחָמָ֖ה\rb* \rb on the Day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb They see|חָ֤זוּ\rb* \rb false visions|שָׁוְא֙\rb* \rb and speak lying|כָּזָ֔ב\rb* \rb divinations|וְקֶ֣סֶם\rb*. \rb They claim|הָאֹֽמְרִים֙\rb*, ‘\rb Thus declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*,’ \rb when the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb send them|שְׁלָחָ֑ם\rb*; \rb yet they wait|וְיִֽחֲל֖וּ\rb* \rb for the fulfillment|לְקַיֵּ֥ם\rb* \rb of their message|דָּבָֽר׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Haven’t you|הֲל֤וֹא\rb* \rb seen|חֲזִיתֶ֔ם\rb* \rb a false|שָׁוְא֙\rb* \rb vision|מַֽחֲזֵה־\rb* \rb and spoken|וְאֹֽמְרִים֙\rb* \rb a lying|כָּזָ֖ב\rb* \rb divination|וּמִקְסַ֥ם\rb* \rb when you proclaim|אֲמַרְתֶּ֑ם\rb*, ‘\rb Thus declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*,’ \rb even though I|וַאֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb have not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb spoken|דִבַּֽרְתִּי׃ס\rb*?
\p \v 8 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: \rb Because|יַ֚עַן\rb* \rb you have uttered|דַּבֶּרְכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb vain words|שָׁ֔וְא\rb* \rb and seen|וַחֲזִיתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb false visions|כָּזָ֑ב\rb*,\rb |לָכֵן֙\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֣י\rb* \rb I am against you|אֲלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb My hand|יָדִ֗י\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיְתָ֣ה\rb* \rb against|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb the prophets|הַנְּבִיאִ֞ים\rb* \rb who see|הַחֹזִ֣ים\rb* \rb false visions|שָׁוְא֮\rb* \rb and speak lying|כָּזָב֒\rb* \rb divinations|וְהַקֹּסְמִ֣ים\rb*. \rb They will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb belong|יִהְי֗וּ\rb* \rb to the council|בְּס֧וֹד\rb* \rb of My people|עַמִּ֣י\rb* \rb or be recorded|יִכָּתֵ֔בוּ\rb* \rb in the register|וּבִכְתָ֤ב\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*, \rb nor will they|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb enter|וְאֶל־\rb*\rb |יָבֹ֑אוּ\rb* \rb the land|אַדְמַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*.\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb Then you will know|וִידַעְתֶּ֕ם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Because|יַ֣עַן\rb*\rb |וּבְיַ֜עַן\rb* \rb they have led My people|עַמִּ֛י\rb* \rb astray|הִטְע֧וּ\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֥ר\rb*, ‘\rb Peace|שָׁל֖וֹם\rb*,’ \rb when there is no|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb peace|שָׁל֑וֹם\rb*,\rb |וְהִנָּ֛ם\rb* \rb and whitewashing|טָחִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb*\rb |תָּפֵֽל׃\rb* \rb any flimsy wall|חַ֔יִץ\rb*\rb |וְהוּא֙\rb* \rb that is built|בֹּ֣נֶה\rb*, \v 11 \rb tell|אֱמֹ֛ר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb those whitewashing the wall|טָחֵ֥י\rb*\rb |תָפֵ֖ל\rb* \rb that it will fall|וְיִפֹּ֑ל\rb*. \rb Rain|גֶּ֣שֶׁם\rb* \rb will come|הָיָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb in torrents|שׁוֹטֵ֗ף\rb*\rb |וְאַתֵּ֜נָה\rb*, \rb I will send hailstones|אַבְנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶלְגָּבִישׁ֙\rb* \rb plunging down|תִּפֹּ֔לְנָה\rb*, \rb and a windstorm|וְר֥וּחַ\rb*\rb |סְעָר֖וֹת\rb* \rb will burst forth|תְּבַקֵּֽעַ׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb Surely|וְהִנֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb when the wall|הַקִּ֑יר\rb* \rb has fallen|נָפַ֣ל\rb*, \rb you will not|הֲלוֹא֙\rb* \rb be asked|יֵאָמֵ֣ר\rb*,\rb |אֲלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* ‘\rb Where|אַיֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb is the whitewash|הַטִּ֖יחַ\rb* \rb with which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you covered it|טַחְתֶּֽם׃ס\rb*?’
\p \v 13 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: \rb In My wrath|בַּֽחֲמָתִ֑י\rb* \rb I will release|וּבִקַּעְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb a windstorm|רֽוּחַ־\rb*\rb |סְעָר֖וֹת\rb*, \rb and in My anger|בְּאַפִּ֣י\rb* \rb torrents|שֹׁטֵף֙\rb* \rb of rain|וְגֶ֤שֶׁם\rb* \rb and hail|וְאַבְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb will fall|יִֽהְיֶ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֶלְגָּבִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb with destructive|לְכָלָֽה׃\rb* \rb fury|בְּחֵמָ֥ה\rb*. \v 14 \rb I will tear down|וְהָ֨רַסְתִּ֜י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the wall|הַקִּ֨יר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you whitewashed|טַחְתֶּ֥ם\rb*\rb |תָּפֵ֛ל\rb* \rb and level|וְהִגַּעְתִּ֥יהוּ\rb* \rb it to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the ground|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*, \rb so that its foundation|יְסֹד֑וֹ\rb* \rb is exposed|וְנִגְלָ֣ה\rb*. \rb The city will fall|וְנָֽפְלָה֙\rb*, \rb and you will be destroyed|וּכְלִיתֶ֣ם\rb* \rb within it|בְּתוֹכָ֔הּ\rb*. \rb Then you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb And after I have vented|וְכִלֵּיתִ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My wrath|חֲמָתִי֙\rb* \rb against the wall|בַּקִּ֔יר\rb* \rb and against those who whitewashed it|וּבַטָּחִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֹת֖וֹ\rb*\rb |תָּפֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb I will say|וְאֹמַ֤ר\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶם֙\rb*: ‘\rb The wall|הַקִּ֔יר\rb* \rb is gone|אֵ֣ין\rb*, \rb and so|וְאֵ֖ין\rb* \rb are those who whitewashed|הַטָּחִ֥ים\rb* \rb it|אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb* — \v 16 \rb those prophets|נְבִיאֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb who prophesied|הַֽנִבְּאִים֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb and saw|וְהַחֹזִ֥ים\rb* \rb a vision|חֲז֣וֹן\rb* \rb of peace|שָׁלֹ֑ם\rb* \rb for her|לָ֖הּ\rb* \rb when there was no|וְאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb peace|שָׁלֹ֔ם\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהֹוִֽה׃פ\rb*.’
\s1 Reproof of False Prophetesses
\p \v 17 \rb Now|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb O son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb set|שִׂ֤ים\rb* \rb your face|פָּנֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the daughters|בְּנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of your people|עַמְּךָ֔\rb* \rb who prophesy|הַמִּֽתְנַבְּא֖וֹת\rb* \rb out of their own imagination|מִֽלִּבְּהֶ֑ן\rb*. \rb Prophesy|וְהִנָּבֵ֖א\rb* \rb against them|עֲלֵיהֶֽן׃\rb* \v 18 \rb and tell them that|וְאָמַרְתָּ֞\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר׀\rb*: \rb Woe|הוֹי֩\rb* \rb to the women who sew|לִֽמְתַפְּר֨וֹת\rb* \rb magic charms|כְּסָת֜וֹת\rb* \rb on|עַ֣ל׀\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb their wrists|אַצִּילֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יָדַ֗י\rb* \rb and make|וְעֹשׂ֧וֹת\rb* \rb veils|הַמִּסְפָּח֛וֹת\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the heads|רֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb of people of every|כָּל־\rb* \rb height|קוֹמָ֖ה\rb*, \rb in order to ensnare|לְצוֹדֵ֣ד\rb* \rb their souls|נְפָשׁ֑וֹת\rb*. \rb Will you ensnare|תְּצוֹדֵ֣דְנָה\rb* \rb the souls|הַנְּפָשׁוֹת֙\rb* \rb of My people|לְעַמִּ֔י\rb*\rb |וּנְפָשׁ֖וֹת\rb* \rb but preserve your own|לָכֶ֥נָה\rb*\rb |תְחַיֶּֽינָה׃\rb*? \v 19 \rb You have profaned|וַתְּחַלֶּלְ֨נָה\rb* \rb Me|אֹתִ֜י\rb* \rb among|אֶל־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֗י\rb* \rb for handfuls|בְּשַׁעֲלֵ֣י\rb* \rb of barley|שְׂעֹרִים֮\rb* \rb and scraps|וּבִפְת֣וֹתֵי\rb* \rb of bread|לֶחֶם֒\rb*. \rb By lying|בְּכַ֨זֶּבְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to My people|לְעַמִּ֖י\rb* \rb who would listen|שֹׁמְעֵ֥י\rb*\rb |כָזָֽב׃ס\rb*, \rb you have killed|לְהָמִ֤ית\rb* \rb those|נְפָשׁוֹת֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb should not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb have died|תְמוּתֶ֔נָה\rb* \rb and spared|וּלְחַיּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb those|נְפָשׁ֖וֹת\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb should not|לֹא־\rb* \rb have lived|תִֽחְיֶ֑ינָה\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֞ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר׀\rb*: \rb See|הִנְנִ֤י\rb*, \rb I am against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the magic charms|כִּסְּתוֹתֵיכֶ֙נָה֙\rb* \rb with which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you|אַ֠תֵּנָה\rb* \rb ensnare|מְצֹדְד֨וֹת\rb*\rb |שָׁ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb souls|הַנְּפָשׁוֹת֙\rb* \rb like birds|לְפֹ֣רְח֔וֹת\rb*, \rb and I will tear|וְקָרַעְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb your arms|זְרוֹעֹֽתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb So I will free|וְשִׁלַּחְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the souls|הַנְּפָשׁ֔וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֛ם\rb* \rb have ensnared|מְצֹדְד֥וֹת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |נְפָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb like birds|לְפֹרְחֹֽת׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb I will also tear off|וְקָרַעְתִּ֞י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your veils|מִסְפְּחֹֽתֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and deliver|וְהִצַּלְתִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּי֙\rb* \rb from your hands|מִיֶּדְכֶ֔ן\rb*, \rb so that they will no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb be|יִהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb prey|לִמְצוּדָ֑ה\rb* \rb in your hands|בְּיֶדְכֶ֖ן\rb*. \rb Then you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֖ן\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Because|יַ֣עַן\rb* \rb you have disheartened|הַכְא֤וֹת\rb*\rb |לֵב־\rb* \rb the righteous|צַדִּיק֙\rb* \rb with your lies|שֶׁ֔קֶר\rb*, \rb even though I|וַאֲנִ֖י\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb have caused them no grief|הִכְאַבְתִּ֑יו\rb*, \rb and because you have encouraged|וּלְחַזֵּק֙\rb*\rb |יְדֵ֣י\rb* \rb the wicked|הָרָ֖ע\rb* \rb not|לְבִלְתִּי־\rb* \rb to turn|שׁ֛וּב\rb* \rb from their evil|רָשָׁ֔ע\rb* \rb ways|מִדַּרְכּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb to save their lives|לְהַחֲיֹתֽוֹ׃\rb*, \v 23 \rb therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb you will no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb longer|ע֑וֹד\rb* \rb see|תֶחֱזֶ֔ינָה\rb* \rb false visions|שָׁ֚וְא\rb* \rb or practice|תִקְסַ֣מְנָה\rb* \rb divination|וְקֶ֖סֶם\rb*.\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb I will deliver|וְהִצַּלְתִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּי֙\rb* \rb from your hands|מִיֶּדְכֶ֔ן\rb*. \rb Then you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֖ן\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.”
\c 14
\s1 Idolatrous Elders Condemned
\r (\ref Romans 14:13–23|ROM 14:13-23\ref*; \ref 1 Corinthians 8:1–13|1CO 8:1-13\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Then some of the elders|מִזִּקְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb came|וַיָּב֤וֹא\rb*\rb |אֵלַי֙\rb*\rb |אֲנָשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb and sat down|וַיֵּשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb before me|לְפָנָֽי׃פ\rb*. \v 2 \rb And the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 3 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb these|הָאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֤ים\rb* \rb have set up|הֶעֱל֤וּ\rb* \rb idols|גִלּֽוּלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb their hearts|לִבָּ֔ם\rb* \rb and put|נָתְנ֖וּ\rb* \rb wicked|עֲוֺנָ֔ם\rb* \rb stumbling blocks|וּמִכְשׁ֣וֹל\rb* \rb before|נֹ֣כַח\rb* \rb their faces|פְּנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Should I consult|הַאִדָּרֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb with them|לָהֶֽם׃ס\rb* \rb in any way|אִדָּרֵ֖שׁ\rb*?
\p \v 4 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֣ן\rb* \rb speak|דַּבֵּר־\rb* \rb to them|א֠וֹתָם\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֨\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר׀\rb*: ‘\rb When|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb any|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb Israelite|יִשְׂרָאֵ֡ל\rb* \rb sets up|יַעֲלֶ֨ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb idols|גִּלּוּלָ֜יו\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb his heart|לִבּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb and puts|יָשִׂים֙\rb* \rb a wicked|עֲוֺנוֹ֙\rb* \rb stumbling block|וּמִכְשׁ֤וֹל\rb* \rb before|נֹ֣כַח\rb* \rb his face|פָּנָ֔יו\rb*, \rb and then comes|וּבָ֖א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִ֑יא\rb*, \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb will answer|נַעֲנֵ֧יתִי\rb* \rb him|ל֦וֹ\rb* \rb according to his great|בְּרֹ֥ב\rb* \rb idolatry|גִּלּוּלָֽיו׃\rb*, \v 5 \rb so that|לְמַ֛עַן\rb* \rb I may take hold|תְּפֹ֥שׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of the hearts|בְּלִבָּ֑ם\rb* \rb of the people|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*. \rb For|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb because of their idols|בְּגִלּֽוּלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb they are all|כֻּלָּֽם׃ס\rb* \rb estranged|נָזֹ֙רוּ֙\rb* \rb from Me|מֵֽעָלַ֔י\rb*.’
\p \v 6 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֞ן\rb* \rb tell|אֱמֹ֣ר׀\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: ‘\rb Repent|שׁ֣וּבוּ\rb* \rb and turn away|וְהָשִׁ֔יבוּ\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb your idols|גִּלּֽוּלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*; \rb turn your faces|פְנֵיכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb away|הָשִׁ֥יבוּ\rb* \rb from|וּמֵעַ֥ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your abominations|תּוֹעֲבֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*. \v 7 \rb For when|כִּי֩\rb* \rb any|אִ֨ישׁ\rb*\rb |אִ֜ישׁ\rb*\rb |מִבֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb Israelite|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb or any foreigner|וּמֵהַגֵּר֮\rb* \rb dwelling|יָג֣וּר\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵל֒\rb* \rb separates himself|וְיִנָּזֵ֣ר\rb* \rb from Me|מֵֽאַחֲרַ֗י\rb*, \rb sets up|וְיַ֤עַל\rb* \rb idols|גִּלּוּלָיו֙\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb his heart|לִבּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and puts|יָשִׂ֖ים\rb* \rb a wicked|עֲוֺנ֔וֹ\rb* \rb stumbling block|וּמִכְשׁ֣וֹל\rb* \rb before|נֹ֣כַח\rb* \rb his face|פָּנָ֑יו\rb*, \rb and then comes|וּבָ֤א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the prophet|הַנָּבִיא֙\rb* \rb to inquire|לִדְרָשׁ־\rb* \rb of Me|בִ֔י\rb*, \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb will answer|נַֽעֲנֶה־\rb* \rb him|לּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb Myself|בִּֽי׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb I will set|וְנָתַתִּ֨י\rb* \rb My face|פָנַ֜י\rb* \rb against that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb man|בָּאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb and make him|וַהֲשִֽׂמֹתִ֙יהוּ֙\rb* \rb a sign|לְא֣וֹת\rb* \rb and a proverb|וְלִמְשָׁלִ֔ים\rb*; \rb I will cut him off|וְהִכְרַתִּ֖יו\rb* \rb from among|מִתּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֑י\rb*. \rb Then you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb But if|כִֽי־\rb* \rb the prophet|וְהַנָּבִ֤יא\rb* \rb is enticed|יְפֻתֶּה֙\rb* \rb to speak|וְדִבֶּ֣ר\rb* \rb a message|דָּבָ֔ר\rb*, \rb then it was I|אֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb who enticed|פִּתֵּ֔יתִי\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb him|הַה֑וּא\rb*\rb |הַנָּבִ֣יא\rb*, \rb and I will stretch out|וְנָטִ֤יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My hand|יָדִי֙\rb* \rb against him|עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb and destroy him|וְהִ֨שְׁמַדְתִּ֔יו\rb* \rb from among|מִתּ֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֥י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb They will bear|וְנָשְׂא֖וּ\rb* \rb their punishment|עֲוֺנָ֑ם\rb*— \rb the punishment|כַּֽעֲוֺן֙\rb* \rb of the inquirer|הַדֹּרֵ֔שׁ\rb* \rb will be|יִֽהְיֶֽה׃\rb* \rb the same as that|כַּעֲוֺ֥ן\rb* \rb of the prophet|הַנָּבִ֖יא\rb*— \v 11 \rb in order that|לְ֠מַעַן\rb* \rb the house|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb may no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֤וֹד\rb* \rb stray|יִתְע֨וּ\rb* \rb from Me|מֵאַֽחֲרַ֔י\rb* \rb and no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb defile themselves|יִטַּמְּא֥וּ\rb* \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb their transgressions|פִּשְׁעֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Then they will be|וְהָ֥יוּ\rb* \rb My|לִ֣י\rb* \rb people|לְעָ֗ם\rb* \rb and I|וַֽאֲנִי֙\rb* \rb will be|אֶהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb their|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb God|לֵֽאלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃פ\rb*.’”
\s1 Four Dire Judgments
\p \v 12 \rb And the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 13 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb if|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֚רֶץ\rb* \rb sins|תֶחֱטָא־\rb* \rb against Me|לִי֙\rb* \rb by acting unfaithfully|לִמְעָל־\rb*\rb |מַ֔עַל\rb*, \rb and I stretch out|וְנָטִ֤יתִי\rb* \rb My hand|יָדִי֙\rb* \rb against it|עָלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb to cut off|וְשָׁבַ֥רְתִּי\rb* \rb its|לָ֖הּ\rb* \rb supply|מַטֵּה־\rb*\f + \fr 14:13 \ft Hebrew \fqa staff\f* \rb of food|לָ֑חֶם\rb*, \rb to send|וְהִשְׁלַחְתִּי־\rb* \rb famine|רָעָ֔ב\rb* \rb upon it|בָ֣הּ\rb*, \rb and to cut off|וְהִכְרַתִּ֥י\rb* \rb from it|מִמֶּ֖נָּה\rb* \rb both man|אָדָ֥ם\rb* \rb and beast|וּבְהֵמָֽה׃\rb*, \v 14 \rb then even if these|הָאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֨שֶׁת\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֤ים\rb*— \rb Noah|נֹ֖חַ\rb*, \rb Daniel|דָּנִאֵל\rb*, \rb and Job|וְאִיּ֑וֹב\rb*— \rb were|וְ֠הָיוּ\rb* \rb in it|בְּתוֹכָ֔הּ\rb*,\rb |הֵ֤מָּה\rb* \rb their righteousness|בְצִדְקָתָם֙\rb* \rb could deliver|יְנַצְּל֣וּ\rb* \rb only themselves|נַפְשָׁ֔ם\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Or if|לֽוּ־\rb* \rb I send wild|רָעָ֛ה\rb*\rb |אַעֲבִ֥יר\rb* \rb beasts|חַיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb through the land|בָּאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb to leave it childless|וְשִׁכְּלָ֑תָּה\rb* \rb and|וְהָיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb desolate|שְׁמָמָה֙\rb*, \rb with no man|מִבְּלִ֣י\rb* \rb passing through it|עוֹבֵ֔ר\rb* \rb for fear|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the beasts|הַחַיָּֽה׃\rb*, \v 16 \rb then as surely|אָ֗נִי\rb* \rb as I live|חַי־\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם֙\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb*, \rb even if these|הָאֵלֶּה֮\rb* \rb three|שְׁלֹ֨שֶׁת\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb were in it|בְּתוֹכָהּ֒\rb*, \rb they could not|אִם־\rb* \rb deliver|יַצִּ֑ילוּ\rb* \rb their own sons|בָּנִ֥ים\rb* \rb or|וְאִם־\rb* \rb daughters|בָּנ֖וֹת\rb*. \rb They|הֵ֤מָּה\rb* \rb alone|לְבַדָּם֙\rb* \rb would be delivered|יִנָּצֵ֔לוּ\rb*, \rb but the land|וְהָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb would be|תִּהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb desolate|שְׁמָמָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb Or|א֛וֹ\rb* \rb if I bring|אָבִ֖יא\rb* \rb a sword|חֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb that|הַהִ֑יא\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb and say|וְאָמַרְתִּ֗י\rb*, ‘\rb Let a sword|חֶ֚רֶב\rb* \rb pass|תַּעֲבֹ֣ר\rb* \rb through it|בָּאָ֔רֶץ\rb*,’ \rb so that I cut off|וְהִכְרַתִּ֥י\rb* \rb from it|מִמֶּ֖נָּה\rb* \rb both man|אָדָ֥ם\rb* \rb and beast|וּבְהֵמָֽה׃\rb*, \v 18 \rb then as surely|אָ֗נִי\rb* \rb as I live|חַי־\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם֙\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb*, \rb even if these|הָאֵלֶּה֮\rb* \rb three|וּשְׁלֹ֨שֶׁת\rb* \rb men|הָאֲנָשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb were in it|בְּתוֹכָהּ֒\rb*, \rb they could not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb deliver|יַצִּ֖ילוּ\rb* \rb their own sons|בָּנִ֣ים\rb* \rb or daughters|וּבָנ֑וֹת\rb*.\rb |כִּ֛י\rb* \rb They|הֵ֥ם\rb* \rb alone|לְבַדָּ֖ם\rb* \rb would be delivered|יִנָּצֵֽלוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb Or|א֛וֹ\rb* \rb if I send|אֲשַׁלַּ֖ח\rb* \rb a plague|דֶּ֥בֶר\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb that|הַהִ֑יא\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb and pour out|וְשָׁפַכְתִּ֨י\rb* \rb My wrath|חֲמָתִ֤י\rb* \rb upon it|עָלֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb through bloodshed|בְּדָ֔ם\rb*, \rb cutting off|לְהַכְרִ֥ית\rb* \rb from it|מִמֶּ֖נָּה\rb* \rb both man|אָדָ֥ם\rb* \rb and beast|וּבְהֵמָֽה׃\rb*, \v 20 \rb then as surely|אָ֗נִי\rb* \rb as I live|חַי־\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם֙\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb*, \rb even if Noah|וְנֹ֨חַ\rb*, \rb Daniel|דָּנִאֵל\rb*, \rb and Job|וְאִיּוֹב֮\rb* \rb were in it|בְּתוֹכָהּ֒\rb*, \rb they could not|אִם־\rb* \rb deliver|יַצִּ֑ילוּ\rb* \rb their own sons|בֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb or|אִם־\rb* \rb daughters|בַּ֖ת\rb*.\rb |הֵ֥מָּה\rb* \rb Their righteousness|בְצִדְקָתָ֖ם\rb* \rb could deliver|יַצִּ֥ילוּ\rb* \rb only themselves|נַפְשָֽׁם׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb For|כִּי֩\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֨ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהֹוִ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֜ר\rb*: ‘\rb How much worse|אַ֣ף\rb* \rb will it be when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I send|שִׁלַּ֖חְתִּי\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָ֑ם\rb* \rb My four|אַרְבַּ֣עַת\rb* \rb dire|הָרָעִ֡ים\rb* \rb judgments|שְׁפָטַ֣י׀\rb*— \rb sword|חֶ֠רֶב\rb*, \rb famine|וְרָעָ֞ב\rb*, \rb wild|רָעָה֙\rb* \rb beasts|וְחַיָּ֤ה\rb*, \rb and plague|וָדֶ֔בֶר\rb*— \rb in order to cut off|לְהַכְרִ֥ית\rb* \rb from it|מִמֶּ֖נָּה\rb* \rb both man|אָדָ֥ם\rb* \rb and beast|וּבְהֵמָֽה׃\rb*?
\p \v 22 \rb Yet , behold|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb*, \rb some survivors|פְּלֵטָ֗ה\rb* \rb will be left|נֽוֹתְרָה־\rb* \rb in it|בָּ֜הּ\rb* — \rb sons|בָּנִ֣ים\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבָנוֹת֒\rb*\rb |הִנָּם֙\rb* \rb who will be brought out|הַֽמּוּצָאִים֮\rb*. \rb They will come out|יוֹצְאִ֣ים\rb* \rb to you|אֲלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and when you see|וּרְאִיתֶ֥ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their conduct|דַּרְכָּ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and actions|עֲלִֽילוֹתָ֑ם\rb*, \rb you will be comforted|וְנִחַמְתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb regarding|עַל־\rb* \rb the disaster|הָֽרָעָה֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I have brought|הֵבֵ֙אתִי֙\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* —\rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have brought|הֵבֵ֖אתִי\rb* \rb upon it|עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb They will bring you consolation|וְנִחֲמ֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you see|תִרְא֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their conduct|דַּרְכָּ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and actions|עֲלִֽילוֹתָ֑ם\rb*, \rb and you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb that|כִּי֩\rb* \rb it was not|לֹ֨א\rb* \rb without cause|חִנָּ֤ם\rb* \rb that I have done|עָשִׂ֙יתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these things|אֲשֶׁר־\rb*\rb |עָשִׂ֣יתִי\rb* \rb within it|בָ֔הּ\rb*,’ \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהֹוִֽה׃פ\rb*.”
\c 15
\s1 Jerusalem the Useless Vine
\p \v 1 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*, \rb how|מַה־\rb* \rb does|יִּֽהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb the wood|עֵץ־\rb* \rb of the vine|הַגֶּ֖פֶן\rb* \rb surpass|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb any other|עֵ֑ץ\rb* \rb branch|הַזְּמוֹרָ֕ה\rb* \rb among the trees|בַּעֲצֵ֥י\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |הָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb in the forest|הַיָּֽעַר׃\rb*? \v 3 \rb Can wood|עֵ֔ץ\rb* \rb be taken|הֲיֻקַּ֤ח\rb* \rb from it|מִמֶּ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb to make|לַעֲשׂ֖וֹת\rb* \rb something useful|לִמְלָאכָ֑ה\rb*? \rb Or|אִם־\rb* \rb can one make|יִקְח֤וּ\rb* \rb from it|מִמֶּ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb a peg|יָתֵ֔ד\rb* \rb on which|עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb to hang|לִתְל֥וֹת\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb utensils|כֶּֽלִי׃\rb*?
\p \v 4 \rb No|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb it is cast|נִתַּ֣ן\rb* \rb into the fire|לָאֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb for fuel|לְאָכְלָ֑ה\rb*.\rb |אֵת֩\rb* \rb The fire|הָאֵשׁ֙\rb* \rb devours|אָכְלָ֤ה\rb* \rb both|שְׁנֵ֨י\rb* \rb ends|קְצוֹתָ֜יו\rb*, \rb and the middle|וְתוֹכ֣וֹ\rb* \rb is charred|נָחָ֔ר\rb*. \rb Can it be useful|הֲיִצְלַ֖ח\rb* \rb for anything|לִמְלָאכָֽה׃\rb*? \v 5 \rb Even|הִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb when it was|בִּֽהְיוֹת֣וֹ\rb* \rb whole|תָמִ֔ים\rb*, \rb it could not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be made|יֵֽעָשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb useful|לִמְלָאכָ֑ה\rb*. \rb How much less|אַ֣ף\rb* \rb can it ever|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb be|וְנַעֲשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb useful|לִמְלָאכָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb when|כִּי־\rb* \rb the fire|אֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb has consumed it|אֲכָלַ֙תְהוּ֙\rb* \rb and charred it|וַיֵּחָ֔ר\rb*!
\p \v 6 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: ‘\rb Like|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb the wood|עֵץ־\rb* \rb of the vine|הַגֶּ֙פֶן֙\rb* \rb among the trees|בְּעֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb of the forest|הַיַּ֔עַר\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have given|נְתַתִּ֥יו\rb* \rb to the fire|לָאֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb for fuel|לְאָכְלָ֑ה\rb*, \rb so|כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb I will give up|נָתַ֔תִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|יֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִָֽם׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb And I will set|וְנָתַתִּ֤י\rb* \rb My face|פָּנַי֙\rb* \rb against them|בָּהֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb Though they may have escaped|יָצָ֔אוּ\rb* \rb the fire|מֵהָאֵ֣שׁ\rb*, \rb yet another fire|וְהָאֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb will consume them|תֹּֽאכְלֵ֑ם\rb*. \rb And when I set|בְּשׂוּמִ֥י\rb* \rb My face|פָּנַ֖י\rb* \rb against them|בָּהֶֽם׃\rb*, \rb you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I am|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb Thus I will make|וְנָתַתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb desolate|שְׁמָמָ֑ה\rb*, \rb because|יַ֚עַן\rb* \rb they have acted unfaithfully|מָ֣עֲלוּ\rb*\rb |מַ֔עַל\rb*,’ \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃פ\rb*.”
\c 16
