\p \v 48 \rb As surely as I|אָ֗נִי\rb* \rb live|חַי־\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם֙\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb*, \rb your sister|אֲחוֹתֵ֔ךְ\rb*\rb |הִ֖יא\rb* \rb Sodom|סְדֹ֣ם\rb* \rb and her daughters|וּבְנוֹתֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb never|אִם־\rb* \rb did|עָֽשְׂתָה֙\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you|אַ֖תְּ\rb* \rb and your daughters|וּבְנוֹתָֽיִךְ׃\rb* \rb have done|עָשִׂ֔ית\rb*. \v 49 \rb Now|הִנֵּה־\rb* \rb this|זֶ֣ה\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֔ה\rb* \rb the iniquity|עֲוֺ֖ן\rb* \rb of your sister|אֲחוֹתֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb Sodom|סְדֹ֣ם\rb*: \rb She|לָהּ֙\rb* \rb and her daughters|וְלִבְנוֹתֶ֔יהָ\rb*\rb |וְיַד־\rb* \rb were|הָ֤יָה\rb* \rb arrogant|גָּא֨וֹן\rb*, \rb overfed|שִׂבְעַת־\rb*\rb |לֶ֜חֶם\rb*, \rb and complacent|הַשְׁקֵ֗ט\rb*\rb |וְשַׁלְוַ֣ת\rb*; \rb they did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb help|הֶחֱזִֽיקָה׃\rb* \rb the poor|עָנִ֥י\rb* \rb and needy|וְאֶבְי֖וֹן\rb*. \v 50 \rb Thus they were haughty|וַֽתִּגְבְּהֶ֔ינָה\rb* \rb and committed|וַתַּעֲשֶׂ֥ינָה\rb* \rb abominations|תוֹעֵבָ֖ה\rb* \rb before Me|לְפָנָ֑י\rb*. \rb Therefore I removed|וָאָסִ֥יר\rb* \rb them|אֶתְהֶ֖ן\rb*, \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have seen|רָאִֽיתִי׃ס\rb*.\f + \fr 16:50 \ft A few Hebrew manuscripts and LXX; MT \fqa as I have seen\f*
\p \v 51 \rb Furthermore, Samaria|וְשֹׁ֣מְר֔וֹן\rb* \rb did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb commit|חָטָ֑אָה\rb* \rb half|כַּחֲצִ֥י\rb* \rb the sins you did|חַטֹּאתַ֖יִךְ\rb*. \rb You have multiplied|וַתַּרְבִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your abominations|תּוֹעֲבוֹתַ֙יִךְ֙\rb* \rb beyond theirs|מֵהֵ֔נָּה\rb*, \rb and all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the abominations|תּוֹעֲבוֹתַ֖יִךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have committed|עָשִׂיתי׃\rb* \rb have made your sisters|אֲחוֹתֵךְ\rb* \rb appear righteous|וַתְּצַדְּקִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*. \v 52 \rb So now|גַּם־\rb* \rb you|אַ֣תְּ׀\rb* \rb must bear|שְׂאִ֣י\rb* \rb your disgrace|כְלִמָּתֵ֗ךְ\rb*, \rb since|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb you have brought justification|פִּלַּלְתְּ֙\rb* \rb for your sisters|לַֽאֲחוֹתֵ֔ךְ\rb*. \rb For they appear more righteous|תִּצְדַּ֣קְנָה\rb* \rb than you|מִמֵּ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb because your sins|בְּחַטֹּאתַ֛יִךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb were more vile|הִתְעַ֥בְתְּ\rb* \rb than theirs|מֵהֵ֖ן\rb*. \rb So you|אַ֥תְּ\rb* \rb too|וְגַם־\rb* \rb must bear|וּשְׂאִ֣י\rb* \rb your shame|בּ֙וֹשִׁי֙\rb* \rb and disgrace|כְלִמָּתֵ֔ךְ\rb*, \rb since you have made your sisters|אַחְיוֹתֵֽךְ׃\rb* \rb appear righteous|בְּצַדֶּקְתֵּ֖ךְ\rb*.
\p \v 53 \rb But I will restore|וְשַׁבְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |שְׁבִית\rb* \rb Sodom|סְדֹם֙\rb* \rb and her daughters|וּבְנוֹתֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb from captivity|שְׁבִ֣יתְהֶ֔ן\rb*,\f + \fr 16:53 \ft Or \fqa restore the fortunes of Sodom and her daughters\f*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb as well as|שְׁבִית\rb* \rb Samaria|שֹׁמְר֖וֹן\rb* \rb and her daughters|וּבְנוֹתֶ֑יהָ\rb*. \rb And I will restore you|וּשְׁבִית\rb*\rb |שְׁבִיתַ֖יִךְ\rb* \rb along with them|בְּתוֹכָֽהְנָה׃\rb*. \v 54 \rb So|לְמַ֙עַן֙\rb* \rb you will bear|תִּשְׂאִ֣י\rb* \rb your disgrace|כְלִמָּתֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb and be ashamed|וְנִכְלַ֕מְתְּ\rb* \rb of all|מִכֹּ֖ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you did|עָשִׂ֑ית\rb* \rb to comfort them|בְּנַחֲמֵ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |אֹתָֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 55 \rb And your sisters|וַאֲחוֹתַ֗יִךְ\rb*, \rb Sodom|סְדֹ֤ם\rb* \rb with her daughters|וּבְנוֹתֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb and Samaria|וְשֹֽׁמְרוֹן֙\rb* \rb with her daughters|וּבְנוֹתֶ֔יהָ\rb*, \rb will return|תָּשֹׁ֣בְןָ\rb* \rb to their former state|לְקַדְמָתָ֔ן\rb*. \rb You|וְאַתְּ֙\rb* \rb and your daughters|וּבְנוֹתַ֔יִךְ\rb*\rb |תְּשֻׁבֶ֖ינָה\rb*\rb |לְקַדְמַתְכֶֽן׃\rb* \rb will also return|תָּשֹׁ֖בְןָ\rb* \rb to your former state|לְקַדְמָתָ֑ן\rb*. \v 56 \rb Did you not|וְל֤וֹא\rb* \rb treat|הָֽיְתָה֙\rb*\rb |בְּפִ֑יךְ\rb* \rb your sister|אֲחוֹתֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb Sodom|סְדֹ֣ם\rb* \rb as an object of scorn|לִשְׁמוּעָ֖ה\rb* \rb in the day|בְּי֖וֹם\rb* \rb of your pride|גְּאוֹנָֽיִךְ׃\rb*, \v 57 \rb before|בְּטֶרֶם֮\rb* \rb your wickedness|רָעָתֵךְ֒\rb* \rb was uncovered|תִּגָּלֶ֣ה\rb*? \rb Even so|כְּמ֗וֹ\rb*, \rb you are now|עֵ֚ת\rb* \rb scorned|חֶרְפַּ֣ת\rb* \rb by the daughters|בְּנוֹת־\rb* \rb of Edom|אֲרָ֔ם\rb*\f + \fr 16:57 \ft Many Hebrew manuscripts and Syriac; most Hebrew manuscripts, LXX, and Vulgate \fqa Aram\f* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb those around her|סְבִיבוֹתֶ֖יהָ\rb*, \rb and by the daughters|בְּנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֑ים\rb*— \rb all those around you|מִסָּבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb who despise|הַשָּׁאט֥וֹת\rb* \rb you|אוֹתָ֖ךְ\rb*. \v 58 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb You|אַ֣תְּ\rb* \rb will bear the consequences|נְשָׂאתִ֑ים\rb* \rb of your lewdness|זִמָּתֵ֥ךְ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb your abominations|תּוֹעֲבוֹתַ֖יִךְ\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\s1 The Covenant Remembered
\p \v 59 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: \rb I will deal|וְעָשִׂית\rb* \rb with you|אוֹתָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb according to|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb your deeds|עָשִׂ֑ית\rb*, \rb since|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you have despised|בָּזִ֥ית\rb* \rb the oath|אָלָ֖ה\rb* \rb by breaking|לְהָפֵ֥ר\rb* \rb the covenant|בְּרִֽית׃\rb*. \v 60 \rb But I|אֲנִ֧י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will remember|וְזָכַרְתִּ֨י\rb* \rb the covenant|בְּרִיתִ֛י\rb*\rb |בְּרִ֥ית\rb* \rb I made with you|אוֹתָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb in the days|בִּימֵ֣י\rb* \rb of your youth|נְעוּרָ֑יִךְ\rb*, \rb and I will establish|וַהֲקִמוֹתִ֥י\rb* \rb an everlasting covenant|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb with you|לָ֖ךְ\rb*. \v 61 \rb Then you will remember|וְזָכַ֣רְתְּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your ways|דְּרָכַיִךְ֮\rb* \rb and be ashamed|וְנִכְלַמְתְּ֒\rb* \rb when you receive|בְּקַחְתֵּ֗ךְ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your older|הַגְּדֹל֣וֹת\rb* \rb and|אֶל־\rb* \rb younger|הַקְּטַנּ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |מִמֵּ֑ךְ\rb* \rb sisters|אֲחוֹתַ֙יִךְ֙\rb*. \rb I will give|וְנָתַתִּ֨י\rb* \rb them|אֶתְהֶ֥ן\rb* \rb to you|לָ֛ךְ\rb* \rb as daughters|לְבָנ֖וֹת\rb*, \rb but not because of|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb My covenant with you|מִבְּרִיתֵֽךְ׃\rb*.
\p \v 62 \rb So I|אֲנִ֛י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will establish|וַהֲקִימוֹתִ֥י\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֖י\rb* \rb with you|אִתָּ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb and you will know|וְיָדַ֖עַתְּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*, \v 63 \rb so that|לְמַ֤עַן\rb* \rb when I make atonement|בְּכַפְּרִי־\rb* \rb for|לְכָל־\rb* \rb all|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you have done|עָשִׂ֔ית\rb*, \rb you will remember|תִּזְכְּרִי֙\rb* \rb and be ashamed|וָבֹ֔שְׁתְּ\rb* \rb and never|וְלֹ֨א\rb*\rb |יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb again|עוֹד֙\rb* \rb open|פִּתְח֣וֹן\rb* \rb your mouth|פֶּ֔ה\rb* \rb because of|מִפְּנֵ֖י\rb* \rb your disgrace|כְּלִמָּתֵ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃ס\rb*.”
\c 17
\s1 The Parable of Two Eagles and a Vine
\r (\ref Matthew 13:24–30|MAT 13:24-30\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb Now the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*, \rb pose|ח֥וּד\rb* \rb a riddle|חִידָ֖ה\rb*; \rb speak a parable|וּמְשֹׁ֣ל\rb*\rb |מָשָׁ֑ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֖ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 3 \rb and tell them that|וְאָמַרְתָּ֞\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר׀\rb*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\rb A great|הַגָּדוֹל֙\rb* \rb eagle|הַנֶּ֤שֶׁר\rb* \rb with great|גְּד֤וֹל\rb* \rb wings|הַכְּנָפַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb and long|אֶ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb pinions|הָאֵ֔בֶר\rb*,\f + \fr 17:3 \fqa Pinions \ft are the outer parts of a bird’s wings, including the flight feathers.\f*
\q2 \rb full|מָלֵא֙\rb* \rb of feathers|הַנּוֹצָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb of many colors|הָֽרִקְמָ֑ה\rb*,
\q1 \rb came|בָּ֚א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Lebanon|הַלְּבָנ֔וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb and took away|וַיִּקַּ֖ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the top|צַמֶּ֥רֶת\rb* \rb of the cedar|הָאָֽרֶז׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb He plucked off|קָטָ֑ף\rb* \rb its topmost|רֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb shoot|יְנִֽיקוֹתָ֖יו\rb*,
\q2 \rb carried it|וַיְבִיאֵ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of merchants|כְּנַ֔עַן\rb*,
\q2 \rb and planted|שָׂמֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb it in a city|בְּעִ֥יר\rb* \rb of traders|רֹכְלִ֖ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb He took|וַיִּקַּח֙\rb* \rb some of the seed|מִזֶּ֣רַע\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb and planted|וַֽיִּתְּנֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb it in fertile|זָ֑רַע\rb* \rb soil|בִּשְׂדֵה־\rb*;\f + \fr 17:5 \ft Hebrew \fqa in a field of seed\f*
\q1 \rb he placed it|קָ֚ח\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb abundant|רַבִּ֔ים\rb* \rb waters|מַ֣יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb and set it out|שָׂמֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb like a willow|צַפְצָפָ֖ה\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb It sprouted|וַיִּצְמַ֡ח\rb* \rb and became|וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb a spreading|סֹרַ֜חַת\rb* \rb vine|לְגֶ֨פֶן\rb*,
\q2 \rb low|שִׁפְלַ֣ת\rb* \rb in height|קוֹמָ֗ה\rb*, \rb with branches|דָּלִיּוֹתָיו֙\rb* \rb turned|לִפְנ֤וֹת\rb* \rb toward him|אֵלָ֔יו\rb*;
\q2 \rb yet its roots|וְשָׁרָשָׁ֖יו\rb* \rb remained|יִֽהְי֑וּ\rb* \rb where it stood|תַּחְתָּ֣יו\rb*.
\q1 \rb So it became|וַתְּהִ֣י\rb* \rb a vine|לְגֶ֔פֶן\rb* \rb and yielded|וַתַּ֣עַשׂ\rb* \rb branches|בַּדִּ֔ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and sent out|וַתְּשַׁלַּ֖ח\rb* \rb shoots|פֹּארֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb But there was|וַיְהִ֤י\rb* \rb another|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb great|גָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb eagle|נֶֽשֶׁר־\rb*
\q2 \rb with great|גְּד֥וֹל\rb* \rb wings|כְּנָפַ֖יִם\rb* \rb and many|וְרַב־\rb* \rb feathers|נוֹצָ֑ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb And behold|וְהִנֵּה֩\rb*, \rb this|הַזֹּ֜את\rb* \rb vine|הַגֶּ֨פֶן\rb* \rb bent|כָּֽפְנָ֧ה\rb* \rb its roots|שָׁרֳשֶׁ֣יהָ\rb* \rb toward him|עָלָ֗יו\rb*.
