\s1 The Parable Explained
\p \v 11 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 12 “\rb Now|נָא֙\rb* \rb say to|אֱמָר־\rb* \rb this rebellious|הַמֶּ֔רִי\rb* \rb house|לְבֵ֣ית\rb*: ‘\rb Do you not|הֲלֹ֥א\rb* \rb know|יְדַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb what|מָה־\rb* \rb these things mean|אֵ֑לֶּה\rb*?’
\p \rb Tell them|אֱמֹ֗ר\rb*, ‘\rb Behold|הִנֵּה־\rb*, \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֤ל\rb* \rb came|בָ֨א\rb* \rb to Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb*, \rb carried off|וַיִּקַּ֤ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its king|מַלְכָּהּ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and officials|שָׂרֶ֔יהָ\rb*, \rb and brought them back|וַיָּבֵ֥א\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb with him|אֵלָ֖יו\rb* \rb to Babylon|בָּבֶֽלָה׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb He took|וַיִּקַּח֙\rb* \rb a member of the royal|הַמְּלוּכָ֔ה\rb* \rb family|מִזֶּ֣רַע\rb*\f + \fr 17:13 \ft Hebrew \fqa the royal seed\f* \rb and made|וַיִּכְרֹ֥ת\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֑ית\rb* \rb with him|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb*, \rb putting|וַיָּבֵ֤א\rb* \rb him|אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb under oath|בְּאָלָ֔ה\rb*.\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Then he carried away|לָקָֽח׃\rb* \rb the leading men|אֵילֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*, \v 14 \rb so that the kingdom|מַמְלָכָ֣ה\rb* \rb would be|לִֽהְיוֹת֙\rb* \rb brought low|שְׁפָלָ֔ה\rb*, \rb unable|לְבִלְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb to lift itself up|הִתְנַשֵּׂ֑א\rb*, \rb surviving only|לְעָמְדָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb by keeping|לִשְׁמֹ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his covenant|בְּרִית֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb But this king rebelled|וַיִּמְרָד־\rb* \rb against Babylon|בּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb by sending|לִשְׁלֹ֤חַ\rb* \rb his envoys|מַלְאָכָיו֙\rb* \rb to Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb to ask for|לָֽתֶת־\rb*\rb |ל֥וֹ\rb* \rb horses|סוּסִ֖ים\rb* \rb and a large|רָ֑ב\rb* \rb army|וְעַם־\rb*. \rb Will he flourish|הֲיִצְלָ֤ח\rb*? \rb Will the one who does|הָעֹשֵׂ֣ה\rb* \rb such|אֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb things escape|הֲיִמָּלֵט֙\rb*? \rb Can he break|וְהֵפֵ֥ר\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֖ית\rb* \rb and yet escape|וְנִמְלָֽט׃\rb*?’
\p \v 16 ‘\rb As surely as|אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹ֗א\rb* \rb I|אָ֗נִי\rb* \rb live|חַי־\rb*,’ \rb declares|נְאֻם֮\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִה֒\rb*, ‘\rb he will die|יָמֽוּת׃\rb* \rb in|בְתוֹךְ־\rb* \rb Babylon|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb*, \rb in the land|בִּמְקוֹם֙\rb* \rb of the king|הַמֶּ֙לֶךְ֙\rb* \rb who enthroned him|הַמַּמְלִ֣יךְ\rb*,\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb whose|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb oath|אָ֣לָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb he despised|בָּזָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and whose|וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb covenant|בְּרִית֑וֹ\rb*\rb |אִתּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb he broke|הֵפֵ֖ר\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \v 17 \rb Pharaoh|פַרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb with his mighty|גָּד֜וֹל\rb* \rb army|בְחַ֨יִל\rb* \rb and vast|רָ֗ב\rb* \rb horde|וּבְקָהָ֣ל\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹא֩\rb* \rb help|יַעֲשֶׂ֨ה\rb* \rb him|אוֹת֤וֹ\rb* \rb in battle|בַּמִּלְחָמָ֔ה\rb*, \rb when ramps|סֹלְלָ֖ה\rb* \rb are built|בִּשְׁפֹּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb and siege walls|דָּיֵ֑ק\rb* \rb constructed|וּבִבְנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb to destroy|לְהַכְרִ֖ית\rb* \rb many|רַבּֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb lives|נְפָשׁ֥וֹת\rb*. \v 18 \rb He despised|וּבָזָ֥ה\rb* \rb the oath|אָלָ֖ה\rb* \rb by breaking|לְהָפֵ֣ר\rb* \rb the covenant|בְּרִ֑ית\rb*. \rb Seeing that|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb he gave|נָתַ֥ן\rb* \rb his hand in pledge|יָד֛וֹ\rb* \rb yet did|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb these things|אֵ֥לֶּה\rb*, \rb he will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb escape|יִמָּלֵֽט׃ס\rb*!’
\p \v 19 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֞ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִה֮\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֨ר\rb*: ‘\rb As|אָנִי֒\rb* \rb surely as|אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹ֗א\rb* \rb I live|חַי־\rb*, \rb I will bring down|וּנְתַתִּ֖יו\rb* \rb upon his head|בְּרֹאשֽׁוֹ׃\rb* \rb My oath|אָֽלָתִי֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he despised|בָּזָ֔ה\rb* \rb and My covenant|וּבְרִיתִ֖י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he broke|הֵפִ֑יר\rb*. \v 20 \rb I will spread|וּפָרַשְׂתִּ֤י\rb* \rb My net|רִשְׁתִּ֔י\rb* \rb over him|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb and catch him|וְנִתְפַּ֖שׂ\rb* \rb in My snare|בִּמְצֽוּדָתִ֑י\rb*. \rb I will bring him|וַהֲבִיאוֹתִ֣יהוּ\rb* \rb to Babylon|בָבֶ֗לָה\rb* \rb and execute judgment|וְנִשְׁפַּטְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb upon him|אִתּוֹ֙\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb for the treason|מָֽעַל־\rb* \rb he committed|מַעֲל֖וֹ\rb* \rb against Me|בִּֽי׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb |וְאֵ֨ת\rb* \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb his choice|מִבְרָחוֹ\rb*\rb |בְּכָל־\rb* \rb troops|אֲגַפָּיו֙\rb*\f + \fr 17:21 \ft Many Hebrew manuscripts; MT \fqa All his fleeing troops\f* \rb will fall|יִפֹּ֔לוּ\rb* \rb by the sword|בַּחֶ֣רֶב\rb*, \rb and those who survive|וְהַנִּשְׁאָרִ֖ים\rb* \rb will be scattered|יִפָּרֵ֑שׂוּ\rb* \rb to every|לְכָל־\rb* \rb wind|ר֣וּחַ\rb*. \rb Then you will know|וִידַעְתֶּ֕ם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb have spoken|דִּבַּֽרְתִּי׃ס\rb*.’
\p \v 22 \rb This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*:
