\p \v 3 \rb As surely as|אָ֕נִי\rb* \rb I live|חַי־\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb*, \rb you will no|אִם־\rb*\rb |יִֽהְיֶ֨ה\rb* \rb longer|ע֗וֹד\rb* \rb quote|מְשֹׁ֛ל\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb proverb|הַמָּשָׁ֥ל\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb Behold|הֵ֤ן\rb*, \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb soul|הַנְּפָשׁוֹת֙\rb* \rb belongs to Me|לִ֣י\rb*; \rb both father|הָאָ֛ב\rb* \rb and|וּכְנֶ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \rb son|הַבֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb are|הֵ֑נָּה\rb* \rb Mine|לִי־\rb*. \rb The soul|הַנֶּ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \rb who sins|הַחֹטֵ֖את\rb* \rb is the one who|הִ֥יא\rb* \rb will die|תָמֽוּת׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Now suppose|כִּי־\rb* \rb a man|וְאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb is|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb righteous|צַדִּ֑יק\rb* \rb and does|וְעָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb what is just|מִשְׁפָּ֖ט\rb* \rb and right|וּצְדָקָֽה׃\rb*:
