\q1 \v 7 \rb He does not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb oppress|יוֹנֶ֔ה\rb* \rb another|וְאִישׁ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb but restores|יָשִׁ֔יב\rb* \rb the pledge|חֲבֹלָת֥וֹ\rb* \rb to the debtor|חוֹב֙\rb*.
\q1 \rb He does not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb commit|יִגְזֹ֑ל\rb* \rb robbery|גְּזֵלָ֖ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb but gives|יִתֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb his bread|לַחְמוֹ֙\rb* \rb to the hungry|לְרָעֵ֣ב\rb*
\q2 \rb and covers|יְכַסֶּה־\rb* \rb the naked|וְעֵירֹ֖ם\rb* \rb with clothing|בָּֽגֶד׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb He does not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb engage|יִתֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb in usury|בַּנֶּ֣שֶׁךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb or|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb take|יִקָּ֔ח\rb* \rb excess interest|וְתַרְבִּית֙\rb*,
\q1 \rb but he withholds his hand|יָד֑וֹ\rb* \rb from iniquity|מֵעָ֖וֶל\rb*
\q2 \rb |יָשִׁ֣יב\rb* \rb and executes|יַֽעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb true|אֱמֶת֙\rb* \rb justice|מִשְׁפַּ֤ט\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb men|אִ֖ישׁ\rb*.\rb |לְאִֽישׁ׃\rb*
\q1 \v 9 \rb He follows|יְהַלֵּ֛ךְ\rb* \rb My statutes|בְּחֻקּוֹתַ֧י\rb*
\q2 \rb and faithfully|אֱמֶ֑ת\rb* \rb keeps|שָׁמַ֖ר\rb*\rb |לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb My ordinances|וּמִשְׁפָּטַ֥י\rb*.
\q1 \rb That man is|הוּא֙\rb* \rb righteous|צַדִּ֥יק\rb*;
\q2 \rb surely he will live|חָיֹ֣ה\rb*\rb |יִֽחְיֶ֔ה\rb*,
\qr \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Now suppose that man has|וְהוֹלִ֥יד\rb* \rb a violent|פָּרִ֖יץ\rb* \rb son|בֵּן־\rb*, \rb who sheds|שֹׁפֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb blood|דָּ֑ם\rb* \rb or does|וְעָ֣שָׂה\rb*\rb |אָ֔ח\rb* \rb any|מֵאַחַ֖ד\rb* \rb of these things|מֵאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb*, \v 11 \rb though the father|וְה֕וּא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb has done|עָשָׂ֑ה\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb none|כָּל־\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb of them|אֵ֖לֶּה\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \rb Indeed|גַ֤ם\rb*, \rb the son eats|אָכַ֔ל\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the mountain|הֶֽהָרִים֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and defiles|טִמֵּֽא׃\rb* \rb his neighbor’s|רֵעֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֥שֶׁת\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb He oppresses|הוֹנָ֔ה\rb* \rb the poor|עָנִ֤י\rb* \rb and needy|וְאֶבְיוֹן֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb he commits robbery|גְּזֵל֣וֹת\rb*\rb |גָּזָ֔ל\rb*
\q2 \rb and does not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb restore|יָשִׁ֑יב\rb* \rb a pledge|חֲבֹ֖ל\rb*.
\q1 \rb He lifts|נָשָׂ֣א\rb* \rb his eyes|עֵינָ֔יו\rb* \rb to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb idols|הַגִּלּוּלִים֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb he commits|עָשָֽׂה׃\rb* \rb abominations|תּוֹעֵבָ֖ה\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb He engages|נָתַ֛ן\rb* \rb in usury|בַּנֶּ֧שֶׁךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb and takes|לָקַ֖ח\rb* \rb excess interest|וְתַרְבִּ֥ית\rb*.
\p \rb Will this son live|וָחָ֑י\rb*? \rb He will not|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |יִֽחְיֶ֗ה\rb*!\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb Since he has committed|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb abominations|הַתּוֹעֵב֤וֹת\rb*, \rb he will surely die|מ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |יוּמָ֔ת\rb*; \rb his blood|דָּמָ֖יו\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶֽה׃\rb* \rb on his own head|בּ֥וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb Now|וְהִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb suppose this son has|הוֹלִ֣יד\rb* \rb a son|בֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb who sees|וַיַּ֕רְא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the sins|חַטֹּ֥את\rb* \rb his father|אָבִ֖יו\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb has committed|עָשָׂ֑ה\rb*, \rb considers them|וַיִּרְאֶ֕ה\rb*, \rb and does not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb do likewise|יַעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb*\rb |כָּהֵֽן׃\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb He does not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb eat|אָכָ֔ל\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the mountain|הֶֽהָרִים֙\rb*
\q2 \rb or|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb look|נָשָׂ֔א\rb*\rb |וְעֵינָיו֙\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the idols|גִּלּוּלֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*.
\q2 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb He does not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb defile|טִמֵּֽא׃\rb* \rb his neighbor’s|רֵעֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֥שֶׁת\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb He does not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb oppress|הוֹנָ֔ה\rb* \rb another|וְאִישׁ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb or retain|חָבָ֔ל\rb* \rb a pledge|חֲבֹל֙\rb*,\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb or commit|גָזָ֑ל\rb* \rb robbery|וּגְזֵלָ֖ה\rb*.\rb |לֹ֣א\rb*
\q1 \rb He gives|נָתָ֔ן\rb* \rb his bread|לַחְמוֹ֙\rb* \rb to the hungry|לְרָעֵ֣ב\rb*
\q2 \rb and covers|כִּסָּה־\rb* \rb the naked|וְעֵר֖וֹם\rb* \rb with clothing|בָֽגֶד׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 \rb He withholds|הֵשִׁ֣יב\rb* \rb his hand|יָד֗וֹ\rb* \rb from harming the poor|מֵעָנִ֞י\rb*\f + \fr 18:17 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa He withholds his hand from iniquity\f*
\q2 \rb and takes|לָקָ֔ח\rb* \rb no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb interest|נֶ֤שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb or usury|וְתַרְבִּית֙\rb*.
\q1 \rb He|ה֗וּא\rb* \rb keeps|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb* \rb My ordinances|מִשְׁפָּטַ֣י\rb*
\q2 \rb and follows|הָלָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb My statutes|בְּחֻקּוֹתַ֖י\rb*.
\p \rb Such a man will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb die|יָמ֛וּת\rb* \rb for his father’s|אָבִ֖יו\rb* \rb iniquity|בַּעֲוֺ֥ן\rb*. \rb He will surely live|חָיֹ֥ה\rb*\rb |יִחְיֶֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb As for his father|אָבִ֞יו\rb*, \rb he will die|מֵ֖ת\rb* \rb for his own iniquity|בַּעֲוֺנֽוֹ׃\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb he practiced|עָ֣שַׁק\rb* \rb extortion|עֹ֗שֶׁק\rb*, \rb robbed|גָּזַל֙\rb*\rb |גֵּ֣זֶל\rb* \rb his brother|אָ֔ח\rb*, \rb and did|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb what|וַאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb was wrong|לֹא־\rb*\rb |ט֛וֹב\rb* \rb among|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb his people|עַמָּ֑יו\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּה־\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb Yet you may ask|וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֕ם\rb*, ‘\rb Why|מַדֻּ֛עַ\rb* \rb shouldn’t the son|הַבֵּ֖ן\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* \rb bear|נָשָׂ֥א\rb* \rb the iniquity|בַּעֲוֺ֣ן\rb* \rb of his father|הָאָ֑ב\rb*?’
\p \rb Since the son|וְהַבֵּ֞ן\rb* \rb has done|עָשָׂ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb what is just|מִשְׁפָּ֧ט\rb* \rb and right|וּצְדָקָ֣ה\rb*, \rb carefully|שָׁמַ֛ר\rb* \rb observing|וַיַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb My statutes|חֻקּוֹתַ֥י\rb*, \rb he will surely live|חָיֹ֥ה\rb*\rb |יִחְיֶֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb The soul|הַנֶּ֥פֶשׁ\rb* \rb who sins|הַחֹטֵ֖את\rb* \rb is the one who|הִ֣יא\rb* \rb will die|תָמ֑וּת\rb*. \rb A son|בֵּ֞ן\rb* \rb will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb bear|יִשָּׂ֣א׀\rb* \rb the iniquity|בַּעֲוֺ֣ן\rb* \rb of his father|הָאָ֗ב\rb*, \rb and a father|וְאָב֙\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb bear|יִשָּׂא֙\rb* \rb the iniquity|בַּעֲוֺ֣ן\rb* \rb of his son|הַבֵּ֔ן\rb*. \rb The righteousness|צִדְקַ֤ת\rb* \rb of the righteous man|הַצַּדִּיק֙\rb* \rb will fall|תִּֽהְיֶ֔ה\rb* \rb upon him|עָלָ֣יו\rb*, \rb and the wickedness|וְרִשְׁעַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the wicked man|רָשָׁע\rb* \rb will fall|תִּֽהְיֶֽה׃ס\rb* \rb upon him|עָלָ֥יו\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb But if|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the wicked man|וְהָרָשָׁ֗ע\rb* \rb turns|יָשׁוּב֙\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the sins|חַטָּאתוֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he has committed|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb*, \rb keeps|וְשָׁמַר֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb My statutes|חֻקּוֹתַ֔י\rb*, \rb and does|וְעָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb what is just|מִשְׁפָּ֖ט\rb* \rb and right|וּצְדָקָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he will surely live|חָיֹ֥ה\rb*\rb |יִחְיֶ֖ה\rb*; \rb he will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb die|יָמֽוּת׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb None|כָּל־\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb of the transgressions|פְּשָׁעָיו֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he has committed|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb* \rb will be held|יִזָּכְר֖וּ\rb* \rb against him|ל֑וֹ\rb*. \rb Because of the righteousness|בְּצִדְקָת֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he has practiced|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*, \rb he will live|יִֽחְיֶֽה׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb Do I take any pleasure in|הֶחָפֹ֤ץ\rb*\rb |אֶחְפֹּץ֙\rb* \rb the death|מ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the wicked|רָשָׁ֔ע\rb*? \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb*. \rb Wouldn’t I prefer|הֲל֛וֹא\rb* \rb that he turn|בְּשׁוּב֥וֹ\rb* \rb from his ways|מִדְּרָכָ֖יו\rb* \rb and live|וְחָיָֽה׃ס\rb*?
\p \v 24 \rb But if a righteous man|צַדִּ֤יק\rb* \rb turns|וּבְשׁ֨וּב\rb* \rb from his righteousness|מִצִּדְקָתוֹ֙\rb* \rb and practices|וְעָ֣שָׂה\rb* \rb iniquity|עָ֔וֶל\rb*, \rb committing|עָשָׂ֧ה\rb* \rb the same abominations|הַתּוֹעֵב֜וֹת\rb* \rb as|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the wicked|הָרָשָׁ֛ע\rb*\rb |יַעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb*, \rb will he live|וָחָ֑י\rb*?\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb None|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb of the righteous acts|צִדְקָתוֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he did|עָשָׂה֙\rb* \rb will be remembered|תִזָּכַ֔רְנָה\rb*. \rb Because of the unfaithfulness|מָעַ֛ל\rb*\rb |בְּמַעֲל֧וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb and sin|וּבְחַטָּאת֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he has committed|חָטָ֖א\rb*, \rb he will die|יָמֽוּת׃\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb Yet you say|וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֕ם\rb*, ‘\rb The way|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֑י\rb* \rb is not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb just|יִתָּכֵ֖ן\rb*.’
\p \rb Hear|שִׁמְעוּ־\rb* \rb now|נָא֙\rb*, \rb O house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*: \rb Is it My way|הֲדַרְכִּי֙\rb* \rb that is unjust|לֹ֣א\rb*\rb |יִתָּכֵ֔ן\rb*? \rb Is it not|הֲלֹ֥א\rb* \rb your ways|דַרְכֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb that are unjust|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |יִתָּכֵֽנוּ׃\rb*?
\p \v 26 \rb If a righteous man|צַדִּ֧יק\rb* \rb turns|בְּשׁוּב־\rb* \rb from his righteousness|מִצִּדְקָת֛וֹ\rb* \rb and practices|וְעָ֥שָׂה\rb* \rb iniquity|עָ֖וֶל\rb*, \rb he will die|וּמֵ֣ת\rb* \rb for this|עֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb He will die|יָמֽוּת׃ס\rb* \rb because of the iniquity|בְּעַוְל֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he has committed|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 27 \rb But if a wicked man|רָשָׁ֗ע\rb* \rb turns|וּבְשׁ֣וּב\rb* \rb from the wickedness|מֵֽרִשְׁעָתוֹ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he has committed|עָשָׂ֔ה\rb* \rb and does|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb what is just|מִשְׁפָּ֖ט\rb* \rb and right|וּצְדָקָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he|ה֖וּא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will save|יְחַיֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb his life|נַפְשׁ֥וֹ\rb*. \v 28 \rb Because he considered|וַיִּרְאֶ֣ה\rb* \rb and turned|וַיָּשׁוֹב\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the transgressions|פְּשָׁעָ֖יו\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he had committed|עָשָׂ֑ה\rb*, \rb he will surely live|חָי֥וֹ\rb*\rb |יִחְיֶ֖ה\rb*; \rb he will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb die|יָמֽוּת׃\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb Yet the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb says|וְאָֽמְרוּ֙\rb*, ‘\rb The way|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֑י\rb* \rb is not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb just|יִתָּכֵ֖ן\rb*.’
\p \rb Are My ways|הַדְּרָכַ֞י\rb* \rb unjust|לֹ֤א\rb*, \rb O house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*? \rb Is it not|הֲלֹ֥א\rb* \rb your ways|דַרְכֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb that are unjust|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |יִתָּכֵֽן׃\rb*?
\p \v 30 \rb Therefore|לָכֵן֩\rb*, \rb O house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb I will judge|אֶשְׁפֹּ֤ט\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶם֙\rb*, \rb each|אִ֨ישׁ\rb* \rb according to his ways|כִּדְרָכָ֜יו\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb*. \rb Repent|שׁ֤וּבוּ\rb* \rb and turn|וְהָשִׁ֙יבוּ֙\rb* \rb from all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb your transgressions|פִּשְׁעֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb so that your iniquity|עָוֺֽן׃\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb become|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb downfall|לְמִכְשׁ֖וֹל\rb*. \v 31 \rb Cast away|הַשְׁלִ֣יכוּ\rb* \rb from yourselves|מֵעֲלֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the transgressions|פִּשְׁעֵיכֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you have committed|פְּשַׁעְתֶּ֣ם\rb*, \rb and fashion|וַעֲשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb for yourselves|לָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb a new|חָדָ֖שׁ\rb* \rb heart|לֵ֥ב\rb* \rb and a new|חֲדָשָׁ֑ה\rb* \rb spirit|וְר֣וּחַ\rb*. \rb Why|וְלָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb should you die|תָמֻ֖תוּ\rb*, \rb O house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*?
\p \v 32 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I take no|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb pleasure|אֶחְפֹּץ֙\rb* \rb in anyone’s death|בְּמ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |הַמֵּ֔ת\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb*. \rb So repent|וְהָשִׁ֖יבוּ\rb* \rb and live|וִֽחְיֽוּ׃פ\rb*![’’]
\c 19
\s1 A Lament for the Princes of Israel
\p \v 1 “\rb As for you|וְאַתָּה֙\rb*, \rb take up|שָׂ֣א\rb* \rb a lament|קִינָ֔ה\rb* \rb for|אֶל־\rb* \rb the princes|נְשִׂיאֵ֖י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 2 \rb and say|וְאָמַרְתָּ֗\rb*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\rb What|מָ֤ה\rb* \rb was your mother|אִמְּךָ֙\rb*?
\q2 \rb A lioness|לְבִיָּ֔א\rb* \rb among|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb the lions|אֲרָי֖וֹת\rb*!
\q1 \rb She lay down|רָבָ֑צָה\rb* \rb among|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the young lions|כְּפִרִ֖ים\rb*;
\q2 \rb she reared|רִבְּתָ֥ה\rb* \rb her cubs|גוּרֶֽיהָ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 3 \rb She brought up|וַתַּ֛עַל\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb of her cubs|מִגֻּרֶ֖יהָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and he became|הָיָ֑ה\rb* \rb a young lion|כְּפִ֣יר\rb*.
\q1 \rb After learning|וַיִּלְמַ֥ד\rb* \rb to tear|לִטְרָף־\rb* \rb his prey|טֶ֖רֶף\rb*,
\q2 \rb he devoured|אָכָֽל׃\rb* \rb men|אָדָ֥ם\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb When the nations|גּוֹיִ֖ם\rb* \rb heard|וַיִּשְׁמְע֥וּ\rb* \rb of him|אֵלָ֛יו\rb*,
\q2 \rb he was trapped|נִתְפָּ֑שׂ\rb* \rb in their pit|בְּשַׁחְתָּ֣ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb With hooks|בַֽחַחִ֖ים\rb* \rb they led him away|וַיְבִאֻ֥הוּ\rb*
\q2 \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 5 \rb When she saw|וַתֵּ֙רֶא֙\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb she had waited in vain|נֽוֹחֲלָ֔ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb that her hope|תִּקְוָתָ֑הּ\rb* \rb was lost|אָבְדָ֖ה\rb*,
\q1 \rb she took|וַתִּקַּ֛ח\rb* \rb another|אֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb of her cubs|מִגֻּרֶ֖יהָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and made him|שָׂמָֽתְהוּ׃\rb* \rb a young lion|כְּפִ֥יר\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb He prowled|וַיִּתְהַלֵּ֥ךְ\rb* \rb among|בְּתוֹךְ־\rb* \rb the lions|אֲרָי֖וֹת\rb*,
\q2 \rb and became|הָיָ֑ה\rb* \rb a young lion|כְּפִ֣יר\rb*.
\q1 \rb After learning|וַיִּלְמַ֥ד\rb* \rb to tear|לִטְרָף־\rb* \rb his prey|טֶ֖רֶף\rb*,
\q2 \rb he devoured|אָכָֽל׃\rb* \rb men|אָדָ֥ם\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb He broke down|וַיֵּ֙דַע֙\rb* \rb their strongholds|אַלְמְנוֹתָ֔יו\rb*\f + \fr 19:7 \ft Or \fqa He knew their widows \ft or \fqa He seized their widows\f*
\q2 \rb and devastated|הֶחֱרִ֑יב\rb* \rb their cities|וְעָרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb The land|אֶ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb and everything in it|וּמְלֹאָ֔הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb shuddered|וַתֵּ֤שַׁם\rb* \rb at the sound|מִקּ֖וֹל\rb* \rb of his roaring|שַׁאֲגָתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb Then the nations|גּוֹיִ֛ם\rb* \rb set out|וַיִּתְּנ֨וּ\rb* \rb against him|עָלָ֥יו\rb*
\q2 \rb from the provinces|מִמְּדִינ֑וֹת\rb* \rb on every side|סָבִ֖יב\rb*.
\q1 \rb They spread|וַֽיִּפְרְשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb their net|רִשְׁתָּ֖ם\rb* \rb over him|עָלָ֛יו\rb*;
\q2 \rb he was trapped|נִתְפָּֽשׂ׃\rb* \rb in their pit|בְּשַׁחְתָּ֥ם\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 \rb With hooks|בַּֽחַחִ֔ים\rb* \rb they caged him|וַֽיִּתְּנֻ֤הוּ\rb*\rb |בַסּוּגַר֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and brought him|וַיְבִאֻ֖הוּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֑ל\rb*.
\q1 \rb They brought him|יְבִאֻ֙הוּ֙\rb* \rb into captivity|בַּמְּצֹד֔וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb so that|לְמַ֗עַן\rb* \rb his roar|קוֹל֛וֹ\rb* \rb was heard|יִשָּׁמַ֥ע\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֖וֹד\rb*
\q2 \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the mountains|הָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb Your mother|אִמְּךָ֥\rb* \rb was like a vine|כַגֶּ֛פֶן\rb* \rb in your vineyard|בְּדָמְךָ֖\rb*,\f + \fr 19:10 \ft Some Hebrew manuscripts; most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa in your bloodline\f*
\q2 \rb planted|שְׁתוּלָ֑ה\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the water|מַ֣יִם\rb*;
\q1 \rb it was|הָיְתָ֖ה\rb* \rb fruitful|פֹּֽרִיָּה֙\rb* \rb and full of branches|וַֽעֲנֵפָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb because of the abundant|רַבִּֽים׃\rb* \rb waters|מִמַּ֥יִם\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb It had|וַיִּֽהְיוּ־\rb* \rb strong|עֹ֗ז\rb* \rb branches|מַטּ֣וֹת\rb*, \rb fit for|אֶל־\rb* \rb a ruler’s|מֹֽשְׁלִ֔ים\rb* \rb scepter|שִׁבְטֵי֙\rb*.
\q2 \rb It towered|וַתִּגְבַּ֥הּ\rb* \rb high|קֽוֹמָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb above|עַל־\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb the thick branches|עֲבֹתִ֑ים\rb*,
\q1 \rb conspicuous|וַיֵּרָ֣א\rb* \rb for its height|בְגָבְה֔וֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb and for its dense|בְּרֹ֖ב\rb* \rb foliage|דָּלִיֹּתָֽיו׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 12 \rb But it was uprooted|וַתֻּתַּ֤שׁ\rb* \rb in fury|בְּחֵמָה֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb cast down|הֻשְׁלָ֔כָה\rb* \rb to the ground|לָאָ֣רֶץ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the east|הַקָּדִ֖ים\rb* \rb wind|וְר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb dried up|הוֹבִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb its fruit|פִּרְיָ֑הּ\rb*.
\q1 \rb Its strong|עֻזָּ֖הּ\rb* \rb branches|מַטֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb were stripped off|הִתְפָּרְק֧וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and they withered|וְיָבֵ֛שׁוּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb the fire|אֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb consumed them|אֲכָלָֽתְהוּ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb Now|וְעַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb it is planted|שְׁתוּלָ֣ה\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb*,
\q2 \rb in a dry|צִיָּ֥ה\rb* \rb and thirsty|וְצָמָֽא׃\rb* \rb land|בְּאֶ֖רֶץ\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 \rb Fire|אֵ֜שׁ\rb* \rb has gone out|וַתֵּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb from its main branch|מִמַּטֵּ֤ה\rb*\rb |בַדֶּ֙יהָ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and devoured|אָכָ֔לָה\rb* \rb its fruit|פִּרְיָ֣הּ\rb*;
\q1 \rb on it|בָ֛הּ\rb* \rb no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb strong|עֹ֖ז\rb* \rb branch|מַטֵּה־\rb* \rb remains|הָ֥יָה\rb*
\q2 \rb fit for a ruler’s|לִמְשׁ֑וֹל\rb* \rb scepter|שֵׁ֣בֶט\rb*.’
\p \rb This|הִ֖יא\rb* \rb is a lament|קִ֥ינָה\rb* \rb and shall be used|וַתְּהִ֥י\rb* \rb as a lament|לְקִינָֽה׃פ\rb*.”
\c 20
\s1 Israel’s Rebellion in Egypt
\p \v 1 \rb |וַיְהִ֣י׀\rb* \rb In the seventh|הַשְּׁבִיעִ֗ית\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָ֣ה\rb*, \rb on the tenth|בֶּעָשׂ֣וֹר\rb* \rb day|לַחֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the fifth month|בַּֽחֲמִשִׁי֙\rb*, \rb some of the elders|מִזִּקְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb came|בָּ֧אוּ\rb*\rb |אֲנָשִׁ֛ים\rb* \rb to inquire|לִדְרֹ֣שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and they sat down|וַיֵּשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb before me|לְפָנָֽי׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 3 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb speak|דַּבֵּ֞ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the elders|זִקְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: \rb Have you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb come|בָּאִ֑ים\rb* \rb to inquire|הֲלִדְרֹ֥שׁ\rb* \rb of Me|אֹתִ֖י\rb*? \rb As surely as|אָ֙נִי֙\rb* \rb I live|חַי־\rb*, \rb I will not|אִם־\rb* \rb be consulted|אִדָּרֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb by you|לָכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Will you judge|הֲתִשְׁפֹּ֣ט\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֔ם\rb*, \rb will you judge them|הֲתִשְׁפּ֖וֹט\rb*, \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֑ם\rb*?\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Confront them with|הוֹדִיעֵֽם׃\rb* \rb the abominations|תּוֹעֲבֹ֥ת\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \v 5 \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִה֒\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֮\rb*: \rb On the day|בְּיוֹם֙\rb* \rb I chose|בָּחֳרִ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|בְיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb I swore an oath|וָאֶשָּׂ֣א\rb*\rb |יָדִ֗י\rb* \rb to the descendants|לְזֶ֙רַע֙\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Jacob|יַֽעֲקֹ֔ב\rb* \rb and made Myself known|וָאִוָּדַ֥ע\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*. \rb With an uplifted|וָאֶשָּׂ֨א\rb* \rb hand|יָדִ֤י\rb* \rb I said|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶם֙\rb*, ‘\rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.’
\p \v 6 \rb On that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb I swore|נָשָׂ֤אתִי\rb*\rb |יָדִי֙\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to bring them|לְהֽוֹצִיאָ֖ם\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֜רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I had searched out|תַּ֣רְתִּי\rb* \rb for them|לָהֶ֗ם\rb*, \rb a land flowing|זָבַ֤ת\rb* \rb with milk|חָלָב֙\rb* \rb and honey|וּדְבַ֔שׁ\rb*, \rb the glory|צְבִ֥י\rb*\rb |הִ֖יא\rb* \rb of all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb lands|הָאֲרָצֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb And I said|וָאֹמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵהֶ֗ם\rb*: ‘\rb Each of you|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb must throw away|הַשְׁלִ֔יכוּ\rb* \rb the abominations|שִׁקּוּצֵ֤י\rb* \rb before his eyes|עֵינָיו֙\rb*, \rb and you must not|אַל־\rb* \rb defile yourselves|תִּטַּמָּ֑אוּ\rb* \rb with the idols|וּבְגִלּוּלֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.’
\p \v 8 \rb But they rebelled|וַיַּמְרוּ־\rb* \rb against Me|בִ֗י\rb* \rb and refused|וְלֹ֤א\rb*\rb |אָבוּ֙\rb* \rb to listen|לִּשְׁמֹ֣עַ\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֔י\rb*. \rb None of them|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb cast away|הִשְׁלִ֔יכוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the abominations|שִׁקּוּצֵ֤י\rb* \rb before their eyes|עֵֽינֵיהֶם֙\rb*, \rb and they did not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb forsake|עָזָ֑בוּ\rb* \rb the idols|גִּלּוּלֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb*. \rb So I resolved|וָאֹמַ֞ר\rb* \rb to pour out|לִשְׁפֹּ֧ךְ\rb* \rb My wrath|חֲמָתִ֣י\rb* \rb upon them|עֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and vent|לְכַלּ֤וֹת\rb* \rb My anger|אַפִּי֙\rb* \rb against them|בָּהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb in|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb But I acted|וָאַ֙עַשׂ֙\rb* \rb for the sake|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb of My name|שְׁמִ֔י\rb*, \rb that it should not|לְבִלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb be profaned|הֵחֵ֛ל\rb* \rb in the eyes|לְעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb* \rb among whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they were living|הֵ֣מָּה\rb*\rb |בְתוֹכָ֑ם\rb*, \rb in whose|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb sight|לְעֵ֣ינֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb I had revealed Myself|נוֹדַ֤עְתִּי\rb* \rb to Israel|אֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb by bringing them|לְהוֹצִיאָ֖ם\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*.
\s1 Israel’s Rebellion in the Wilderness
\p \v 10 \rb So I brought them|וָאֽוֹצִיאֵ֖ם\rb* \rb out of the land|מֵאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and led them|וָאֲבִאֵ֖ם\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the wilderness|הַמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb And I gave|וָאֶתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb them|לָהֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My statutes|חֻקּוֹתַ֔י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and made known|הוֹדַ֣עְתִּי\rb* \rb to them|אוֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb My ordinances|מִשְׁפָּטַ֖י\rb*— \rb for the man|הָאָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb does these things|יַעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb will live|וָחַ֥י\rb* \rb by them|בָּהֶֽם׃\rb*.\f + \fr 20:11 \ft See \ref Leviticus 18:5|LEV 18:5\ref*; also in Ezekiel 20:13 and 21.\f* \v 12 \rb I also|וְגַ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb gave|נָתַ֣תִּי\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb My Sabbaths|שַׁבְּתוֹתַי֙\rb*\rb |לִהְי֣וֹת\rb* \rb as a sign|לְא֔וֹת\rb* \rb between us|בֵּינִ֖י\rb*\rb |וּבֵֽינֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb so that they would know|לָדַ֕עַת\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb who sanctifies them|מְקַדְּשָֽׁם׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Yet the house|בֵֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb rebelled|וַיַּמְרוּ־\rb* \rb against Me|בִ֨י\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֗ר\rb*. \rb They did not|לֹא־\rb* \rb follow|הָלָ֜כוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb My statutes|בְּחֻקּוֹתַ֨י\rb* \rb and they rejected|מָאָ֗סוּ\rb* \rb My ordinances|מִשְׁפָּטַ֣י\rb*— \rb though the man|הָֽאָדָם֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb does these things|יַעֲשֶׂ֨ה\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֤ם\rb* \rb will live|וָחַ֣י\rb* \rb by them|בָּהֶ֔ם\rb* — \rb and they|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb utterly|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb profaned|חִלְּל֣וּ\rb* \rb My Sabbaths|שַׁבְּתֹתַ֖י\rb*. \rb Then I resolved|וָאֹמַ֞ר\rb* \rb to pour|לִשְׁפֹּ֨ךְ\rb* \rb out My wrath|חֲמָתִ֧י\rb* \rb upon them|עֲלֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb and put an end to them|לְכַלּוֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֖ר\rb*. \v 14 \rb But I acted|וָאֶעֱשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb for the sake|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb of My name|שְׁמִ֑י\rb*, \rb so that it would not|לְבִלְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb be profaned|הֵחֵל֙\rb* \rb in the eyes|לְעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb in whose|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb sight|לְעֵינֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb I had brought them out|הוֹצֵאתִ֖ים\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb Moreover|וְגַם־\rb*, \rb with an uplifted hand|יָדִ֛י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb swore|נָשָׂ֧אתִי\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb* \rb that I would not|לְבִלְתִּי֩\rb* \rb bring|הָבִ֨יא\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֜ם\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I had given them|נָתַ֗תִּי\rb*— \rb a land flowing|זָבַ֤ת\rb* \rb with milk|חָלָב֙\rb* \rb and honey|וּדְבַ֔שׁ\rb*, \rb the glory|צְבִ֥י\rb*\rb |הִ֖יא\rb* \rb of all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb lands|הָאֲרָצֽוֹת׃\rb* — \v 16 \rb because|יַ֜עַן\rb* \rb they kept rejecting|מָאָ֗סוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb My ordinances|בְּמִשְׁפָּטַ֣י\rb*, \rb refusing|לֹא־\rb* \rb to walk|הָלְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb in|בָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb My statutes|חֻקּוֹתַי֙\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb profaning|חִלֵּ֑לוּ\rb* \rb My Sabbaths|שַׁבְּתוֹתַ֖י\rb*; \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb their hearts|לִבָּ֥ם\rb* \rb continually went|הֹלֵֽךְ׃\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb their idols|גִלּוּלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*. \v 17 \rb Yet I looked on them with pity|וַתָּ֧חָס\rb*\rb |עֵינִ֛י\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and did not destroy them|מִֽשַּׁחֲתָ֑ם\rb* \rb or|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb bring|עָשִׂ֧יתִי\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb to an end|כָּלָ֖ה\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb In the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֔ר\rb* \rb I said|וָאֹמַ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb their children|בְּנֵיהֶם֙\rb*: ‘\rb Do not|אַל־\rb* \rb walk|תֵּלֵ֔כוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb in the statutes|בְּחוּקֵּ֤י\rb* \rb of your fathers|אֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb or keep|תִּשְׁמֹ֑רוּ\rb* \rb their ordinances|מִשְׁפְּטֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אַל־\rb* \rb or defile|תִּטַּמָּֽאוּ׃\rb* \rb yourselves with their idols|וּבְגִלּוּלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אַל־\rb*. \v 19 \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*; \rb walk|לֵ֑כוּ\rb* \rb in My statutes|בְּחֻקּוֹתַ֖י\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb keep|שִׁמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb My ordinances|מִשְׁפָּטַ֥י\rb*, \rb and practice them|וַעֲשׂ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אוֹתָֽם׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb Keep My Sabbaths|שַׁבְּתוֹתַ֖י\rb* \rb holy|קַדֵּ֑שׁוּ\rb*, \rb that they may be|וְהָי֤וּ\rb* \rb a sign|לְאוֹת֙\rb* \rb between us|בֵּינִ֣י\rb*\rb |וּבֵֽינֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb so that you may know|לָדַ֕עַת\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb your God|אֱלֹהֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.’
\p \v 21 \rb But the children|הַבָּנִ֗ים\rb* \rb rebelled|וַיַּמְרוּ־\rb* \rb against Me|בִ֣י\rb*. \rb They did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb walk|הָ֠לָכוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb in My statutes|בְּחֻקּוֹתַ֣י\rb* \rb or carefully|שָׁמְר֜וּ\rb* \rb observe|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֗ם\rb* \rb My ordinances|מִשְׁפָּטַ֨י\rb*\rb |לֹא־\rb* — \rb though the man|הָֽאָדָם֙\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb does these things|יַעֲשֶׂ֨ה\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֤ם\rb* \rb will live|וָחַ֣י\rb* \rb by them|בָּהֶ֔ם\rb* —\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and they profaned|חִלֵּ֑לוּ\rb* \rb My Sabbaths|שַׁבְּתוֹתַ֖י\rb*. \rb So I resolved|וָאֹמַ֞ר\rb* \rb to pour|לִשְׁפֹּ֧ךְ\rb* \rb out My wrath|חֲמָתִ֣י\rb* \rb upon them|עֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and vent|לְכַלּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb My anger|אַפִּ֛י\rb* \rb against them|בָּ֖ם\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּֽר׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb But I withheld|וַהֲשִׁבֹ֙תִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My hand|יָדִ֔י\rb* \rb and acted|וָאַ֖עַשׂ\rb* \rb for the sake|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb of My name|שְׁמִ֑י\rb*, \rb so that it would not|לְבִלְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb be profaned|הֵחֵל֙\rb* \rb in the eyes|לְעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb in whose|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb sight|לְעֵינֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb I had brought them out|הוֹצֵ֥אתִי\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb However|גַּם־\rb*,\rb |אֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb with an uplifted hand I swore|נָשָׂ֧אתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |יָדִ֛י\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַּמִּדְבָּ֑ר\rb* \rb that I would scatter|לְהָפִ֤יץ\rb* \rb them|אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb and disperse|וּלְזָר֥וֹת\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb throughout the lands|בָּאֲרָצֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb For|יַ֜עַן\rb* \rb they did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb practice|עָשׂוּ֙\rb* \rb My ordinances|מִשְׁפָּטַ֤י\rb*, \rb but they rejected|מָאָ֔סוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb My statutes|וְחֻקּוֹתַ֣י\rb* \rb and profaned|חִלֵּ֑לוּ\rb*\rb |וְאַחֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb My Sabbaths|שַׁבְּתוֹתַ֖י\rb*, \rb fixing|הָי֖וּ\rb* \rb their eyes|עֵינֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb on the idols|גִּלּוּלֵ֣י\rb* \rb of their fathers|אֲבוֹתָ֔ם\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb also|וְגַם־\rb* \rb gave them|נָתַ֣תִּי\rb* \rb over|לָהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to statutes|חֻקִּ֖ים\rb* \rb that were not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb good|טוֹבִ֑ים\rb* \rb and ordinances|וּמִ֨שְׁפָּטִ֔ים\rb* \rb by which|בָּהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb they could not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb live|יִֽחְי֖וּ\rb*. \v 26 \rb And I pronounced them unclean|וָאֲטַמֵּ֤א\rb*\rb |אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb through their gifts|בְּמַתְּנוֹתָ֔ם\rb* — \rb the sacrifice|בְּהַעֲבִ֖יר\rb* \rb of every|כָּל־\rb* \rb firstborn in the fire|פֶּ֣טֶר\rb*\rb |רָ֑חַם\rb* — \rb so that|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb I might devastate them|אֲשִׁמֵּ֔ם\rb*, \rb in order|לְמַ֙עַן֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they would know|יֵֽדְע֔וּ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\s1 Israel’s Rebellion in the Land
\p \v 27 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֞ן\rb*, \rb son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֔ם\rb*, \rb speak|דַּבֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֤ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*, \rb and tell them that|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb*\rb |אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*: \rb In this way|זֹ֚את\rb* \rb also|ע֗וֹד\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲב֣וֹתֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb blasphemed|גִּדְּפ֤וּ\rb* \rb Me|אוֹתִי֙\rb* \rb by their unfaithfulness|מָֽעַל׃\rb* \rb against|בְּמַעֲלָ֥ם\rb* \rb Me|בִּ֖י\rb*. \v 28 \rb When I brought them|וָאֲבִיאֵם֙\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I swore|נָשָׂ֙אתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |יָדִ֔י\rb* \rb to give|לָתֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb them|לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and they saw|וַיִּרְאוּ֩\rb* \rb any|כָל־\rb* \rb high|רָמָ֜ה\rb*\rb |וְכָל־\rb* \rb hill|גִּבְעָ֨ה\rb* \rb or leafy|עָבֹ֗ת\rb* \rb tree|עֵ֣ץ\rb*, \rb there|שָׁ֤ם\rb* \rb they offered|וַיִּזְבְּחוּ־\rb* \rb their sacrifices|זִבְחֵיהֶם֙\rb*, \rb presented|וַיִּתְּנוּ־\rb*\rb |שָׁם֙\rb* \rb offerings|קָרְבָּנָ֔ם\rb* \rb that provoked Me|כַּ֣עַס\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sent up|וַיָּשִׂ֣ימוּ\rb*\rb |שָׁ֗ם\rb* \rb their fragrant|נִיח֣וֹחֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb incense|רֵ֚יחַ\rb*, \rb and poured out|וַיַּסִּ֥יכוּ\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their drink offerings|נִסְכֵּיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 29 \rb So I asked them|וָאֹמַ֣ר\rb*:\rb |אֲלֵהֶ֔ם\rb* ‘\rb What|מָ֣ה\rb* \rb is this high place|הַבָּמָ֔ה\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb go|הַבָּאִ֖ים\rb*?’
\p (\rb And to|עַ֖ד\rb* \rb this|הַזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*\rb |שָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb it is called|וַיִּקָּרֵ֤א\rb*\rb |שְׁמָהּ֙\rb* \rb Bamah|בָּמָ֔ה\rb*.\f + \fr 20:29 \fqa Bamah \ft means \fqa high place\ft .\f*)
\p \v 30 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֞ן\rb* \rb tell|אֱמֹ֣ר׀\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: \rb Will you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb defile yourselves|נִטְמְאִ֑ים\rb* \rb the way|הַבְּדֶ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb your fathers did|אֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb prostituting|זֹנִֽים׃\rb* \rb yourselves|אַתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb with|וְאַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb their abominations|שִׁקּוּצֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*? \v 31 \rb When you offer|וּבִשְׂאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb your gifts|מַתְּנֹֽתֵיכֶ֡ם\rb*, \rb sacrificing your sons|בְּנֵיכֶ֨ם\rb*\rb |בְּֽהַעֲבִיר֩\rb* \rb in the fire|בָּאֵ֜שׁ\rb*,\f + \fr 20:31 \ft Literally \fqa making your sons pass through the fire\f* \rb you|אַתֶּם֩\rb* \rb continue to defile|נִטְמְאִ֤֨ים\rb* \rb yourselves with all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb your idols|גִּלּֽוּלֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb this day|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb*. \rb So should I|וַאֲנִ֛י\rb* \rb be consulted|אִדָּרֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb by you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb O house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*? \rb As surely as|אָ֗נִי\rb* \rb I live|חַי־\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם֙\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb*, \rb I will not|אִם־\rb* \rb be consulted|אִדָּרֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb by you|לָכֶֽם׃\rb*!
\p \v 32 \rb When|אֲשֶׁ֣ר׀\rb* \rb you|אַתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb say|אֹמְרִ֗ים\rb*, ‘\rb Let us be|נִֽהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb like the nations|כַגּוֹיִם֙\rb*, \rb like the peoples|כְּמִשְׁפְּח֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the lands|הָאֲרָצ֔וֹת\rb*, \rb serving|לְשָׁרֵ֖ת\rb* \rb wood|עֵ֥ץ\rb* \rb and stone|וָאָֽבֶן׃\rb*,’\rb |וְהָֽעֹלָה֙\rb* \rb what you have in|עַל־\rb* \rb mind|ר֣וּחֲכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb will never|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb come to pass|תִֽהְיֶ֑ה\rb*.
\s1 Judgment and Restoration
\p \v 33 \rb As surely as|אָ֕נִי\rb* \rb I live|חַי־\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb*,\rb |אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹ֠א\rb* \rb with a strong|חֲזָקָ֜ה\rb* \rb hand|בְּיָ֨ד\rb*, \rb an outstretched|נְטוּיָ֛ה\rb* \rb arm|וּבִזְר֧וֹעַ\rb*, \rb and outpoured|שְׁפוּכָ֖ה\rb* \rb wrath|וּבְחֵמָ֥ה\rb* \rb I will rule|אֶמְל֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb over you|עֲלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 34 \rb With a strong|חֲזָקָה֙\rb* \rb hand|בְּיָ֤ד\rb*, \rb an outstretched|נְטוּיָ֔ה\rb* \rb arm|וּבִזְר֣וֹעַ\rb*, \rb and outpoured|שְׁפוּכָֽה׃\rb* \rb wrath|וּבְחֵמָ֖ה\rb* \rb I will bring|וְהוֹצֵאתִ֤י\rb* \rb you out|אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the peoples|הָ֣עַמִּ֔ים\rb* \rb and gather|וְקִבַּצְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb*\f + \fr 20:34 \ft LXX \fqa receive you\ft ; see also \ref 2 Corinthians 6:17|2CO 6:17\ref*.\f* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the lands|הָ֣אֲרָצ֔וֹת\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have been scattered|נְפוֹצֹתֶ֖ם\rb*. \v 35 \rb And I will bring|וְהֵבֵאתִ֣י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the wilderness|מִדְבַּ֖ר\rb* \rb of the nations|הָֽעַמִּ֑ים\rb*, \rb where|שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb I will enter into judgment|וְנִשְׁפַּטְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb with you|אִתְּכֶם֙\rb* \rb face|פָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb face|פָּנִֽים׃\rb*.
\p \v 36 \rb Just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I entered into judgment|נִשְׁפַּ֙טְתִּי֙\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲב֣וֹתֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בְּמִדְבַּ֖ר\rb* \rb of the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*,\f + \fr 20:36 \ft Or \fqa in the wilderness after bringing them out of Egypt\f* \rb so|כֵּ֚ן\rb* \rb I will enter into judgment|אִשָּׁפֵ֣ט\rb* \rb with you|אִתְּכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*. \v 37 \rb I will make you pass|וְהַעֲבַרְתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb the rod|הַשָּׁ֑בֶט\rb* \rb and will bring|וְהֵבֵאתִ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb you into the bond|בְּמָסֹ֥רֶת\rb* \rb of the covenant|הַבְּרִֽית׃\rb*. \v 38 \rb And I will purge you|וּבָרוֹתִ֣י\rb* \rb of|מִכֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb those who rebel|הַמֹּרְדִ֤ים\rb* \rb and transgress|וְהַפּֽוֹשְׁעִים֙\rb* \rb against Me|בִּ֔י\rb*. \rb I will bring them out|אוֹצִ֣יא\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb of the land|מֵאֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb in which they dwell|מְגֽוּרֵיהֶם֙\rb*, \rb but they will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb enter|וְאֶל־\rb*\rb |יָב֑וֹא\rb* \rb the land|אַדְמַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*. \rb Then you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 39 \rb And as for you|וְאַתֶּ֨ם\rb*, \rb O house|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb*, \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהֹוִ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר׀\rb*: \rb Go|לְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb and serve|עֲבֹ֔דוּ\rb* \rb your idols|גִּלּוּלָיו֙\rb*, \rb every one of you|אִ֤ישׁ\rb*. \rb But afterward|וְאַחַ֕ר\rb*, \rb you will surely|אִם־\rb*\rb |אֵינְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb listen|שֹׁמְעִ֣ים\rb* \rb to Me|אֵלָ֑י\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and you will no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb longer|ע֔וֹד\rb* \rb defile|תְחַלְּלוּ־\rb* \rb My holy|קָדְשִׁי֙\rb* \rb name|שֵׁ֤ם\rb* \rb with your gifts|בְּמַתְּנֽוֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and idols|וּבְגִלּוּלֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 40 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb on My holy|קָדְשִׁ֞י\rb* \rb mountain|בְהַר־\rb*, \rb the high|מְר֣וֹם\rb* \rb mountain|בְּהַ֣ר׀\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם֙\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb*, \rb there|שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֧ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb*, \rb all of them|כֻּלֹּ֖ה\rb*, \rb will serve Me|יַעַבְדֻ֜נִי\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֑רֶץ\rb*. \rb There|שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb I will accept|אֶרְצֵ֔ם\rb* \rb them|וְשָׁ֞ם\rb* \rb and will require|אֶדְר֣וֹשׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your offerings|תְּרוּמֹֽתֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and choice|רֵאשִׁ֛ית\rb* \rb gifts|מַשְׂאוֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb along with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb your holy sacrifices|קָדְשֵׁיכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 41 \rb When I bring|בְּהוֹצִיאִ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb you from|מִן־\rb* \rb the peoples|הָ֣עַמִּ֔ים\rb* \rb and gather|וְקִבַּצְתִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb you from|מִן־\rb* \rb the lands|הָ֣אֲרָצ֔וֹת\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have been scattered|נְפֹצֹתֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb I will accept|אֶרְצֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶם֒\rb* \rb you as a pleasing|נִיחֹחַ֮\rb* \rb aroma|בְּרֵ֣יחַ\rb*. \rb And I will show My holiness|וְנִקְדַּשְׁתִּ֥י\rb* \rb through you|בָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in the sight|לְעֵינֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִֽם׃\rb*. \v 42 \rb Then you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּם֙\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb when I bring|בַּהֲבִיאִ֥י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אַדְמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*,\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I swore|נָשָׂ֙אתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |יָדִ֔י\rb* \rb to give|לָתֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb your fathers|לַאֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 43 \rb There|שָׁ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb you will remember|וּזְכַרְתֶּם־\rb* \rb your ways|דַּרְכֵיכֶם֙\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the deeds|עֲלִיל֣וֹתֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb with which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have defiled yourselves|נִטְמֵאתֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb and you will loathe|וּנְקֹֽטֹתֶם֙\rb* \rb yourselves|בִּפְנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb for all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the evils|רָעוֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have done|עֲשִׂיתֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 44 \rb Then you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּם֙\rb*, \rb O house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb when I have dealt|בַּעֲשׂוֹתִ֥י\rb* \rb with you|אִתְּכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb for the sake|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb of My name|שְׁמִ֑י\rb* \rb and not according to|לֹא֩\rb* \rb your wicked|הָרָעִ֜ים\rb* \rb ways|כְדַרְכֵיכֶ֨ם\rb* \rb and corrupt|הַנִּשְׁחָתוֹת֙\rb* \rb acts|וְכַעֲלִילֽוֹתֵיכֶ֤ם\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃פ\rb*.”
\s1 A Prophecy against the South
\p \v 45 \rb Now the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 46 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb set|שִׂ֤ים\rb* \rb your face|פָּנֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb toward|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb the south|תֵּימָ֔נָה\rb*,\f + \fr 20:46 \ft Hebrew \fqa toward Teman\f* \rb preach|וְהַטֵּ֖ף\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb it|דָּר֑וֹם\rb*, \rb and prophesy|וְהִנָּבֵ֛א\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the forest|יַ֥עַר\rb*\rb |הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb of the Negev|נֶֽגֶב׃\rb*. \v 47 \rb Say|וְאָֽמַרְתָּ֙\rb* \rb to the forest|לְיַ֣עַר\rb* \rb of the Negev|הַנֶּ֔גֶב\rb*: \rb Hear|שְׁמַ֖ע\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*! \rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֡ה\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֣י\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: \rb I am about to ignite|מַֽצִּית־\rb* \rb in you|בְּךָ֣׀\rb* \rb a fire|אֵ֡שׁ\rb*, \rb and it will devour|וְאָכְלָ֣ה\rb* \rb all|כָל־\rb* \rb your|בְךָ֣\rb* \rb trees|עֵֽץ־\rb*, \rb both green|לַח֩\rb* \rb and|וְכָל־\rb* \rb dry|יָבֵ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |עֵ֨ץ\rb*. \rb The blazing|שַׁלְהֶ֔בֶת\rb* \rb flame|לַהֶ֣בֶת\rb* \rb will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb be quenched|תִכְבֶּה֙\rb*, \rb and by it|בָ֥הּ\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb face|פָּנִ֖ים\rb* \rb from south|מִנֶּ֥גֶב\rb* \rb to north|צָפֽוֹנָה׃\rb* \rb will be scorched|וְנִצְרְבוּ־\rb*. \v 48 \rb Then all|כָּל־\rb* \rb people|בָּשָׂ֔ר\rb* \rb will see|וְרָאוּ֙\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb have kindled it|בִּֽעַרְתִּ֑יהָ\rb*; \rb it will not|לֹ֖א\rb* \rb be quenched|תִּכְבֶּֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 49 \rb Then I said|וָאֹמַ֕ר\rb*, “\rb Ah|אֲהָ֖הּ\rb*, \rb Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb*, \rb they|הֵ֚מָּה\rb* \rb are saying|אֹמְרִ֣ים\rb* \rb of me|לִ֔י\rb*, ‘\rb Is he|הֽוּא׃פ\rb* \rb not|הֲלֹ֛א\rb* \rb just telling|מְמַשֵּׁ֥ל\rb* \rb parables|מְשָׁלִ֖ים\rb*?’”
\c 21
\s1 God’s Sword of Judgment
\p \v 1 \rb And the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb set|שִׂ֤ים\rb* \rb your face|פָּנֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb* \rb and preach|וְהַטֵּ֖ף\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the sanctuaries|מִקְדָּשִׁ֑ים\rb*. \rb Prophesy|וְהִנָּבֵ֖א\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אַדְמַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \v 3 \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֞\rb*\rb |לְאַדְמַ֣ת\rb* \rb her|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֣י\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: ‘\rb I am against you|אֵלַ֔יִךְ\rb*, \rb and I will draw|וְהוֹצֵאתִ֥י\rb* \rb My sword|חַרְבִּ֖י\rb* \rb from its sheath|מִתַּעְרָ֑הּ\rb* \rb and cut off|וְהִכְרַתִּ֥י\rb* \rb from you|מִמֵּ֖ךְ\rb* \rb both the righteous|צַדִּ֥יק\rb* \rb and the wicked|וְרָשָֽׁע׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb Because|יַ֛עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I will cut off|הִכְרַ֥תִּי\rb* \rb both the righteous|צַדִּ֣יק\rb* \rb and the wicked|וְרָשָׁ֑ע\rb*, \rb My sword|חַרְבִּ֧י\rb*\rb |לָ֠כֵן\rb* \rb will be|תֵּצֵ֨א\rb* \rb unsheathed|מִתַּעְרָ֛הּ\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb everyone|כָּל־\rb*\rb |בָּשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb from south|מִנֶּ֥גֶב\rb* \rb to north|צָפֽוֹן׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb Then all|כָּל־\rb* \rb flesh|בָּשָׂ֔ר\rb* \rb will know|וְיָֽדְעוּ֙\rb* \rb that|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb have taken|הוֹצֵ֥אתִי\rb* \rb My sword|חַרְבִּ֖י\rb* \rb from its sheath|מִתַּעְרָ֑הּ\rb*, \rb not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb to return it|תָשׁ֖וּב\rb* \rb again|עֽוֹד׃ס\rb*.’
\p \v 6 \rb But you|וְאַתָּ֥ה\rb*, \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֖ם\rb*, \rb groan|הֵֽאָנַ֑ח\rb*! \rb Groan|תֵּֽאָנַ֖ח\rb* \rb before their eyes|לְעֵינֵיהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb with a broken|בְּשִׁבְר֤וֹן\rb* \rb heart|מָתְנַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb and bitter grief|וּבִמְרִיר֔וּת\rb*. \v 7 \rb And|וְהָיָה֙\rb* \rb when|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they ask|יֹאמְר֣וּ\rb*, ‘\rb Why|עַל־\rb*\rb |מָ֖ה\rb* \rb are you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb groaning|נֶאֱנָ֑ח\rb*?’ \rb you are to say|וְאָמַרְתָּ֡\rb*, ‘\rb Because of|אֶל־\rb* \rb the news|שְׁמוּעָ֣ה\rb* \rb that|כִֽי־\rb* \rb is coming|בָאָ֡ה\rb*. \rb Every|כָּל־\rb* \rb heart|לֵב֩\rb* \rb will melt|וְנָמֵ֣ס\rb*, \rb and every|כָל־\rb* \rb hand|יָדַ֜יִם\rb* \rb will go limp|וְרָפ֨וּ\rb*. \rb Every|כָל־\rb* \rb spirit|ר֗וּחַ\rb* \rb will faint|וְכִהֲתָ֣ה\rb*, \rb and every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb knee|בִּרְכַּ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb will turn to|תֵּלַ֣כְנָה\rb* \rb water|מַּ֔יִם\rb*.’ \rb Yes|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb*, \rb it is coming|בָאָה֙\rb* \rb and it will surely happen|וְנִֽהְיָ֔תָה\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃פ\rb*.”
\p \v 8 \rb Again the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 9 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*, \rb prophesy|הִנָּבֵא֙\rb* \rb and tell them|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֖ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֑י\rb*\rb |אֱמֹ֕ר\rb* \rb says|וְאָ֣מַרְתָּ֔\rb*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\rb A sword|חֶ֥רֶב\rb*, \rb a sword|חֶ֛רֶב\rb*,
\q2 \rb sharpened|הוּחַ֖דָּה\rb* \rb and|וְגַם־\rb* \rb polished|מְרוּטָֽה׃\rb* —
\q1 \v 10 \rb it is sharpened|הוּחַ֔דָּה\rb*\rb |לְמַעַן־\rb*\rb |הֱיֵה־\rb* \rb for|לְמַ֨עַן\rb* \rb the slaughter|טֶ֙בַח֙\rb*\rb |טְבֹ֤חַ\rb*,
\q2 \rb polished|מֹרָ֑טָּה\rb*\rb |א֣וֹ\rb* \rb to flash like lightning|בָּ֖רָק\rb*!
\q1 \rb Should we rejoice|נָשִׂ֔ישׂ\rb* \rb in the scepter|שֵׁ֥בֶט\rb* \rb of My son|בְּנִ֖י\rb*?
\q2 \rb The sword despises|מֹאֶ֥סֶת\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb such stick|עֵֽץ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb The sword|חֶ֙רֶב֙\rb* \rb is appointed|וַיִּתֵּ֥ן\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֛הּ\rb* \rb to be polished|לְמָרְטָ֖ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb to be grasped|לִתְפֹּ֣שׂ\rb* \rb in the hand|בַּכָּ֑ף\rb*.
\q1 \rb It|הִֽיא־\rb* \rb is sharpened|הוּחַ֤דָּה\rb* \rb and|וְהִ֣יא\rb* \rb polished|מֹרָ֔טָּה\rb*,
\q2 \rb to be placed|לָתֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb in the hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of the slayer|הוֹרֵֽג׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 12 \rb Cry out|זְעַ֤ק\rb* \rb and wail|וְהֵילֵל֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb O son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֔ם\rb*,
\q1 \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb the sword|הִיא֙\rb* \rb is wielded|הָיתָ֣ה\rb* \rb against My people|בְעַמִּ֔י\rb*;
\q2 \rb it|הִ֖יא\rb* \rb is against all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the princes|נְשִׂיאֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*!
\q1 \rb They are|הָי֣וּ\rb* \rb tossed|מְגוּרֵ֤י\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the sword|חֶ֙רֶב֙\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֔י\rb*;
\q2 \rb therefore|לָכֵ֖ן\rb* \rb strike|סְפֹ֥ק\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb your thigh|יָרֵֽךְ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 21:12 \ft Or \fqa beat your breast\f*
\q1 \v 13 \rb Surely|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb testing will come|בֹ֔חַן\rb*!
\q2 \rb And what|וּמָ֕ה\rb* \rb if|אִם־\rb* \rb even|גַּם־\rb* \rb the scepter|שֵׁ֥בֶט\rb*,
\q1 \rb which the sword despises|מֹאֶ֖סֶת\rb*,
\q2 \rb does not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb continue|יִֽהְיֶ֑ה\rb*?’
\qr \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃פ\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 ‘\rb So then|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֔ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb prophesy|הִנָּבֵ֕א\rb* \rb and strike|וְהַ֖ךְ\rb* \rb your hands together|כַּ֣ף\rb*.\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |כָּ֑ף\rb*
\q1 \rb Let the sword|חֶ֤רֶב\rb* \rb strike two times|וְתִכָּפֵ֞ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb even three|שְׁלִישִׁ֙תָה֙\rb*.
\q1 \rb It|הִ֗יא\rb* \rb is a sword|חֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb that slays|חֲלָלִ֔ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb a sword|חֶ֚רֶב\rb* \rb of great|הַגָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb slaughter|חָלָ֣ל\rb*
\q2 \rb closing in on every side|הַחֹדֶ֖רֶת\rb*\rb |לָהֶֽם׃\rb*!
\b 
\q1 \v 15 \rb So that|לְמַ֣עַן׀\rb* \rb their hearts|לֵ֗ב\rb* \rb may melt|לָמ֣וּג\rb*
\q2 \rb and many|וְהַרְבֵּה֙\rb* \rb may stumble|הַמִּכְשֹׁלִ֔ים\rb*,
\q1 \rb I have appointed|נָתַ֖תִּי\rb* \rb at|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb their gates|שַׁ֣עֲרֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*
\q2 \rb a sword|חָ֑רֶב\rb* \rb for slaughter|אִבְחַת־\rb*.
\q1 \rb Yes|אָ֛ח\rb*, \rb it is ready|עֲשׂוּיָ֥ה\rb* \rb to flash like lightning|לְבָרָ֖ק\rb*;
\q2 \rb it is drawn|מְעֻטָּ֥ה\rb* \rb for slaughter|לְטָֽבַח׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 16 \rb Slash|הִתְאַחֲדִ֥י\rb* \rb to the right|הֵימִ֖נִי\rb*;
\q2 \rb set your blade|הָשִׂ֣ימִי\rb* \rb to the left|הַשְׂמִ֑ילִי\rb*—
\q2 \rb wherever|אָ֖נָה\rb* \rb your blade|פָּנַ֥יִךְ\rb* \rb is directed|מֻעָדֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 17 \rb I|אֲנִ֗י\rb* \rb too|וְגַם־\rb* \rb will strike|אַכֶּ֤ה\rb* \rb My hands together|כַפִּי֙\rb*,\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |כַּפִּ֔י\rb*
\q2 \rb and I will satisfy|וַהֲנִחֹתִ֖י\rb* \rb My wrath|חֲמָתִ֑י\rb*.’
\qr \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb have spoken|דִּבַּֽרְתִּי׃פ\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 19 “\rb Now you|וְאַתָּ֨ה\rb*, \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֜ם\rb*, \rb mark out|שִׂים־\rb* \rb two|שְׁנַ֣יִם\rb* \rb roads|דְּרָכִ֗ים\rb* \rb for the sword|חֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb* \rb to take|לָבוֹא֙\rb*, \rb both|שְׁנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb starting|יֵצְא֣וּ\rb* \rb from the same|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb land|מֵאֶ֥רֶץ\rb*. \rb And make|בָּרֵ֔א\rb* \rb a signpost|וְיָ֣ד\rb* \rb where the road|דֶּֽרֶךְ־\rb* \rb branches off|בְּרֹ֥אשׁ\rb* \rb to each city|עִ֖יר\rb*\rb |בָּרֵֽא׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb Mark out|תָּשִׂ֔ים\rb* \rb one road|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb for the sword|חֶ֔רֶב\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb to come|לָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb against Rabbah|רַבַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the Ammonites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עַמּ֑וֹן\rb*, \rb and another|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb against Judah|יְהוּדָ֥ה\rb* \rb into fortified|בְּצוּרָֽה׃\rb* \rb Jerusalem|בִירוּשָׁלִַ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the king|מֶלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֜ל\rb* \rb stands|עָמַ֨ד\rb* \rb at|אֶל־\rb* \rb the fork|אֵ֣ם\rb* \rb in the road|הַדֶּ֗רֶךְ\rb*, \rb at the junction|בְּרֹ֛אשׁ\rb* \rb of the two|שְׁנֵ֥י\rb* \rb roads|הַדְּרָכִ֖ים\rb*, \rb to seek|לִקְסָם־\rb* \rb an omen|קָ֑סֶם\rb*: \rb He shakes|קִלְקַ֤ל\rb* \rb the arrows|בַּֽחִצִּים֙\rb*, \rb he consults|שָׁאַ֣ל\rb* \rb the idols|בַּתְּרָפִ֔ים\rb*, \rb he examines|רָאָ֖ה\rb* \rb the liver|בַּכָּבֵֽד׃\rb*.
