\c 22
\s1 The Sins of Jerusalem
\p \v 1 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb As for you|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֔ם\rb*, \rb will you judge her|הֲתִשְׁפֹּ֥ט\rb*? \rb Will you pass judgment|הֲתִשְׁפֹּ֖ט\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb on the city|עִ֣יר\rb* \rb of bloodshed|הַדָּמִ֑ים\rb*? \rb Then confront her|וְה֣וֹדַעְתָּ֔הּ\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb with all|כָּל־\rb* \rb her abominations|תּוֹעֲבוֹתֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \v 3 \rb and tell her|וְאָמַרְתָּ֗\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: ‘\rb O city|עִ֣יר\rb* \rb who brings her own doom|עִתָּ֑הּ\rb*\rb |לָב֣וֹא\rb* \rb by shedding|שֹׁפֶ֥כֶת\rb* \rb blood|דָּ֛ם\rb* \rb within her walls|בְּתוֹכָ֖הּ\rb* \rb and making|וְעָשְׂתָ֧ה\rb* \rb idols|גִלּוּלִ֛ים\rb*\rb |עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb to defile herself|לְטָמְאָֽה׃\rb*, \v 4 \rb you are guilty|אָשַׁ֗מְתְּ\rb* \rb of the blood|בְּדָמֵ֨ךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you have shed|שָׁפַ֜כְתְּ\rb*, \rb and you are defiled|טָמֵ֔את\rb* \rb by the idols|וּבְגִלּוּלַ֤יִךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you have made|עָשִׂית֙\rb*. \rb You have brought your days|יָמַ֔יִךְ\rb* \rb to a close|וַתַּקְרִ֣יבִי\rb* \rb and have come|וַתָּב֖וֹא\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the end of your years|שְׁנוֹתָ֑יִךְ\rb*. \rb Therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֗ן\rb* \rb I have made you|נְתַתִּ֤יךְ\rb* \rb a reproach|חֶרְפָּה֙\rb* \rb to the nations|לַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb and a mockery|וְקַלָּסָ֖ה\rb* \rb to all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the lands|הָאֲרָצֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb Those near|הַקְּרֹב֛וֹת\rb* \rb and far|וְהָרְחֹק֥וֹת\rb*\rb |מִמֵּ֖ךְ\rb* \rb will mock|יִתְקַלְּסוּ־\rb* \rb you|בָ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb O infamous city|טְמֵאַ֣ת\rb*\rb |הַשֵּׁ֔ם\rb*, \rb full|רַבַּ֖ת\rb* \rb of turmoil|הַמְּהוּמָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb See how|הִנֵּה֙\rb* \rb every|אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb prince|נְשִׂיאֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb within you|בָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb has used|הָ֣יוּ\rb* \rb his power|לִזְרֹע֖וֹ\rb* \rb to|לְמַ֖עַן\rb* \rb shed|שְׁפָךְ־\rb* \rb blood|דָּֽם׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb Father|אָ֤ב\rb* \rb and mother|וָאֵם֙\rb* \rb are treated with contempt|הֵקַ֣לּוּ\rb*. \rb Within your walls|בָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb the foreign resident|לַגֵּ֛ר\rb* \rb is exploited|עָשׂ֥וּ\rb*\rb |בַעֹ֖שֶׁק\rb*\rb |בְּתוֹכֵ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb the fatherless|יָת֥וֹם\rb* \rb and the widow|וְאַלְמָנָ֖ה\rb* \rb are oppressed|ה֥וֹנוּ\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb You have despised|בָּזִ֑ית\rb* \rb My holy things|קָדָשַׁ֖י\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb profaned|חִלָּֽלְתְּ׃\rb* \rb My Sabbaths|שַׁבְּתֹתַ֖י\rb*. \v 9 \rb Among you|בָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb are|הָ֥יוּ\rb* \rb slanderous|רָכִ֛יל\rb* \rb men|אַנְשֵׁ֥י\rb* \rb bent on|לְמַ֣עַן\rb*\rb |שְׁפָךְ־\rb* \rb bloodshed|דָּ֑ם\rb*; \rb within you|בָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb are those who eat|אָ֣כְלוּ\rb* \rb on|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the mountain shrines|הֶֽהָרִים֙\rb* \rb and commit|עָשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb acts of indecency|זִמָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |בְתוֹכֵֽךְ׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb In you|בָ֑ךְ\rb* \rb they have uncovered|גִּלָּה־\rb* \rb the nakedness|עֶרְוַת־\rb* \rb of their fathers|אָ֖ב\rb*; \rb in you|בָֽךְ׃\rb* \rb they violate|עִנּוּ־\rb* \rb women during their menstrual impurity|טְמֵאַ֥ת\rb*\rb |הַנִּדָּ֖ה\rb*. \v 11 \rb One man|וְאִ֣ישׁ׀\rb* \rb commits|עָשָׂה֙\rb* \rb an abomination|תּֽוֹעֵבָ֔ה\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb his neighbor’s|רֵעֵ֗הוּ\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֣שֶׁת\rb*; \rb another|וְאִ֥ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb wickedly|בְזִמָּ֑ה\rb* \rb defiles|טִמֵּ֣א\rb* \rb his daughter-in-law|כַּלָּת֖וֹ\rb*; \rb and yet another|וְאִ֛ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb violates|עִנָּה־\rb* \rb his sister|אֲחֹת֥וֹ\rb*, \rb his own father’s|אָבִ֖יו\rb* \rb daughter|בַת־\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb In you|בָ֖ךְ\rb* \rb they take|לָֽקְחוּ־\rb* \rb bribes|שֹׁ֥חַד\rb* \rb to|לְמַ֣עַן\rb* \rb shed|שְׁפָךְ־\rb* \rb blood|דָּ֑ם\rb*. \rb You engage|לָקַ֗חַתְּ\rb* \rb in usury|נֶ֧שֶׁךְ\rb*, \rb take|וַתְּבַצְּעִ֤י\rb* \rb excess interest|וְתַרְבִּ֣ית\rb*, \rb and extort|בַּעֹ֔שֶׁק\rb* \rb your neighbors|רֵעַ֙יִךְ֙\rb*. \rb But Me|וְאֹתִ֣י\rb* \rb you have forgotten|שָׁכַ֔חַתְּ\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Now look|וְהִנֵּה֙\rb*, \rb I strike|הִכֵּ֣יתִי\rb* \rb My hands|כַפִּ֔י\rb* \rb together against|אֶל־\rb* \rb your unjust gain|בִּצְעֵ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |עָשִׂ֑ית\rb* \rb and against|וְעַ֨ל־\rb* \rb the blood you have shed|דָּמֵ֔ךְ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |הָי֖וּ\rb* \rb in your midst|בְּתוֹכֵֽךְ׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb Will your courage|לִבֵּךְ֙\rb* \rb endure|הֲיַעֲמֹ֤ד\rb* \rb or|אִם־\rb* \rb your hands|יָדַ֔יִךְ\rb* \rb be strong|תֶּחֱזַ֣קְנָה\rb* \rb in the day|לַיָּמִ֕ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb deal|עֹשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb with you|אוֹתָ֑ךְ\rb*? \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb have spoken|דִּבַּ֥רְתִּי\rb*, \rb and I will act|וְעָשִֽׂיתִי׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb I will disperse|וַהֲפִיצוֹתִ֤י\rb*\rb |אוֹתָךְ֙\rb* \rb you among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb and scatter you|וְזֵרִיתִ֖יךְ\rb* \rb throughout the lands|בָּאֲרָצ֑וֹת\rb*; \rb I will purge|וַהֲתִמֹּתִ֥י\rb* \rb your uncleanness|טֻמְאָתֵ֖ךְ\rb*\rb |מִמֵּֽךְ׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb And when you have defiled|וְנִחַ֥לְתְּ\rb* \rb yourself|בָּ֖ךְ\rb*\f + \fr 22:16 \ft Or \fqa And when I have allotted you your inheritance\f* \rb in the eyes|לְעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the nations|גוֹיִ֑ם\rb*, \rb then you will know|וְיָדַ֖עַתְּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.’”
