\p \v 43 \rb Then I said|וָאֹמַ֕ר\rb* \rb of her who had grown old|לַבָּלָ֖ה\rb* \rb in adulteries|נִֽאוּפִ֑ים\rb*: ‘\rb Now|עַתָּ\rb* \rb let them use her as a prostitute|יִזְנֻה\rb*\rb |תַזְנוּתֶ֖הָ\rb*, \rb for that is all she is|וָהִֽיא׃\rb*!’
\p \v 44 \rb And they slept|וַיָּב֣וֹא\rb* \rb with her|אֵלֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb as with|כְּב֖וֹא\rb* \rb a prostitute|אִשָּׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |זוֹנָ֑ה\rb*; \rb they slept with|בָּ֗אוּ\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb Oholah|אָֽהֳלָה֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb and Oholibah|אָ֣הֳלִיבָ֔ה\rb*, \rb those lewd|הַזִּמָּֽה׃\rb* \rb women|אִשֹּׁ֖ת\rb*. \v 45 \rb But righteous|צַדִּיקִ֗ם\rb*\rb |הֵ֚מָּה\rb* \rb men|וַאֲנָשִׁ֣ים\rb* \rb will sentence|יִשְׁפְּט֣וּ\rb* \rb them|אֽוֹתְהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb to the punishment of|וּמִשְׁפַּ֖ט\rb* \rb those who commit adultery|נֹֽאֲפ֔וֹת\rb* \rb and bloodshed|שֹׁפְכ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |דָּ֑ם\rb*\rb |מִשְׁפַּט֙\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb they|הֵ֔נָּה\rb* \rb are adulteresses|נֹֽאֲפֹת֙\rb* \rb with blood|וְדָ֖ם\rb* \rb on their hands|בִּֽידֵיהֶֽן׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 46 \rb |כִּ֛י\rb* \rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb*\rb |הַעֲלֵ֤ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*: ‘\rb Bring a mob|קָהָ֔ל\rb* \rb against them|עֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb and consign|וְנָתֹ֥ן\rb* \rb them|אֶתְהֶ֖ן\rb* \rb to terror|לְזַעֲוָ֥ה\rb* \rb and plunder|וְלָבַֽז׃\rb*. \v 47 \rb The mob|קָהָ֔ל\rb* \rb will stone|וְרָגְמ֨וּ\rb* \rb them|עֲלֵיהֶ֥ן\rb* \rb and cut them|אֶ֙בֶן֙\rb* \rb down|וּבָרֵ֥א\rb*\rb |אוֹתְהֶ֖ן\rb* \rb with their swords|בְּחַרְבוֹתָ֑ם\rb*. \rb They will kill|יַהֲרֹ֔גוּ\rb* \rb their sons|בְּנֵיהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבְנֽוֹתֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb and burn down|יִשְׂרֹֽפוּ׃\rb* \rb their houses|וּבָתֵּיהֶ֖ן\rb*\rb |בָּאֵ֥שׁ\rb*. \v 48 \rb So I will put an end|וְהִשְׁבַּתִּ֥י\rb* \rb to indecency|זִמָּ֖ה\rb* \rb in|מִן־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the women|הַנָּשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb will be admonished|וְנִֽוַּסְּרוּ֙\rb* \rb not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb to imitate|תַעֲשֶׂ֖ינָה\rb* \rb your behavior|כְּזִמַּתְכֶֽנָה׃\rb*. \v 49 \rb They will repay|וְנָתְנ֤וּ\rb* \rb you for your indecency|זִמַּתְכֶ֙נָה֙\rb*,\rb |עֲלֵיכֶ֔ן\rb* \rb and you will bear the consequences|תִּשֶּׂ֑אינָה\rb* \rb of your sins|וַחֲטָאֵ֥י\rb* \rb of idolatry|גִלּוּלֵיכֶ֖ן\rb*. \rb Then you will know|וִידַעְתֶּ֕ם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃פ\rb*.’”
\c 24
\s1 The Parable of the Cooking Pot
\p \v 1 \rb In the ninth|הַתְּשִׁיעִית֙\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָ֤ה\rb*, \rb on the tenth|בֶּעָשׂ֥וֹר\rb* \rb day|לַחֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the tenth|הָעֲשִׂירִ֔י\rb* \rb month|בַּחֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֨ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִי֩\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֜י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb write down|כְּתוֹב\rb*\rb |לְךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*\rb |שֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb today’s date|הַיּ֔וֹם\rb*, \rb for|אֶת־\rb* \rb on this|הַזֶּ֑ה\rb* \rb very|עֶ֖צֶם\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶל֙\rb* \rb has laid siege|סָמַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְר֣וּשָׁלִַ֔ם\rb*\rb |הַזֶּֽה׃\rb*\rb |בְּעֶ֖צֶם\rb*\rb |הַיּ֥וֹם\rb*. \v 3 \rb Now speak a parable|וּמְשֹׁ֤ל\rb*\rb |מָשָׁ֔ל\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb this rebellious|הַמֶּ֙רִי֙\rb* \rb house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\rb Put the pot|הַסִּיר֙\rb* \rb on the fire|שְׁפֹ֤ת\rb*;
\q2 \rb put it on|שְׁפֹ֔ת\rb* \rb and|וְגַם־\rb* \rb pour|יְצֹ֥ק\rb* \rb in|בּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb the water|מָֽיִם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb Put in|אֱסֹ֤ף\rb* \rb the pieces|נְתָחֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb of meat|אֵלֶ֔יהָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb good|ט֖וֹב\rb* \rb piece|נֵ֥תַח\rb*—
\q1 \rb thigh|יָרֵ֣ךְ\rb* \rb and shoulder|וְכָתֵ֑ף\rb* —
\q2 \rb fill|מַלֵּֽא׃\rb* \rb it with choice|מִבְחַ֥ר\rb* \rb bones|עֲצָמִ֖ים\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb Take|לָק֔וֹחַ\rb* \rb the choicest|מִבְחַ֤ר\rb* \rb of the flock|הַצֹּאן֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and|וְגַ֛ם\rb* \rb pile the fuel|דּ֥וּר\rb*\rb |הָעֲצָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb beneath it|תַּחְתֶּ֑יהָ\rb*.
\q1 \rb Bring it to a boil|רְתָחֶ֔יהָ\rb*\rb |רַתַּ֣ח\rb*
\q2 \rb and|גַּם־\rb* \rb cook|בָּשְׁל֥וּ\rb* \rb the bones|עֲצָמֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb in it|בְּתוֹכָֽהּ׃ס\rb*.’
\p \v 6 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֞ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהֹוִ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר׀\rb*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\rb Woe|אוֹי֮\rb* \rb to the city|עִ֣יר\rb* \rb of bloodshed|הַדָּמִים֒\rb*,
\q2 \rb to the pot|סִ֚יר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb now rusted|חֶלְאָתָ֣ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb whose rust|וְחֶ֨לְאָתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb come off|יָצְאָ֖ה\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֑נָּה\rb*!
\q1 \rb Empty|הוֹצִיאָ֔הּ\rb* \rb it piece|לִנְתָחֶ֤יהָ\rb* \rb by piece|לִנְתָחֶ֙יהָ֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb cast|נָפַ֥ל\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb lots|גּוֹרָֽל׃\rb* \rb for its contents|עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb*.\f + \fr 24:6 \ft Or \fqa let no lot fall upon it\f*
\q1 \v 7 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb the blood she shed|דָמָהּ֙\rb* \rb is|הָיָ֔ה\rb* \rb still within her|בְּתוֹכָ֣הּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb she poured it out|שָׂמָ֑תְהוּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the bare|צְחִ֥יחַ\rb* \rb rock|סֶ֖לַע\rb*;
\q1 \rb she did not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb pour|שְׁפָכַ֙תְהוּ֙\rb* \rb it on|עַל־\rb* \rb the ground|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb to cover|לְכַסּ֥וֹת\rb*\rb |עָלָ֖יו\rb* \rb it with dust|עָפָֽר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb In order to stir up|לְהַעֲל֤וֹת\rb* \rb wrath|חֵמָה֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and take vengeance|לִנְקֹ֣ם\rb*\rb |נָקָ֔ם\rb*,
\q1 \rb I have placed|נָתַ֥תִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb her blood|דָּמָ֖הּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the bare|צְחִ֣יחַ\rb* \rb rock|סָ֑לַע\rb*,
\q2 \rb so that it would not|לְבִלְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb be covered|הִכָּסֽוֹת׃פ\rb*.’
\p \v 9 \rb Yes|לָכֵ֗ן\rb*, \rb this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\rb Woe|א֖וֹי\rb* \rb to the city|עִ֣יר\rb* \rb of bloodshed|הַדָּמִ֑ים\rb*!\rb |גַּם־\rb*
\q2 \rb I, too|אֲנִ֖י\rb*, \rb will pile the kindling|הַמְּדוּרָֽה׃\rb* \rb high|אַגְדִּ֥יל\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb Pile on|הַרְבֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb the logs|הָעֵצִים֙\rb* \rb and kindle|הַדְלֵ֣ק\rb* \rb the fire|הָאֵ֔שׁ\rb*;
\q2 \rb cook|הָתֵ֖ם\rb* \rb the meat well|הַבָּשָׂ֑ר\rb*
\q1 \rb and mix in|וְהַרְקַח֙\rb* \rb the spices|הַמֶּרְקָחָ֔ה\rb*;
\q2 \rb let the bones|וְהָעֲצָמ֖וֹת\rb* \rb be burned|יֵחָֽרוּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb Set|וְהַעֲמִידֶ֥הָ\rb* \rb the empty|רֵקָ֑ה\rb* \rb pot on|עַל־\rb* \rb its coals|גֶּחָלֶ֖יהָ\rb*
\q2 \rb until|לְמַ֨עַן\rb* \rb it becomes hot|תֵּחַ֜ם\rb* \rb and its copper|נְחֻשְׁתָּ֗הּ\rb* \rb glows|וְחָ֣רָה\rb*.
\q1 \rb Then its impurity|טֻמְאָתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb will melt|וְנִתְּכָ֤ה\rb* \rb within|בְתוֹכָהּ֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb its rust|חֶלְאָתָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb will be consumed|תִּתֻּ֖ם\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb It has frustrated|הֶלְאָ֑ת\rb* \rb every effort|תְּאֻנִ֖ים\rb*;
\q2 \rb its thick|רַבַּ֣ת\rb* \rb rust|חֶלְאָתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb has not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb been removed|תֵצֵ֤א\rb*\rb |מִמֶּ֙נָּה֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb even by the fire|בְּאֵ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |חֶלְאָתָֽהּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb Because|יַ֤עַן\rb* \rb of the indecency|זִמָּ֑ה\rb* \rb of your uncleanness|בְּטֻמְאָתֵ֖ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb I tried to cleanse you|טִֽהַרְתִּיךְ֙\rb*,
\q1 \rb but you would not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb be purified|טָהַ֔רְתְּ\rb*
\q2 \rb from your filthiness|מִטֻּמְאָתֵךְ֙\rb*.
\q1 \rb You will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be pure|תִטְהֲרִי־\rb* \rb again|ע֔וֹד\rb*
\q2 \rb until|עַד־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My wrath|חֲמָתִ֖י\rb* \rb against you|בָּֽךְ׃\rb* \rb has subsided|הֲנִיחִ֥י\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 \rb I|אֲנִ֨י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֤ה\rb*, \rb have spoken|דִּבַּ֙רְתִּי֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb the time is coming|בָּאָ֣ה\rb*, \rb and I will act|וְעָשִׂ֔יתִי\rb*.
\q1 \rb I will not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb refrain|אֶפְרַ֥ע\rb* \rb or|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb show pity|אָח֖וּס\rb*,
\q2 \rb nor|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb will I relent|אֶנָּחֵ֑ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb I will judge you|שְׁפָט֔וּךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb according to your ways|כִּדְרָכַ֤יִךְ\rb* \rb and deeds|וְכַעֲלִילוֹתַ֙יִךְ֙\rb*,’
\qr \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהֹוִֽה׃פ\rb*.”
\s1 Ezekiel’s Wife Dies
\p \v 15 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 16 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*, \rb behold|הִנְנִ֨י\rb*, \rb I am about to take away|לֹקֵ֧חַ\rb* \rb the desire|מַחְמַ֥ד\rb* \rb of your eyes|עֵינֶ֖יךָ\rb*\rb |מִמְּךָ֛\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb with a fatal blow|בְּמַגֵּפָ֑ה\rb*. \rb But you must not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb mourn|תִסְפֹּד֙\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb or weep|תִבְכֶּ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְל֥וֹא\rb* \rb or let your tears|דִּמְעָתֶֽךָ׃\rb* \rb flow|תָב֖וֹא\rb*. \v 17 \rb Groan|הֵאָנֵ֣ק׀\rb* \rb quietly|דֹּ֗ם\rb*; \rb do not|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |תַֽעֲשֶׂ֔ה\rb* \rb mourn|אֵ֣בֶל\rb* \rb for the dead|מֵתִים֙\rb*. \rb Put|חֲב֣וֹשׁ\rb* \rb on|עָלֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb your turban|פְאֵֽרְךָ֙\rb* \rb and strap|תָּשִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb your sandals|וּנְעָלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb on your feet|בְּרַגְלֶ֑יךָ\rb*; \rb do not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb cover|תַעְטֶה֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb your lips|שָׂפָ֔ם\rb* \rb or eat|תֹאכֵֽל׃\rb* \rb the bread|וְלֶ֥חֶם\rb* \rb of mourners|אֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb So I spoke|וָאֲדַבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֙\rb* \rb in the morning|בַּבֹּ֔קֶר\rb*, \rb and in the evening|בָּעָ֑רֶב\rb* \rb my wife|אִשְׁתִּ֖י\rb* \rb died|וַתָּ֥מָת\rb*. \rb And the next morning|בַּבֹּ֖קֶר\rb* \rb I did|וָאַ֥עַשׂ\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I had been commanded|צֻוֵּֽיתִי׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb Then the people|הָעָ֑ם\rb* \rb asked me|וַיֹּאמְר֥וּ\rb*,\rb |אֵלַ֖י\rb* “\rb Won’t|הֲלֹֽא־\rb* \rb you tell|תַגִּ֥יד\rb* \rb us|לָ֙נוּ֙\rb* \rb what|מָה־\rb* \rb these things|אֵ֣לֶּה\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb are doing|עֹשֶֽׂה׃\rb* \rb mean to us|לָּ֔נוּ\rb*?”
\p \v 20 \rb So I answered|וָאֹמַ֖ר\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, “\rb The word|דְּבַ֨ר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֖י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*: \v 21 \rb Tell|אֱמֹ֣ר׀\rb* \rb the house|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִה֒\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֮\rb*: ‘\rb I am about to desecrate|מְחַלֵּ֤ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My sanctuary|מִקְדָּשִׁי֙\rb*, \rb the pride|גְּא֣וֹן\rb* \rb of your power|עֻזְּכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb the desire|מַחְמַ֥ד\rb* \rb of your eyes|עֵֽינֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb and the delight|וּמַחְמַ֣ל\rb* \rb of your soul|נַפְשְׁכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb And the sons|וּבְנֵיכֶ֧ם\rb* \rb and daughters|וּבְנֽוֹתֵיכֶ֛ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you left behind|עֲזַבְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb will fall|יִפֹּֽלוּ׃\rb* \rb by the sword|בַּחֶ֥רֶב\rb*.’
\p \v 22 \rb Then you will do|וַעֲשִׂיתֶ֖ם\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I have done|עָשִׂ֑יתִי\rb*:\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb You will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb cover|תַעְט֔וּ\rb* \rb your lips|שָׂפָם֙\rb* \rb or eat|תֹאכֵֽלוּ׃\rb* \rb the bread|וְלֶ֥חֶם\rb* \rb of mourners|אֲנָשִׁ֖ים\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb*. \v 23 \rb Your turbans|וּפְאֵרֵכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb will remain on|עַל־\rb* \rb your heads|רָאשֵׁיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and your sandals|וְנַֽעֲלֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb on your feet|בְּרַגְלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb You will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb mourn|תִסְפְּד֖וּ\rb* \rb or|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb weep|תִבְכּ֑וּ\rb*, \rb but you will waste away|וּנְמַקֹּתֶם֙\rb* \rb because of your sins|בַּעֲוֺנֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and you will groan|וּנְהַמְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb among|אֶל־\rb*\rb |אִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb yourselves|אָחִֽיו׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 ‘\rb Thus Ezekiel|יְחֶזְקֵ֤אל\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb a sign|לְמוֹפֵ֔ת\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶם֙\rb*; \rb you will do|תַּעֲשׂ֑וּ\rb* \rb everything|כְּכֹ֥ל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he has done|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*. \rb When this happens|בְּבֹאָ֕הּ\rb*, \rb you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֕ם\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃ס\rb*.’
\p \v 25 \rb And you|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֔ם\rb*,\rb |הֲל֗וֹא\rb* \rb know that on the day|בְּי֨וֹם\rb* \rb I take|קַחְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb away|מֵהֶם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their stronghold|מָ֣עוּזָּ֔ם\rb*, \rb their pride|תִּפְאַרְתָּ֑ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and joy|מְשׂ֖וֹשׂ\rb* — \rb the desire|מַחְמַ֤ד\rb* \rb of their eyes|עֵֽינֵיהֶם֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb which uplifted|מַשָּׂ֣א\rb* \rb their souls|נַפְשָׁ֔ם\rb* — \rb and their sons|בְּנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb and daughters as well|וּבְנוֹתֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*, \v 26 \rb on that|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb a fugitive|הַפָּלִ֖יט\rb* \rb will come|יָב֥וֹא\rb*\rb |אֵלֶ֑יךָ\rb* \rb and tell you the news|לְהַשְׁמָע֖וּת\rb*\rb |אָזְנָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb On that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb your mouth|פִּ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will be opened|יִפָּ֤תַח\rb* \rb to him who has escaped|הַפָּלִ֔יט\rb*; \rb you will speak|וּתְדַבֵּ֕ר\rb* \rb and no|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb longer|ע֑וֹד\rb* \rb be mute|תֵֽאָלֵ֖ם\rb*. \rb So you will be|וְהָיִ֤יתָ\rb* \rb a sign|לְמוֹפֵ֔ת\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶם֙\rb*, \rb and they will know|וְיָדְע֖וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.”
\c 25
\s1 A Prophecy against Ammon
\p \v 1 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*, \rb set|שִׂ֥ים\rb* \rb your face|פָּנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Ammonites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֑וֹן\rb* \rb and prophesy|וְהִנָּבֵ֖א\rb* \rb against them|עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb Tell|וְאָֽמַרְתָּ֙\rb* \rb the Ammonites|לִבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמּ֔וֹן\rb* \rb to hear|שִׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb*, \rb for this is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֡ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*: ‘\rb Because|יַעַן֩\rb* \rb you exclaimed|אָמְרֵ֨ךְ\rb*, “\rb Aha|הֶאָ֜ח\rb*!” \rb when My sanctuary|מִקְדָּשִׁ֣י\rb*\rb |כִֽי־\rb* \rb was profaned|נִחָ֗ל\rb*,\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb when the land|אַדְמַ֤ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb was laid waste|נָשַׁ֔מָּה\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb when the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*\rb |כִּ֥י\rb* \rb went|הָלְכ֖וּ\rb* \rb into exile|בַּגּוֹלָֽה׃\rb*, \v 4 \rb therefore|לָכֵ֡ן\rb* \rb I will indeed|הִנְנִי֩\rb* \rb give you|נֹתְנָ֨ךְ\rb* \rb as a possession|לְמֽוֹרָשָׁ֗ה\rb* \rb to the people|לִבְנֵי־\rb* \rb of the East|קֶ֜דֶם\rb*. \rb They will set up|וְיִשְּׁב֤וּ\rb* \rb their camps|טִירֽוֹתֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb and pitch|וְנָ֥תְנוּ\rb* \rb their tents|מִשְׁכְּנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb among you|בָ֖ךְ\rb*. \rb They|הֵ֚מָּה\rb* \rb will eat|יֹאכְל֣וּ\rb* \rb your fruit|פִרְיֵ֔ךְ\rb*\rb |וְהֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb and drink|יִשְׁתּ֥וּ\rb* \rb your milk|חֲלָבֵֽךְ׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb I will make|וְנָתַתִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Rabbah|רַבָּה֙\rb* \rb a pasture|לִנְוֵ֣ה\rb* \rb for camels|גְמַלִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |בְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb Ammon|עַמּ֖וֹן\rb*\f + \fr 25:5 \ft Hebrew \fqa and the Ammonites\f* \rb a resting place for|לְמִרְבַּץ־\rb* \rb sheep|צֹ֑אן\rb*. \rb Then you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.’
\p \v 6 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: ‘\rb Because|יַ֚עַן\rb* \rb you clapped|מַחְאֲךָ֣\rb* \rb your hands|יָ֔ד\rb* \rb and stomped|וְרַקְעֲךָ֖\rb* \rb your feet|בְּרָ֑גֶל\rb* \rb and rejoiced|וַתִּשְׂמַ֤ח\rb* \rb over|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אַדְמַ֖ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb with a heart|בְּנֶ֔פֶשׁ\rb* \rb full|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb of contempt|שָֽׁאטְךָ֙\rb*, \v 7 \rb therefore|לָכֵ֡ן\rb* \rb I will indeed|הִנְנִי֩\rb* \rb stretch out|נָטִ֨יתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My hand|יָדִ֜י\rb* \rb against you|עָלֶ֗יךָ\rb* \rb and give you|וּנְתַתִּ֤יךָֽ־\rb* \rb as plunder|לְבַג\rb* \rb to the nations|לַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb*. \rb I will cut you off|וְהִכְרַתִּ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the peoples|הָ֣עַמִּ֔ים\rb* \rb and exterminate you|וְהַאֲבַדְתִּ֖יךָ\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the countries|הָאֲרָצ֑וֹת\rb*. \rb I will destroy you|אַשְׁמִ֣ידְךָ֔\rb*, \rb and you will know|וְיָדַעְתָּ֖\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.’
\s1 A Prophecy against Moab
\p \v 8 \rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*: ‘\rb Because|יַ֗עַן\rb* \rb Moab|מוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb and Seir|וְשֵׂעִ֔יר\rb*\f + \fr 25:8 \ft LXX does not include \fqa and Seir\ft .\f* \rb said|אֲמֹ֤ר\rb*, “\rb Look|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָֽה׃\rb* \rb is like all|כְּכָֽל־\rb* \rb the other nations|הַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb*,” \v 9 \rb therefore|לָכֵן֩\rb* \rb I will indeed|הִנְנִ֨י\rb* \rb expose|פֹתֵ֜חַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the flank|כֶּ֤תֶף\rb* \rb of Moab|מוֹאָב֙\rb* \rb beginning with its frontier|מִקָּצֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb cities|מֵהֶ֣עָרִ֔ים\rb* —\rb |מֵֽעָרָ֖יו\rb*\rb |בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb Beth-jeshimoth|הַיְשִׁימֹ֔ת\rb*,\rb |בַּ֥עַל\rb* \rb Baal-meon|מְע֖וֹן\rb*, \rb and Kiriathaim|וְקִרְיָתְמָה׃\rb* — \rb the glory|צְבִ֗י\rb* \rb of the land|אֶ֚רֶץ\rb*. \v 10 \rb I will give it|וּנְתַתִּ֖יהָ\rb* \rb along with|עַל־\rb*\rb |לִבְנֵי־\rb* \rb the Ammonites|עַמּ֔וֹן\rb* \rb as a possession|לְמֽוֹרָשָׁ֑ה\rb* \rb to the people|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the East|קֶ֙דֶם֙\rb*, \rb so that|לְמַ֛עַן\rb*\rb |בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb the Ammonites|עַמּ֖וֹן\rb* \rb will no longer|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb be remembered|תִזָּכֵ֥ר\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִֽם׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb So I will execute|אֶעֱשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb judgments|שְׁפָטִ֑ים\rb* \rb on Moab|וּבְמוֹאָ֖ב\rb*, \rb and they will know|וְיָדְע֖וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.’
\s1 A Prophecy against Edom
\p \v 12 \rb This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: ‘\rb Because|יַ֣עַן\rb* \rb Edom|אֱד֛וֹם\rb* \rb acted|עֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb vengefully|בִּנְקֹ֥ם\rb*\rb |נָקָ֖ם\rb* \rb against the house|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and in so doing|וְנִקְּמ֥וּ\rb*\rb |בָהֶֽם׃\rb* \rb incurred grievous guilt|וַיֶּאְשְׁמ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אָשׁ֖וֹם\rb*, \v 13 \rb therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: \rb I will stretch out|וְנָטִ֤תִי\rb* \rb My hand|יָדִי֙\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Edom|אֱד֔וֹם\rb* \rb and cut off|וְהִכְרַתִּ֥י\rb* \rb from it|מִמֶּ֖נָּה\rb* \rb both man|אָדָ֣ם\rb* \rb and beast|וּבְהֵמָ֑ה\rb*. \rb I will make|וּנְתַתִּ֤יהָ\rb* \rb it a wasteland|חָרְבָּה֙\rb*, \rb and from Teman|מִתֵּימָ֔ן\rb* \rb to Dedan|וּדְדָ֖נֶה\rb* \rb they will fall|יִפֹּֽלוּ׃\rb* \rb by the sword|בַּחֶ֥רֶב\rb*. \v 14 \rb I will take|וְנָתַתִּ֨י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My vengeance|נִקְמָתִ֜י\rb* \rb on Edom|בֶּאֱד֗וֹם\rb* \rb by the hand|בְּיַד֙\rb* \rb of My people|עַמִּ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb and they will deal|וְעָשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb with Edom|בֶאֱד֔וֹם\rb* \rb according to My anger|כְּאַפִּ֖י\rb* \rb and wrath|וְכַחֲמָתִ֑י\rb*. \rb Then they will know|וְיָֽדְעוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My vengeance|נִקְמָתִ֔י\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃פ\rb*.’
\s1 A Prophecy against the Philistines
\p \v 15 \rb This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: ‘\rb Because|יַ֛עַן\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb acted|עֲשׂ֥וֹת\rb* \rb in vengeance|בִּנְקָמָ֑ה\rb*, \rb taking|וַיִּנָּקְמ֤וּ\rb* \rb vengeance|נָקָם֙\rb* \rb with malice|בִּשְׁאָ֣ט\rb* \rb of soul|בְּנֶ֔פֶשׁ\rb* \rb to destroy Judah|לְמַשְׁחִ֖ית\rb* \rb with ancient|עוֹלָֽם׃\rb* \rb hostility|אֵיבַ֥ת\rb*, \v 16 \rb therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: \rb Behold|הִנְנִ֨י\rb*, \rb I will stretch out|נוֹטֶ֤ה\rb* \rb My hand|יָדִי֙\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the Philistines|פְּלִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb and I will cut off|וְהִכְרַתִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Cherethites|כְּרֵתִ֑ים\rb* \rb and destroy|וְהַ֣אֲבַדְתִּ֔י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the remnant|שְׁאֵרִ֖ית\rb* \rb along|ח֥וֹף\rb* \rb the coast|הַיָּֽם׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb I will execute|וְעָשִׂ֤יתִי\rb* \rb great|גְּדֹל֔וֹת\rb* \rb vengeance|נְקָמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb against them|בָם֙\rb* \rb with furious|חֵמָ֑ה\rb* \rb reproof|בְּתוֹכְח֖וֹת\rb*. \rb Then they will know|וְיָֽדְעוּ֙\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb when I lay|בְּתִתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My vengeance|נִקְמָתִ֖י\rb* \rb upon them|בָּֽם׃ס\rb*.’”
\c 26
\s1 A Prophecy against Tyre
\r (\ref Isaiah 23:1–18|ISA 23:1-18\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb In the eleventh month of the twelfth|בְּעַשְׁתֵּֽי־\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֥ה\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֖ה\rb*,\f + \fr 26:1 \ft Likely reading of the original Hebrew text; MT \fqa In the eleventh year\f* \rb on the first|בְּאֶחָ֣ד\rb* \rb day of the month|לַחֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb*,\rb |הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֛י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb because|יַ֠עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb Tyre|צֹּ֤ר\rb* \rb has said|אָ֨מְרָה\rb* \rb of|עַל־\rb* \rb Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb*, ‘\rb Aha|הֶאָ֔ח\rb*! \rb The gate|דַּלְת֥וֹת\rb* \rb to the nations|הָעַמִּ֖ים\rb* \rb is broken|נִשְׁבְּרָ֛ה\rb*; \rb it has swung open|נָסֵ֣בָּה\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָ֑י\rb*; \rb now that she lies in ruins|הָחֳרָֽבָה׃\rb* \rb I will be filled|אִמָּלְאָ֖ה\rb*,’ \v 3 \rb therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: ‘\rb Behold|הִנְנִ֥י\rb*, \rb O Tyre|צֹ֑ר\rb*, \rb I am against you|עָלַ֖יִךְ\rb*, \rb and I will raise up|וְהַעֲלֵיתִ֤י\rb* \rb many|רַבִּ֔ים\rb* \rb nations|גּוֹיִ֣ם\rb* \rb against you|עָלַ֙יִךְ֙\rb*, \rb as the sea|הַיָּ֖ם\rb* \rb brings up|כְּהַעֲל֥וֹת\rb* \rb its waves|לְגַלָּֽיו׃\rb*. \v 4 \rb They will destroy|וְשִׁחֲת֞וּ\rb* \rb the walls|חֹמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Tyre|צֹ֗ר\rb* \rb and demolish|וְהָֽרְסוּ֙\rb* \rb her towers|מִגְדָּלֶ֔יהָ\rb*. \rb I will scrape|וְסִֽחֵיתִ֥י\rb* \rb the soil|עֲפָרָ֖הּ\rb* \rb from her|מִמֶּ֑נָּה\rb* \rb and make|וְנָתַתִּ֥י\rb* \rb her|אוֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb a bare|לִצְחִ֥יחַ\rb* \rb rock|סָֽלַע׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb She will become|תִּֽהְיֶה֙\rb* \rb a place|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb to spread|מִשְׁטַ֨ח\rb* \rb nets|חֲרָמִ֤ים\rb* \rb in the sea|הַיָּ֔ם\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb have spoken|דִבַּ֔רְתִּי\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb*. \rb She will become|וְהָיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb plunder|לְבַ֖ז\rb* \rb for the nations|לַגּוֹיִֽם׃\rb*, \v 6 \rb and the villages|וּבְנוֹתֶ֙יהָ֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb on her mainland|בַּשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb will be slain|תֵּהָרַ֑גְנָה\rb* \rb by the sword|בַּחֶ֖רֶב\rb*. \rb Then they will know|וְיָדְע֖וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.’
\p \v 7 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: ‘\rb Behold|הִנְנִ֧י\rb*, \rb I will bring|מֵבִ֣יא\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Tyre|צֹ֗ר\rb* \rb from the north|מִצָּפ֖וֹן\rb* \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְרֶאצַּ֧ר\rb*\f + \fr 26:7 \ft Hebrew \fqa Nebuchadrezzar\ft , a variant of \fqa Nebuchadnezzar \ft (king of Babylon). The latter spelling is used throughout Ezekiel for consistency.\f* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֛ל\rb*, \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of kings|מְלָכִ֑ים\rb*, \rb with horses|בְּס֛וּס\rb* \rb and chariots|וּבְרֶ֥כֶב\rb*, \rb with cavalry|וּבְפָרָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb and a great|רָֽב׃\rb* \rb company|וְקָהָ֥ל\rb* \rb of troops|וְעַם־\rb*. \v 8 \rb He will slaughter|יַהֲרֹ֑ג\rb* \rb the villages|בְּנוֹתַ֥יִךְ\rb* \rb of your mainland|בַּשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb with the sword|בַּחֶ֣רֶב\rb*; \rb he will set up|וְנָתַ֨ן\rb* \rb siege works|דָּיֵ֗ק\rb* \rb against you|עָלַ֜יִךְ\rb*, \rb build|וְשָׁפַ֤ךְ\rb* \rb a ramp to your walls|סֹֽלְלָ֔ה\rb*\rb |עָלַ֙יִךְ֙\rb*, \rb and raise|וְהֵקִ֥ים\rb* \rb his shields|צִנָּֽה׃\rb* \rb against you|עָלַ֖יִךְ\rb*. \v 9 \rb He will direct|יִתֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb the blows|וּמְחִ֣י\rb* \rb of his battering rams|קָֽבָלּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb against your walls|בְּחֹֽמוֹתָ֑יִךְ\rb* \rb and tear down|יִתֹּ֖ץ\rb* \rb your towers|וּמִ֨גְדְּלֹתַ֔יִךְ\rb* \rb with his axes|בְּחַרְבוֹתָֽיו׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb His multitude|מִשִּׁפְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb of horses|סוּסָ֖יו\rb* \rb will cover you|יְכַסֵּ֣ךְ\rb* \rb in their dust|אֲבָקָ֑ם\rb*.
\p \rb When he enters|בְּבֹאוֹ֙\rb* \rb your gates|בִּשְׁעָרַ֔יִךְ\rb* \rb as an army entering|כִּמְבוֹאֵ֖י\rb* \rb a breached|מְבֻקָּעָֽה׃\rb* \rb city|עִ֥יר\rb*, \rb your walls|חֽוֹמוֹתַ֔יִךְ\rb* \rb will shake|תִּרְעַ֙שְׁנָה֙\rb* \rb from the noise|מִקּוֹל֩\rb* \rb of cavalry|פָּרַ֨שׁ\rb*, \rb wagons|וְגַלְגַּ֜ל\rb*, \rb and chariots|וָרֶ֗כֶב\rb*. \v 11 \rb The hooves|בְּפַרְס֣וֹת\rb* \rb of his horses|סוּסָ֔יו\rb* \rb will trample|יִרְמֹ֖ס\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your streets|חֽוּצוֹתָ֑יִךְ\rb*. \rb He will slaughter|יַהֲרֹ֔ג\rb* \rb your people|עַמֵּךְ֙\rb* \rb with the sword|בַּחֶ֣רֶב\rb*, \rb and your mighty|עֻזֵּ֖ךְ\rb* \rb pillars|וּמַצְּב֥וֹת\rb* \rb will fall|תֵּרֵֽד׃\rb* \rb to the ground|לָאָ֥רֶץ\rb*. \v 12 \rb They will plunder|וְשָׁלְל֣וּ\rb* \rb your wealth|חֵילֵ֗ךְ\rb* \rb and pillage|וּבָֽזְזוּ֙\rb* \rb your merchandise|רְכֻלָּתֵ֔ךְ\rb*. \rb They will demolish|וְהָֽרְסוּ֙\rb* \rb your walls|חוֹמוֹתַ֔יִךְ\rb*, \rb tear down|יִתֹּ֑צוּ\rb* \rb your beautiful|חֶמְדָּתֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb homes|וּבָתֵּ֥י\rb*, \rb and throw|יָשִֽׂימוּ׃\rb* \rb your stones|וַאֲבָנַ֤יִךְ\rb* \rb and timber|וְעֵצַ֙יִךְ֙\rb* \rb and soil|וַֽעֲפָרֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb into|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the water|מַ֖יִם\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb So I will silence|וְהִשְׁבַּתִּ֖י\rb* \rb the sound|הֲמ֣וֹן\rb* \rb of your songs|שִׁירָ֑יִךְ\rb*, \rb and the music|וְק֣וֹל\rb* \rb of your lyres|כִּנּוֹרַ֔יִךְ\rb* \rb will no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb longer|עֽוֹד׃\rb* \rb be heard|יִשָּׁמַ֖ע\rb*. \v 14 \rb I will make you|וּנְתַתִּ֞יךְ\rb* \rb a bare|לִצְחִ֣יחַ\rb* \rb rock|סֶ֗לַע\rb*, \rb and you will become|תִּֽהְיֶ֔ה\rb* \rb a place to spread|מִשְׁטַ֤ח\rb* \rb the fishing nets|חֲרָמִים֙\rb*. \rb You will never|לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |ע֑וֹד\rb* \rb be rebuilt|תִבָּנֶ֖ה\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֤י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוִֽה׃ס\rb*, \rb have spoken|דִּבַּ֔רְתִּי\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוָה֙\rb*.’
\p \v 15 \rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֖ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֛ר\rb* \rb to Tyre|לְצ֑וֹר\rb*: ‘\rb Will not|הֲלֹ֣א׀\rb* \rb the coastlands|הָאִיִּֽים׃\rb* \rb quake|יִרְעֲשׁ֖וּ\rb* \rb at the sound|מִקּ֣וֹל\rb* \rb of your downfall|מַפַּלְתֵּ֗ךְ\rb*, \rb when the wounded|חָלָ֜ל\rb*\rb |בֵּהָ֤רֵֽג\rb* \rb groan|בֶּאֱנֹ֨ק\rb* \rb at the slaughter|הֶ֙רֶג֙\rb* \rb in your midst|בְּתוֹכֵ֔ךְ\rb*?
\p \v 16 \rb All|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb the princes|נְשִׂיאֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the sea|הַיָּ֔ם\rb* \rb will descend|וְֽיָרְד֞וּ\rb* \rb from|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb their thrones|כִּסְאוֹתָ֗ם\rb*, \rb remove|וְהֵסִ֙ירוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their robes|מְעִ֣ילֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and strip off|יִפְשֹׁ֑טוּ\rb* \rb their embroidered|רִקְמָתָ֖ם\rb* \rb garments|בִּגְדֵ֥י\rb*. \rb Clothed|יִלְבָּ֙שׁוּ֙\rb* \rb with terror|חֲרָד֤וֹת׀\rb*, \rb they will sit|יֵשֵׁ֔בוּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the ground|הָאָ֣רֶץ\rb*, \rb trembling|וְחָֽרְדוּ֙\rb* \rb every moment|לִרְגָעִ֔ים\rb*, \rb appalled|וְשָׁמְמ֖וּ\rb* \rb over you|עָלָֽיִךְ׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb Then they will lament|וְנָשְׂא֨וּ\rb*\rb |קִינָה֙\rb* \rb for you|עָלַ֤יִךְ\rb*, \rb saying|וְאָ֣מְרוּ\rb*\rb |לָ֔ךְ\rb*,
\b 
\q1 “\rb How|אֵ֣יךְ\rb* \rb you have perished|אָבַ֔דְתְּ\rb*, \rb O city|הָעִ֣יר\rb* \rb of renown|הַהֻלָּ֗לָה\rb*
\q2 \rb inhabited|נוֹשֶׁ֖בֶת\rb* \rb by seafaring men|מִיַּמִּ֑ים\rb*—
\q1 \rb she who|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb was|הָיְתָ֨ה\rb* \rb powerful|חֲזָקָ֤ה\rb* \rb on the sea|בַיָּם֙\rb*,\rb |הִ֣יא\rb* \rb along with her people|וְיֹשְׁבֶ֔יהָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb imposed|נָתְנ֥וּ\rb* \rb terror|חִתִּיתָ֖ם\rb* \rb on all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb peoples|יוֹשְׁבֶֽיהָ׃\rb*!\f + \fr 26:17 \ft Or \fqa on all her inhabitants\f*
\q1 \v 18 \rb Now|עַתָּה֙\rb* \rb the coastlands|הָֽאִיִּ֔ן\rb* \rb tremble|יֶחְרְד֣וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb on the day|י֖וֹם\rb* \rb of your downfall|מַפַּלְתֵּ֑ךְ\rb*;
\q1 \rb the islands|הָאִיִּ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb in the sea|בַּיָּ֖ם\rb*
\q2 \rb are dismayed|וְנִבְהֲל֛וּ\rb* \rb by your demise|מִצֵּאתֵֽךְ׃ס\rb*.”’
\p \v 19 \rb For|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: ‘\rb When I make|בְּתִתִּ֤י\rb* \rb you|אֹתָךְ֙\rb* \rb a desolate|נֶחֱרֶ֔בֶת\rb* \rb city|עִ֣יר\rb* \rb like other deserted|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |נוֹשָׁ֑בוּ\rb* \rb cities|כֶּעָרִ֖ים\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb and when I raise up|בְּהַעֲל֤וֹת\rb* \rb the deep|תְּה֔וֹם\rb* \rb against you|עָלַ֙יִךְ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb so that the mighty|הָרַבִּֽים׃\rb* \rb waters|הַמַּ֥יִם\rb* \rb cover you|וְכִסּ֖וּךְ\rb*, \v 20 \rb then I will bring you down|וְהוֹרַדְתִּיךְ֩\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb those who descend|י֨וֹרְדֵי\rb* \rb to the Pit|ב֜וֹר\rb*, \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb of antiquity|עוֹלָ֗ם\rb*. \rb I will make you dwell|וְ֠הוֹשַׁבְתִּיךְ\rb* \rb in the earth|בְּאֶ֨רֶץ\rb* \rb below|תַּחְתִּיּ֜וֹת\rb* \rb like the ancient|מֵֽעוֹלָם֙\rb* \rb ruins|כָּחֳרָב֤וֹת\rb*, \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb those who descend|י֣וֹרְדֵי\rb* \rb to the Pit|ב֔וֹר\rb*, \rb so that|לְמַ֖עַן\rb* \rb you will no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb longer be inhabited|תֵשֵׁ֑בִי\rb* \rb or set|וְנָתַתִּ֥י\rb* \rb in splendor|צְבִ֖י\rb*\f + \fr 26:20 \ft LXX \fqa or take your place\f* \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of the living|חַיִּֽים׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb I will make|אֶתְּנֵ֖ךְ\rb* \rb you an object of horror|בַּלָּה֥וֹת\rb*, \rb and you will be no more|וְאֵינֵ֑ךְ\rb*. \rb You will be sought|וּֽתְבֻקְשִׁ֗י\rb*, \rb but will never|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |לְעוֹלָ֔ם\rb* \rb be found|תִמָּצְאִ֥י\rb*\rb |עוֹד֙\rb*,’ \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהֹוִֽה׃ס\rb*.”
\c 27
\s1 A Lament for Tyre
\p \v 1 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Now you|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֔ם\rb*, \rb take up|שָׂ֥א\rb* \rb a lament|קִינָֽה׃\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb Tyre|צֹ֖ר\rb*. \v 3 \rb Tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb Tyre|לְצ֗וֹר\rb*, \rb who dwells|הַיֹּשַׁבְתִּי\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the gateway|מְבוֹאֹ֣ת\rb* \rb to the sea|יָ֔ם\rb*, \rb merchant|רֹכֶ֙לֶת֙\rb* \rb of the peoples|הָֽעַמִּ֔ים\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb many|רַבִּ֑ים\rb* \rb coasts|אִיִּ֖ים\rb*, \rb that this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*:
