\c 28
\s1 A Prophecy against the Ruler of Tyre
\p \v 1 \rb And the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֡ם\rb*, \rb tell|אֱמֹר֩\rb* \rb the ruler|לִנְגִ֨יד\rb* \rb of Tyre|צֹ֜ר\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהֹוִ֗ה\rb*\rb |יַ֣עַן\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר׀\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \rb Your heart|לִבְּךָ֙\rb* \rb is proud|גָּבַ֤הּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and you have said|וַתֹּ֙אמֶר֙\rb*,
\q1 ‘\rb I|אָ֔נִי\rb* \rb am a god|אֵ֣ל\rb*;
\q2 \rb I sit|יָשַׁ֖בְתִּי\rb* \rb in the seat|מוֹשַׁ֧ב\rb* \rb of gods|אֱלֹהִ֛ים\rb*
\q2 \rb in the heart|בְּלֵ֣ב\rb* \rb of the sea|יַמִּ֑ים\rb*.’
\q1 \rb Yet you|וְאַתָּ֤ה\rb* \rb are a man|אָדָם֙\rb* \rb and not|וְֽלֹא־\rb* \rb a god|אֵ֔ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb though you have regarded|וַתִּתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb your heart|לִבְּךָ֖\rb*
\q2 \rb as that|כְּלֵ֥ב\rb* \rb of a god|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb Behold|הִנֵּ֥ה\rb*, \rb you|אַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb are wiser|חָכָ֛ם\rb* \rb than Daniel|מִדָּנִאֵל\rb*;\rb |כָּל־\rb*
\q2 \rb no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb secret|סָת֖וּם\rb* \rb is hidden from you|עֲמָמֽוּךָ׃\rb*!
\q1 \v 4 \rb By your wisdom|בְּחָכְמָֽתְךָ֙\rb* \rb and understanding|וּבִתְבוּנָ֣תְךָ֔\rb*
\q2 \rb you have gained|עָשִׂ֥יתָ\rb* \rb your|לְּךָ֖\rb* \rb wealth|חָ֑יִל\rb*
\q1 \rb and amassed|וַתַּ֛עַשׂ\rb* \rb gold|זָהָ֥ב\rb* \rb and silver|וָכֶ֖סֶף\rb*
\q2 \rb for your treasuries|בְּאוֹצְרוֹתֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb By your great|בְּרֹ֧ב\rb* \rb skill|חָכְמָתְךָ֛\rb* \rb in trading|בִּרְכֻלָּתְךָ֖\rb*
\q2 \rb you have increased|הִרְבִּ֣יתָ\rb* \rb your wealth|חֵילֶ֑ךָ\rb*,
\q1 \rb but your heart|לְבָבְךָ֖\rb* \rb has grown proud|וַיִּגְבַּ֥הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb because of it|בְּחֵילֶֽךָ׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֕ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \rb Because|יַ֛עַן\rb* \rb you regard|תִּתְּךָ֥\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your heart|לְבָבְךָ֖\rb*
\q2 \rb as the heart|כְּלֵ֥ב\rb* \rb of a god|אֱלֹהִֽים׃\rb*,
\q1 \v 7 \rb |לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb behold|הִנְנִ֨י\rb*, \rb I will bring|מֵבִ֤יא\rb* \rb foreigners|זָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb against you|עָלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb the most ruthless|עָרִיצֵ֖י\rb* \rb of nations|גּוֹיִ֑ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb They will draw|וְהֵרִ֤יקוּ\rb* \rb their swords|חַרְבוֹתָם֙\rb*
\q2 \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the beauty|יְפִ֣י\rb* \rb of your wisdom|חָכְמָתֶ֔ךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and will defile|וְחִלְּל֖וּ\rb* \rb your splendor|יִפְעָתֶֽךָ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb They will bring you down|יֽוֹרִד֑וּךָ\rb* \rb to the Pit|לַשַּׁ֖חַת\rb*,
\q2 \rb and you will die|מְמוֹתֵ֥י\rb* \rb a violent|חָלָ֖ל\rb* \rb death|וָמַ֛תָּה\rb*
\q2 \rb in the heart|בְּלֵ֥ב\rb* \rb of the seas|יַמִּֽים׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 9 \rb Will you still say|הֶאָמֹ֤ר\rb*\rb |תֹּאמַר֙\rb*, ‘\rb I|אָ֔נִי\rb* \rb am a god|אֱלֹהִ֣ים\rb*,’
\q2 \rb in the presence|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of those who slay you|הֹֽרְגֶ֑ךָ\rb*?
\q1 \rb You|וְאַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb will be only a man|אָדָ֛ם\rb*, \rb not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb a god|אֵ֖ל\rb*,
\q2 \rb in the hands|בְּיַ֥ד\rb* \rb of those who wound you|מְחַלְלֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb You will die|תָּמ֖וּת\rb* \rb the death|מוֹתֵ֧י\rb* \rb of the uncircumcised|עֲרֵלִ֛ים\rb*
\q2 \rb at the hands|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of foreigners|זָרִ֑ים\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \rb For|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb have spoken|דִבַּ֔רְתִּי\rb*,
\qr \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃ס\rb*.”
\s1 A Lament for the King of Tyre
\p \v 11 \rb Again the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 12 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*, \rb take up|שָׂ֥א\rb* \rb a lament|קִינָ֖ה\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Tyre|צ֑וֹר\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָמַ֣רְתָּ\rb* \rb him|לּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\rb You|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb were the seal|חוֹתֵ֣ם\rb* \rb of perfection|תָּכְנִ֔ית\rb*,
\q2 \rb full of|מָלֵ֥א\rb* \rb wisdom|חָכְמָ֖ה\rb* \rb and perfect|וּכְלִ֥יל\rb* \rb in beauty|יֹֽפִי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb You were|הָיִ֗יתָ\rb* \rb in Eden|בְּעֵ֨דֶן\rb*,
\q2 \rb the garden|גַּן־\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֜ים\rb*.
\q1 \rb Every kind|כָּל־\rb* \rb of precious|יְקָרָ֤ה\rb* \rb stone|אֶ֨בֶן\rb* \rb adorned you|מְסֻכָתֶ֙ךָ֙\rb*:\f + \fr 28:13 \ft The precise identification of some of these gemstones is uncertain.\f*
\q2 \rb ruby|אֹ֣דֶם\rb*, \rb topaz|פִּטְדָ֞ה\rb*, \rb and diamond|וְיָהֲלֹ֗ם\rb*,
\q1 \rb beryl|תַּרְשִׁ֥ישׁ\rb*, \rb onyx|שֹׁ֙הַם֙\rb*, \rb and jasper|וְיָ֣שְׁפֵ֔ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb sapphire|סַפִּ֣יר\rb*,\f + \fr 28:13 \ft Or \fqa lapis lazuli\f* \rb turquoise|נֹ֔פֶךְ\rb*, \rb and emerald|וּבָרְקַ֖ת\rb*.
\q1 \rb Your mountings|וּנְקָבֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb and settings|תֻּפֶּ֤יךָ\rb* \rb were crafted|מְלֶ֨אכֶת\rb* \rb in gold|וְזָהָ֑ב\rb*,
\q2 \rb prepared|כּוֹנָֽנוּ׃\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb of your creation|הִבָּרַאֲךָ֖\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb You|אַ֨תְּ־\rb* \rb were anointed|מִמְשַׁ֖ח\rb* \rb as a guardian|הַסּוֹכֵ֑ךְ\rb* \rb cherub|כְּר֔וּב\rb*,
\q2 \rb for I had ordained you|וּנְתַתִּ֗יךָ\rb*.
\q1 \rb You were|הָיִ֔יתָ\rb* \rb on the holy|קֹ֤דֶשׁ\rb* \rb mountain|בְּהַ֨ר\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִים֙\rb*;
\q2 \rb you walked|הִתְהַלָּֽכְתָּ׃\rb* \rb among|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the fiery|אֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb stones|אַבְנֵי־\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 \rb From the day|מִיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb you were created|הִבָּֽרְאָ֑ךְ\rb*
\q2 \rb you|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb were blameless|תָּמִ֤ים\rb* \rb in your ways|בִּדְרָכֶ֔יךָ\rb*—
\q2 \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb wickedness|עַוְלָ֖תָה\rb* \rb was found|נִמְצָ֥א\rb* \rb in you|בָּֽךְ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 16 \rb By the vastness|בְּרֹ֣ב\rb* \rb of your trade|רְכֻלָּתְךָ֗\rb*,
\q2 \rb you|תוֹכְךָ֛\rb* \rb were filled|מָל֧וּ\rb* \rb with violence|חָמָ֖ס\rb*, \rb and you sinned|וַֽתֶּחֱטָ֑א\rb*.
\q1 \rb So I drove you in disgrace|וָאֶחַלֶּלְךָ֩\rb*
\q2 \rb from the mountain|מֵהַ֨ר\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֤ים\rb*,
\q1 \rb and I banished you|וָֽאַבֶּדְךָ֙\rb*, \rb O guardian|הַסֹּכֵ֔ךְ\rb* \rb cherub|כְּר֣וּב\rb*,
\q2 \rb from among|מִתּ֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the fiery|אֵֽשׁ׃\rb* \rb stones|אַבְנֵי־\rb*.
\q1 \v 17 \rb Your heart|לִבְּךָ֙\rb* \rb grew proud|גָּבַ֤הּ\rb* \rb of your beauty|בְּיָפְיֶ֔ךָ\rb*;
\q2 \rb you corrupted|שִׁחַ֥תָּ\rb* \rb your wisdom|חָכְמָתְךָ֖\rb* \rb because|עַל־\rb* \rb of your splendor|יִפְעָתֶ֑ךָ\rb*;
\q1 \rb so I cast you|הִשְׁלַכְתִּ֗יךָ\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the earth|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb*;
\q2 \rb I made you|נְתַתִּ֖יךָ\rb* \rb a spectacle|לְרַ֥אֲוָה\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֧י\rb* \rb kings|מְלָכִ֛ים\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 18 \rb By the multitude|מֵרֹ֣ב\rb* \rb of your iniquities|עֲוֺנֶ֗יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and the dishonesty|בְּעֶ֙וֶל֙\rb* \rb of your trading|רְכֻלָּ֣תְךָ֔\rb*
\q2 \rb you have profaned|חִלַּ֖לְתָּ\rb* \rb your sanctuaries|מִקְדָּשֶׁ֑יךָ\rb*.
\q1 \rb So I made fire|אֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb come|וָֽאוֹצִא־\rb* \rb from within you|מִתּֽוֹכְךָ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb and it|הִ֣יא\rb* \rb consumed you|אֲכָלַ֔תְךָ\rb*.
\q1 \rb I reduced|וָאֶתֶּנְךָ֤\rb* \rb you to ashes|לְאֵ֙פֶר֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the ground|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb in the eyes|לְעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who saw you|רֹאֶֽיךָ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 19 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb the nations|בָּֽעַמִּ֔ים\rb* \rb who know you|יוֹדְעֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb are appalled|שָׁמְמ֖וּ\rb* \rb over you|עָלֶ֑יךָ\rb*.
\q1 \rb You have come|הָיִ֔יתָ\rb* \rb to a horrible end|בַּלָּה֣וֹת\rb*
\q2 \rb and will be no more|וְאֵינְךָ֖\rb*\rb |עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָֽם׃פ\rb*.’”
\s1 A Prophecy against Sidon
\p \v 20 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 21 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*, \rb set|שִׂ֥ים\rb* \rb your face|פָּנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Sidon|צִיד֑וֹן\rb* \rb and prophesy|וְהִנָּבֵ֖א\rb* \rb against her|עָלֶֽיהָ׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb And you are to declare|וְאָמַרְתָּ֗\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\rb Behold|הִנְנִ֤י\rb*, \rb I am against you|עָלַ֙יִךְ֙\rb*, \rb O Sidon|צִיד֔וֹן\rb*,
\q2 \rb and I will be glorified|וְנִכְבַּדְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb within you|בְּתוֹכֵ֑ךְ\rb*.
\q1 \rb They will know|וְֽיָדְע֞וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*
\q2 \rb when I execute|בַּעֲשׂ֥וֹתִי\rb* \rb judgments|שְׁפָטִ֖ים\rb* \rb against her|בָ֛הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and demonstrate My holiness|וְנִקְדַּ֥שְׁתִּי\rb* \rb through her|בָֽהּ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 23 \rb I will send|וְשִׁלַּחְתִּי־\rb* \rb a plague|דֶּ֤בֶר\rb* \rb against her|בָ֞הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb and shed blood|וָדָם֙\rb* \rb in her streets|בְּח֣וּצוֹתֶ֔יהָ\rb*;
\q1 \rb the slain|חָלָל֙\rb* \rb will fall|וְנִפְלַ֤ל\rb* \rb within her|בְּתוֹכָ֔הּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb while the sword|בְּחֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb is against her|עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb on every side|מִסָּבִ֑יב\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \rb Then they will know|וְיָדְע֖וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb For the people|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb will|יִהְיֶ֨ה\rb* \rb no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer face|ע֜וֹד\rb* \rb a pricking|מַמְאִיר֙\rb* \rb brier|סִלּ֤וֹן\rb* \rb or a painful|מַכְאִ֔ב\rb* \rb thorn|וְק֣וֹץ\rb* \rb from all|מִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb around them|סְבִ֣יבֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb who treat them with contempt|הַשָּׁאטִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֑ם\rb*. \rb Then they will know|וְיָ֣דְע֔וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃ס\rb*.’
\s1 The Restoration of Israel
\r (\ref Jeremiah 30:1–17|JER 30:1-17\ref*)
\p \v 25 \rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִה֒\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֮\rb*: ‘\rb When I gather|בְּקַבְּצִ֣י׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the peoples|הָֽעַמִּים֙\rb* \rb among whom|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they have been scattered|נָפֹ֣צוּ\rb*, \rb I will show Myself holy|וְנִקְדַּ֥שְׁתִּי\rb* \rb among them|בָ֖ם\rb* \rb in the sight|לְעֵינֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb*.
\p \rb Then they will dwell|וְיָֽשְׁבוּ֙\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb their own land|אַדְמָתָ֔ם\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have given|נָתַ֖תִּי\rb* \rb to My servant|לְעַבְדִּ֥י\rb* \rb Jacob|לְיַעֲקֹֽב׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb And there they will dwell|וְיָשְׁב֣וּ\rb*\rb |עָלֶיהָ֮\rb* \rb securely|לָבֶטַח֒\rb*, \rb build|וּבָנ֤וּ\rb* \rb houses|בָתִּים֙\rb*, \rb and plant|וְנָטְע֣וּ\rb* \rb vineyards|כְרָמִ֔ים\rb*. \rb They will dwell|וְיָשְׁב֖וּ\rb* \rb securely|לָבֶ֑טַח\rb* \rb when I execute|בַּעֲשׂוֹתִ֣י\rb* \rb judgments|שְׁפָטִ֗ים\rb* \rb against all those|בְּכֹ֨ל\rb* \rb around them|מִסְּבִ֣יבוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb who treat them with contempt|הַשָּׁאטִ֤ים\rb*\rb |אֹתָם֙\rb*. \rb Then they will know|וְיָ֣דְע֔וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb their God|אֱלֹהֵיהֶֽם׃ס\rb*.’”
\c 29
\s1 A Prophecy against Pharaoh
\p \v 1 \rb In the tenth|הָעֲשִׂירִ֔ית\rb* \rb year|בַּשָּׁנָה֙\rb*, \rb on the twelfth|בִּשְׁנֵ֥ים\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb day|לַחֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the tenth month|בָּעֲשִׂרִ֕י\rb*, \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*, \rb set|שִׂ֣ים\rb* \rb your face|פָּנֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb and prophesy|וְהִנָּבֵ֣א\rb* \rb against him|עָלָ֔יו\rb* \rb and against|וְעַל־\rb* \rb all|כֻּלָּֽהּ׃\rb* \rb Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb*. \v 3 \rb Speak|דַּבֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb to him and tell him|וְאָמַרְתָּ֜\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר׀\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \rb Behold|הִנְנִ֤י\rb*, \rb I am against you|עָלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb O Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֣ה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*,
\q1 \rb O great|הַגָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb monster|הַתַּנִּים֙\rb* \rb who lies|הָרֹבֵ֖ץ\rb*
\q2 \rb among|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb his rivers|יְאֹרָ֑יו\rb*,
\q1 \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֛ר\rb*, ‘\rb The Nile is mine|יְאֹרִ֖י\rb*;
\q2 \rb I|וַאֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb made it myself|עֲשִׂיתִֽנִי׃\rb*.’
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb But I will put|וְנָתַתִּ֤י\rb* \rb hooks|חַחִיִּים\rb* \rb in your jaws|בִּלְחָיֶ֔יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and cause|וְהִדְבַּקְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb the fish|דְגַת־\rb* \rb of your streams|יְאֹרֶ֖יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb to cling to your scales|בְּקַשְׂקְשֹׂתֶ֑יךָ\rb*.
\q1 \rb I will haul you up|וְהַעֲלִיתִ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb out of|מִתּ֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb your rivers|יְאֹרֶ֔יךָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the fish|דְּגַ֣ת\rb* \rb of your streams|יְאֹרֶ֔יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb will cling|תִּדְבָּֽק׃\rb* \rb to your scales|בְּקַשְׂקְשֹׂתֶ֖יךָ\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb I will leave|וּנְטַשְׁתִּ֣יךָ\rb* \rb you in the desert|הַמִּדְבָּ֗רָה\rb*,
\q2 \rb you|אוֹתְךָ֙\rb* \rb and|וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the fish|דְּגַ֣ת\rb* \rb of your streams|יְאֹרֶ֔יךָ\rb*.
\q1 \rb You will fall|תִּפּ֔וֹל\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the open|פְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb field|הַשָּׂדֶה֙\rb*
\q2 \rb and will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb be taken away|תֵאָסֵ֖ף\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֣א\rb*
\q2 \rb or gathered for burial|תִקָּבֵ֑ץ\rb*.
\q1 \rb I have given you|נְתַתִּ֥יךָ\rb* \rb as food|לְאָכְלָֽה׃\rb*
\q2 \rb to the beasts|לְחַיַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֛רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb and the birds|וּלְע֥וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמַ֖יִם\rb*.
\q1 \v 6 \rb Then all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb will know|וְיָֽדְעוּ֙\rb* \rb that|כִּ֖י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \rb For|יַ֧עַן\rb* \rb you were only|הֱיוֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb a staff|מִשְׁעֶ֥נֶת\rb* \rb of reeds|קָנֶ֖ה\rb*
\q2 \rb to the house|לְבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb When Israel took hold|בְּתָפְשָׂ֨ם\rb* \rb of you|בְּךָ֤\rb* \rb with their hands|בַכַּפְךָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb you splintered|תֵּר֔וֹץ\rb*, \rb tearing|וּבָקַעְתָּ֥\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb their|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb shoulders|כָּתֵ֑ף\rb*;
\q1 \rb when they leaned|וּבְהִֽשָּׁעֲנָ֤ם\rb* \rb on you|עָלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb you broke|תִּשָּׁבֵ֔ר\rb*, \rb and their backs|מָתְנָֽיִם׃ס\rb* \rb were wrenched|וְהַעֲמַדְתָּ֥\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*.\f + \fr 29:7 \ft Syriac (see also LXX and Vulgate); Hebrew \fqa and you caused their loins to shake.\f*
\s1 The Desolation of Egypt
\p \v 8 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֛י\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: \rb I will bring|מֵבִ֥יא\rb* \rb a sword|חָ֑רֶב\rb* \rb against you|עָלַ֖יִךְ\rb* \rb and cut off|וְהִכְרַתִּ֥י\rb* \rb from you|מִמֵּ֖ךְ\rb* \rb man|אָדָ֥ם\rb* \rb and beast|וּבְהֵמָֽה׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb The land|אֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb will become|וְהָיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb a desolate|לִשְׁמָמָ֣ה\rb* \rb wasteland|וְחָרְבָּ֔ה\rb*. \rb Then they will know|וְיָדְע֖וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*.
\p \rb Because|יַ֧עַן\rb* \rb you said|אָמַ֛ר\rb*, ‘\rb The Nile is|יְאֹ֥ר\rb* \rb mine|לִ֖י\rb*; \rb I|וַאֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb made it|עָשִֽׂיתִי׃\rb*,’ \v 10 \rb therefore|לָכֵ֛ן\rb* \rb I am|הִנְנִ֥י\rb* \rb against you|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb and against|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb your rivers|יְאֹרֶ֑יךָ\rb*. \rb I will turn|וְנָתַתִּ֞י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֗יִם\rb* \rb into a ruin|לְחָרְבוֹת֙\rb*, \rb a desolate|שְׁמָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb wasteland|חֹ֣רֶב\rb* \rb from Migdol|מִמִּגְדֹּ֥ל\rb* \rb to Syene|סְוֵנֵ֖ה\rb*, \rb and as far as|וְעַד־\rb* \rb the border|גְּב֥וּל\rb* \rb of Cush|כּֽוּשׁ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 29:10 \ft That is, the upper Nile region\f* \v 11 \rb No|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb foot|רֶ֣גֶל\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb or|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb beast|בְּהֵמָ֖ה\rb* \rb will pass|תַעֲבָר־\rb* \rb through|בָּהּ֙\rb*,\rb |וְרֶ֥גֶל\rb*\rb |תַעֲבָר־\rb* \rb and|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb it will be uninhabited|תֵשֵׁ֖ב\rb* \rb for forty|אַרְבָּעִ֥ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb I will make|וְנָתַתִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|אֶרֶץ֩\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֨יִם\rb* \rb a desolation|שְׁמָמָ֜ה\rb* \rb among|בְּת֣וֹךְ׀\rb* \rb desolate|נְשַׁמּ֗וֹת\rb* \rb lands|אֲרָצ֣וֹת\rb*, \rb and her cities|וְעָרֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb will lie|תִּֽהְיֶ֣יןָ\rb* \rb desolate|שְׁמָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb for forty|אַרְבָּעִ֖ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָ֑ה\rb* \rb among|בְּת֨וֹךְ\rb* \rb the ruined|מָֽחֳרָבוֹת֙\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֤ים\rb*. \rb And I will disperse|וַהֲפִצֹתִ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb and scatter them|וְֽזֵרִיתִ֖ים\rb* \rb throughout the countries|בָּאֲרָצֽוֹת׃פ\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb For|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*: \rb At the end|מִקֵּ֞ץ\rb* \rb of forty|אַרְבָּעִ֤ים\rb* \rb years|שָׁנָה֙\rb* \rb I will gather|אֲקַבֵּ֣ץ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the nations|הָעַמִּ֖ים\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they were scattered|נָפֹ֥צוּ\rb*\rb |שָֽׁמָּה׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb I will restore|וְשַׁבְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb from captivity|שְׁב֣וּת\rb*\f + \fr 29:14 \ft Or \fqa restore the fortunes of Egypt\f* \rb and bring them back|וַהֲשִׁבֹתִ֤י\rb*\rb |אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Pathros|פַּתְר֔וֹס\rb*, \rb the land|אֶ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb of their origin|מְכֽוּרָתָ֑ם\rb*. \rb There|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb they will be|וְהָ֥יוּ\rb* \rb a lowly|שְׁפָלָֽה׃\rb* \rb kingdom|מַמְלָכָ֥ה\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb |מִן־\rb* \rb Egypt will be|תִּהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb the lowliest|שְׁפָלָ֔ה\rb* \rb of kingdoms|הַמַּמְלָכוֹת֙\rb* \rb and will never|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb again|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb exalt itself|תִתְנַשֵּׂ֥א\rb* \rb above|עַל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb*. \rb For I will diminish Egypt|וְהִ֨מְעַטְתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb so that it will never again|לְבִלְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb rule|רְד֥וֹת\rb* \rb over the nations|בַּגּוֹיִֽם׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb Egypt will never|וְלֹ֣א\rb*\rb |עוֹד֩\rb* \rb again be|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb an object of trust|לְמִבְטָח֙\rb* \rb for the house|לְבֵ֨ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֤ל\rb*, \rb but will remind them|מַזְכִּ֣יר\rb* \rb of their iniquity|עָוֺ֔ן\rb* \rb in turning|בִּפְנוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb to the Egyptians|אַחֲרֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Then they will know|וְיָ֣דְע֔וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb am the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃פ\rb*.”
\s1 Egypt the Reward of Nebuchadnezzar
\p \v 17 \rb In the twenty-seventh|בְּעֶשְׂרִ֤ים\rb*\rb |וָשֶׁ֙בַע֙\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*, \rb on the first|בְּאֶחָ֣ד\rb* \rb day|לַחֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the first month|בָּֽרִאשׁ֖וֹן\rb*, \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 18 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְרֶאצַּ֣ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּ֠בֶל\rb* \rb caused his army|חֵיל֜וֹ\rb* \rb to labor|הֶעֱבִ֨יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb strenuously|עֲבֹדָ֤ה\rb*\rb |גְדֹלָה֙\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Tyre|צֹ֔ר\rb*. \rb Every|כָּל־\rb* \rb head|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb was made bald|מֻקְרָ֔ח\rb* \rb and every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb shoulder|כָּתֵ֖ף\rb* \rb made raw|מְרוּטָ֑ה\rb*. \rb But he|ל֤וֹ\rb* \rb and his army|וּלְחֵילוֹ֙\rb* \rb received|הָ֨יָה\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb wages|וְ֠שָׂכָר\rb* \rb from Tyre|מִצֹּ֔ר\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the labor|הָעֲבֹדָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they expended|עָבַ֥ד\rb* \rb on it|עָלֶֽיהָ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֥י\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: \rb I will give|נֹתֵ֛ן\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb to Nebuchadnezzar|לִנְבוּכַדְרֶאצַּ֥ר\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb who will carry off|וְנָשָׂ֨א\rb* \rb its wealth|הֲמֹנָ֜הּ\rb*, \rb seize|וְשָׁלַ֤ל\rb* \rb its spoil|שְׁלָלָהּ֙\rb*, \rb and remove|וּבָזַ֣ז\rb* \rb its plunder|בִּזָּ֔הּ\rb*. \rb This will be|וְהָיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb the wages|שָׂכָ֖ר\rb* \rb for his army|לְחֵילֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb I have given|נָתַ֥תִּי\rb* \rb him|ל֖וֹ\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb* \rb as the reward|פְּעֻלָּתוֹ֙\rb* \rb for his labor|עָ֣בַד\rb*, \rb because|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb it was done|עָ֣שׂוּ\rb* \rb for Me|לִ֔י\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb In that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb I will cause a horn|קֶ֙רֶן֙\rb* \rb to sprout|אַצְמִ֤יחַ\rb* \rb for the house|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb and|וּלְךָ֛\rb* \rb I will open|אֶתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb your mouth|פֶּ֖ה\rb* \rb to speak|פִּתְחֽוֹן־\rb* \rb among them|בְּתוֹכָ֑ם\rb*. \rb Then they will know|וְיָדְע֖וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.”
\c 30
\s1 A Lament for Egypt
\p \v 1 \rb Again the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*, \rb prophesy|הִנָּבֵא֙\rb* \rb and declare|וְאָ֣מַרְתָּ֔\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \rb Wail|הֵילִ֖ילוּ\rb*, ‘\rb Alas|הָ֥הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb for that day|לַיּֽוֹם׃\rb*!’
\q1 \v 3 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the day is|י֔וֹם\rb* \rb near|קָר֣וֹב\rb*,
\q2 \rb the Day|י֖וֹם\rb* \rb of the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb is near|וְקָר֥וֹב\rb*.
\q1 \rb It will be|יִֽהְיֶֽה׃\rb* \rb a day|י֣וֹם\rb* \rb of clouds|עָנָ֔ן\rb*,
\q2 \rb a time|עֵ֥ת\rb* \rb of doom for the nations|גּוֹיִ֖ם\rb*.\f + \fr 30:3 \ft Hebrew does not include \fqa of doom\ft .\f*
\b 
\q1 \v 4 \rb A sword|חֶ֙רֶב֙\rb* \rb will come|וּבָאָ֥ה\rb* \rb against Egypt|בְּמִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*,
\q2 \rb |וְהָיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb and there will be anguish|חַלְחָלָה֙\rb* \rb in Cush|בְּכ֔וּשׁ\rb*\f + \fr 30:4 \ft That is, the upper Nile region; also in verses 5 and 9\f*
\q1 \rb when the slain|חָלָ֖ל\rb* \rb fall|בִּנְפֹ֥ל\rb* \rb in Egypt|בְּמִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*,
\q2 \rb its wealth|הֲמוֹנָ֔הּ\rb* \rb is taken away|וְלָקְח֣וּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb and its foundations|יְסוֹדֹתֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \rb are torn down|וְנֶהֶרְס֖וּ\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb Cush|כּ֣וּשׁ\rb*, \rb Put|וּפ֤וּט\rb*, \rb and Lud|וְלוּד֙\rb*,\f + \fr 30:5 \ft Or \fqa Lydia\f*
\q2 \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the various peoples|הָעֶ֣רֶב\rb*,
\q1 \rb as well as Libya|וְכ֔וּב\rb* \rb and the men|וּבְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the covenant|הַבְּרִ֑ית\rb* \rb land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb*,
\q2 \rb will fall|יִפֹּֽלוּ׃פ\rb* \rb with Egypt|אִתָּ֖ם\rb* \rb by the sword|בַּחֶ֥רֶב\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 6 \rb For this is what|כֹּ֚ה\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \rb The allies|סֹמְכֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb will fall|וְנָֽפְלוּ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb and her proud|גְּא֣וֹן\rb* \rb strength|עֻזָּ֑הּ\rb* \rb will collapse|וְיָרַ֖ד\rb*.
\q1 \rb From Migdol|מִמִּגְדֹּ֣ל\rb* \rb to Syene|סְוֵנֵ֗ה\rb*\f + \fr 30:6 \ft That is, Aswan; see \ref Isaiah 49:12|ISA 49:12\ref*\f*
\q2 \rb they will fall|יִפְּלוּ־\rb* \rb by the sword|בַּחֶ֙רֶב֙\rb* \rb within her|בָ֔הּ\rb*,
\qr \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 7 \rb They will be desolate|וְנָשַׁ֕מּוּ\rb* \rb among|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb desolate|נְשַׁמּ֑וֹת\rb* \rb lands|אֲרָצ֣וֹת\rb*,
\q2 \rb and their cities|וְעָרָ֕יו\rb* \rb will lie|תִּֽהְיֶֽינָה׃\rb* \rb among|בְּתוֹךְ־\rb* \rb ruined|נַחֲרָב֖וֹת\rb* \rb cities|עָרִ֥ים\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 8 \rb Then they will know|וְיָדְע֖וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*
\q2 \rb when I set|בְּתִתִּי־\rb* \rb fire|אֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb to Egypt|בְּמִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb her helpers|עֹזְרֶֽיהָ׃\rb* \rb are shattered|וְנִשְׁבְּר֖וּ\rb*.
\b 
\li1 \v 9 \rb On that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb messengers|מַלְאָכִ֤ים\rb* \rb will go out|יֵצְא֨וּ\rb* \rb from Me|מִלְּפָנַי֙\rb* \rb in ships|בַּצִּ֔ים\rb* \rb to frighten|לְהַחֲרִ֖יד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Cush|כּ֣וּשׁ\rb* \rb out of complacency|בֶּ֑טַח\rb*. \rb Anguish|חַלְחָלָ֤ה\rb* \rb will come|וְהָיְתָ֨ה\rb* \rb upon them|בָהֶם֙\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb of Egypt’s doom|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*.\f + \fr 30:9 \ft Hebrew \fqa the day of Egypt\f* \rb For|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb it is indeed|הִנֵּ֖ה\rb* \rb coming|בָּאָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 10 \rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \rb I will put an end|וְהִשְׁבַּתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the hordes|הֲמ֣וֹן\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb by the hand|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb of Nebuchadnezzar|נְבוּכַדְרֶאצַּ֥ר\rb* \rb king|מֶלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶֽל׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 11 \rb He|ה֠וּא\rb* \rb and his people|וְעַמּ֤וֹ\rb* \rb with him|אִתּוֹ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb the most ruthless|עָרִיצֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the nations|גוֹיִ֔ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb will be brought in|מֽוּבָאִ֖ים\rb* \rb to destroy|לְשַׁחֵ֣ת\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*.
\q1 \rb They will draw|וְהֵרִ֤יקוּ\rb* \rb their swords|חַרְבוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb and fill|וּמָלְא֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb with the slain|חָלָֽל׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 12 \rb I will make|וְנָתַתִּ֤י\rb* \rb the streams|יְאֹרִים֙\rb* \rb dry up|חָֽרָבָ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and sell|וּמָכַרְתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb to|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb the wicked|רָעִ֑ים\rb*.
\q1 \rb By the hands|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of foreigners|זָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb I will bring desolation|וַהֲשִׁמֹּתִ֞י\rb*
\q2 \rb upon the land|אֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb and everything in it|וּמְלֹאָהּ֙\rb*.
\qr \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb have spoken|דִּבַּֽרְתִּי׃ס\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 13 \rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֞ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \rb I will destroy|וְהַאֲבַדְתִּ֨י\rb* \rb the idols|גִלּוּלִ֜ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and put an end|וְהִשְׁבַּתִּ֤י\rb* \rb to the images|אֱלִילִים֙\rb* \rb in Memphis|מִנֹּ֔ף\rb*.\f + \fr 30:13 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa Noph\ft ; also in verse 16\f*
\q1 \rb There will no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb longer|ע֑וֹד\rb* \rb be|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb a prince|וְנָשִׂ֥יא\rb*\rb |מֵאֶֽרֶץ־\rb* \rb in Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and I will instill|וְנָתַתִּ֥י\rb* \rb fear|יִרְאָ֖ה\rb* \rb in that land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb*\rb |מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 14 \rb I will lay waste|וַהֲשִׁמֹּתִי֙\rb* \rb Pathros|פַּתְר֔וֹס\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*,
\q2 \rb set|וְנָתַ֥תִּי\rb* \rb fire|אֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb to Zoan|בְּצֹ֑עַן\rb*,
\q2 \rb and execute|וְעָשִׂ֥יתִי\rb* \rb judgment|שְׁפָטִ֖ים\rb* \rb on Thebes|בְּנֹֽא׃\rb*.\f + \fr 30:14 \ft Hebrew \fqa No\ft ; also in verses 15 and 16\f*
\q1 \v 15 \rb I will pour out|וְשָׁפַכְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb My wrath|חֲמָתִ֔י\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb Pelusium|סִ֖ין\rb*,\f + \fr 30:15 \ft Hebrew \fqa Sin\ft ; also in verse 16\f*
\q2 \rb the stronghold|מָע֣וֹז\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָ֑יִם\rb*,
\q2 \rb and cut off|וְהִכְרַתִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the crowds|הֲמ֥וֹן\rb* \rb of Thebes|נֹֽא׃\rb*.
