\s1 Pharaoh’s Power Broken
\p \v 20 \rb In the eleventh|בְּאַחַ֤ת\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵה֙\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*, \rb on the seventh|בְּשִׁבְעָ֣ה\rb* \rb day|לַחֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the first month|בָּֽרִאשׁ֖וֹן\rb*, \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 21 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb I have broken|שָׁבָ֑רְתִּי\rb* \rb the arm|זְר֛וֹעַ\rb* \rb of Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֥ה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb*. \rb See|וְהִנֵּ֣ה\rb*, \rb it has not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb been bound up|חֻ֠בְּשָׁה\rb* \rb for healing|רְפֻא֜וֹת\rb*,\rb |לָתֵ֨ת\rb*\rb |לָשׂ֥וּם\rb* \rb or splinted|חִתּ֛וּל\rb*\rb |לְחָבְשָׁ֥הּ\rb* \rb for strength|לְחָזְקָ֖הּ\rb* \rb to hold|לִתְפֹּ֥שׂ\rb* \rb the sword|בֶּחָֽרֶב׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֞ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהֹוִ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר׀\rb*: \rb Behold|הִנְנִי֙\rb*, \rb I am against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֣ה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*. \rb I will break|וְשָֽׁבַרְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his arms|זְרֹ֣עֹתָ֔יו\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb both the strong one|הַחֲזָקָ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the one already broken|הַנִּשְׁבָּ֑רֶת\rb*, \rb and will make the sword|הַחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb fall|וְהִפַּלְתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb from his hand|מִיָּדֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb I will disperse|וַהֲפִצוֹתִ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb* \rb and scatter them|וְזֵרִיתִ֖ם\rb* \rb throughout the lands|בָּאֲרָצֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb I will strengthen|וְחִזַּקְתִּ֗י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the arms|זְרֹעוֹת֙\rb* \rb of Babylon’s|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb and place|וְנָתַתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My sword|חַרְבִּ֖י\rb* \rb in his hand|בְּיָד֑וֹ\rb*, \rb but I will break|וְשָׁבַרְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the arms|זְרֹע֣וֹת\rb* \rb of Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֔ה\rb*, \rb who will groan|וְנָאַ֛ק\rb* \rb before him|לְפָנָֽיו׃\rb* \rb like|נַאֲק֥וֹת\rb* \rb a mortally wounded man|חָלָ֖ל\rb*. \v 25 \rb I will strengthen|וְהַחֲזַקְתִּ֗י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the arms|זְרֹעוֹת֙\rb* \rb of Babylon’s|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb* \rb king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb*, \rb but Pharaoh’s|פַּרְעֹ֖ה\rb* \rb arms|וּזְרֹע֥וֹת\rb* \rb will fall limp|תִּפֹּ֑לְנָה\rb*.
\p \rb Then they will know|וְֽיָדְע֞וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb when I place|בְּתִתִּ֤י\rb* \rb My sword|חַרְבִּי֙\rb* \rb in the hand|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb of Babylon’s|בָּבֶ֔ל\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb*, \rb and he wields|וְנָטָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb it against|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרָֽיִם׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb I will disperse|וַהֲפִצוֹתִ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Egyptians|מִצְרַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb and scatter|וְזֵרִיתִ֥י\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb throughout the lands|בָּאֲרָצ֑וֹת\rb*. \rb Then they will know|וְיָדְע֖וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.”
