\p \v 10 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: ‘\rb Since|יַ֕עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb it became great|גָּבַ֖הְתָּ\rb*\f + \fr 31:10 \ft Hebrew \fqa you became great\f* \rb in height|בְּקוֹמָ֑ה\rb* \rb and set|וַיִּתֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb its top|צַמַּרְתּוֹ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb among|בֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb the clouds|עֲבוֹתִ֔ים\rb*,\f + \fr 31:10 \ft Or \fqa through the thick boughs\f* \rb and it grew proud|וְרָ֥ם\rb*\rb |לְבָב֖וֹ\rb* \rb on account of its height|בְּגָבְהֽוֹ׃\rb*, \v 11 \rb I delivered it|וְאֶ֨תְּנֵ֔הוּ\rb* \rb into the hand|בְּיַ֖ד\rb* \rb of the ruler|אֵ֣יל\rb* \rb of the nations|גּוֹיִ֑ם\rb*, \rb for him|עָשׂ֤וֹ\rb* \rb to deal|יַֽעֲשֶׂה֙\rb* \rb with it|ל֔וֹ\rb* \rb according to its wickedness|כְּרִשְׁע֖וֹ\rb*. \rb I have banished it|גֵּרַשְׁתִּֽהוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Foreigners|זָרִ֛ים\rb*, \rb the most ruthless|עָרִיצֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the nations|גוֹיִ֖ם\rb*, \rb cut it down|וַיִּכְרְתֻ֧הוּ\rb* \rb and left it|וַֽיִּטְּשֻׁ֑הוּ\rb*. \rb Its branches|דָלִיּוֹתָ֗יו\rb* \rb have fallen|נָפְל֣וּ\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the mountains|הֶ֠הָרִים\rb* \rb and in every|וּבְכָל־\rb* \rb valley|גֵּ֨אָי֜וֹת\rb*; \rb its boughs|פֹֽארֹתָיו֙\rb* \rb lay broken|וַתִּשָּׁבַ֤רְנָה\rb* \rb in all|בְּכֹל֙\rb* \rb the earth’s|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb ravines|אֲפִיקֵ֣י\rb*. \rb And all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the peoples|עַמֵּ֥י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb left|וַיֵּרְד֧וּ\rb* \rb its shade|מִצִּלּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb and abandoned it|וַֽיִּטְּשֻֽׁהוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb the birds|ע֣וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמָ֑יִם\rb* \rb nested|יִשְׁכְּנ֖וּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb its fallen trunk|מַפַּלְתּ֥וֹ\rb*, \rb and all|כֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the beasts|חַיַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶֽה׃\rb* \rb lived|הָי֔וּ\rb* \rb among|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb its boughs|פֹּארֹתָ֣יו\rb*. \v 14 \rb This happened so that|לְמַ֡עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb no|לֹא־\rb* \rb other|כָּל־\rb* \rb trees|עֲצֵי־\rb* \rb by the waters|מַ֗יִם\rb* \rb would become great|יִגְבְּה֨וּ\rb* \rb in height|בְקוֹמָתָ֜ם\rb* \rb and|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb set|יִתְּנ֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their tops|צַמַּרְתָּם֙\rb* \rb among|בֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb the clouds|עֲבֹתִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and no other|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb well-watered|שֹׁ֣תֵי\rb*\rb |מָ֑יִם\rb* \rb trees|אֵלֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb would reach them|יַעַמְד֧וּ\rb* \rb in height|בְּגָבְהָ֖ם\rb*.\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they have all|כֻלָּם֩\rb* \rb been consigned|נִתְּנ֨וּ\rb* \rb to death|לַמָּ֜וֶת\rb*, \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the depths|תַּחְתִּ֗ית\rb* \rb of the earth|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb*, \rb among|בְּת֛וֹךְ\rb* \rb the mortals|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |אָדָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb who descend|י֥וֹרְדֵי\rb* \rb to the Pit|בֽוֹר׃ס\rb*.’
\p \v 15 \rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֞ר\rb*: ‘\rb On the day|בְּי֨וֹם\rb* \rb it was brought down|רִדְתּ֤וֹ\rb* \rb to Sheol|שְׁא֙וֹלָה֙\rb*, \rb I caused mourning|הֶאֱבַ֜לְתִּי\rb*. \rb I covered|כִּסֵּ֤תִי\rb* \rb the deep|תְּה֔וֹם\rb* \rb because of it|עָלָיו֙\rb*;\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb I held back|וָֽאֶמְנַע֙\rb* \rb its rivers|נַהֲרוֹתֶ֔יהָ\rb*; \rb its abundant|רַבִּ֑ים\rb* \rb waters|מַ֣יִם\rb* \rb were restrained|וַיִּכָּלְא֖וּ\rb*. \rb I made Lebanon|לְבָנ֔וֹן\rb* \rb mourn|וָאַקְדִּ֤ר\rb* \rb for it|עָלָיו֙\rb*, \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the trees|עֲצֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb fainted|עֻלְפֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb because of it|עָלָ֥יו\rb*. \v 16 \rb I made the nations|גוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb quake|הִרְעַ֣שְׁתִּי\rb* \rb at the sound|מִקּ֤וֹל\rb* \rb of its downfall|מַפַּלְתּוֹ֙\rb*, \rb when I cast it down|בְּהוֹרִדִ֥י\rb*\rb |אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb to Sheol|שְׁא֖וֹלָה\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb those who descend|י֣וֹרְדֵי\rb* \rb to the Pit|ב֑וֹר\rb*.
\p \rb Then all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the trees|עֲצֵי־\rb* \rb of Eden|עֵ֔דֶן\rb*, \rb the choicest|מִבְחַ֥ר\rb* \rb and best|וְטוֹב־\rb* \rb of Lebanon|לְבָנ֖וֹן\rb*, \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the well-watered trees|שֹׁ֥תֵי\rb*\rb |מָֽיִם׃\rb*, \rb were consoled|וַיִּנָּ֨חֲמ֜וּ\rb* \rb in the earth|בְּאֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb below|תַּחְתִּית֙\rb*. \v 17 \rb They|הֵ֗ם\rb* \rb too|גַּם־\rb* \rb descended|יָרְד֥וּ\rb* \rb with it|אִתּ֛וֹ\rb* \rb to Sheol|שְׁא֖וֹלָה\rb*, \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb those slain|חַלְלֵי־\rb* \rb by the sword|חָ֑רֶב\rb*. \rb As its allies|וּזְרֹע֛וֹ\rb* \rb they had lived|יָשְׁב֥וּ\rb* \rb in its shade|בְצִלּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb among|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the nations|גּוֹיִֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb Who|מִ֨י\rb* \rb then|כָּ֛כָה\rb* \rb is like you|דָמִ֥יתָ\rb* \rb in glory|בְּכָב֥וֹד\rb* \rb and greatness|וּבְגֹ֖דֶל\rb* \rb among the trees|בַּעֲצֵי־\rb* \rb of Eden|עֵ֑דֶן\rb*? \rb You also will be brought down|וְהוּרַדְתָּ֨\rb* \rb to the depths|תַּחְתִּ֗ית\rb* \rb of the earth|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb to be with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the trees|עֲצֵי־\rb* \rb of Eden|עֵ֜דֶן\rb*.\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb You will lie|תִּשְׁכַּב֙\rb* \rb among|בְּת֨וֹךְ\rb* \rb the uncircumcised|עֲרֵלִ֤ים\rb*, \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb those slain|חַלְלֵי־\rb* \rb by the sword|חֶ֔רֶב\rb*. \rb This|ה֤וּא\rb* \rb is Pharaoh|פַרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his multitude|הֲמוֹנֹ֔ה\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃ס\rb*.’”
\c 32
\s1 A Lament for Pharaoh King of Egypt
\p \v 1 \rb In the twelfth|בִּשְׁתֵּ֣י\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֣ה\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*, \rb on the first|בְּאֶחָ֣ד\rb* \rb day|לַחֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the twelfth|בִּשְׁנֵי־\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb* \rb month|חֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb take up|שָׂ֤א\rb* \rb a lament|קִינָה֙\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֣ה\rb* \rb king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb* \rb and say|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb to him|אֵלָ֔יו\rb*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\rb You are like|נִדְמֵ֑יתָ\rb* \rb a lion|כְּפִ֥יר\rb* \rb among the nations|גּוֹיִ֖ם\rb*;
\q2 \rb you|וְאַתָּה֙\rb* \rb are like a monster|כַּתַּנִּ֣ים\rb* \rb in the seas|בַּיַּמִּ֔ים\rb*.
\q1 \rb You thrash about|וַתָּ֣גַח\rb* \rb in your rivers|בְּנַהֲרוֹתֶ֗יךָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb churning up|וַתִּדְלַח־\rb* \rb the waters|מַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb with your feet|בְּרַגְלֶ֔יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and muddying|וַתִּרְפֹּ֖ס\rb* \rb the streams|נַהֲרוֹתָֽם׃\rb*.’
\b 
\q1 \v 3 \rb This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\rb I will spread|וּפָרַשְׂתִּ֤י\rb* \rb My net|רִשְׁתִּ֔י\rb* \rb over you|עָלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*
\q2 \rb with a company|בִּקְהַ֖ל\rb* \rb of many|רַבִּ֑ים\rb* \rb peoples|עַמִּ֣ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb and they will draw you up|וְהֶעֱל֖וּךָ\rb* \rb in My net|בְּחֶרְמִֽי׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb I will abandon|וּנְטַשְׁתִּ֣יךָ\rb* \rb you on the land|בָאָ֔רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb and hurl you|אֲטִילֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb into|עַל־\rb* \rb the open|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb field|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb*.
\q1 \rb I will cause all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the birds|ע֣וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb to settle|וְהִשְׁכַּנְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb upon you|עָלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*,
\q1 \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the beasts|חַיַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*
\q2 \rb to eat their fill|וְהִשְׂבַּעְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb of you|מִמְּךָ֖\rb*.
\q1 \v 5 \rb I will put|וְנָתַתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your flesh|בְּשָׂרְךָ֖\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the mountains|הֶֽהָרִ֑ים\rb*
\q2 \rb and fill|וּמִלֵּאתִ֥י\rb* \rb the valleys|הַגֵּאָי֖וֹת\rb* \rb with your remains|רָמוּתֶֽךָ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 32:5 \ft Or \fqa your lofty stature\f*
\q1 \v 6 \rb I will drench|וְהִשְׁקֵיתִ֨י\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֧רֶץ\rb*
\q2 \rb with the flow|צָפָתְךָ֛\rb* \rb of your blood|מִדָּמְךָ֖\rb*,
\q1 \rb all the way to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the mountains|הֶֽהָרִ֑ים\rb* —
\q2 \rb the ravines|וַאֲפִקִ֖ים\rb* \rb will be filled|יִמָּלְא֥וּן\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 7 \rb When I extinguish you|בְכַבּֽוֹתְךָ֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb I will cover|וְכִסֵּיתִ֤י\rb* \rb the heavens|שָׁמַ֔יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb and darken|וְהִקְדַּרְתִּ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their stars|כֹּֽכְבֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb I will cover|אֲכַסֶּ֔נּוּ\rb* \rb the sun|שֶׁ֚מֶשׁ\rb* \rb with a cloud|בֶּעָנָ֣ן\rb*,
\q2 \rb and the moon|וְיָרֵ֖חַ\rb* \rb will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb give its light|יָאִ֥יר\rb*\rb |אוֹרֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 8 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb the shining|מְא֤וֹרֵי\rb* \rb lights|אוֹר֙\rb* \rb in the heavens|בַּשָּׁמַ֔יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb I will darken|אַקְדִּירֵ֖ם\rb* \rb over you|עָלֶ֑יךָ\rb*,
\q1 \rb and I will bring|וְנָתַ֤תִּי\rb* \rb darkness|חֹ֙שֶׁךְ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb upon|עַֽל־\rb* \rb your land|אַרְצְךָ֔\rb*,’
\qr \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 9 ‘\rb I will trouble|וְהִ֨כְעַסְתִּ֔י\rb* \rb the hearts|לֵ֖ב\rb* \rb of many|רַבִּ֑ים\rb* \rb peoples|עַמִּ֣ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb when I bring about|בַּהֲבִיאִ֤י\rb* \rb your destruction|שִׁבְרְךָ֙\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb countries|אֲרָצ֖וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 32:9 \ft Hebrew; LXX \fqa when I lead you into captivity among the nations, into countries\f*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you do not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb know|יְדַעְתָּֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 10 \rb I will cause many|רַבִּ֗ים\rb* \rb peoples|עַמִּ֣ים\rb*
\q2 \rb to be appalled|וַהֲשִׁמּוֹתִ֨י\rb* \rb over you|עָלֶ֜יךָ\rb*,
\q1 \rb and their kings|וּמַלְכֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb will shudder in horror|יִשְׂעֲר֤וּ\rb*\rb |שַׂ֔עַר\rb* \rb because of you|עָלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb when I brandish|בְּעוֹפְפִ֥י\rb* \rb My sword|חַרְבִּ֖י\rb* \rb before|עַל־\rb* \rb them|פְּנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb On the day|בְּי֖וֹם\rb* \rb of your downfall|מַפַּלְתֶּֽךָ׃ס\rb*
\q2 \rb each of them|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb will tremble|וְחָרְד֤וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb every moment|לִרְגָעִים֙\rb* \rb for his life|לְנַפְשׁ֔וֹ\rb*.’
\b 
\q1 \v 11 \rb For|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*:
\b 
\q1 ‘\rb The sword|חֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb of the king|מֶֽלֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Babylon|בָּבֶ֖ל\rb*
\q2 \rb will come against you|תְּבוֹאֶֽךָ׃\rb*!
\q1 \v 12 \rb I will make your hordes|הֲמוֹנֶ֔ךָ\rb* \rb fall|אַפִּ֣יל\rb*
\q2 \rb by the swords|בְּחַרְב֤וֹת\rb* \rb of the mighty|גִּבּוֹרִים֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb the most ruthless|עָרִיצֵ֥י\rb* \rb of all|כֻּלָּ֑ם\rb* \rb nations|גוֹיִ֖ם\rb*.
\q1 \rb They will ravage|וְשָֽׁדְדוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the pride|גְּא֣וֹן\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֔יִם\rb*
\q2 \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb her multitudes|הֲמוֹנָֽהּ׃\rb* \rb will be destroyed|וְנִשְׁמַ֖ד\rb*.
\q1 \v 13 \rb I will slaughter|וְהַֽאֲבַדְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb her cattle|בְּהֶמְתָּ֔הּ\rb*
\q2 \rb beside|מֵעַ֖ל\rb* \rb the abundant|רַבִּ֑ים\rb* \rb waters|מַ֣יִם\rb*.
\q1 \rb No|וְלֹ֨א\rb* \rb human|אָדָם֙\rb* \rb foot|רֶֽגֶל־\rb* \rb will muddy them|תִדְלָחֵ֤ם\rb* \rb again|ע֔וֹד\rb*,
\q2 \rb and no|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb cattle|בְּהֵמָ֖ה\rb* \rb hooves|וּפַרְס֥וֹת\rb* \rb will disturb them|תִדְלָחֵֽם׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 14 \rb Then|אָ֚ז\rb* \rb I will let her waters|מֵֽימֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb settle|אַשְׁקִ֣יעַ\rb*
\q2 \rb and will make her rivers|וְנַהֲרוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb flow|אוֹלִ֑יךְ\rb* \rb like oil|כַּשֶּׁ֣מֶן\rb*,’
\qr \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 15 ‘\rb When I make|בְּתִתִּי֩\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֨רֶץ\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֜יִם\rb* \rb a desolation|שְׁמָמָ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and empty|וּנְשַׁמָּ֗ה\rb* \rb it|אֶ֚רֶץ\rb* \rb of all that filled it|מִמְּלֹאָ֔הּ\rb*,
\q1 \rb when I strike down|בְּהַכּוֹתִ֖י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who live|י֣וֹשְׁבֵי\rb* \rb there|בָ֑הּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb then they will know|וְיָדְע֖וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.’
\p \v 16 \rb This|הִיא֙\rb* \rb is the lament|וְק֣וֹנְנ֔וּהָ\rb* \rb they will chant for her|קִינָ֥ה\rb*; \rb the daughters|בְּנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb* \rb will chant it|תְּקוֹנֵ֣נָּה\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֑הּ\rb*. \rb Over|עַל־\rb* \rb Egypt|מִצְרַ֤יִם\rb*\rb |וְעַל־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb her multitudes|הֲמוֹנָהּ֙\rb* \rb they will chant it|תְּקוֹנֵ֣נָּה\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֔הּ\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃פ\rb*.”
\s1 Egypt Cast into the Pit
\p \v 17 \rb In the twelfth|בִּשְׁתֵּ֣י\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֣ה\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb*, \rb on the fifteenth|בַּחֲמִשָּׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb day of the month|לַחֹ֑דֶשׁ\rb*,\f + \fr 32:17 \ft Presumably the fifteenth day of the twelfth month (see verse 1); LXX \fqa on the fifteenth day of the first month\ft .\f*\rb |הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַֽיְהִי֙\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 18 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*, \rb wail|נְהֵ֛ה\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb the multitudes|הֲמ֥וֹן\rb* \rb of Egypt|מִצְרַ֖יִם\rb*, \rb and consign|וְהוֹרִדֵ֑הוּ\rb* \rb her|א֠וֹתָהּ\rb* \rb and the daughters|וּבְנ֨וֹת\rb* \rb of the mighty|אַדִּרִ֛ם\rb* \rb nations|גּוֹיִ֧ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the depths|תַּחְתִּיּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the earth|אֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb those who descend|י֥וֹרְדֵי\rb* \rb to the Pit|בֽוֹר׃\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \v 19 \rb Whom|מִמִּ֖י\rb* \rb do you surpass in beauty|נָעָ֑מְתָּ\rb*?
\q2 \rb Go down|רְדָ֥ה\rb* \rb and be placed|וְהָשְׁכְּבָ֖ה\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the uncircumcised|עֲרֵלִֽים׃\rb*!
\q1 \v 20 \rb They will fall|יִפֹּ֑לוּ\rb* \rb among|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb those slain|חַלְלֵי־\rb* \rb by the sword|חֶ֖רֶב\rb*.
\q2 \rb The sword|חֶ֣רֶב\rb* \rb is appointed|נִתָּ֔נָה\rb*!
\q1 \rb Let them drag her away|מָשְׁכ֥וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb along with all|וְכָל־\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֖הּ\rb* \rb her multitudes|הֲמוֹנֶֽיהָ׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 21 \rb Mighty|גִבּוֹרִ֛ים\rb* \rb chiefs|אֵלֵ֧י\rb* \rb will speak|יְדַבְּרוּ־\rb* \rb from the midst|מִתּ֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb of Sheol|שְׁא֖וֹל\rb*
\q2 \rb about Egypt|אֶת־\rb* \rb and her allies|עֹֽזְרָ֑יו\rb*:
\q1 ‘\rb They have come down|יָֽרְד֛וּ\rb* \rb and lie|שָׁכְב֥וּ\rb* \rb with the uncircumcised|הָעֲרֵלִ֖ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb with those slain|חַלְלֵי־\rb* \rb by the sword|חָֽרֶב׃\rb*.’
\b 
\q1 \v 22 \rb Assyria|אַשּׁוּר֙\rb* \rb is there|שָׁ֤ם\rb* \rb with her whole|וְכָל־\rb* \rb company|קְהָלָ֔הּ\rb*;
\q2 \rb her graves|קִבְרֹתָ֑יו\rb* \rb are all around her|סְבִֽיבוֹתָ֖יו\rb*.
\q1 \rb All of them|כֻּלָּ֣ם\rb* \rb are slain|חֲלָלִ֔ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb fallen|הַנֹּפְלִ֖ים\rb* \rb by the sword|בֶּחָֽרֶב׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 23 \rb Her|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb graves|קִבְרֹתֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb are set|נִתְּנ֤וּ\rb* \rb in the depths|בְּיַרְכְּתֵי־\rb* \rb of the Pit|ב֔וֹר\rb*,
\q2 \rb and her company|קְהָלָ֔הּ\rb* \rb is|וַיְהִ֣י\rb* \rb all around|סְבִיב֖וֹת\rb* \rb her grave|קְבֻרָתָ֑הּ\rb*.
\q1 \rb All|כֻּלָּ֤ם\rb* \rb of them are slain|חֲלָלִים֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb fallen|נֹפְלִ֣ים\rb* \rb by the sword|בַּחֶ֔רֶב\rb*—
\q1 \rb those who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb once spread|נָתְנ֥וּ\rb* \rb terror|חִתִּ֖ית\rb*
\q2 \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of the living|חַיִּֽים׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 24 \rb Elam|עֵילָם֙\rb* \rb is there|שָׁ֤ם\rb*
\q2 \rb with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb her multitudes|הֲמוֹנָ֔הּ\rb* \rb around|סְבִיב֖וֹת\rb* \rb her grave|קְבֻרָתָ֑הּ\rb*.
\q1 \rb All|כֻּלָּ֣ם\rb* \rb of them are slain|חֲלָלִים֩\rb*,
\q2 \rb fallen|הַנֹּפְלִ֨ים\rb* \rb by the sword|בַּחֶ֜רֶב\rb*—
\q1 \rb those|אֲ‍ֽשֶׁר־\rb* \rb who went down|יָרְד֥וּ\rb* \rb uncircumcised|עֲרֵלִ֣ים׀\rb*
\q2 \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the earth|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb below|תַּחְתִּיּ֗וֹת\rb*,
\q1 \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb once spread|נָתְנ֤וּ\rb* \rb their terror|חִתִּיתָם֙\rb*
\q2 \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the living|חַיִּ֔ים\rb*.
\q1 \rb They bear|וַיִּשְׂא֥וּ\rb* \rb their disgrace|כְלִמָּתָ֖ם\rb*
\q2 \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb those who descend|י֥וֹרְדֵי\rb* \rb to the Pit|בֽוֹר׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 25 \rb Among|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb the slain|חֲ֠לָלִים\rb* \rb they prepare|נָתְנ֨וּ\rb*
\q2 \rb a resting place|מִשְׁכָּ֥ב\rb* \rb for Elam|לָהּ֙\rb*
\q1 \rb with all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb her hordes|הֲמוֹנָ֔הּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb with her graves|קִבְרֹתֶ֑הָ\rb* \rb all around her|סְבִֽיבוֹתָ֖יו\rb*.
\q1 \rb All|כֻּלָּ֣ם\rb* \rb of them are uncircumcised|עֲרֵלִ֣ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb slain|חַלְלֵי־\rb* \rb by the sword|חֶ֡רֶב\rb*,
\q1 \rb although|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb their terror|חִתִּיתָ֜ם\rb* \rb was once spread|נִתַּ֨ן\rb*
\q2 \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the living|חַיִּ֗ים\rb*.
\q1 \rb They bear|וַיִּשְׂא֤וּ\rb* \rb their disgrace|כְלִמָּתָם֙\rb*
\q2 \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb those who descend|י֣וֹרְדֵי\rb* \rb to the Pit|ב֔וֹר\rb*.
\q2 \rb They are placed|נִתָּֽן׃\rb* \rb among|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the slain|חֲלָלִ֖ים\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 26 \rb Meshech|מֶ֤שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb and Tubal|תֻּבַל֙\rb* \rb are there|שָׁ֣ם\rb*
\q2 \rb with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb their multitudes|הֲמוֹנָ֔הּ\rb*,
\q2 \rb with their graves|קִבְרוֹתֶ֑יהָ\rb* \rb all around them|סְבִֽיבוֹתָ֖יו\rb*.
\q1 \rb All|כֻּלָּ֤ם\rb* \rb of them are uncircumcised|עֲרֵלִים֙\rb*,
\q2 \rb slain|מְחֻ֣לְלֵי\rb* \rb by the sword|חֶ֔רֶב\rb*,
\q1 \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they spread|נָתְנ֥וּ\rb* \rb their terror|חִתִּיתָ֖ם\rb*
\q2 \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of the living|חַיִּֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 27 \rb They do not|וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb lie down|יִשְׁכְּבוּ֙\rb*
\q2 \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the fallen|נֹפְלִ֖ים\rb* \rb warriors|גִּבּוֹרִ֔ים\rb* \rb of old|מֵעֲרֵלִ֑ים\rb*,\f + \fr 32:27 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa warriors of the uncircumcised \f*
\q1 \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb went down|יָרְדֽוּ־\rb* \rb to Sheol|שְׁא֣וֹל\rb*
\q2 \rb with their weapons|בִּכְלֵֽי־\rb* \rb of war|מִלְחַמְתָּם֩\rb*,
\q1 \rb whose swords|חַרְבוֹתָ֜ם\rb* \rb were placed|וַיִּתְּנ֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb under|תַּ֣חַת\rb* \rb their heads|רָאשֵׁיהֶ֗ם\rb*,
\q2 \rb whose shields|עֲוֺֽנֹתָם֙\rb*\f + \fr 32:27 \ft Likely reading of the original Hebrew text; MT \fqa iniquities\f* \rb rested|וַתְּהִ֤י\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb their bones|עַצְמוֹתָ֔ם\rb*,
\q1 \rb although|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the terror|חִתִּ֥ית\rb* \rb of the mighty|גִּבּוֹרִ֖ים\rb*
\q2 \rb was once in the land|בְּאֶ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb of the living|חַיִּֽים׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 28 \rb But you too|וְאַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb will be shattered|תִּשָּׁבַ֥ר\rb*
\q2 \rb and lie down|וְתִשְׁכַּ֖ב\rb* \rb among|בְּת֧וֹךְ\rb* \rb the uncircumcised|עֲרֵלִ֛ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb those slain|חַלְלֵי־\rb* \rb by the sword|חָֽרֶב׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 29 \rb Edom|אֱד֗וֹם\rb* \rb is there|שָׁ֣מָּה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb her kings|מְלָכֶ֙יהָ֙\rb* \rb and princes|נְשִׂיאֶ֔יהָ\rb*,
\q1 \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb despite their might|בִגְבוּרָתָ֖ם\rb*
\q2 \rb are laid|נִתְּנ֥וּ\rb* \rb among|אֶת־\rb* \rb those slain|חַלְלֵי־\rb* \rb by the sword|חָ֑רֶב\rb*.
\q1 \rb They|הֵ֛מָּה\rb* \rb lie down|יִשְׁכָּ֖בוּ\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the uncircumcised|עֲרֵלִ֥ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb with|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb those who descend|יֹ֥רְדֵי\rb* \rb to the Pit|בֽוֹר׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 30 \rb All|כֻּלָּ֖ם\rb* \rb the leaders|נְסִיכֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the north|צָפ֛וֹן\rb*
\q2 \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the Sidonians|צִֽדֹנִ֑י\rb* \rb are there|שָׁ֣מָּה\rb*;
\q1 \rb they|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb went down|יָרְד֣וּ\rb* \rb in disgrace|בּוֹשִׁ֔ים\rb* \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb the slain|חֲלָלִ֗ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb despite the terror|בְּחִתִּיתָ֤ם\rb* \rb of their might|מִגְבֽוּרָתָם֙\rb*.
\q1 \rb They lie|וַיִּשְׁכְּב֤וּ\rb* \rb uncircumcised|עֲרֵלִים֙\rb*
\q2 \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb those slain|חַלְלֵי־\rb* \rb by the sword|חֶ֔רֶב\rb*
\q1 \rb and bear|וַיִּשְׂא֥וּ\rb* \rb their shame|כְלִמָּתָ֖ם\rb*
\q2 \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb those who descend|י֥וֹרְדֵי\rb* \rb to the Pit|בֽוֹר׃\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \v 31 \rb |אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb Pharaoh|פַרְעֹ֔ה\rb* \rb will see them|יִרְאֶ֣ה\rb*
\q2 \rb and be comforted|וְנִחַ֖ם\rb* \rb over|עַל־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his multitude|הֲמוֹנֹה\rb*—
\q1 \rb Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹ֣ה\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his army|חֵיל֔וֹ\rb*,
\q2 \rb slain|חַלְלֵי־\rb* \rb by the sword|חֶ֙רֶב֙\rb*,
\qr \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 32 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I will spread|נָתַ֥תִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My terror|חִתִּיתוֹ\rb*
\q2 \rb in the land|בְּאֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of the living|חַיִּ֑ים\rb*,
\q1 \rb so that Pharaoh|פַּרְעֹה֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb his multitude|הֲמוֹנֹ֔ה\rb*
\q2 \rb will be laid to rest|וְהֻשְׁכַּב֩\rb* \rb among|בְּת֨וֹךְ\rb* \rb the uncircumcised|עֲרֵלִ֜ים\rb*,
\q2 \rb with|אֶת־\rb* \rb those slain|חַלְלֵי־\rb* \rb by the sword|חֶ֗רֶב\rb*,
\qr \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃פ\rb*.”
\c 33
\s1 Ezekiel the Watchman for Israel
\p \v 1 \rb Again the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb speak|דַּבֵּ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your people|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עַמְּךָ֙\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*: ‘\rb Suppose|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I bring|אָבִ֥יא\rb* \rb the sword|חָ֑רֶב\rb* \rb against|עָלֶ֖יהָ\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֕רֶץ\rb*, \rb and the people|עַם־\rb* \rb of that land|הָאָ֜רֶץ\rb* \rb choose|וְלָקְח֨וּ\rb* \rb a|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb man|אִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb from among them|מִקְצֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb appointing|וְנָתְנ֥וּ\rb* \rb him|אֹת֛וֹ\rb* \rb as their|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb watchman|לְצֹפֶֽה׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb and he sees|וְרָאָ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sword|הַחֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb coming|בָּאָ֣ה\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb that land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb and blows|וְתָקַ֥ע\rb* \rb the ram’s horn|בַּשּׁוֹפָ֖ר\rb* \rb to warn|וְהִזְהִ֥יר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Then if anyone hears|וְשָׁמַ֨ע\rb*\rb |הַשֹּׁמֵ֜עַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sound|ק֤וֹל\rb* \rb of the horn|הַשּׁוֹפָר֙\rb* \rb but fails|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb to heed the warning|נִזְהָ֔ר\rb*, \rb and the sword|חֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb comes|וַתָּ֥בוֹא\rb* \rb and takes him away|וַתִּקָּחֵ֑הוּ\rb*, \rb his blood|דָּמ֥וֹ\rb* \rb will be|יִֽהְיֶֽה׃\rb* \rb on his own head|בְרֹאשׁ֖וֹ\rb*. \v 5 \rb |אֵת֩\rb* \rb Since he heard|שָׁמַע֙\rb* \rb the sound|ק֨וֹל\rb* \rb of the horn|הַשּׁוֹפָ֤ר\rb* \rb but failed|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb to heed the warning|נִזְהָ֔ר\rb*, \rb his blood|דָּמ֖וֹ\rb* \rb will be|יִֽהְיֶ֑ה\rb* \rb on his own head|בּ֣וֹ\rb*. \rb If he|וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb had heeded the warning|נִזְהָ֖ר\rb*, \rb he would have saved|מִלֵּֽט׃\rb* \rb his life|נַפְשׁ֥וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb But if|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the watchman|וְ֠הַצֹּפֶה\rb* \rb sees|יִרְאֶ֨ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sword|הַחֶ֜רֶב\rb* \rb coming|בָּאָ֗ה\rb* \rb and fails|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb to blow|תָקַ֤ע\rb* \rb the horn|בַּשּׁוֹפָר֙\rb*\rb |לֹֽא־\rb* \rb to warn|נִזְהָ֔ר\rb* \rb the people|וְהָעָ֣ם\rb*, \rb and the sword|חֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb comes|וַתָּב֣וֹא\rb* \rb and takes away|וַתִּקַּ֥ח\rb*\rb |מֵהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb a life|נָ֑פֶשׁ\rb*, \rb then that one|ה֚וּא\rb* \rb will be taken away|נִלְקָ֔ח\rb* \rb in his iniquity|בַּעֲוֺנ֣וֹ\rb*, \rb but I will hold the watchman|הַצֹּפֶ֥ה\rb* \rb accountable|אֶדְרֹֽשׁ׃ס\rb* \rb for his blood|וְדָמ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |מִיַּֽד־\rb*.’
\p \v 7 \rb As for you|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb O son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֔ם\rb*, \rb I have made|נְתַתִּ֖יךָ\rb* \rb you a watchman|צֹפֶ֥ה\rb* \rb for the house|לְבֵ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*; \rb so hear|וְשָׁמַעְתָּ֤\rb* \rb the word|דָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb from|מִמֶּֽנִּי׃\rb* \rb My mouth|מִפִּי֙\rb* \rb and give them the warning from Me|וְהִזְהַרְתָּ֥\rb*. \v 8 \rb If I say|בְּאָמְרִ֣י\rb* \rb to the wicked|לָרָשָׁ֗ע\rb*, ‘\rb O wicked man|רָשָׁע֙\rb*, \rb you will surely die|מ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |תָּמ֔וּת\rb*,’ \rb but you do not|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb speak out|דִבַּ֔רְתָּ\rb* \rb to dissuade|לְהַזְהִ֥יר\rb* \rb him|רָשָׁ֖ע\rb* \rb from his way|מִדַּרְכּ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb then that|ה֤וּא\rb* \rb wicked man|רָשָׁע֙\rb* \rb will die|יָמ֔וּת\rb* \rb in his iniquity|בַּעֲוֺנ֣וֹ\rb*, \rb yet I will hold you accountable for|מִיָּדְךָ֥\rb*\rb |אֲבַקֵּֽשׁ׃\rb* \rb his blood|וְדָמ֖וֹ\rb*. \v 9 \rb But if|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb you|וְ֠אַתָּה\rb* \rb warn|הִזְהַ֨רְתָּ\rb* \rb the wicked man|רָשָׁ֤ע\rb* \rb to turn|לָשׁ֣וּב\rb* \rb from his way|מִדַּרְכּוֹ֙\rb*, \rb and he does not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb turn|שָׁ֖ב\rb* \rb from it|מִדַּרְכּ֑וֹ\rb*, \rb he|ה֚וּא\rb* \rb will die|יָמ֔וּת\rb* \rb in his iniquity|בַּעֲוֺנ֣וֹ\rb*, \rb but you|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb will have saved|הִצַּֽלְתָּ׃ס\rb* \rb your life|נַפְשְׁךָ֥\rb*.\f + \fr 33:9 \ft See \ref Acts 20:25–26|ACT 20:25-26\ref*\f*
\s1 The Message of the Watchman
\p \v 10 \rb Now as for you|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb tell|אֱמֹר֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb that this is what|כֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb they have said|אֲמַרְתֶּם֙\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb*\rb |כִּֽי־\rb*: ‘\rb Our transgressions|פְשָׁעֵ֥ינוּ\rb* \rb and our sins|וְחַטֹּאתֵ֖ינוּ\rb* \rb are heavy|עָלֵ֑ינוּ\rb* \rb upon us|וּבָ֛ם\rb*, \rb and we|אֲנַ֥חְנוּ\rb* \rb are wasting away because of them|נְמַקִּ֖ים\rb*! \rb How|וְאֵ֥יךְ\rb* \rb can we live|נִֽחְיֶֽה׃\rb*?’
\p \v 11 \rb Say|אֱמֹ֨ר\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶ֜ם\rb*: ‘\rb As surely as I|אָ֣נִי׀\rb* \rb live|חַי־\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֣ם׀\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֗ה\rb*, \rb I take no|אִם־\rb* \rb pleasure|אֶחְפֹּץ֙\rb* \rb in the death|בְּמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the wicked|הָרָשָׁ֔ע\rb*, \rb but rather|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb that the wicked|רָשָׁ֛ע\rb* \rb should turn|בְּשׁ֥וּב\rb* \rb from their ways|מִדַּרְכּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and live|וְחָיָ֑ה\rb*. \rb Turn|שׁ֣וּבוּ\rb*! \rb Turn|שׁ֜וּבוּ\rb* \rb from your evil|הָרָעִ֛ים\rb* \rb ways|מִדַּרְכֵיכֶ֧ם\rb*! \rb For why|וְלָ֥מָּה\rb* \rb should you die|תָמ֖וּתוּ\rb*, \rb O house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃פ\rb*?’
\p \v 12 \rb Therefore|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb say|אֱמֹ֤ר\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your people|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |עַמְּךָ֙\rb*: ‘\rb The righteousness|צִדְקַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the righteous man|הַצַּדִּ֗יק\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֤א\rb* \rb deliver him|תַצִּילֶ֙נּוּ֙\rb* \rb in the day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb of his transgression|פִּשְׁע֔וֹ\rb*; \rb neither|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb will the wickedness|וְרִשְׁעַ֤ת\rb* \rb of the wicked man|הָֽרָשָׁע֙\rb* \rb cause him to stumble|יִכָּ֣שֶׁל\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֖וֹם\rb* \rb he turns|שׁוּב֣וֹ\rb* \rb from his wickedness|מֵֽרִשְׁע֑וֹ\rb*. \rb Nor will|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb the righteous man|וְצַדִּ֗יק\rb* \rb be able|יוּכַ֛ל\rb* \rb to survive|לִֽחְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb by his righteousness|בָּ֖הּ\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb he sins|חֲטֹאתֽוֹ׃\rb*.’
\p \v 13 \rb If I tell|בְּאָמְרִ֤י\rb* \rb the righteous man|לַצַּדִּיק֙\rb* \rb that he will surely live|חָיֹ֣ה\rb*\rb |יִֽחְיֶ֔ה\rb*, \rb but he then|וְהֽוּא־\rb* \rb trusts|בָטַ֥ח\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb his righteousness|צִדְקָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb and commits|וְעָ֣שָׂה\rb* \rb iniquity|עָ֑וֶל\rb*, \rb then none|כָּל־\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb of his righteous works|צִדְקָתוֹ\rb* \rb will be remembered|תִזָּכַ֔רְנָה\rb*; \rb he will die|יָמֽוּת׃\rb* \rb because of the iniquity|וּבְעַוְל֥וֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he has committed|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb But if I tell|וּבְאָמְרִ֥י\rb* \rb the wicked man|לָֽרָשָׁ֖ע\rb*, ‘\rb You will surely die|מ֣וֹת\rb*\rb |תָּמ֑וּת\rb*,’ \rb and he turns|וְשָׁב֙\rb* \rb from his sin|מֵֽחַטָּאת֔וֹ\rb* \rb and does|וְעָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb what is just|מִשְׁפָּ֖ט\rb* \rb and right|וּצְדָקָֽה׃\rb*— \v 15 \rb if he|רָשָׁע֙\rb* \rb restores|יָשִׁ֤יב\rb* \rb a pledge|חֲבֹ֨ל\rb*, \rb makes restitution|יְשַׁלֵּ֔ם\rb* \rb for what he has stolen|גְּזֵלָ֣ה\rb*, \rb and walks|הָלַ֔ךְ\rb* \rb in the statutes|בְּחֻקּ֤וֹת\rb* \rb of life|הַֽחַיִּים֙\rb* \rb without|לְבִלְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb practicing|עֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb iniquity|עָ֑וֶל\rb*— \rb then he will surely live|חָי֥וֹ\rb*\rb |יִֽחְיֶ֖ה\rb*; \rb he will not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb die|יָמֽוּת׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb None|כָּל־\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb of the sins|חַטָּאתוֹ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb he has committed|חָטָ֔א\rb* \rb will be held|תִזָּכַ֖רְנָה\rb* \rb against him|ל֑וֹ\rb*. \rb He has done|עָשָׂ֖ה\rb* \rb what is just|מִשְׁפָּ֧ט\rb* \rb and right|וּצְדָקָ֛ה\rb*; \rb he will surely live|חָי֥וֹ\rb*\rb |יִֽחְיֶֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb Yet your people|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמְּךָ֔\rb* \rb say|וְאָמְרוּ֙\rb*, ‘\rb The way|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֑י\rb* \rb is not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb just|יִתָּכֵ֖ן\rb*.’ \rb But it is|וְהֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb their way|דַּרְכָּ֥ם\rb* \rb that is not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb just|יִתָּכֵֽן׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb If a righteous man|צַדִּ֥יק\rb* \rb turns|בְּשׁוּב־\rb* \rb from his righteousness|מִצִּדְקָת֖וֹ\rb* \rb and commits|וְעָ֣שָׂה\rb* \rb iniquity|עָ֑וֶל\rb*, \rb he will die|וּמֵ֖ת\rb* \rb for it|בָּהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb But if a wicked man|רָשָׁע֙\rb* \rb turns|וּבְשׁ֤וּב\rb* \rb from his wickedness|מֵֽרִשְׁעָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb and does|וְעָשָׂ֥ה\rb* \rb what is just|מִשְׁפָּ֖ט\rb* \rb and right|וּצְדָקָ֑ה\rb*, \rb he|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb will live|יִֽחְיֶֽה׃\rb* \rb because of this|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb Yet you say|וַאֲמַרְתֶּ֕ם\rb*, ‘\rb The way|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֑י\rb* \rb is not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb just|יִתָּכֵ֖ן\rb*.’ \rb But I will judge|אֶשְׁפּ֥וֹט\rb* \rb each|אִ֧ישׁ\rb* \rb of you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb according to his ways|כִּדְרָכָ֛יו\rb*, \rb O house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל פ\rb*.”
\s1 Word of Jerusalem’s Fall
\p \v 21 \rb |וַיְהִ֞י\rb* \rb In the twelfth|בִּשְׁתֵּ֧י\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֣ה\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֗ה\rb* \rb of our exile|לְגָלוּתֵ֑נוּ\rb*, \rb on the fifth day|בַּחֲמִשָּׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |לַחֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the tenth month|בָּעֲשִׂרִ֛י\rb*, \rb a fugitive|הַפָּלִ֧יט\rb* \rb from Jerusalem|מִירוּשָׁלִַ֛ם\rb* \rb came|בָּא־\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֨י\rb* \rb and reported|לֵאמֹ֖ר\rb*, “\rb The city|הָעִֽיר׃\rb* \rb has been taken|הֻכְּתָ֥ה\rb*!”
\p \v 22 \rb Now the evening|בָּעֶ֗רֶב\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb the fugitive|הַפָּלִ֔יט\rb* \rb arrived|בּ֣וֹא\rb*, \rb the hand|וְיַד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֩\rb* \rb was|הָיְתָ֨ה\rb* \rb upon me|אֵלַ֜י\rb*, \rb and He opened|וַיִּפְתַּ֣ח\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb my mouth|פִּ֔י\rb* \rb before|עַד־\rb* \rb the man came|בּ֥וֹא\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb in the morning|בַּבֹּ֑קֶר\rb*. \rb So my mouth|פִּ֔י\rb* \rb was opened|וַיִּפָּ֣תַח\rb* \rb and I was no|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb longer|עֽוֹד׃פ\rb* \rb mute|נֶאֱלַ֖מְתִּי\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהֹוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 24 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb those living|יֹ֠שְׁבֵי\rb* \rb in the|הָאֵ֜לֶּה\rb* \rb ruins|הֶחֳרָב֨וֹת\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|אַדְמַ֤ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb are saying|אֹמְרִ֣ים\rb*,\rb |לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* ‘\rb Abraham|אַבְרָהָ֔ם\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb only one man|אֶחָד֙\rb*, \rb yet he possessed|וַיִּירַ֖שׁ\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*. \rb But we|וַאֲנַ֣חְנוּ\rb* \rb are many|רַבִּ֔ים\rb*; \rb surely the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb has been given|נִתְּנָ֥ה\rb* \rb to us|לָ֛נוּ\rb* \rb as a possession|לְמוֹרָשָֽׁה׃ס\rb*.’
\p \v 25 \rb Therefore|לָכֵן֩\rb* \rb tell|אֱמֹ֨ר\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהֹוִ֗ה\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר׀\rb*: ‘\rb You eat|תֹּאכֵ֛לוּ\rb* \rb meat with the blood in it|הַדָּ֧ם׀\rb*, \rb lift up|תִּשְׂא֥וּ\rb* \rb your eyes|וְעֵינֵכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb your idols|גִּלּוּלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb and shed|תִּשְׁפֹּ֑כוּ\rb* \rb blood|וְדָ֣ם\rb*. \rb Should you then possess|תִּירָֽשׁוּ׃\rb* \rb the land|וְהָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*? \v 26 \rb You have relied|עֲמַדְתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb on|עַֽל־\rb* \rb your swords|חַרְבְּכֶם֙\rb*, \rb you have committed|עֲשִׂיתֶ֣ן\rb* \rb detestable acts|תּוֹעֵבָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and each|וְאִ֛ישׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of you has defiled|טִמֵּאתֶ֑ם\rb* \rb his neighbor’s|רֵעֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb wife|אֵ֥שֶׁת\rb*. \rb Should you then possess|תִּירָֽשׁוּ׃ס\rb* \rb the land|וְהָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*?’
\p \v 27 \rb Tell|תֹאמַ֨ר\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb that this|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִה֮\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֨ר\rb*: ‘\rb As surely as I|אָנִי֒\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹ֞א\rb* \rb live|חַי־\rb*, \rb those|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb in the ruins|בֶּֽחֳרָבוֹת֙\rb* \rb will fall|יִפֹּ֔לוּ\rb* \rb by the sword|בַּחֶ֣רֶב\rb*, \rb those|וַֽאֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the open field|פְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |הַשָּׂדֶ֔ה\rb* \rb I will give|נְתַתִּ֖יו\rb* \rb to be devoured|לְאָכְל֑וֹ\rb* \rb by wild animals|לַחַיָּ֥ה\rb*, \rb and those|וַאֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb in the strongholds|בַּמְּצָד֥וֹת\rb* \rb and caves|וּבַמְּעָר֖וֹת\rb* \rb will die|יָמֽוּתוּ׃\rb* \rb by plague|בַּדֶּ֥בֶר\rb*. \v 28 \rb I will make|וְנָתַתִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb a desolate|שְׁמָמָ֣ה\rb* \rb waste|וּמְשַׁמָּ֔ה\rb*, \rb and the pride|גְּא֣וֹן\rb* \rb of her strength|עֻזָּ֑הּ\rb* \rb will come to an end|וְנִשְׁבַּ֖ת\rb*. \rb The mountains|הָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb will become desolate|וְשָֽׁמְמ֛וּ\rb*, \rb so that no one|מֵאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb will pass through|עוֹבֵֽר׃\rb*. \v 29 \rb Then they will know|וְיָדְע֖וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb when I have made|בְּתִתִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb a desolate|שְׁמָמָ֣ה\rb* \rb waste|וּמְשַׁמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb because of|עַ֥ל\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the abominations|תּוֹעֲבֹתָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they have committed|עָשֽׂוּ׃ס\rb*.’
\p \v 30 \rb As for you|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֔ם\rb*, \rb your people|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |עַמְּךָ֗\rb* \rb are talking|הַנִּדְבָּרִ֤ים\rb* \rb about you|בְּךָ֙\rb* \rb near|אֵ֣צֶל\rb* \rb the city walls|הַקִּיר֔וֹת\rb* \rb and in the doorways|וּבְפִתְחֵ֖י\rb* \rb of their houses|הַבָּתִּ֑ים\rb*. \rb One|חַ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb speaks|וְדִבֶּר־\rb* \rb to|אֶת־\rb* \rb another|אַחַ֗ד\rb*, \rb each|אִ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb saying|לֵאמֹ֔ר\rb* \rb to his brother|אָחִיו֙\rb*, ‘\rb Come|בֹּֽאוּ־\rb*\rb |נָ֣א\rb* \rb and hear|וְשִׁמְע֔וּ\rb*\rb |מָ֣ה\rb* \rb the message|הַדָּבָ֔ר\rb* \rb that has come|הַיּוֹצֵ֖א\rb* \rb from|מֵאֵ֥ת\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*!’
\p \v 31 \rb So My people|עָ֞ם\rb* \rb come|וְיָב֣וֹאוּ\rb* \rb to you|אֵ֠לֶיךָ\rb* \rb as usual|כִּמְבוֹא־\rb*,\rb |עַמִּ֔י\rb* \rb sit|וְיֵשְׁב֤וּ\rb* \rb before you|לְפָנֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*, \rb and hear|וְשָֽׁמְעוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your words|דְּבָרֶ֔יךָ\rb*;\rb |וְאוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb but they do not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb put them into practice|יַֽעֲשׂ֑וּ\rb*. \rb Although|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb they|הֵ֣מָּה\rb* \rb express|עֹשִׂ֔ים\rb*\rb |אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb love|עֲגָבִ֤ים\rb* \rb with their mouths|בְּפִיהֶם֙\rb*, \rb their hearts|לִבָּ֥ם\rb* \rb pursue|הֹלֵֽךְ׃\rb* \rb dishonest gain|בִצְעָ֖ם\rb*. \v 32 \rb Indeed, you are|וְהִנְּךָ֤\rb* \rb to them|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb like a singer of love|עֲגָבִ֔ים\rb* \rb songs|כְּשִׁ֣יר\rb* \rb with a beautiful|יְפֵ֥ה\rb* \rb voice|ק֖וֹל\rb*, \rb who skillfully|וּמֵטִ֣ב\rb* \rb plays an instrument|נַגֵּ֑ן\rb*. \rb They hear|וְשָֽׁמְעוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your words|דְּבָרֶ֔יךָ\rb* \rb but do not|אֵינָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אוֹתָֽם׃\rb* \rb put them into practice|וְעֹשִׂ֥ים\rb*. \v 33 \rb So when it comes to pass|וּבְבֹאָ֑הּ\rb*— \rb and surely|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb* \rb it will come|בָאָ֔ה\rb*— \rb then they will know|וְיָ֣דְע֔וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb a prophet|נָבִ֖יא\rb* \rb has been|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb among them|בְתוֹכָֽם׃ס\rb*.”
\c 34
\s1 A Prophecy against Israel’s Shepherds
\p \v 1 \rb Then the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*, \rb prophesy|הִנָּבֵ֖א\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the shepherds|רוֹעֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb Prophesy|הִנָּבֵ֣א\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֩\rb* \rb them|לָרֹעִ֜ים\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר׀\rb*: ‘\rb Woe|ה֤וֹי\rb* \rb to the shepherds|רֹעֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb*\rb |הָיוּ֙\rb* \rb only feed|רֹעִ֣ים\rb* \rb themselves|אוֹתָ֔ם\rb*! \rb Should not|הֲל֣וֹא\rb* \rb the shepherds|הָרֹעִֽים׃\rb* \rb feed|יִרְע֖וּ\rb* \rb their flock|הַצֹּ֔אן\rb*? \v 3 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb You eat|תֹּאכֵ֙לוּ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the fat|הַחֵ֤לֶב\rb*, \rb wear|תִּלְבָּ֔שׁוּ\rb* \rb the wool|הַצֶּ֣מֶר\rb*, \rb and butcher|תִּזְבָּ֑חוּ\rb* \rb the fattened sheep|הַבְּרִיאָ֖ה\rb*, \rb but you do not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb feed|תִרְעֽוּ׃\rb* \rb the flock|הַצֹּ֖אן\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb You have not|לֹ֨א\rb* \rb strengthened|חִזַּקְתֶּ֜ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the weak|הַנַּחְלוֹת֩\rb*, \rb healed|רִפֵּאתֶ֗ם\rb* \rb the sick|הַחוֹלָ֣ה\rb*,\rb |לֹֽא־\rb* \rb bound up|חֲבַשְׁתֶּ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the injured|וְלַנִּשְׁבֶּ֙רֶת֙\rb*,\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb brought back|הֲשֵׁבֹתֶ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the strays|הַנִּדַּ֙חַת֙\rb*,\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb or searched for|בִקַּשְׁתֶּ֑ם\rb* \rb the lost|הָאֹבֶ֖דֶת\rb*. \rb Instead|לֹ֣א\rb*, \rb you have ruled|רְדִיתֶ֥ם\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb with violence|וּבְחָזְקָ֛ה\rb* \rb and cruelty|וּבְפָֽרֶךְ׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb They were scattered|וַתְּפוּצֶ֖ינָה\rb* \rb for lack of|מִבְּלִ֣י\rb* \rb a shepherd|רֹעֶ֑ה\rb*, \rb and when they were scattered|וַתְּפוּצֶֽינָה׃\rb* \rb they became|וַתִּהְיֶ֧ינָה\rb* \rb food|לְאָכְלָ֛ה\rb* \rb for all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the wild|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb beasts|חַיַּ֥ת\rb*. \v 6 \rb My flock|צֹאנִי֙\rb* \rb went astray|יִשְׁגּ֤וּ\rb* \rb on all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb the mountains|הֶ֣הָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb and|וְעַ֖ל\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb high|רָמָ֑ה\rb*\rb |וְעַ֨ל\rb* \rb hill|גִּבְעָ֣ה\rb*. \rb They were scattered|נָפֹ֣צוּ\rb*\rb |צֹאנִ֔י\rb* \rb over the face|פְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the earth|הָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb*, \rb with no one|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb to search for them|דּוֹרֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb or|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb seek them out|מְבַקֵּֽשׁ׃\rb*.’
\p \v 7 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֣ן\rb*, \rb you shepherds|רֹעִ֔ים\rb*, \rb hear|שִׁמְע֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַ֥ר\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*: \v 8 ‘\rb As surely as I|אָ֜נִי\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb live|חַי־\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֣ם׀\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֗ה\rb*,\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb because|יַ֣עַן\rb* \rb My flock|צֹאנִ֣י׀\rb* \rb lacks|מֵאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb a shepherd|רֹעֶ֔ה\rb* \rb and has become|הֱיֽוֹת־\rb* \rb prey|לָבַ֡ז\rb*\rb |וַתִּֽהְיֶינָה֩\rb* \rb and|צֹאנִ֨י\rb* \rb food|לְאָכְלָ֜ה\rb* \rb for every|לְכָל־\rb* \rb wild|הַשָּׂדֶה֙\rb* \rb beast|חַיַּ֤ת\rb*, \rb and because My shepherds|רֹעַ֖י\rb* \rb did not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb search|דָרְשׁ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for My flock|צֹאנִ֑י\rb* \rb but fed|וַיִּרְע֤וּ\rb*\rb |הָֽרֹעִים֙\rb* \rb themselves|אוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb instead|וְאֶת־\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb*\rb |רָעֽוּ׃ס\rb*\rb |צֹאנִ֖י\rb*, \v 9 \rb therefore|לָכֵן֙\rb*, \rb you shepherds|הָֽרֹעִ֔ים\rb*, \rb hear|שִׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*!’
\p \v 10 \rb This is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֞ר\rb*: ‘\rb Behold|הִנְנִ֨י\rb*, \rb I am against|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb the shepherds|הָרֹעִ֜ים\rb*, \rb and I will demand|וְֽדָרַשְׁתִּ֧י\rb* \rb from them|מִיָּדָ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My flock|צֹאנִ֣י\rb* \rb and remove them|וְהִשְׁבַּתִּים֙\rb* \rb from tending|מֵרְע֣וֹת\rb* \rb the flock|צֹ֔אן\rb*, \rb so that they can no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb feed|יִרְע֥וּ\rb*\rb |הָרֹעִ֖ים\rb* \rb themselves|אוֹתָ֑ם\rb*. \rb For I will deliver|וְהִצַּלְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb My flock|צֹאנִי֙\rb* \rb from their mouths|מִפִּיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and it will no longer|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb be|תִהְיֶ֥יןָ\rb* \rb food|לְאָכְלָֽה׃ס\rb* \rb for them|לָהֶ֖ם\rb*.’
\s1 The Good Shepherd
\r (\ref Psalm 23:1–6|PSA 23:1-6\ref*; \ref John 10:1–21|JHN 10:1-21\ref*)
\p \v 11 \rb For|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*: ‘\rb Behold|הִנְנִי־\rb*, \rb I Myself|אָ֕נִי\rb* \rb will search for|וְדָרַשְׁתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My flock|צֹאנִ֖י\rb* \rb and seek them out|וּבִקַּרְתִּֽים׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb As a shepherd|רֹעֶ֨ה\rb* \rb looks for|כְּבַקָּרַת֩\rb* \rb his scattered|נִפְרָשׁ֔וֹת\rb* \rb sheep|עֶדְר֜וֹ\rb* \rb when|בְּיוֹם־\rb* \rb he is|הֱיוֹת֤וֹ\rb* \rb among|בְתוֹךְ־\rb* \rb the flock|צֹאנוֹ֙\rb*, \rb so|כֵּ֖ן\rb* \rb I will look for|אֲבַקֵּ֣ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My flock|צֹאנִ֑י\rb*.
\p \rb I will rescue them|וְהִצַּלְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb from|אֶתְהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the places|הַמְּקוֹמֹת֙\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they were scattered|נָפֹ֣צוּ\rb*\rb |שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb on a day|בְּי֥וֹם\rb* \rb of clouds|עָנָ֖ן\rb* \rb and darkness|וַעֲרָפֶֽל׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb I will bring them out|וְהוֹצֵאתִ֣ים\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the peoples|הָעַמִּ֗ים\rb*, \rb gather them|וְקִבַּצְתִּים֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the countries|הָ֣אֲרָצ֔וֹת\rb*, \rb and bring them|וַהֲבִיאֹתִ֖ים\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb their own land|אַדְמָתָ֑ם\rb*. \rb I will feed them|וּרְעִיתִים֙\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the mountains|הָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb in the ravines|בָּאֲפִיקִ֕ים\rb*, \rb and in all|וּבְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the settlements|מוֹשְׁבֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb I will feed|אֶרְעֶ֣ה\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb in good|טּוֹב֙\rb* \rb pasture|בְּמִרְעֶה־\rb*, \rb and the lofty|מְרֽוֹם־\rb* \rb mountains|וּבְהָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb their grazing land|נְוֵהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb There|שָׁ֤ם\rb* \rb they will lie down|תִּרְבַּ֙צְנָה֙\rb* \rb in a good|טּ֔וֹב\rb* \rb grazing land|בְּנָ֣וֶה\rb*; \rb they will feed|תִּרְעֶ֖ינָה\rb* \rb in rich|שָׁמֵ֛ן\rb* \rb pasture|וּמִרְעֶ֥ה\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the mountains|הָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb I|אֲנִ֨י\rb* \rb will tend|אֶרְעֶ֤ה\rb* \rb My flock|צֹאנִי֙\rb*\rb |וַאֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb and make them lie down|אַרְבִּיצֵ֔ם\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb I will seek|אֲבַקֵּשׁ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the lost|הָאֹבֶ֤דֶת\rb*, \rb bring back|אָשִׁ֔יב\rb* \rb the strays|הַנִּדַּ֣חַת\rb*, \rb bind up|אֶחֱבֹ֔שׁ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the broken|וְלַנִּשְׁבֶּ֣רֶת\rb*, \rb and strengthen|אֲחַזֵּ֑ק\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the weak|הַחוֹלָ֖ה\rb*; \rb but the sleek|הַשְּׁמֵנָ֧ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and strong|הַחֲזָקָ֛ה\rb* \rb I will destroy|אַשְׁמִ֖יד\rb*. \rb I will shepherd them|אֶרְעֶ֥נָּה\rb* \rb with justice|בְמִשְׁפָּֽט׃\rb*.’
\p \v 17 \rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb*\rb |הִנְנִ֤י\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb* \rb to you|וְאַתֵּ֣נָה\rb*, \rb My flock|צֹאנִ֔י\rb*: ‘\rb I will judge|שֹׁפֵט֙\rb* \rb between|בֵּֽין־\rb* \rb one sheep|שֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb and another|לָשֶׂ֔ה\rb*, \rb between the rams|לָאֵילִ֖ים\rb* \rb and the goats|וְלָעַתּוּדִֽים׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb Is it not enough|הַמְעַ֣ט\rb* \rb for|מִכֶּ֗ם\rb* \rb you to feed on|תִּרְע֔וּ\rb* \rb the good|הַטּוֹב֙\rb* \rb pasture|הַמִּרְעֶ֤ה\rb*? \rb Must you also trample|תִּרְמְס֖וּ\rb* \rb the rest|וְיֶ֙תֶר֙\rb* \rb of the pasture|מִרְעֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb with your feet|בְּרַגְלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*? \rb Is it not enough for you to drink|תִּשְׁתּ֔וּ\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb* \rb the clear|וּמִשְׁקַע־\rb* \rb waters|מַ֣יִם\rb*? \rb Must you also muddy|תִּרְפֹּשֽׂוּן׃\rb* \rb the rest|הַנּ֣וֹתָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb with your feet|בְּרַגְלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*? \v 19 \rb Why must My flock|וְצֹאנִ֑י\rb* \rb feed on|תִּרְעֶ֔ינָה\rb* \rb what your feet|רַגְלֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb have trampled|מִרְמַ֤ס\rb*, \rb and drink|תִּשְׁתֶּֽינָה׃ס\rb* \rb what your feet|רַגְלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb have muddied|וּמִרְפַּ֥שׂ\rb*?’
\p \v 20 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֖ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֛ר\rb* \rb to them|אֲלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*: ‘\rb Behold|הִנְנִי־\rb*, \rb I Myself|אָ֕נִי\rb* \rb will judge|וְשָֽׁפַטְתִּי֙\rb* \rb between|בֵּֽין־\rb* \rb the fat|בִרְיָ֔ה\rb* \rb sheep|שֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb and|וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb the lean|רָזָֽה׃\rb* \rb sheep|שֶׂ֖ה\rb*. \v 21 \rb Since|יַ֗עַן\rb* \rb you shove|תֶּהְדֹּ֔פוּ\rb* \rb with flank|בְּצַ֤ד\rb* \rb and shoulder|וּבְכָתֵף֙\rb*, \rb butting|תְּנַגְּח֖וּ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the weak ones|הַנַּחְל֑וֹת\rb* \rb with your horns|וּבְקַרְנֵיכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb until|עַ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb you have scattered|הֲפִיצוֹתֶ֛ם\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֖נָה\rb* \rb abroad|הַחֽוּצָה׃\rb*, \v 22 \rb I will save|וְהוֹשַׁעְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb My flock|לְצֹאנִ֔י\rb*, \rb and they will no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb be|תִהְיֶ֥ינָה\rb* \rb prey|לָבַ֑ז\rb*. \rb I will judge|וְשָׁ֣פַטְתִּ֔י\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb one sheep|שֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb and another|לָשֶֽׂה׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb I will appoint|וַהֲקִמֹתִ֨י\rb* \rb over them|עֲלֵיהֶ֜ם\rb* \rb one|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb shepherd|רֹעֶ֤ה\rb*, \rb My servant|עַבְדִּ֣י\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֑יד\rb*, \rb and he will feed|וְרָעָ֣ה\rb* \rb them|אֶתְהֶ֔ן\rb*.\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb He|ה֚וּא\rb* \rb will feed|יִרְעֶ֣ה\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb and|וְהֽוּא־\rb* \rb be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb their|לָהֶ֖ן\rb* \rb shepherd|לְרֹעֶֽה׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb I|וַאֲנִ֣י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb will be|אֶהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb their|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb God|לֵֽאלֹהִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and My servant|וְעַבְדִּ֥י\rb* \rb David|דָוִ֖ד\rb* \rb will be a prince|נָשִׂ֣יא\rb* \rb among them|בְתוֹכָ֑ם\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb have spoken|דִּבַּֽרְתִּי׃\rb*.
\s1 The Covenant of Peace
\p \v 25 \rb I will make|וְכָרַתִּ֤י\rb* \rb with them|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of peace|שָׁל֔וֹם\rb* \rb and rid|וְהִשְׁבַּתִּ֥י\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb wild|רָעָ֖ה\rb* \rb animals|חַיָּֽה־\rb*, \rb so that they may dwell|וְיָשְׁב֤וּ\rb* \rb securely|לָבֶ֔טַח\rb* \rb in the wilderness|בַמִּדְבָּר֙\rb* \rb and sleep|וְיָשְׁנ֖וּ\rb* \rb in the forest|בַּיְּעָרִֽים׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb I will make|וְנָתַתִּ֥י\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb and the places around|וּסְבִיב֥וֹת\rb* \rb My hill|גִּבְעָתִ֖י\rb* \rb a blessing|בְּרָכָ֑ה\rb*. \rb I will send down|וְהוֹרַדְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb showers|הַגֶּ֙שֶׁם֙\rb* \rb in season|בְּעִתּ֔וֹ\rb*— \rb showers|גִּשְׁמֵ֥י\rb* \rb of blessing|בְרָכָ֖ה\rb*\rb |יִֽהְיֽוּ׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb The trees|עֵ֨ץ\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will give|וְנָתַן֩\rb* \rb their fruit|פִּרְי֗וֹ\rb*, \rb and the land|וְהָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb will yield|תִּתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb its produce|יְבוּלָ֔הּ\rb*; \rb My flock will be|וְהָי֥וּ\rb* \rb secure|לָבֶ֑טַח\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb their land|אַדְמָתָ֖ם\rb*. \rb Then they will know|וְֽיָדְע֞וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb when I have broken|בְּשִׁבְרִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the bars|מֹט֣וֹת\rb* \rb of their yoke|עֻלָּ֔ם\rb* \rb and delivered them|וְהִ֨צַּלְתִּ֔ים\rb* \rb from the hands|מִיַּ֖ד\rb* \rb that enslaved|הָעֹבְדִ֥ים\rb* \rb them|בָּהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb They will no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֥וֹד\rb* \rb be|יִהְי֨וּ\rb* \rb prey|בַּז֙\rb* \rb for the nations|לַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb*, \rb and the beasts|וְחַיַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb consume them|תֹאכְלֵ֑ם\rb*. \rb They will dwell securely|וְיָשְׁב֥וּ\rb*\rb |לָבֶ֖טַח\rb*, \rb and no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb one will frighten them|מַחֲרִֽיד׃\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb And I will raise up|וַהֲקִמֹתִ֥י\rb* \rb for them|לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb a garden|מַטָּ֖ע\rb* \rb of renown|לְשֵׁ֑ם\rb*, \rb and they will no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֜וֹד\rb* \rb be|יִהְי֨וּ\rb* \rb victims|אֲסֻפֵ֤י\rb* \rb of famine|רָעָב֙\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb or|וְלֹֽא־\rb*\rb |ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb bear|יִשְׂא֥וּ\rb* \rb the scorn|כְּלִמַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִֽם׃\rb*. \v 30 \rb Then they will know|וְיָדְע֗וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֧י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb* \rb their God|אֱלֹהֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb am with them|אִתָּ֑ם\rb*, \rb and that they|וְהֵ֗מָּה\rb*, \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb are My people|עַמִּי֙\rb*,’ \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 31 ‘\rb You|וְאַתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb are My flock|צֹאנִ֛י\rb*, \rb the sheep|צֹ֥אן\rb* \rb of My pasture|מַרְעִיתִ֖י\rb*, \rb My people|אָדָ֣ם\rb*\rb |אַתֶּ֑ם\rb*, \rb and I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb am your God|אֱלֹ֣הֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*,’ \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃פ\rb*.”
\c 35
\s1 A Prophecy against Mount Seir
\p \v 1 \rb Moreover, the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*, \rb set|שִׂ֥ים\rb* \rb your face|פָּנֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Mount|הַ֣ר\rb* \rb Seir|שֵׂעִ֑יר\rb* \rb and prophesy|וְהִנָּבֵ֖א\rb* \rb against it|עָלָֽיו׃\rb*, \v 3 \rb and declare|וְאָמַ֣רְתָּ\rb*\rb |לּ֗וֹ\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*:
\b 
\q1 \rb Behold|הִנְנִ֥י\rb*, \rb I am against you|אֵלֶ֖יךָ\rb*,
\q2 \rb O Mount|הַר־\rb* \rb Seir|שֵׂעִ֑יר\rb*.
\q1 \rb I will stretch out|וְנָטִ֤יתִי\rb* \rb My hand|יָדִי֙\rb* \rb against you|עָלֶ֔יךָ\rb*
\q2 \rb and make|וּנְתַתִּ֖יךָ\rb* \rb you a desolate|שְׁמָמָ֥ה\rb* \rb waste|וּמְשַׁמָּֽה׃\rb*.
\q1 \v 4 \rb I will turn your cities|עָרֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb into|אָשִׂ֔ים\rb* \rb ruins|חָרְבָּ֣ה\rb*,
\q2 \rb and you|וְאַתָּ֖ה\rb* \rb will become|תִֽהְיֶ֑ה\rb* \rb a desolation|שְׁמָמָ֣ה\rb*.
\b 
\q1 \rb Then you will know|וְיָדַעְתָּ֖\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Because|יַ֗עַן\rb* \rb you harbored|הֱי֤וֹת\rb* \rb an ancient|עוֹלָ֔ם\rb* \rb hatred|אֵיבַ֣ת\rb* \rb and delivered|וַתַּגֵּ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb over to|עַל־\rb*\rb |יְדֵי־\rb* \rb the sword|חָ֑רֶב\rb* \rb in the time|בְּעֵ֣ת\rb* \rb of their disaster|אֵידָ֔ם\rb* \rb at the final stage|בְּעֵ֖ת\rb*\rb |קֵֽץ׃\rb* \rb of their punishment|עֲוֺ֥ן\rb*, \v 6 \rb therefore|לָכֵ֣ן\rb* \rb as surely as I|אָ֗נִי\rb* \rb live|חַי־\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם֙\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb*, \rb I will give you over|אֶעֶשְׂךָ֖\rb* \rb to bloodshed|לְדָ֥ם\rb* \rb and it|וְדָ֣ם\rb* \rb will pursue you|יִרְדֲּפֶ֑ךָ\rb*. \rb Since|אִם־\rb* \rb you did not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb hate|שָׂנֵ֖אתָ\rb* \rb bloodshed|דָ֛ם\rb*, \rb it|וְדָ֥ם\rb* \rb will pursue you|יִרְדֲּפֶֽךָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb I will make|וְנָֽתַתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Mount|הַ֣ר\rb* \rb Seir|שֵׂעִ֔יר\rb* \rb a desolate|לְשִֽׁמְמָ֖ה\rb* \rb waste|וּשְׁמָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb and will cut off|וְהִכְרַתִּ֥י\rb* \rb from it|מִמֶּ֖נּוּ\rb* \rb those who come|וָשָֽׁב׃\rb* \rb and go|עֹבֵ֥ר\rb*. \v 8 \rb I will fill|וּמִלֵּאתִ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its mountains|הָרָ֖יו\rb* \rb with the slain|חֲלָלָ֑יו\rb*; \rb those killed|חַלְלֵי־\rb* \rb by the sword|חֶ֖רֶב\rb* \rb will fall|יִפְּל֥וּ\rb* \rb on your hills|גִּבְעוֹתֶ֤יךָ\rb*, \rb in your valleys|וְגֵאוֹתֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*, \rb and in all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb your ravines|אֲפִיקֶ֔יךָ\rb*. \v 9 \rb I will make|אֶתֶּנְךָ֔\rb* \rb you a perpetual|עוֹלָם֙\rb* \rb desolation|שִֽׁמְמ֤וֹת\rb*, \rb and your cities|וְעָרֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb will not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be inhabited|תֵישַׁבְנָה\rb*. \rb Then you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Because|יַ֣עַן\rb* \rb you have said|אֲ֠מָרְךָ\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* ‘\rb These two|שְׁנֵ֨י\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִ֜ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and|שְׁתֵּ֧י\rb* \rb countries|הָאֲרָצ֛וֹת\rb* \rb will be|תִהְיֶ֖ינָה\rb* \rb ours|לִ֥י\rb*, \rb and we will possess them|וִֽירַשְׁנ֑וּהָ\rb*,’ \rb even though the LORD|וַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb was|הָיָֽה׃\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֥ם\rb*, \v 11 \rb therefore|לָכֵ֣ן\rb* \rb as surely as I|אָ֗נִי\rb* \rb live|חַי־\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם֮\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִה֒\rb*, \rb I will treat you|וְעָשִׂ֗יתִי\rb* \rb according to the anger|כְּאַפְּךָ֙\rb* \rb and jealousy|וּכְקִנְאָ֣תְךָ֔\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you showed|עָשִׂ֔יתָה\rb* \rb in your hatred|מִשִּׂנְאָתֶ֖יךָ\rb* \rb against them|בָּ֑ם\rb*, \rb and I will make Myself known|וְנוֹדַ֥עְתִּי\rb* \rb among them|בָ֖ם\rb* \rb when|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I judge you|אֶשְׁפְּטֶֽךָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Then you will know|וְֽיָדַעְתָּ֮\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֒\rb*, \rb have heard|שָׁמַ֣עְתִּי׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb every|כָּל־\rb* \rb contemptuous word|נָאָֽצוֹתֶ֗יךָ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you uttered|אָמַ֛רְתָּ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the mountains|הָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb when you said|לֵאמֹ֣ר׀\rb*, ‘\rb They are desolate|שָׁמֵמָה\rb*; \rb they are given|נִתְּנ֖וּ\rb* \rb to us|לָ֥נוּ\rb* \rb to devour|לְאָכְלָֽה׃\rb*!’ \v 13 \rb You boasted|וַתַּגְדִּ֤ילוּ\rb* \rb against Me|עָלַי֙\rb* \rb with your mouth|בְּפִיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and multiplied|וְהַעְתַּרְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb your words|דִּבְרֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb against Me|עָלַ֖י\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb heard it Myself|שָׁמָֽעְתִּי׃ס\rb*!
\p \v 14 \rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*: \rb While the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb earth|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb rejoices|כִּשְׂמֹ֙חַ֙\rb*, \rb I will make|אֶעֱשֶׂה־\rb* \rb you|לָּֽךְ׃\rb* \rb desolate|שְׁמָמָ֖ה\rb*. \v 15 \rb As you rejoiced|כְּשִׂמְחָ֨תְךָ֜\rb* \rb when the inheritance|לְנַחְלַ֧ת\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb*\rb |עַ֥ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb became desolate|שָׁמֵ֖מָה\rb*, \rb so|כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb will I do|אֶעֱשֶׂה־\rb* \rb to you|לָּ֑ךְ\rb*. \rb You will become|תִֽהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb a desolation|שְׁמָמָ֨ה\rb*, \rb O Mount|הַר־\rb* \rb Seir|שֵׂעִיר֙\rb*, \rb and so will all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb of Edom|אֱד֣וֹם\rb*\rb |כֻּלָּ֔הּ\rb*. \rb Then they will know|וְיָדְע֖וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.[’’]
\c 36
\s1 A Prophecy to the Mountains of Israel
\p \v 1 “\rb And you|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֔ם\rb*, \rb prophesy|הִנָּבֵ֖א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the mountains|הָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and say|וְאָ֣מַרְתָּ֔\rb*: \rb O mountains|הָרֵי֙\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb hear|שִׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: \rb Because|יַ֣עַן\rb* \rb the enemy|הָאוֹיֵ֛ב\rb* \rb has said|אָמַ֧ר\rb* \rb of you|עֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*, ‘\rb Aha|הֶאָ֑ח\rb*! \rb The ancient|עוֹלָ֔ם\rb* \rb heights|וּבָמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb have become|הָ֥יְתָה\rb* \rb our|לָּֽנוּ׃\rb* \rb possession|לְמֽוֹרָשָׁ֖ה\rb*,’ \v 3 \rb therefore|לָכֵן֙\rb* \rb prophesy|הִנָּבֵ֣א\rb* \rb and declare|וְאָמַרְתָּ֔\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*: \rb Because|יַ֣עַן\rb*\rb |בְּיַ֡עַן\rb* \rb they have made you desolate|שַׁמּוֹת֩\rb* \rb and have trampled|וְשָׁאֹ֨ף\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb on every side|מִסָּבִ֗יב\rb*, \rb so that you became|לִֽהְיוֹתְכֶ֤ם\rb* \rb a possession|מֽוֹרָשָׁה֙\rb* \rb of the rest|לִשְׁאֵרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb and were taken up|וַתֵּֽעֲל֛וּ\rb* \rb in slander|וְדִבַּת־\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the lips|שְׂפַ֥ת\rb* \rb of their talkers|לָשׁ֖וֹן\rb*\rb |עָֽם׃\rb*, \v 4 \rb therefore|לָכֵן֙\rb*, \rb O mountains|הָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb hear|שִׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb*.
\p \rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְ֠הוִה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר\rb* \rb to the mountains|לֶהָרִ֨ים\rb* \rb and hills|וְלַגְּבָע֜וֹת\rb*, \rb to the ravines|לָאֲפִיקִ֣ים\rb* \rb and valleys|וְלַגֵּאָי֗וֹת\rb*, \rb to the desolate|הַשֹּֽׁמְמוֹת֙\rb* \rb ruins|וְלֶחֳרָב֤וֹת\rb* \rb and abandoned|הַנֶּעֱזָב֔וֹת\rb* \rb cities|וְלֶעָרִ֣ים\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb have become|הָי֤וּ\rb* \rb a spoil|לְבַז֙\rb* \rb and a mockery|וּלְלַ֔עַג\rb* \rb to the rest|לִשְׁאֵרִ֥ית\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb around you|מִסָּבִֽיב׃ס\rb*. \v 5 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִה֒\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֮\rb*: \rb Surely|אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹ֠א\rb* \rb in My burning|בְּאֵ֨שׁ\rb* \rb zeal|קִנְאָתִ֥י\rb* \rb I have spoken|דִבַּ֛רְתִּי\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the rest|שְׁאֵרִ֥ית\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb*, \rb and against|וְעַל־\rb* \rb all|כֻּלָּ֑א\rb* \rb Edom|אֱד֣וֹם\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb took|נָתְנֽוּ־\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My land|אַרְצִ֣י׀\rb*\rb |לָ֠הֶם\rb* \rb as their own possession|לְמ֨וֹרָשָׁ֜ה\rb* \rb with wholehearted|כָּל־\rb*\rb |לֵבָב֙\rb* \rb joy|בְּשִׂמְחַ֤ת\rb* \rb and utter contempt|בִּשְׁאָ֣ט\rb*\rb |נֶ֔פֶשׁ\rb*, \rb so that|לְמַ֥עַן\rb* \rb its pastureland|מִגְרָשָׁ֖הּ\rb* \rb became plunder|לָבַֽז׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֕ן\rb*, \rb prophesy|הִנָּבֵ֖א\rb* \rb concerning|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|אַדְמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֡\rb* \rb the mountains|לֶהָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb and hills|וְ֠לַגְּבָעוֹת\rb*, \rb the ravines|לָאֲפִיקִ֨ים\rb* \rb and valleys|וְלַגֵּאָי֜וֹת\rb*, \rb that this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר׀\rb*: \rb Behold|הִנְנִ֨י\rb*, \rb I have spoken|דִּבַּ֔רְתִּי\rb* \rb in My burning|וּבַחֲמָתִי֙\rb* \rb zeal|בְקִנְאָתִ֤י\rb* \rb because|יַ֛עַן\rb* \rb you have endured|נְשָׂאתֶֽם׃\rb* \rb the reproach|כְּלִמַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of the nations|גּוֹיִ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: \rb I|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb have sworn|נָשָׂ֣אתִי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb with an uplifted hand|יָדִ֑י\rb* \rb that surely|אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹ֤א\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb around|מִסָּבִ֔יב\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֣ם\rb*\rb |הֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb will endure|יִשָּֽׂאוּ׃\rb* \rb reproach of their own|כְּלִמָּתָ֥ם\rb*. \v 8 \rb But you|וְאַתֶּ֞ם\rb*, \rb O mountains|הָרֵ֤י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*, \rb will produce|תִּתֵּ֔נוּ\rb* \rb branches|עַנְפְּכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb and bear|תִּשְׂא֖וּ\rb* \rb fruit|וּפֶרְיְכֶ֥ם\rb* \rb for My people|לְעַמִּ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they will soon|קֵרְב֖וּ\rb* \rb come home|לָבֽוֹא׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb For|כִּ֖י\rb* \rb behold|הִנְנִ֣י\rb*, \rb I am on your side|אֲלֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*; \rb I will turn|וּפָנִ֣יתִי\rb* \rb toward you|אֲלֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and you will be tilled|וְנֶעֱבַדְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb and sown|וְנִזְרַעְתֶּֽם׃\rb*. \v 10 \rb I will multiply|וְהִרְבֵּיתִ֤י\rb* \rb the people|אָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb upon you|עֲלֵיכֶם֙\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* — \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb in its entirety|כֻּלֹּ֑ה\rb*. \rb The cities|הֶֽעָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb will be inhabited|וְנֹֽשְׁבוּ֙\rb* \rb and the ruins|וְהֶחֳרָב֖וֹת\rb* \rb rebuilt|תִּבָּנֶֽינָה׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb I will fill|וְהִרְבֵּיתִ֧י\rb*\rb |עֲלֵיכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb you with people|אָדָ֥ם\rb* \rb and animals|וּבְהֵמָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and they will multiply|וְרָב֣וּ\rb* \rb and be fruitful|וּפָר֑וּ\rb*. \rb I will make you as inhabited|וְהוֹשַׁבְתִּ֨י\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֜ם\rb* \rb as you once were|כְּקַדְמֽוֹתֵיכֶ֗ם\rb*, \rb and I will make you prosper|וְהֵטִֽבֹתִי֙\rb* \rb more than before|מֵרִאשֹׁ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb*. \rb Then you will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Yes, I will cause|אֶת־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֤י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb to walk|וְהוֹלַכְתִּי֩\rb* \rb upon you|עֲלֵיכֶ֨ם\rb*; \rb they will possess you|וִֽירֵשׁ֔וּךָ\rb*, \rb and you will be|וְהָיִ֥יתָ\rb* \rb their|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb inheritance|לְנַחֲלָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and you will no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb longer|תוֹסִ֥ף\rb*\rb |ע֖וֹד\rb* \rb deprive them of their children|לְשַׁכְּלָֽם׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb For this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: \rb Because|יַ֚עַן\rb* \rb people say|אֹמְרִ֣ים\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֔ם\rb*, ‘\rb You|אָתִּי\rb* \rb devour|אֹכֶ֥לֶת\rb* \rb men|אָדָ֖ם\rb* \rb and deprive your nation|גּוֹיֵךְ\rb*\rb |הָיִֽית׃\rb* \rb of its children|וּמְשַׁכֶּ֥לֶת\rb*,’ \v 14 \rb therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb you will no|לֹא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֔וֹד\rb* \rb devour|תֹ֣אכְלִי\rb* \rb men|אָדָם֙\rb* \rb or deprive|תְכַשְּׁלִי\rb*\rb |ע֑וֹד\rb* \rb your nation of its children|וְגוֹיֵךְ\rb*,\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb I will no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb longer allow|עוֹד֙\rb* \rb the taunts|כְּלִמַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb to be heard|אַשְׁמִ֨יעַ\rb* \rb against you|אֵלַ֤יִךְ\rb*, \rb and you will no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb longer|ע֑וֹד\rb* \rb endure|תִשְׂאִי־\rb* \rb the reproach|וְחֶרְפַּ֥ת\rb* \rb of the peoples|עַמִּ֖ים\rb* \rb or|לֹא־\rb*\rb |ע֔וֹד\rb* \rb cause your nation|וְגוֹיֵךְ\rb* \rb to stumble|תַכְשִׁ֣לִי\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃ס\rb*.”
\s1 A New Heart and a New Spirit
\r (\ref Romans 8:9–11|ROM 8:9-11\ref*; \ref Galatians 5:16–26|GAL 5:16-26\ref*)
\p \v 16 \rb Again the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 17 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb when the people|בֵּ֤ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb lived|יֹשְׁבִ֣ים\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb their land|אַדְמָתָ֔ם\rb*, \rb they defiled|וַיְטַמְּא֣וּ\rb* \rb it|אוֹתָ֔הּ\rb* \rb by their own ways|בְּדַרְכָּ֖ם\rb* \rb and deeds|וּבַעֲלִֽילוֹתָ֑ם\rb*. \rb Their behavior|דַרְכָּ֖ם\rb* \rb before Me|לְפָנָֽי׃\rb* \rb was|הָיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb like the uncleanness|כְּטֻמְאַת֙\rb* \rb of a woman’s impurity|הַנִּדָּ֔ה\rb*. \v 18 \rb So I poured out|וָאֶשְׁפֹּ֤ךְ\rb* \rb My wrath|חֲמָתִי֙\rb* \rb upon them|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb because of|עַל־\rb* \rb the blood|הַדָּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they had shed|שָׁפְכ֣וּ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb and because they had defiled|טִמְּאֽוּהָ׃\rb* \rb it with their idols|וּבְגִלּוּלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb I dispersed|וָאָפִ֤יץ\rb* \rb them|אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb*, \rb and they were scattered|וַיִּזָּר֖וּ\rb* \rb throughout the lands|בָּאֲרָצ֑וֹת\rb*. \rb I judged them|שְׁפַטְתִּֽים׃\rb* \rb according to their ways|כְּדַרְכָּ֥ם\rb* \rb and deeds|וְכַעֲלִילוֹתָ֖ם\rb*. \v 20 \rb |וַיָּב֗וֹא\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb And wherever|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they went|בָּ֣אוּ\rb* \rb among the nations|הַגּוֹיִם֙\rb*,\rb |שָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb they profaned|וַֽיְחַלְּל֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My holy|קָדְשִׁ֑י\rb* \rb name|שֵׁ֣ם\rb*, \rb because it was said|בֶּאֱמֹ֤ר\rb* \rb of them|לָהֶם֙\rb*, ‘\rb These|אֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb are the people|עַם־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֣ה\rb*, \rb yet they had to leave|יָצָֽאוּ׃\rb* \rb His land|וּמֵאַרְצ֖וֹ\rb*.’ \v 21 \rb But I had concern|וָאֶחְמֹ֖ל\rb* \rb for|עַל־\rb* \rb My holy|קָדְשִׁ֑י\rb* \rb name|שֵׁ֣ם\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb had profaned|חִלְּל֙וּהוּ֙\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they had gone|בָּ֥אוּ\rb*.\rb |שָֽׁמָּה׃ס\rb*
\p \v 22 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֞ן\rb* \rb tell|אֱמֹ֣ר\rb* \rb the house|לְבֵֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: \rb It is not|לֹ֧א\rb* \rb for your sake|לְמַעַנְכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb that I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb will act|עֹשֶׂ֖ה\rb*, \rb O house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb but|כִּ֤י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb for My holy|קָדְשִׁי֙\rb* \rb name|לְשֵׁם־\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you profaned|חִלַּלְתֶּ֔ם\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you went|בָּ֥אתֶם\rb*.\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb* \v 23 \rb I will show the holiness|וְקִדַּשְׁתִּ֞י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of My great|הַגָּד֗וֹל\rb* \rb name|שְׁמִ֣י\rb*, \rb which has been profaned|הַֽמְחֻלָּל֙\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb*— \rb the name|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you have profaned|חִלַּלְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb among them|בְּתוֹכָ֑ם\rb*. \rb Then the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֜ם\rb* \rb will know|וְיָדְע֨וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם֙\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb*, \rb when I show My holiness|בְּהִקָּדְשִׁ֥י\rb* \rb in you|בָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb before their eyes|לְעֵינֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb For I will take|וְלָקַחְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶם֙\rb* \rb from among|מִן־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb and gather|וְקִבַּצְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb out of all|מִכָּל־\rb* \rb the countries|הָאֲרָצ֑וֹת\rb*, \rb and I will bring|וְהֵבֵאתִ֥י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb back into|אֶל־\rb* \rb your own land|אַדְמַתְכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb I will also sprinkle|וְזָרַקְתִּ֧י\rb* \rb clean|טְהוֹרִ֖ים\rb* \rb water|מַ֥יִם\rb* \rb on you|עֲלֵיכֶ֛ם\rb*, \rb and you will be clean|וּטְהַרְתֶּ֑ם\rb*. \rb I will cleanse|אֲטַהֵ֥ר\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶֽם׃\rb* \rb from all|מִכֹּ֧ל\rb* \rb your impurities|טֻמְאוֹתֵיכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb and all|וּמִכָּל־\rb* \rb your idols|גִּלּ֥וּלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*. \v 26 \rb I will give|וְנָתַתִּ֤י\rb* \rb you|לָכֶם֙\rb* \rb a new|חָדָ֔שׁ\rb* \rb heart|לֵ֣ב\rb* \rb and put|אֶתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb a new|חֲדָשָׁ֖ה\rb* \rb spirit|וְר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb within you|בְּקִרְבְּכֶ֑ם\rb*; \rb I will remove|וַהֲסִ֨רֹתִ֜י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your heart|לֵ֤ב\rb* \rb of stone|הָאֶ֙בֶן֙\rb* \rb and give|וְנָתַתִּ֥י\rb* \rb you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb a heart|לֵ֥ב\rb*\rb |בָּשָֽׂר׃\rb* \rb of flesh|מִבְּשַׂרְכֶ֔ם\rb*. \v 27 \rb And|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb I will put|אֶתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb My Spirit|רוּחִ֖י\rb* \rb within you|בְּקִרְבְּכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and cause|וְעָשִׂ֗יתִי\rb*\rb |אֵ֤ת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you to walk|תֵּלֵ֔כוּ\rb* \rb in My statutes|בְּחֻקַּי֙\rb* \rb and to carefully|תִּשְׁמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb observe|וַעֲשִׂיתֶֽם׃\rb* \rb My ordinances|וּמִשְׁפָּטַ֥י\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb Then you will live|וִישַׁבְתֶּ֣ם\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I gave|נָתַ֖תִּי\rb* \rb your forefathers|לַאֲבֹֽתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*; \rb you will be|וִהְיִ֤יתֶם\rb* \rb My|לִי֙\rb* \rb people|לְעָ֔ם\rb*, \rb and I|וְאָ֣נֹכִ֔י\rb* \rb will be|אֶהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb your|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb God|לֵאלֹהִֽים׃\rb*. \v 29 \rb I will save|וְהוֹשַׁעְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb from all|מִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb your uncleanness|טֻמְאֽוֹתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb I will summon|וְקָרָ֤אתִי\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the grain|הַדָּגָן֙\rb* \rb and make it plentiful|וְהִרְבֵּיתִ֣י\rb*,\rb |אֹת֔וֹ\rb* \rb and I will not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb bring|אֶתֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb famine|רָעָֽב׃\rb* \rb upon you|עֲלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*. \v 30 \rb I will also make the fruit|פְּרִ֣י\rb* \rb of the trees|הָעֵ֔ץ\rb* \rb and the crops|וּתְנוּבַ֖ת\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֑ה\rb* \rb plentiful|וְהִרְבֵּיתִי֙\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb so that|לְמַ֗עַן\rb*\rb |אֲ֠שֶׁר\rb* \rb you will no|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb longer|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb bear|תִקְח֥וּ\rb* \rb reproach|חֶרְפַּ֥ת\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִֽם׃\rb* \rb on account of famine|רָעָ֖ב\rb*.
\p \v 31 \rb Then you will remember|וּזְכַרְתֶּם֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your evil|הָרָעִ֔ים\rb* \rb ways|דַּרְכֵיכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb and wicked deeds|וּמַעַלְלֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |טוֹבִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and you will loathe|וּנְקֹֽטֹתֶם֙\rb* \rb yourselves|בִּפְנֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb for|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb your iniquities|עֲוֺנֹ֣תֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and|וְעַ֖ל\rb* \rb abominations|תּוֹעֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 32 \rb It is not|לֹ֧א\rb* \rb for your sake|לְמַעַנְכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb that I|אֲנִֽי־\rb* \rb will act|עֹשֶׂ֗ה\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם֙\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* — \rb let it be known|יִוָּדַ֖ע\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Be ashamed|בּ֧וֹשׁוּ\rb* \rb and disgraced|וְהִכָּלְמ֛וּ\rb* \rb for your ways|מִדַּרְכֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb O house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*!
\p \v 33 \rb This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: \rb On the day|בְּיוֹם֙\rb* \rb I cleanse|טַהֲרִ֣י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb from all|מִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb your iniquities|עֲוֺנֽוֹתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb I will cause the cities|הֶ֣עָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb to be resettled|וְהֽוֹשַׁבְתִּי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and the ruins|הֶחֳרָבֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb to be rebuilt|וְנִבְנ֖וּ\rb*. \v 34 \rb The desolate|הַנְּשַׁמָּ֖ה\rb* \rb land|וְהָאָ֥רֶץ\rb* \rb will be cultivated|תֵּֽעָבֵ֑ד\rb* \rb instead of|תַּ֚חַת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb lying|הָיְתָ֣ה\rb* \rb desolate|שְׁמָמָ֔ה\rb* \rb in the sight|לְעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb who pass through|עוֹבֵֽר׃\rb*. \v 35 \rb Then they will say|וְאָמְר֗וּ\rb*, ‘\rb This|הַלֵּ֙זוּ֙\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb that was desolate|הַנְּשַׁמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb has become|הָיְתָ֖ה\rb* \rb like the garden|כְּגַן־\rb* \rb of Eden|עֵ֑דֶן\rb*. \rb The cities|וְהֶעָרִ֧ים\rb* \rb that were once ruined|הֶחֳרֵב֛וֹת\rb*, \rb desolate|וְהַֽנְשַׁמּ֥וֹת\rb*, \rb and destroyed|וְהַנֶּהֱרָס֖וֹת\rb* \rb are now fortified|בְּצוּר֥וֹת\rb* \rb and inhabited|יָשָֽׁבוּ׃\rb*.’
\p \v 36 \rb Then the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֗ם\rb* \rb around you|סְבִיבוֹתֵיכֶם֒\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb remain|יִֽשָּׁאֲרוּ֮\rb* \rb will know|וְיָדְע֣וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י׀\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb*, \rb have rebuilt|בָּנִ֙יתִי֙\rb* \rb what was destroyed|הַנֶּ֣הֱרָס֔וֹת\rb*, \rb and I have replanted|נָטַ֖עְתִּי\rb* \rb what was desolate|הַנְּשַׁמָּ֑ה\rb*. \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*, \rb have spoken|דִּבַּ֥רְתִּי\rb*, \rb and I will do it|וְעָשִֽׂיתִי׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 37 \rb This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: \rb Once again|ע֗וֹד\rb* \rb I will hear the plea|אִדָּרֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb of the house|לְבֵֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb and do|לַעֲשׂ֣וֹת\rb* \rb for them|לָהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb this|זֹ֛את\rb*: \rb I will multiply|אַרְבֶּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb their people|אָדָֽם׃\rb* \rb like a flock|כַּצֹּ֖אן\rb*. \v 38 \rb Like the numerous flocks|כְּצֹ֣אן\rb* \rb for sacrifices|קָֽדָשִׁ֗ים\rb*\rb |כְּצֹ֤אן\rb* \rb at Jerusalem|יְרוּשָׁלִַ֙ם֙\rb* \rb during her appointed feasts|בְּמ֣וֹעֲדֶ֔יהָ\rb*, \rb so|כֵּ֤ן\rb* \rb the ruined|הֶחֳרֵב֔וֹת\rb* \rb cities|הֶעָרִ֣ים\rb* \rb will be|תִּהְיֶ֙ינָה֙\rb* \rb filled|מְלֵא֖וֹת\rb* \rb with flocks|צֹ֣אן\rb* \rb of people|אָדָ֑ם\rb*. \rb Then they will know|וְיָדְע֖וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.”
\c 37
\s1 The Valley of Dry Bones
\p \v 1 \rb The hand|יַד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָה֒\rb* \rb was|הָיְתָ֣ה\rb* \rb upon me|עָלַי֮\rb*, \rb and He brought me out|וַיּוֹצִאֵ֤נִי\rb* \rb by His|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb Spirit|בְר֙וּחַ֙\rb* \rb and set me down|וַיְנִיחֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb in the middle|בְּת֣וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the valley|הַבִּקְעָ֑ה\rb*, \rb and it was|וְהִ֖יא\rb* \rb full of|מְלֵאָ֥ה\rb* \rb bones|עֲצָמֽוֹת׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb He led me|וְהֶעֱבִירַ֥נִי\rb* \rb all|סָבִ֣יב׀\rb* \rb around|סָבִ֑יב\rb* \rb among them|עֲלֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb and I saw|וְהִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb a great|מְאֹד֙\rb* \rb many bones|רַבּ֤וֹת\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the floor|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the valley|הַבִּקְעָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and indeed|וְהִנֵּ֖ה\rb*, \rb they were very|מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb dry|יְבֵשׁ֥וֹת\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb Then He asked|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*, “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*, \rb can these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb bones|הָעֲצָמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb come to life|הֲתִחְיֶ֖ינָה\rb*?”
\p “\rb O Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֖ה\rb*,” \rb I replied|וָאֹמַ֕ר\rb*, “\rb only You|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb know|יָדָֽעְתָּ׃\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb And He said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*, “\rb Prophesy|הִנָּבֵ֖א\rb* \rb concerning|עַל־\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb bones|הָעֲצָמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, ‘\rb Dry|הַיְבֵשׁ֔וֹת\rb* \rb bones|הָעֲצָמוֹת֙\rb*, \rb hear|שִׁמְע֖וּ\rb* \rb the word|דְּבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*! \v 5 \rb This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb* \rb to these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb bones|לָעֲצָמ֖וֹת\rb*: \rb I|אֲנִ֜י\rb* \rb will cause breath|ר֖וּחַ\rb*\f + \fr 37:5 \ft Or \fqa spirit\ft ; also in verses 6, 9, and 10\f* \rb to enter|מֵבִ֥יא\rb* \rb you|בָכֶ֛ם\rb*, \rb and you will come to life|וִחְיִיתֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb I will attach|וְנָתַתִּי֩\rb* \rb tendons|גִּדִ֜ים\rb* \rb to you|עֲלֵיכֶ֨ם\rb* \rb and make flesh|בָּשָׂ֗ר\rb* \rb grow|וְֽהַעֲלֵתִ֧י\rb* \rb upon you|עֲלֵיכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb and cover|וְקָרַמְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb you|עֲלֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb with skin|ע֔וֹר\rb*. \rb I will put|וְנָתַתִּ֥י\rb* \rb breath|ר֖וּחַ\rb* \rb within you|בָכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb so that you will come to life|וִחְיִיתֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Then you will know|וִידַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.’”
\p \v 7 \rb So I prophesied|וְנִבֵּ֖אתִי\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I had been commanded|צֻוֵּ֑יתִי\rb*. \rb And as I prophesied|כְּהִנָּֽבְאִי֙\rb*, \rb there was|וַֽיְהִי־\rb* \rb suddenly|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb a noise|ק֤וֹל\rb*, \rb a rattling|רַ֔עַשׁ\rb*, \rb and the bones|עֲצָמ֔וֹת\rb* \rb came together|וַתִּקְרְב֣וּ\rb*, \rb bone|עֶ֖צֶם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb bone|עַצְמֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb As I looked on|וְרָאִ֜יתִי\rb*, \rb tendons|גִּדִים֙\rb* \rb appeared|וְהִנֵּֽה־\rb* \rb on them|עֲלֵיהֶ֤ם\rb*, \rb flesh|וּבָשָׂ֣ר\rb* \rb grew|עָלָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and skin|ע֖וֹר\rb*\rb |מִלְמָ֑עְלָה\rb* \rb covered them|וַיִּקְרַ֧ם\rb*;\rb |עֲלֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb but there was no|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb breath|וְר֖וּחַ\rb* \rb in them|בָּהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Then He said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*, “\rb Prophesy|הִנָּבֵ֖א\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the breath|הָר֑וּחַ\rb*; \rb prophesy|הִנָּבֵ֣א\rb*, \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָ֠דָם\rb*, \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֨\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the breath|הָר֜וּחַ\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר׀\rb*: \rb Come|בֹּ֣אִי\rb* \rb from the four|מֵאַרְבַּ֤ע\rb* \rb winds|הָר֔וּחַ\rb*, \rb O breath|רוּחוֹת֙\rb*, \rb and breathe|וּפְחִ֛י\rb* \rb into these|הָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb slain|בַּהֲרוּגִ֥ים\rb*, \rb so that they may live|וְיִֽחְיֽוּ׃\rb*!”
\p \v 10 \rb So I prophesied|וְהִנַּבֵּ֖אתִי\rb* \rb as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb He had commanded me|צִוָּ֑נִי\rb*, \rb and the breath|הָר֜וּחַ\rb* \rb entered|וַתָּבוֹא֩\rb* \rb them|בָהֶ֨ם\rb*, \rb and they came to life|וַיִּֽחְי֗וּ\rb* \rb and stood|וַיַּֽעַמְדוּ֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb their feet|רַגְלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* — \rb a vast|גָּד֥וֹל\rb*\rb |מְאֹד־\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃ס\rb* \rb army|חַ֖יִל\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb Then He said|וַיֹּאמֶר֮\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַי֒\rb*, “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֕ם\rb*, \rb these|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb* \rb bones|הָעֲצָמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb are the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*. \rb Look|הִנֵּ֣ה\rb*, \rb they|הֵ֑מָּה\rb* \rb are saying|אֹמְרִ֗ים\rb*, ‘\rb Our bones|עַצְמוֹתֵ֛ינוּ\rb* \rb are dried up|יָבְשׁ֧וּ\rb*, \rb and our hope|תִקְוָתֵ֖נוּ\rb* \rb has perished|וְאָבְדָ֥ה\rb*; \rb we are cut off|נִגְזַ֥רְנוּ\rb*.’
\p \v 12 \rb Therefore|לָכֵן֩\rb* \rb prophesy|הִנָּבֵ֨א\rb* \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֜\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִה֒\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֮\rb*: ‘\rb O|הִנֵּה֩\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֑י\rb*, \rb I|אֲנִ֨י\rb* \rb will open|פֹתֵ֜חַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your graves|קִבְרֽוֹתֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and bring you up|וְהַעֲלֵיתִ֥י\rb* \rb from|אֶתְכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb them|מִקִּבְרוֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb and I will bring you back|וְהֵבֵאתִ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אַדְמַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*. \v 13 \rb Then you, My people|עַמִּֽי׃\rb*, \rb will know|וִֽידַעְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*, \rb when I open|בְּפִתְחִ֣י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb your graves|קִבְרֽוֹתֵיכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and bring you up|וּבְהַעֲלוֹתִ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶתְכֶ֛ם\rb* \rb from them|מִקִּבְרוֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*. \v 14 \rb I will put|וְנָתַתִּ֨י\rb* \rb My Spirit|רוּחִ֤י\rb* \rb in you|בָכֶם֙\rb* \rb and you will live|וִחְיִיתֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and I will settle|וְהִנַּחְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb you|אֶתְכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb your own land|אַדְמַתְכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Then you will know|וִידַעְתֶּ֞ם\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֧י\rb*, \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֛ה\rb*, \rb have spoken|דִּבַּ֥רְתִּי\rb*, \rb and I will do it|וְעָשִׂ֖יתִי\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃פ\rb*.’”
\s1 One Nation with One King
\p \v 15 \rb Again the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 16 “\rb And you|וְאַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb take|קַח־\rb* \rb a single|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb stick|עֵ֣ץ\rb*\f + \fr 37:16 \ft Or \fqa branch\ft ; also in verses 17, 19, and 20\f* \rb and write|וּכְתֹ֤ב\rb* \rb on it|עָלָיו֙\rb*: ‘\rb Belonging to Judah|לִֽיהוּדָ֔ה\rb* \rb and to the Israelites|וְלִבְנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb associated with him|חֲבֵרוֹ\rb*.’ \rb Then take|וּלְקַח֙\rb* \rb another|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb stick|עֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb and write|וּכְת֣וֹב\rb* \rb on it|עָלָ֗יו\rb*: ‘\rb Belonging to Joseph|לְיוֹסֵף֙\rb*— \rb the stick|עֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֔יִם\rb*— \rb and to all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb associated with him|חֲבֵרוֹ׃\rb*.’ \v 17 \rb Then join|וְקָרַ֨ב\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֜ם\rb* \rb together|אֶחָ֧ד\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |אֶחָ֛ד\rb* \rb into one|אֶחָ֑ד\rb* \rb stick|לְעֵ֣ץ\rb*, \rb so that they become|וְהָי֥וּ\rb* \rb one|לַאֲחָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb in your hand|בְּיָדֶֽךָ׃\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb When|וְכַֽאֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb your people|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |עַמְּךָ֖\rb*\rb |לֵאמֹ֑ר\rb* \rb ask|יֹאמְר֣וּ\rb* \rb you|אֵלֶ֔יךָ\rb*, ‘\rb Won’t|הֲלֽוֹא־\rb* \rb you explain|תַגִּ֥יד\rb* \rb to us|לָ֖נוּ\rb* \rb what|מָה־\rb* \rb you mean by|לָּֽךְ׃\rb* \rb these|אֵ֥לֶּה\rb*?’ \v 19 \rb you are to tell|דַּבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִה֒\rb*\rb |הִנֵּה֩\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֮\rb*: ‘\rb I|אֲנִ֨י\rb* \rb will take|לֹקֵ֜חַ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the stick|עֵ֤ץ\rb* \rb of Joseph|יוֹסֵף֙\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb is in the hand|בְּיַד־\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֔יִם\rb*, \rb and the tribes|וְשִׁבְטֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb associated with him|חֲבֵרוֹ\rb*, \rb and I will put|וְנָתַתִּי֩\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֨ם\rb* \rb together with|עָלָ֜יו\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the stick|עֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb*. \rb I will make them|וַֽעֲשִׂיתִם֙\rb* \rb into a single|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb stick|לְעֵ֣ץ\rb*, \rb and they will become|וְהָי֥וּ\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb in My hand|בְּיָדִֽי׃\rb*.’
\p \v 20 \rb When the sticks|הָעֵצִ֜ים\rb* \rb on which|אֲ‍ֽשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you write|תִּכְתֹּ֧ב\rb* \rb are|וְהָי֨וּ\rb* \rb in your hand|בְּיָדְךָ֖\rb* \rb and in full view of the people|לְעֵינֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*, \v 21 \rb you are to tell|וְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb them|אֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִה֒\rb*\rb |הִנֵּ֨ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֮\rb*: ‘\rb I|אֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb will take|לֹקֵ֙חַ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb out of|מִבֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֖ם\rb* \rb to which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they have gone|הָֽלְכוּ־\rb*,\rb |שָׁ֑ם\rb* \rb and I will gather them|וְקִבַּצְתִּ֤י\rb* \rb from|אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb all around|מִסָּבִ֔יב\rb* \rb and bring|וְהֵבֵאתִ֥י\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb their own land|אַדְמָתָֽם׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb I will make|וְעָשִׂ֣יתִי\rb* \rb them|אֹ֠תָם\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֤ד\rb* \rb nation|לְג֨וֹי\rb* \rb in the land|בָּאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb*, \rb on the mountains|בְּהָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb and one|אֶחָ֛ד\rb* \rb king|וּמֶ֧לֶךְ\rb* \rb will rule over|יִֽהְיֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |לְמֶ֑לֶךְ\rb* \rb all of them|לְכֻלָּ֖ם\rb*. \rb Then they will no|וְלֹ֤א\rb*\rb |עוֹד֙\rb* \rb longer|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb be|יִהְיֶה\rb* \rb two|לִשְׁנֵ֣י\rb* \rb nations|גוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb and will never|וְלֹ֨א\rb* \rb again|עֽוֹד׃\rb* \rb be divided|יֵחָ֥צוּ\rb* \rb into two|לִשְׁתֵּ֥י\rb* \rb kingdoms|מַמְלָכ֖וֹת\rb*.
\p \v 23 \rb They will no|וְלֹ֧א\rb* \rb longer|ע֗וֹד\rb* \rb defile themselves|יִֽטַמְּא֣וּ\rb* \rb with their idols|בְּגִלּֽוּלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb or detestable images|וּבְשִׁקּ֣וּצֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb or with any|וּבְכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb of their transgressions|פִּשְׁעֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb I will save|וְהוֹשַׁעְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֗ם\rb* \rb from all|מִכֹּ֤ל\rb* \rb their apostasies|מוֹשְׁבֹֽתֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb by which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they sinned|חָטְא֣וּ\rb*,\f + \fr 37:23 \ft Many Hebrew manuscripts (see also LXX); most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa all their dwelling places where they sinned\f* \rb and I will cleanse them|וְטִהַרְתִּ֤י\rb*.\rb |אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb Then they will be|וְהָיוּ־\rb* \rb My|לִ֣י\rb* \rb people|לְעָ֔ם\rb*, \rb and I|וַאֲנִ֕י\rb* \rb will be|אֶהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb their|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb God|לֵאלֹהִֽים׃\rb*. \v 24 \rb My servant|וְעַבְדִּ֤י\rb* \rb David|דָוִד֙\rb* \rb will be king|מֶ֣לֶךְ\rb* \rb over them|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb and there will be|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb shepherd|וְרוֹעֶ֥ה\rb* \rb for all of them|לְכֻלָּ֑ם\rb*. \rb They will follow|יֵלֵ֔כוּ\rb* \rb My ordinances|וּבְמִשְׁפָּטַ֣י\rb* \rb and keep|יִשְׁמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb and observe|וְעָשׂ֥וּ\rb* \rb My statutes|וְחֻקֹּתַ֥י\rb*.\rb |אוֹתָֽם׃\rb*
\p \v 25 \rb They will live|וְיָשְׁב֣וּ\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I gave|נָתַ֙תִּי֙\rb* \rb to My servant|לְעַבְדִּ֣י\rb* \rb Jacob|לְיַֽעֲקֹ֔ב\rb*, \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb your fathers|אֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb* \rb lived|יָֽשְׁבוּ־\rb*. \rb They will live|וְיָשְׁב֣וּ\rb* \rb there|עָלֶ֡יהָ\rb*\rb |הֵ֠מָּה\rb* \rb forever|עַד־\rb*\rb |עוֹלָ֔ם\rb* \rb with their children|וּבְנֵיהֶ֞ם\rb* \rb and grandchildren|וּבְנֵ֤י\rb*\rb |בְנֵיהֶם֙\rb*, \rb and My servant|עַבְדִּ֔י\rb* \rb David|וְדָוִ֣ד\rb* \rb will be their prince|נָשִׂ֥יא\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָֽם׃\rb*. \v 26 \rb And I will make|וְכָרַתִּ֤י\rb* \rb a covenant|בְּרִ֣ית\rb* \rb of peace|שָׁל֔וֹם\rb* \rb with them|לָהֶם֙\rb*; \rb it will be|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb*\rb |אוֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb an everlasting|עוֹלָ֖ם\rb* \rb covenant|בְּרִ֥ית\rb*. \rb I will establish them|וּנְתַתִּים֙\rb* \rb and multiply|וְהִרְבֵּיתִ֣י\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֔ם\rb*, \rb and I will set|וְנָתַתִּ֧י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My sanctuary|מִקְדָּשִׁ֛י\rb* \rb among them|בְּתוֹכָ֖ם\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָֽם׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb My dwelling place|מִשְׁכָּנִי֙\rb*\f + \fr 37:27 \ft Or \fqa My tabernacle\f* \rb will be|וְהָיָ֤ה\rb* \rb with them|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*; \rb I will be|וְהָיִ֥יתִי\rb* \rb their|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb God|לֵֽאלֹהִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and they|וְהֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb will be|יִֽהְיוּ־\rb* \rb My|לִ֥י\rb* \rb people|לְעָֽם׃\rb*.\f + \fr 37:27 \ft Cited in \ref 2 Corinthians 6:16|2CO 6:16\ref*\f* \v 28 \rb Then the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb* \rb will know|וְיָֽדְעוּ֙\rb* \rb that|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb sanctify|מְקַדֵּ֖שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb when My sanctuary|מִקְדָּשִׁ֛י\rb* \rb is|בִּהְי֧וֹת\rb* \rb among them|בְּתוֹכָ֖ם\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָֽם׃ס\rb*.’”
\c 38
\s1 A Prophecy against Gog
\p \v 1 \rb And the word|דְבַר־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb came|וַיְהִ֥י\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֥י\rb*, \rb saying|לֵאמֹֽר׃\rb*, \v 2 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb set|שִׂ֤ים\rb* \rb your face|פָּנֶ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb against|אֶל־\rb* \rb Gog|גּוֹג֙\rb* \rb of the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Magog|הַמָּג֔וֹג\rb*, \rb the chief|רֹ֖אשׁ\rb* \rb prince|נְשִׂ֕יא\rb* \rb of Meshech|מֶ֣שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb and Tubal|וְתֻבָ֑ל\rb*.\f + \fr 38:2 \ft Or \fqa of Magog, the prince of Rosh, Meshech, and Tubal\f* \rb Prophesy|וְהִנָּבֵ֖א\rb* \rb against him|עָלָֽיו׃\rb* \v 3 \rb and declare|וְאָ֣מַרְתָּ֔\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*: \rb Behold|הִנְנִ֤י\rb*, \rb I am against you|אֵלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*, \rb O Gog|גּ֔וֹג\rb*, \rb chief|רֹ֖אשׁ\rb* \rb prince|נְשִׂ֕יא\rb* \rb of Meshech|מֶ֥שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb and Tubal|וְתֻבָֽל׃\rb*.\f + \fr 38:3 \ft Or \fqa Gog, the prince of Rosh, Meshech, and Tubal\f* \v 4 \rb I will turn you around|וְשׁ֣וֹבַבְתִּ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb put|וְנָתַתִּ֥י\rb* \rb hooks|חַחִ֖ים\rb* \rb in your jaws|בִּלְחָיֶ֑יךָ\rb*, \rb and bring you out|וְהוֹצֵאתִי֩\rb*\rb |אוֹתְךָ֨\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your army|חֵילֶ֜ךָ\rb* — \rb your horses|סוּסִ֣ים\rb*, \rb your horsemen|וּפָרָשִׁ֗ים\rb* \rb in full|כֻּלָּ֔ם\rb* \rb armor|לְבֻשֵׁ֤י\rb*\rb |מִכְלוֹל֙\rb*, \rb and a great|רָב֙\rb* \rb company|קָהָ֥ל\rb* \rb armed with shields|צִנָּ֣ה\rb* \rb and bucklers|וּמָגֵ֔ן\rb*, \rb all|כֻּלָּֽם׃\rb* \rb brandishing|תֹּפְשֵׂ֥י\rb* \rb their swords|חֲרָב֖וֹת\rb*. \v 5 \rb Persia|פָּרַ֛ס\rb*, \rb Cush|כּ֥וּשׁ\rb*,\f + \fr 38:5 \ft That is, the upper Nile region\f* \rb and Put|וּפ֖וּט\rb* \rb will accompany them|אִתָּ֑ם\rb*, \rb all|כֻּלָּ֖ם\rb* \rb with shields|מָגֵ֥ן\rb* \rb and helmets|וְכוֹבָֽע׃\rb*, \v 6 \rb as well as Gomer|גֹּ֚מֶר\rb* \rb with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb its troops|אֲגַפֶּ֔יהָ\rb*, \rb and Beth-togarmah|בֵּ֚ית\rb*\rb |תּֽוֹגַרְמָ֔ה\rb* \rb from the far|יַרְכְּתֵ֥י\rb* \rb north|צָפ֖וֹן\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb with all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its troops|אֲגַפָּ֑יו\rb*— \rb the many|רַבִּ֖ים\rb* \rb nations|עַמִּ֥ים\rb* \rb with you|אִתָּֽךְ׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb Get ready|הִכֹּן֙\rb*; \rb prepare|וְהָכֵ֣ן\rb* \rb yourself|לְךָ֔\rb*, \rb you|אַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb your company|קְהָלֶ֖ךָ\rb* \rb gathered|הַנִּקְהָלִ֣ים\rb* \rb around you|עָלֶ֑יךָ\rb*; \rb you will be|וְהָיִ֥יתָ\rb* \rb their|לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb guard|לְמִשְׁמָֽר׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb After a long|רַבִּים֮\rb* \rb time|מִיָּמִ֣ים\rb* \rb you will be summoned|תִּפָּקֵד֒\rb*. \rb In the latter|בְּאַחֲרִ֨ית\rb* \rb years|הַשָּׁנִ֜ים\rb* \rb you will enter|תָּב֣וֹא׀\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֣רֶץ׀\rb* \rb that has recovered|מְשׁוֹבֶ֣בֶת\rb* \rb from war|מֵחֶ֗רֶב\rb*, \rb whose people were gathered|מְקֻבֶּ֙צֶת֙\rb* \rb from many|רַבִּ֔ים\rb* \rb nations|מֵעַמִּ֣ים\rb* \rb to|עַ֚ל\rb* \rb the mountains|הָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb had long|תָּמִ֑יד\rb* \rb been|הָי֥וּ\rb* \rb desolate|לְחָרְבָּ֖ה\rb*. \rb They|וְהִיא֙\rb* \rb had been brought out|הוּצָ֔אָה\rb* \rb from the nations|מֵעַמִּ֣ים\rb*, \rb and all|כֻּלָּֽם׃\rb* \rb now dwell|וְיָשְׁב֥וּ\rb* \rb securely|לָבֶ֖טַח\rb*. \v 9 \rb You|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb your troops|אֲגַפֶּ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb and many|רַבִּ֖ים\rb* \rb peoples|וְעַמִּ֥ים\rb* \rb with you|אוֹתָֽךְ׃ס\rb* \rb will go up|וְעָלִ֙יתָ֙\rb*, \rb advancing|תָב֔וֹא\rb* \rb like a thunderstorm|כַּשֹּׁאָ֣ה\rb*; \rb you will be|תִּֽהְיֶ֑ה\rb* \rb like a cloud|כֶּעָנָ֛ן\rb* \rb covering|לְכַסּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb This is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*:\rb |וְהָיָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb On that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*, \rb thoughts|דְבָרִים֙\rb* \rb will arise|יַעֲל֤וּ\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb your mind|לְבָבֶ֔ךָ\rb*, \rb and you will devise|וְחָשַׁבְתָּ֖\rb* \rb an evil|רָעָֽה׃\rb* \rb plan|מַחֲשֶׁ֥בֶת\rb*. \v 11 \rb You will say|וְאָמַרְתָּ֗\rb*, ‘\rb I will go up|אֶֽעֱלֶה֙\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb a land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of unwalled villages|פְּרָז֔וֹת\rb*; \rb I will come against|אָבוֹא֙\rb* \rb a quiet people|הַשֹּׁ֣קְטִ֔ים\rb* \rb who dwell|יֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb* \rb securely|לָבֶ֑טַח\rb*, \rb all|כֻּלָּ֗ם\rb* \rb of them living|יֹֽשְׁבִים֙\rb* \rb without|בְּאֵ֣ין\rb* \rb walls|חוֹמָ֔ה\rb* \rb or|אֵ֥ין\rb* \rb bars|וּבְרִ֥יחַ\rb* \rb or gates|וּדְלָתַ֖יִם\rb*— \v 12 \rb in order to seize|לִשְׁלֹ֥ל\rb* \rb the spoil|שָׁלָ֖ל\rb* \rb and carry off the plunder|וְלָבֹ֣ז\rb*\rb |בַּ֑ז\rb*, \rb to turn|לְהָשִׁ֨יב\rb* \rb a hand|יָדְךָ֜\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the desolate places|חֳרָב֣וֹת\rb* \rb now inhabited|נוֹשָׁבֹ֗ת\rb* \rb and against|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb a people|עַם֙\rb* \rb gathered|מְאֻסָּ֣ף\rb* \rb from the nations|מִגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb*, \rb who have acquired|עֹשֶׂה֙\rb* \rb livestock|מִקְנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb and possessions|וְקִנְיָ֔ן\rb* \rb and who live|יֹשְׁבֵ֖י\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the center|טַבּ֥וּר\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃\rb*.’
\p \v 13 \rb Sheba|שְׁבָ֡א\rb* \rb and Dedan|וּ֠דְדָן\rb* \rb and the merchants|וְסֹחֲרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Tarshish|תַרְשִׁ֤ישׁ\rb* \rb with all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb its villages|כְּפִרֶ֙יהָ֙\rb*\f + \fr 38:13 \ft Or \fqa young lions\f* \rb will ask|יֹאמְר֣וּ\rb*\rb |לְךָ֔\rb*, ‘\rb Have you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb come|בָ֔א\rb* \rb to capture|הֲלִשְׁלֹ֤ל\rb* \rb the plunder|שָׁלָל֙\rb*? \rb Have you assembled|הִקְהַ֣לְתָּ\rb* \rb your hordes|קְהָלֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb to carry away|הֲלָבֹ֥ז\rb* \rb loot|בַּ֖ז\rb*, \rb to make off|לָשֵׂ֣את׀\rb* \rb with silver|כֶּ֣סֶף\rb* \rb and gold|וְזָהָ֗ב\rb*, \rb to take|לָקַ֙חַת֙\rb* \rb cattle|מִקְנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb and goods|וְקִנְיָ֔ן\rb*, \rb to seize|לִשְׁלֹ֖ל\rb* \rb great|גָּדֽוֹל׃ס\rb* \rb spoil|שָׁלָ֥ל\rb*?’
\p \v 14 \rb Therefore|לָכֵן֙\rb* \rb prophesy|הִנָּבֵ֣א\rb*, \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֔ם\rb*, \rb and tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֣\rb* \rb Gog|לְג֔וֹג\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*: \rb On that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb when My people|עַמִּ֧י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֛ל\rb* \rb are dwelling|בְּשֶׁ֨בֶת\rb* \rb securely|לָבֶ֖טַח\rb*, \rb will you not|הֲל֣וֹא׀\rb* \rb take notice of this|תֵּדָֽע׃\rb*?\f + \fr 38:14 \ft LXX \fqa will you not rouse yourself?\f* \v 15 \rb And you will come|וּבָ֤אתָ\rb* \rb from your place|מִמְּקֽוֹמְךָ֙\rb* \rb out of the far|מִיַּרְכְּתֵ֣י\rb* \rb north|צָפ֔וֹן\rb*— \rb you|אַתָּ֕ה\rb* \rb and many|רַבִּ֖ים\rb* \rb peoples|וְעַמִּ֥ים\rb* \rb with you|אִתָּ֑ךְ\rb*, \rb all|כֻּלָּ֔ם\rb* \rb riding|רֹכְבֵ֤י\rb* \rb horses|סוּסִים֙\rb*— \rb a mighty|גָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb horde|קָהָ֥ל\rb*, \rb a huge|רָֽב׃\rb* \rb army|וְחַ֥יִל\rb*. \v 16 \rb You will advance|וְעָלִ֙יתָ֙\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb like a cloud|כֶּֽעָנָ֖ן\rb* \rb covering|לְכַסּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*. \rb It will happen|תִּֽהְיֶ֗ה\rb* \rb in the latter|בְּאַחֲרִ֨ית\rb* \rb days|הַיָּמִ֜ים\rb*, \rb O Gog|גּֽוֹג׃ס\rb*, \rb that I will bring you|וַהֲבִאוֹתִ֙יךָ֙\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb My land|אַרְצִ֔י\rb*, \rb so that|לְמַעַן֩\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֜ם\rb* \rb may know|דַּ֨עַת\rb* \rb Me|אֹתִ֗י\rb* \rb when I show Myself holy|בְּהִקָּדְשִׁ֥י\rb* \rb in you|בְךָ֛\rb* \rb before their eyes|לְעֵינֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֞ר\rb*: \rb Are you|הַֽאַתָּה־\rb* \rb the one|ה֨וּא\rb* \rb of whom|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I have spoken|דִּבַּ֜רְתִּי\rb* \rb in former|קַדְמוֹנִ֗ים\rb* \rb days|בְּיָמִ֣ים\rb* \rb through|בְּיַד֙\rb* \rb My servants|עֲבָדַי֙\rb*, \rb the prophets|נְבִיאֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb who in those|הָהֵ֖ם\rb* \rb times|בַּיָּמִ֥ים\rb* \rb prophesied|הַֽנִּבְּאִ֛ים\rb* \rb for years|שָׁנִ֑ים\rb* \rb that I would bring|לְהָבִ֥יא\rb* \rb you|אֹתְךָ֖\rb* \rb against them|עֲלֵיהֶֽם׃ס\rb*? \v 18 \rb Now|וְהָיָ֣ה׀\rb* \rb on that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb*\rb |בְּי֨וֹם\rb* \rb when Gog|גוֹג֙\rb* \rb comes|בּ֥וֹא\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the land|אַדְמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb*, \rb My wrath|חֲמָתִ֖י\rb*\rb |בְּאַפִּֽי׃\rb* \rb will flare up|תַּעֲלֶ֥ה\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb In My zeal|וּבְקִנְאָתִ֥י\rb* \rb and fiery|בְאֵשׁ־\rb* \rb rage|עֶבְרָתִ֖י\rb* \rb I proclaim|דִּבַּ֑רְתִּי\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א׀\rb* \rb that on that|הַה֗וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb there will be|יִֽהְיֶה֙\rb* \rb a great|גָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb earthquake|רַ֣עַשׁ\rb* \rb in|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the land|אַדְמַ֥ת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 20 \rb The fish|דְּגֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the sea|הַיָּם֩\rb*, \rb the birds|וְע֨וֹף\rb* \rb of the air|הַשָּׁמַ֜יִם\rb*, \rb the beasts|וְחַיַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֗ה\rb*, \rb every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb creature|הָרֶ֙מֶשׂ֙\rb* \rb that crawls|הָרֹמֵ֣שׂ\rb* \rb upon|עַל־\rb* \rb the ground|הָֽאֲדָמָ֔ה\rb*, \rb and all|וְכֹל֙\rb* \rb mankind|הָֽאָדָ֔ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the face|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאֲדָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb will tremble|וְרָעֲשׁ֣וּ\rb* \rb at My presence|מִפָּנַ֡י\rb*. \rb The mountains|הֶהָרִ֗ים\rb* \rb will be thrown down|וְנֶהֶרְס֣וּ\rb*, \rb the cliffs|הַמַּדְרֵג֔וֹת\rb* \rb will collapse|וְנָֽפְלוּ֙\rb*, \rb and every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb wall|חוֹמָ֖ה\rb* \rb will fall|תִּפּֽוֹל׃\rb* \rb to the ground|לָאָ֥רֶץ\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb And I will summon|וְקָרָ֨אתִי\rb* \rb a sword|חֶ֔רֶב\rb* \rb against Gog|עָלָ֤יו\rb* \rb on all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb My mountains|הָרַי֙\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb*, \rb and every man’s|אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb sword|חֶ֥רֶב\rb* \rb will be|תִּֽהְיֶֽה׃\rb* \rb against his brother|בְּאָחִ֥יו\rb*. \v 22 \rb I will execute judgment|וְנִשְׁפַּטְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb upon him|אִתּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb with plague|בְּדֶ֣בֶר\rb* \rb and bloodshed|וּבְדָ֑ם\rb*. \rb I will pour out|אַמְטִ֤יר\rb* \rb torrents|שׁוֹטֵף֩\rb* \rb of rain|וְגֶ֣שֶׁם\rb*, \rb hailstones|וְאַבְנֵ֨י\rb*\rb |אֶלְגָּבִ֜ישׁ\rb*, \rb fire|אֵ֣שׁ\rb*, \rb and sulfur|וְגָפְרִ֗ית\rb* \rb on him|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb and on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb his troops|אֲגַפָּ֔יו\rb* \rb and on|וְעַל־\rb* \rb the many|רַבִּ֖ים\rb* \rb nations|עַמִּ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb with him|אִתּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb I will magnify|וְהִתְגַּדִּלְתִּי֙\rb* \rb and sanctify Myself|וְהִתְקַדִּשְׁתִּ֔י\rb*, \rb and I will reveal Myself|וְנ֣וֹדַעְתִּ֔י\rb* \rb in the sight|לְעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of many|רַבִּ֑ים\rb* \rb nations|גּוֹיִ֣ם\rb*. \rb Then they will know|וְיָדְע֖וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃ס\rb*.[’’]
\c 39
\s1 The Slaughter of Gog’s Armies
\p \v 1 “\rb As for you|וְאַתָּ֤ה\rb*, \rb O son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָם֙\rb*, \rb prophesy|הִנָּבֵ֣א\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb Gog|גּ֔וֹג\rb* \rb and declare|וְאָ֣מַרְתָּ֔\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*: \rb Behold|הִנְנִ֤י\rb*, \rb I am against you|אֵלֶ֙יךָ֙\rb*, \rb O Gog|גּ֔וֹג\rb*, \rb chief|רֹ֖אשׁ\rb* \rb prince|נְשִׂ֕יא\rb* \rb of Meshech|מֶ֥שֶׁךְ\rb* \rb and Tubal|וְתֻבָֽל׃\rb*.\f + \fr 39:1 \ft Or \fqa Gog, prince of Rosh, Meshech, and Tubal\f* \v 2 \rb I will turn you around|וְשֹׁבַבְתִּ֙יךָ֙\rb*, \rb drive you along|וְשִׁשֵּׁאתִ֔יךָ\rb*, \rb bring you up|וְהַעֲלִיתִ֖יךָ\rb* \rb from the far|מִיַּרְכְּתֵ֣י\rb* \rb north|צָפ֑וֹן\rb*, \rb and send you|וַהֲבִאוֹתִ֖ךָ\rb* \rb against|עַל־\rb* \rb the mountains|הָרֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb Then I will strike|וְהִכֵּיתִ֥י\rb* \rb the bow|קַשְׁתְּךָ֖\rb* \rb from your left|שְׂמֹאולֶ֑ךָ\rb* \rb hand|מִיַּ֣ד\rb* \rb and dash down|אַפִּֽיל׃\rb* \rb the arrows|וְחִצֶּ֕יךָ\rb* \rb from your right|יְמִינְךָ֖\rb* \rb hand|מִיַּ֥ד\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb On|עַל־\rb* \rb the mountains|הָרֵ֨י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֜ל\rb* \rb you will fall|תִּפּ֗וֹל\rb* — \rb you|אַתָּה֙\rb* \rb and all|וְכָל־\rb* \rb your troops|אֲגַפֶּ֔יךָ\rb* \rb and the nations|וְעַמִּ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb with you|אִתָּ֑ךְ\rb*. \rb I will give you|נְתַתִּ֥יךָ\rb* \rb as food|לְאָכְלָֽה׃\rb* \rb to every|כָּל־\rb* \rb kind|כָּנָ֛ף\rb* \rb of ravenous|לְעֵ֨יט\rb* \rb bird|צִפּ֧וֹר\rb* \rb and wild|הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb* \rb beast|וְחַיַּ֥ת\rb*. \v 5 \rb You will fall|תִּפּ֑וֹל\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb the open field|פְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |הַשָּׂדֶ֖ה\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֚י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb have spoken|דִבַּ֔רְתִּי\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb I will send|וְשִׁלַּחְתִּי־\rb* \rb fire|אֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb on Magog|בְּמָג֔וֹג\rb* \rb and on those who dwell|וּבְיֹשְׁבֵ֥י\rb* \rb securely|לָבֶ֑טַח\rb* \rb in the coastlands|הָאִיִּ֖ים\rb*, \rb and they will know|וְיָדְע֖וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb So|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb I will make My holy|קָדְשִׁ֜י\rb* \rb name|שֵׁ֨ם\rb* \rb known|אוֹדִ֗יעַ\rb* \rb among|בְּתוֹךְ֙\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֣י\rb* \rb Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb and will no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֑וֹד\rb* \rb allow it|שֵׁם־\rb*\rb |קָדְשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb to be profaned|אַחֵ֥ל\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Then the nations|הַגּוֹיִם֙\rb* \rb will know|וְיָדְע֤וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּי־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֣י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb*, \rb the Holy|קָד֖וֹשׁ\rb* \rb One in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb Yes|הִנֵּ֤ה\rb*, \rb it is coming|בָאָה֙\rb*, \rb and it will surely happen|וְנִֽהְיָ֔תָה\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb*. \rb This|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb is the day|הַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb of which|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I have spoken|דִּבַּֽרְתִּי׃\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb Then those who dwell|יֹשְׁבֵ֣י׀\rb* \rb in the cities|עָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb will go out|וְֽיָצְא֞וּ\rb*, \rb kindle fires|וּבִעֲר֡וּ\rb*, \rb and burn up|וְ֠הִשִּׂיקוּ\rb* \rb the weapons|בְּנֶ֨שֶׁק\rb*— \rb the bucklers|וּמָגֵ֤ן\rb* \rb and shields|וְצִנָּה֙\rb*, \rb the bows|בְּקֶ֣שֶׁת\rb* \rb and arrows|וּבְחִצִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb the clubs|וּבְמַקֵּ֥ל\rb*\rb |יָ֖ד\rb* \rb and spears|וּבְרֹ֑מַח\rb*. \rb For seven|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb years|שָׁנִֽים׃\rb*\rb |וּבִעֲר֥וּ\rb*\rb |בָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb they will use them for fuel|אֵ֖שׁ\rb*. \v 10 \rb They will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb gather|יִשְׂא֨וּ\rb* \rb wood|עֵצִ֜ים\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the countryside|הַשָּׂדֶ֗ה\rb*\rb |וְלֹ֤א\rb* \rb or cut it|יַחְטְבוּ֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the forests|הַיְּעָרִ֔ים\rb*, \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb they will use the weapons|בַנֶּ֖שֶׁק\rb* \rb for fuel|יְבַֽעֲרוּ־\rb*\rb |אֵ֑שׁ\rb*. \rb They will loot|וְשָׁלְל֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb those who looted them|שֹׁלְלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and plunder|וּבָֽזְזוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb those who plundered them|בֹּ֣זְזֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 11 \rb And|וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb on that|הַה֡וּא\rb* \rb day|בַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb I will give|אֶתֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb Gog|לְגוֹג֩׀\rb* \rb a burial|קֶ֜בֶר\rb* \rb place|מְקֽוֹם־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֨ם\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb*, \rb the Valley|גֵּ֤י\rb* \rb of the Travelers|הָעֹֽבְרִים֙\rb*, \rb east|קִדְמַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the Sea|הַיָּ֔ם\rb*.\f + \fr 39:11 \ft That is, the Dead Sea\f* \rb It|הִ֖יא\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will block|וְחֹסֶ֥מֶת\rb* \rb those who travel through|הָעֹֽבְרִ֑ים\rb*, \rb because Gog|גּוֹג֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and all|כָּל־\rb* \rb his hordes|הֲמוֹנֹ֔ה\rb* \rb will be buried|וְקָ֣בְרוּ\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֗ם\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb So it will be called|וְקָ֣רְא֔וּ\rb*\rb |גֵּ֖יא\rb*\rb |הֲמ֥וֹן\rb* \rb the Valley of Hamon-gog|גּֽוֹג׃\rb*.\f + \fr 39:11 \fqa Hamon-gog \ft means \fqa multitude of Gog\ft .\f* \v 12 \rb For seven|שִׁבְעָ֖ה\rb* \rb months|חֳדָשִֽׁים׃\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb will be burying them|וּקְבָרוּם֙\rb* \rb in order|לְמַ֖עַן\rb* \rb to cleanse|טַהֵ֣ר\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*. \v 13 \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb will bury them|וְקָֽבְרוּ֙\rb*, \rb and it will bring them|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb*\rb |לָהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb renown|לְשֵׁ֑ם\rb* \rb on the day|י֚וֹם\rb* \rb I display My glory|הִכָּ֣בְדִ֔י\rb*,\f + \fr 39:13 \ft Or \fqa and the day I display My glory will be a day of renown\f* \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb And men|וְאַנְשֵׁ֨י\rb* \rb will be employed|יַבְדִּ֙ילוּ֙\rb* \rb to continually|תָמִ֤יד\rb* \rb pass|עֹבְרִ֣ים\rb* \rb through the land|בָּאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb to cleanse it|לְטַֽהֲרָ֑הּ\rb* \rb by burying|מְקַבְּרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the invaders|הָעֹבְרִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb who remain|הַנּוֹתָרִ֛ים\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the ground|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*. \rb At the end|מִקְצֵ֥ה\rb* \rb of the seven|שִׁבְעָֽה־\rb* \rb months|חֳדָשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb they will begin their search|יַחְקֹֽרוּ׃\rb*. \v 15 \rb As they pass|וְעָבְר֤וּ\rb*\rb |הָעֹֽבְרִים֙\rb* \rb through the land|בָּאָ֔רֶץ\rb*, \rb anyone who sees|וְרָאָה֙\rb* \rb a human|אָדָ֔ם\rb* \rb bone|עֶ֣צֶם\rb* \rb will set up|וּבָנָ֥ה\rb* \rb a pillar|צִיּ֑וּן\rb* \rb next to it|אֶצְל֖וֹ\rb*, \rb until|עַ֣ד\rb* \rb the gravediggers|קָבְר֤וּ\rb*\rb |אֹתוֹ֙\rb* \rb have buried|הַֽמְקַבְּרִ֔ים\rb* \rb it in|אֶל־\rb*\rb |גֵּ֖יא\rb*\rb |הֲמ֥וֹן\rb* \rb the Valley of Hamon-gog|גּֽוֹג׃\rb*. \v 16 (\rb Even the city|עִ֛יר\rb* \rb will be|וְגַ֥ם\rb* \rb named|שֶׁם־\rb* \rb Hamonah|הֲמוֹנָ֖ה\rb*.\f + \fr 39:16 \fqa Hamonah \ft means \fqa multitude \ft or \fqa horde\ft .\f*) \rb And so they will cleanse|וְטִהֲר֥וּ\rb* \rb the land|הָאָֽרֶץ׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb And as for you|וְאַתָּ֨ה\rb*, \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֜ם\rb*, \rb this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהֹוִ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֣ר׀\rb*: \rb Call out to|אֱמֹר֩\rb* \rb every kind|כָּל־\rb*\rb |כָּנָ֜ף\rb* \rb of bird|לְצִפּ֨וֹר\rb* \rb and to every|וּלְכֹ֣ל׀\rb* \rb beast|חַיַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the field|הַשָּׂדֶ֗ה\rb*: ‘\rb Assemble|הִקָּבְצ֤וּ\rb* \rb and come|וָבֹ֙אוּ֙\rb* \rb together|הֵאָסְפ֣וּ\rb* \rb from all around|מִסָּבִ֔יב\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the sacrificial feast|זִבְחִ֗י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֜י\rb* \rb am preparing|זֹבֵ֤חַ\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶם֙\rb*,\rb |זֶ֣בַח\rb* \rb a great|גָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb feast on|עַ֖ל\rb* \rb the mountains|הָרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb There you will eat|וַאֲכַלְתֶּ֥ם\rb* \rb flesh|בָּשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb and drink|וּשְׁתִ֥יתֶם\rb* \rb blood|דָּֽם׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb You will eat|תֹּאכֵ֔לוּ\rb* \rb the flesh|בְּשַׂ֤ר\rb* \rb of the mighty|גִּבּוֹרִים֙\rb* \rb and drink|תִּשְׁתּ֑וּ\rb* \rb the blood|וְדַם־\rb* \rb of the princes|נְשִׂיאֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the earth|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb as though they were rams|אֵילִ֨ים\rb*, \rb lambs|כָּרִ֤ים\rb*, \rb goats|וְעַתּוּדִים֙\rb*, \rb and bulls|פָּרִ֔ים\rb* — \rb all|כֻּלָּֽם׃\rb* \rb the fattened animals|מְרִיאֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Bashan|בָשָׁ֖ן\rb*. \v 19 \rb At the sacrifice|מִזִּבְחִ֖י\rb* \rb I am preparing|זָבַ֥חְתִּי\rb*\rb |לָכֶֽם׃\rb*, \rb you will eat|וַאֲכַלְתֶּם־\rb* \rb fat|חֵ֣לֶב\rb* \rb until you are gorged|לְשָׂבְעָ֔ה\rb* \rb and drink|וּשְׁתִ֥יתֶם\rb* \rb blood|דָּ֖ם\rb* \rb until you are drunk|לְשִׁכָּר֑וֹן\rb*. \v 20 \rb And at|עַל־\rb* \rb My table|שֻׁלְחָנִי֙\rb* \rb you will eat your fill|וּשְׂבַעְתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb of horses|ס֣וּס\rb* \rb and riders|וָרֶ֔כֶב\rb*, \rb of mighty men|גִּבּ֖וֹר\rb* \rb and warriors|אִ֣ישׁ\rb*\rb |מִלְחָמָ֑ה\rb* \rb of every kind|וְכָל־\rb*,’ \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*.
\s1 Israel to Be Restored
\p \v 21 \rb I will display|וְנָתַתִּ֥י\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My glory|כְּבוֹדִ֖י\rb* \rb among the nations|בַּגּוֹיִ֑ם\rb*, \rb and all|כָל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֗ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will see|וְרָא֣וּ\rb* \rb the judgment|מִשְׁפָּטִי֙\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb I execute|עָשִׂ֔יתִי\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the hand|יָדִ֖י\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I lay|שַׂ֥מְתִּי\rb* \rb upon them|בָהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb From|מִן־\rb* \rb that|הַה֖וּא\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֥וֹם\rb* \rb forward|וָהָֽלְאָה׃\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb will know|וְיָֽדְעוּ֙\rb* \rb that|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֥י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb their God|אֱלֹֽהֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \v 23 \rb And the nations|הַ֠גּוֹיִם\rb* \rb will know|וְיָדְע֣וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the house|בֵֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֗ל\rb* \rb went into exile|גָּל֣וּ\rb* \rb for their iniquity|בַעֲוֺנָ֞ם\rb*, \rb because|עַ֚ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they were unfaithful|מָֽעֲלוּ־\rb* \rb to Me|בִ֔י\rb*. \rb So I hid|וָאַסְתִּ֥ר\rb* \rb My face|פָּנַ֖י\rb* \rb from them|מֵהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb and delivered them|וָֽאֶתְּנֵם֙\rb* \rb into the hands|בְּיַ֣ד\rb* \rb of their enemies|צָרֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb so that they all|כֻּלָּֽם׃\rb* \rb fell|וַיִּפְּל֥וּ\rb* \rb by the sword|בַחֶ֖רֶב\rb*. \v 24 \rb I dealt|עָשִׂ֣יתִי\rb* \rb with them|אֹתָ֑ם\rb* \rb according to their uncleanness|כְּטֻמְאָתָ֥ם\rb* \rb and transgressions|וּכְפִשְׁעֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb and I hid|וָאַסְתִּ֥ר\rb* \rb My face|פָּנַ֖י\rb* \rb from them|מֵהֶֽם׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb Therefore|לָכֵ֗ן\rb* \rb this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: \rb Now|עַתָּ֗ה\rb* \rb I will restore|אָשִׁיב֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Jacob|יַֽעֲקֹ֔ב\rb* \rb from captivity|שְׁבִית\rb*\f + \fr 39:25 \ft Or \fqa restore the fortunes of Jacob\f* \rb and will have compassion|וְרִֽחַמְתִּ֖י\rb* \rb on the whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and I will be jealous|וְקִנֵּאתִ֖י\rb* \rb for My holy|קָדְשִֽׁי׃\rb* \rb name|לְשֵׁ֥ם\rb*. \v 26 \rb They will forget|וְנָשׂוּ֙\rb*\f + \fr 39:26 \ft A few Hebrew manuscripts; MT \fqa They will bear\f* \rb their disgrace|כְּלִמָּתָ֔ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the treachery|מָעֲלוּ־\rb* \rb they committed|מַעֲלָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb against Me|בִ֑י\rb*, \rb when they dwell|בְּשִׁבְתָּ֧ם\rb* \rb securely|לָבֶ֖טַח\rb* \rb in|עַל־\rb* \rb their land|אַדְמָתָ֛ם\rb*, \rb with no|וְאֵ֥ין\rb* \rb one to frighten them|מַחֲרִֽיד׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb When I bring them back|בְּשׁוֹבְבִ֤י\rb*\rb |אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the peoples|הָ֣עַמִּ֔ים\rb* \rb and gather|וְקִבַּצְתִּ֣י\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb out of the lands|מֵֽאַרְצ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of their enemies|אֹֽיְבֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb I will show My holiness|וְנִקְדַּ֣שְׁתִּי\rb* \rb in them|בָ֔ם\rb* \rb in the sight|לְעֵינֵ֖י\rb* \rb of many|רַבִּֽים׃\rb* \rb nations|הַגּוֹיִ֥ם\rb*. \v 28 \rb Then they will know|וְיָדְע֗וּ\rb* \rb that|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb I|אֲנִ֤י\rb* \rb am the LORD|יְהוָה֙\rb* \rb their God|אֱלֹ֣הֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb when I regather them|וְכִנַּסְתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb their own land|אַדְמָתָ֑ם\rb*, \rb not leaving|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb any|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb of them|מֵהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |שָֽׁם׃\rb* \rb behind|אוֹתִ֥יר\rb* \rb after their exile|בְּהַגְלוֹתִ֤י\rb*\rb |אֹתָם֙\rb* \rb among|אֶל־\rb* \rb the nations|הַגּוֹיִ֔ם\rb*. \v 29 \rb And I will no|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֛וֹד\rb* \rb hide|אַסְתִּ֥יר\rb* \rb My face|פָּנַ֖י\rb* \rb from them|מֵהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb for|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb I will pour out|שָׁפַ֤כְתִּי\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My Spirit|רוּחִי֙\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃פ\rb*.”
\c 40
\s1 The Man with a Measuring Rod
\r (\ref Zechariah 2:1–5|ZEC 2:1-5\ref*)
\p \v 1 \rb In the twenty-fifth|בְּעֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |וְחָמֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֣ה\rb* \rb of our exile|לְ֠גָלוּתֵנוּ\rb*, \rb at the beginning|בְּרֹ֨אשׁ\rb* \rb of the year|הַשָּׁנָ֜ה\rb*, \rb on the tenth|בֶּעָשׂ֣וֹר\rb* \rb day of the month|לַחֹ֗דֶשׁ\rb* — \rb in the fourteenth|בְּאַרְבַּ֤ע\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵה֙\rb* \rb year|שָׁנָ֔ה\rb* \rb after|אַחַ֕ר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb Jerusalem|הָעִ֑יר\rb* \rb had been struck down|הֻכְּתָ֖ה\rb* — \rb on that|הַזֶּ֗ה\rb* \rb very|בְּעֶ֣צֶם׀\rb* \rb day|הַיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the hand|יַד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֔ה\rb* \rb was|הָיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb upon me|עָלַי֙\rb*, \rb and He took|וַיָּבֵ֥א\rb* \rb me|אֹתִ֖י\rb* \rb there|שָֽׁמָּה׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb In visions|בְּמַרְא֣וֹת\rb* \rb of God|אֱלֹהִ֔ים\rb* \rb He took me|הֱבִיאַ֖נִי\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the land|אֶ֣רֶץ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb* \rb and set me|וַיְנִיחֵ֗נִי\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb a very|מְאֹ֔ד\rb*\rb |וְעָלָ֥יו\rb* \rb high|גָּבֹ֙הַּ֙\rb* \rb mountain|הַ֤ר\rb*, \rb on whose southern slope|מִנֶּֽגֶב׃\rb* \rb was a structure|כְּמִבְנֵה־\rb* \rb that resembled a city|עִ֖יר\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb So He took|וַיָּבֵ֨יא\rb* \rb me|אוֹתִ֜י\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֗מָּה\rb*, \rb and I saw|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb a man|אִישׁ֙\rb* \rb whose appearance|מַרְאֵ֙הוּ֙\rb*\rb |כְּמַרְאֵ֣ה\rb* \rb was like bronze|נְחֹ֔שֶׁת\rb*. \rb He|וְה֥וּא\rb* \rb was standing|עֹמֵ֖ד\rb* \rb in the gateway|בַּשָּֽׁעַר׃\rb* \rb with a linen|פִּשְׁתִּ֥ים\rb* \rb cord|וּפְתִיל־\rb* \rb and a measuring|הַמִּדָּ֑ה\rb* \rb rod|וּקְנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb in his hand|בְּיָד֖וֹ\rb*. \v 4 “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֡ם\rb*,” \rb he said|וַיְדַבֵּ֨ר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֜י\rb*\rb |הָאִ֗ישׁ\rb*, “\rb look|רְאֵ֣ה\rb* \rb with your eyes|בְעֵינֶיךָ֩\rb*, \rb hear|שְּׁמָ֜ע\rb* \rb with your ears|וּבְאָזְנֶ֨יךָ\rb*, \rb and pay attention|וְשִׂ֣ים\rb*\rb |לִבְּךָ֗\rb* \rb to everything|לְכֹ֤ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb am going to show you|מַרְאֶ֣ה\rb*,\rb |אוֹתָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb for|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb that|לְמַ֥עַן\rb* \rb is why|הַרְאוֹתְכָ֖ה\rb* \rb you have been brought|הֻבָ֣אתָה\rb* \rb here|הֵ֑נָּה\rb*. \rb Report|הַגֵּ֛ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the house|לְבֵ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb* \rb everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you|אַתָּ֥ה\rb* \rb see|רֹאֶ֖ה\rb*.”
\s1 The East Gate
\p \v 5 \rb And I saw|וְהִנֵּ֥ה\rb* \rb a wall|חוֹמָ֛ה\rb* \rb surrounding|סָבִ֣יב׀\rb*\rb |סָבִ֑יב\rb*\rb |מִח֥וּץ\rb* \rb the temple area|לַבַּ֖יִת\rb*. \rb Now the length of the measuring|הַמִּדָּ֗ה\rb* \rb rod|קְנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb in the man’s|הָאִ֜ישׁ\rb* \rb hand|וּבְיַ֨ד\rb* \rb was six long|שֵׁשׁ־\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֤וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 40:5 \fqa 6 long cubits\ft , the length of the reed used for measuring, is approximately 10.5 feet or 3.2 meters; similarly in verses 6, 7, and 12. The long cubit of about 21 inches or 53.3 centimeters is the basic unit of length throughout Ezekiel 40 to 48.\f* (\rb each measuring a cubit|בָּֽאַמָּה֙\rb* \rb and a handbreadth|וָטֹ֔פַח\rb*), \rb and he measured|וַיָּ֜מָד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the wall to be|הַבִּנְיָן֙\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb rod|קָנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb thick|רֹ֤חַב\rb* \rb and one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb rod|קָנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb high|וְקוֹמָ֖ה\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb Then he came|וַיָּב֗וֹא\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the gate|שַׁ֙עַר֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb facing|פָּנָיו֙\rb*\rb |דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb east|הַקָּדִ֔ימָה\rb* \rb and climbed|וַיַּ֖עַל\rb* \rb its steps|בְּמַעֲלוֹתוֹ\rb*. \rb He measured|וַיָּ֣מָד׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the threshold|סַ֣ף\rb* \rb of the gate to be|הַשַּׁ֗עַר\rb* \rb one|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb rod|קָנֶ֤ה\rb* \rb deep|רֹ֔חַב\rb*\rb |וְאֵת֙\rb*\rb |אֶחָ֔ד\rb*\rb |סַ֣ף\rb*\rb |קָנֶ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֶחָ֖ד\rb*\rb |רֹֽחַב׃\rb*.\f + \fr 40:6 \ft Hebrew \fqa one reed deep, even one threshold, one reed deep.\f* \v 7 \rb Each gate chamber|וְהַתָּ֗א\rb* \rb was one|אֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb rod|קָנֶ֨ה\rb* \rb long|אֹ֙רֶךְ֙\rb* \rb and one rod|וְקָנֶ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb wide|רֹ֔חַב\rb*, \rb and there were five|חָמֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֑וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 40:7 \fqa 5 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 8.75 feet or 2.7 meters; also in verses 30 and 48.\f* \rb between|וּבֵ֥ין\rb* \rb the gate chambers|הַתָּאִ֖ים\rb*. \rb The inner threshold|וְסַ֣ף\rb* \rb of the gate|הַ֠שַּׁעַר\rb* \rb by|מֵאֵ֨צֶל\rb* \rb the portico|אוּלָ֥ם\rb*\rb |הַשַּׁ֛עַר\rb* \rb facing inward|מֵֽהַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb was one|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb rod deep|קָנֶ֥ה\rb*. \v 8 \rb Then he measured|וַיָּ֜מָד\rb* \rb the portico|אֻלָ֥ם\rb* \rb of the gateway|הַשַּׁ֛עַר\rb* \rb inside|מֵהַבַּ֖יִת\rb*;\f + \fr 40:8 \ft Literally \fqa the portico of the gateway inside, one rod\f* \v 9 \rb it was|וַיָּ֜מָד\rb*\rb |אֻלָ֤ם\rb*\rb |הַשַּׁ֙עַר֙\rb* \rb eight|שְׁמֹנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb cubits deep|אַמּ֔וֹת\rb*,\f + \fr 40:9 \fqa 8 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 14 feet or 4.3 meters.\f* \rb and its jambs were|וְאֵילוֹ\rb* \rb two|שְׁתַּ֣יִם\rb* \rb cubits thick|אַמּ֑וֹת\rb*.\f + \fr 40:9 \fqa 2 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 3.5 feet or 1.1 meters.\f* \rb And the portico|וְאֻלָ֥ם\rb* \rb of the gateway|הַשַּׁ֖עַר\rb* \rb faced the temple|מֵהַבָּֽיִת׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb There were three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֤ה\rb* \rb gate chambers|וְתָאֵ֨י\rb* \rb on each side|מִפֹּה֙\rb*\rb |וּשְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |מִפֹּ֔ה\rb* \rb of the east|הַקָּדִ֗ים\rb* \rb gate|הַשַּׁ֜עַר\rb*,\rb |דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb each with the same|אַחַ֖ת\rb*\rb |לִשְׁלָשְׁתָּ֑ם\rb* \rb measurements|מִדָּ֥ה\rb*, \rb and the gateposts|לָאֵילִ֖ם\rb* \rb on either side|מִפֹּ֥ה\rb*\rb |וּמִפּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb also had the same|אַחַ֛ת\rb* \rb measurements|וּמִדָּ֥ה\rb*. \v 11 \rb And he measured|וַיָּ֛מָד\rb* \rb the width|רֹ֥חַב\rb* \rb of the gateway|הַשַּׁ֖עַר\rb* \rb entrance|פֶּֽתַח־\rb* \rb to be ten|עֶ֣שֶׂר\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֑וֹת\rb*,\f + \fr 40:11 \fqa 10 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 17.5 feet or 5.3 meters.\f* \rb and its length|אֹ֣רֶךְ\rb*\rb |הַשַּׁ֔עַר\rb* \rb was thirteen|שְׁל֥וֹשׁ\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּֽוֹת׃\rb*.\f + \fr 40:11 \fqa 13 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 22.75 feet or 6.9 meters.\f*
\p \v 12 \rb In front|לִפְנֵ֤י\rb* \rb of each gate chamber|הַתָּאוֹת֙\rb* \rb was a wall|וּגְב֞וּל\rb* \rb one|אֶחָ֔ת\rb* \rb cubit high|אַמָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb and the gate chambers|וְהַתָּ֕א\rb* \rb were six|שֵׁשׁ־\rb*\rb |אַמּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb cubits|וְאַמָּה־\rb*\rb |אַחַ֥ת\rb*\rb |גְּב֖וּל\rb* \rb square|מִפּֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 13 \rb Then he measured|וַיָּ֣מָד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the gateway|הַשַּׁ֗עַר\rb* \rb from the roof|מִגַּ֤ג\rb* \rb of one gate chamber|הַתָּא֙\rb* \rb to the roof|לְגַגּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb of the opposite one|רֹ֕חַב\rb*; \rb the distance was twenty-five|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְחָמֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֑וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 40:13 \fqa 25 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 43.75 feet or 13.3 meters; also in verses 21, 25, 29, 30, 33, and 36.\f* \rb from doorway|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to|נֶ֥גֶד\rb* \rb doorway|פָּֽתַח׃\rb*.
\p \v 14 \rb Next he measured|וַיַּ֥עַשׂ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the gateposts|אֵילִ֖ים\rb* \rb to be sixty|שִׁשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb cubits high|אַמָּ֑ה\rb*.\f + \fr 40:14 \fqa 60 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 105 feet or 32 meters.\f* \rb The gateway extended|הַשַּׁ֖עַר\rb*\rb |סָבִ֥יב׀\rb* \rb around|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb to|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the gatepost|אֵיל֙\rb* \rb of the courtyard|הֶֽחָצֵ֔ר\rb*. \v 15 \rb And the distance from|וְעַ֗ל\rb*\rb |פְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb the entrance|הַיֹּאתוֹן\rb* \rb of the gateway|הַשַּׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the far end of|לִפְנֵ֕י\rb* \rb its|הַשַּׁ֖עַר\rb* \rb inner|הַפְּנִימִ֑י\rb* \rb portico|אֻלָ֥ם\rb* \rb was fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֖ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּֽה׃\rb*.\f + \fr 40:15 \fqa 50 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 87.5 feet or 26.7 meters; also in verses 21, 25, 29, 33, and 36.\f*
\p \v 16 \rb The gate chambers|הַתָּאִ֡ים\rb*\rb |וְאֶל֩\rb* \rb and their side pillars|אֵלֵיהֵ֨מָה\rb*\f + \fr 40:16 \ft Or \fqa gateposts \ft or \fqa jambs \ft or \fqa projecting walls\ft ; here and throughout Ezekiel 40 and 41.\f* \rb had|אֶֽל־\rb* \rb beveled|אֲטֻמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb windows|וְחַלֹּנ֣וֹת\rb* \rb all around|סָבִ֣יב׀\rb*\rb |סָבִ֔יב\rb*\rb |וְכֵ֖ן\rb* \rb the inside|לִפְנִ֤ימָה\rb* \rb of the gateway|לַשַּׁ֙עַר֙\rb*. \rb The porticos|לָאֵֽלַמּ֑וֹת\rb* \rb also had windows|וְחַלּוֹנ֞וֹת\rb* \rb all around|סָבִ֤יב׀\rb*\rb |סָבִיב֙\rb* \rb on the inside|לִפְנִ֔ימָה\rb*.\rb |וְאֶל־\rb* \rb Each side pillar|אַ֖יִל\rb* \rb was decorated with palm trees|תִּמֹרִֽים׃\rb*.
\s1 The Outer Court
\p \v 17 \rb Then he brought me|וַיְבִיאֵ֗נִי\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the outer|הַחִ֣יצוֹנָ֔ה\rb* \rb court|הֶֽחָצֵר֙\rb*, \rb and there|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb were chambers|לְשָׁכוֹת֙\rb* \rb and a pavement|וְרִֽצְפָ֔ה\rb* \rb laid out|עָשׂ֥וּי\rb* \rb all around|סָבִ֣יב׀\rb*\rb |סָבִ֑יב\rb* \rb the court|לֶחָצֵ֖ר\rb*. \rb Thirty|שְׁלֹשִׁ֥ים\rb* \rb chambers|לְשָׁכ֖וֹת\rb* \rb faced|אֶל־\rb* \rb the pavement|הָרִֽצְפָֽה׃\rb*, \v 18 \rb which flanked|כֶּ֣תֶף\rb* \rb the gateways|הַשְּׁעָרִ֔ים\rb* \rb and corresponded to|לְעֻמַּ֖ת\rb* \rb the length|אֹ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the gates|הַשְּׁעָרִ֑ים\rb*;\rb |הָרִֽצְפָ֖ה\rb* \rb this was the lower|הַתַּחְתּוֹנָֽה׃\rb* \rb pavement|וְהָרִֽצְפָה֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb Then he measured|וַיָּ֣מָד\rb* \rb the distance|רֹ֡חַב\rb* \rb from the front|מִלִּפְנֵי֩\rb* \rb of the lower|הַתַּחְתּ֜וֹנָה\rb* \rb gateway|הַשַּׁ֨עַר\rb* \rb to the outside|מִח֖וּץ\rb*\rb |לִפְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the inner|הַפְּנִימִ֛י\rb* \rb court|הֶחָצֵ֧ר\rb*; \rb it was a hundred|מֵאָ֣ה\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֑ה\rb*\f + \fr 40:19 \fqa 100 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 175 feet or 53.3 meters; also in verses 23, 27, and 47.\f* \rb on the east side|הַקָּדִ֖ים\rb* \rb as well as on the north|וְהַצָּפֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\s1 The North Gate
\p \v 20 \rb He also measured|מָדַ֥ד\rb* \rb the length|אָרְכּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and width|וְרָחְבּֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb of the gateway|וְהַשַּׁ֗עַר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb of the outer|הַחִֽיצוֹנָ֑ה\rb* \rb court|לֶחָצֵ֖ר\rb* \rb facing|פָּנָיו֙\rb*\rb |דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb north|הַצָּפ֔וֹן\rb*. \v 21 \rb Its three|שְׁלוֹשָׁ֤ה\rb* \rb gate chambers|וְתָאוֹ\rb* \rb on each side|מִפּוֹ֙\rb*,\rb |וּשְׁלֹשָׁ֣ה\rb*\rb |מִפּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb its side pillars|וְאֵילוֹ\rb*, \rb and its portico|וְאֵלַמּוֹ\rb* \rb all had|הָיָ֔ה\rb* \rb the same measurements|כְּמִדַּ֖ת\rb* \rb as the first|הָרִאשׁ֑וֹן\rb* \rb gate|הַשַּׁ֣עַר\rb*: \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֤ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּה֙\rb* \rb long|אָרְכּ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |חָמֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb and twenty-five|וְעֶשְׂרִ֖ים\rb* \rb cubits|בָּאַמָּֽה׃\rb* \rb wide|וְרֹ֕חַב\rb*. \v 22 \rb Its windows|וְחַלּוֹנוֹ\rb*, \rb portico|וְאֵלַמּוֹ\rb*, \rb and palm trees|וְתִמֹרוֹ\rb* \rb had the same measurements|כְּמִדַּ֣ת\rb* \rb as those of the gate|הַשַּׁ֔עַר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb facing|פָּנָ֖יו\rb*\rb |דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb east|הַקָּדִ֑ים\rb*. \rb Seven|שֶׁ֙בַע֙\rb* \rb steps|וּבְמַעֲל֥וֹת\rb* \rb led up|יַֽעֲלוּ־\rb* \rb to it|ב֔וֹ\rb*, \rb with its portico|וְאֵילַמּוֹ\rb* \rb opposite them|לִפְנֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
