\s1 The South Gate
\p \v 24 \rb Then he led me|וַיּוֹלִכֵ֙נִי֙\rb* \rb to|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb the south side|הַדָּר֔וֹם\rb*, \rb and I saw|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb a gateway|שַׁ֖עַר\rb* \rb facing|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb south|הַדָּר֑וֹם\rb*. \rb He measured|וּמָדַ֤ד\rb* \rb its side pillars|אֵילוֹ\rb* \rb and portico|וְאֵילַמּוֹ\rb*, \rb and they had the same measurements|כַּמִּדּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb as the others|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb Both the gateway and its portico|וּלְאֵילַמּוֹ\rb* \rb had windows|וְחַלּוֹנִ֨ים\rb* \rb all around|סָבִ֣יב׀\rb*\rb |סָבִ֔יב\rb*, \rb like the other|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb windows|כְּהַחֲלֹּנ֖וֹת\rb*. \rb It was fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֤ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּה֙\rb* \rb long|אֹ֔רֶךְ\rb*\rb |חָמֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb and twenty-five|וְעֶשְׂרִ֖ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּֽה׃\rb* \rb wide|וְרֹ֕חַב\rb*. \v 26 \rb Seven|שִׁבְעָה֙\rb* \rb steps|וּמַעֲל֤וֹת\rb* \rb led up to it|עֹלוֹתוֹ\rb*, \rb and its portico|וְאֵלַמּוֹ\rb* \rb was opposite them|לִפְנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*; \rb it had palm trees|וְתִמֹרִ֣ים\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb its side pillars|אֵילוֹ׃\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb on each side|מִפּ֛וֹ\rb*\rb |וְאֶחָ֥ד\rb*\rb |מִפּ֖וֹ\rb*.
