\s1 The Gates of the Inner Court
\p \v 28 \rb Next he brought me|וַיְבִיאֵ֛נִי\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the inner|הַפְּנִימִ֖י\rb* \rb court|חָצֵ֥ר\rb* \rb through the south|הַדָּר֑וֹם\rb* \rb gate|בְּשַׁ֣עַר\rb*, \rb and he measured|וַיָּ֙מָד֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the south|הַדָּר֔וֹם\rb* \rb gate|הַשַּׁ֣עַר\rb*; \rb it had the same measurements|כַּמִּדּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb as the others|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb*. \v 29 \rb Its gate chambers|וְתָאוֹ\rb*, \rb side pillars|וְאֵילוֹ\rb*, \rb and portico|וְאֵלַמּוֹ\rb* \rb had the same measurements|כַּמִּדּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb as the others|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb*. \rb Both the gateway and its portico|וּלְאֵלַמּוֹ\rb* \rb had windows|וְחַלּוֹנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb all around|סָבִ֣יב׀\rb*\rb |סָבִ֑יב\rb*; \rb it was fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֤ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּה֙\rb* \rb long|אֹ֔רֶךְ\rb* \rb and twenty-five|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |וְחָמֵ֖שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb wide|וְרֹ֕חַב\rb*. \v 30 (\rb The porticoes|וְאֵֽלַמּ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |סָבִ֣יב׀\rb* \rb around the inner court|סָבִ֑יב\rb* \rb were twenty-five|וְעֶשְׂרִים֙\rb*\rb |חָמֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb long|אֹ֗רֶךְ\rb* \rb and five|חָמֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb deep|וְרֹ֖חַב\rb*.\f + \fr 40:30 \ft The porticoes were approximately 43.75 feet long and 8.75 feet deep (13.3 meters long and 2.7 meters deep).\f*) \v 31 \rb Its portico|וְאֵלַמָּ֗ו\rb* \rb faced|אֶל־\rb* \rb the outer|הַחִ֣צוֹנָ֔ה\rb* \rb court|חָצֵר֙\rb*, \rb and its side pillars|אֵילוֹ\rb* \rb were decorated with palm trees|וְתִמֹרִ֖ים\rb*.\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb Eight|שְׁמוֹנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb steps|וּמַעֲל֥וֹת\rb* \rb led up to it|מַעֲלוֹ\rb*.
\p \v 32 \rb And he brought me|וַיְבִיאֵ֛נִי\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the inner|הַפְּנִימִ֖י\rb* \rb court|הֶחָצֵ֥ר\rb* \rb on|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb the east side|הַקָּדִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and he measured|וַיָּ֣מָד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the gateway|הַשַּׁ֔עַר\rb*; \rb it had the same measurements|כַּמִּדּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb as the others|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb*. \v 33 \rb Its gate chambers|וְתָאוֹ\rb*, \rb side pillars|וְאֵלוֹ\rb*, \rb and portico|וְאֵלַמּוֹ\rb* \rb had the same measurements|כַּמִּדּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb as the others|הָאֵ֔לֶּה\rb*. \rb Both the gateway and its portico|וּלְאֵלַמּוֹ\rb* \rb had windows|וְחַלּוֹנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb all around|סָבִ֣יב׀\rb*\rb |סָבִ֑יב\rb*. \rb It was fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb long|אֹ֚רֶךְ\rb* \rb and twenty-five|וְעֶשְׂרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |חָמֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּֽה׃\rb* \rb wide|וְרֹ֕חַב\rb*. \v 34 \rb Its portico|וְאֵלַמּוֹ\rb* \rb faced the outer|הַחִ֣יצוֹנָ֔ה\rb* \rb court|לֶֽחָצֵר֙\rb*, \rb and its side pillars|אֵלוֹ\rb* \rb were decorated with palm trees|וְתִמֹרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb on each side|מִפּ֣וֹ\rb*\rb |וּמִפּ֑וֹ\rb*. \rb Eight|וּשְׁמֹנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb steps|מַעֲל֖וֹת\rb* \rb led up to it|מַעֲלוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 35 \rb Then he brought me|וַיְבִיאֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the north|הַצָּפ֑וֹן\rb* \rb gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb and measured it|וּמָדַ֖ד\rb*. \rb It had the same measurements|כַּמִּדּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb as the others|הָאֵֽלֶּה׃\rb*, \v 36 \rb as did its gate chambers|תָּאוֹ\rb*, \rb side pillars|אֵלוֹ\rb*, \rb and portico|וְאֵלַמּוֹ\rb*. \rb It also had windows|וְחַלּוֹנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb all around|סָבִ֣יב׀\rb*\rb |סָבִ֑יב\rb*. \rb It was fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb long|אֹ֚רֶךְ\rb* \rb and twenty-five|וְעֶשְׂרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |חָמֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּֽה׃\rb* \rb wide|וְרֹ֕חַב\rb*. \v 37 \rb Its portico|וְאֵילוֹ\rb*\f + \fr 40:37 \ft LXX and Vulgate (see also verses 26, 31, and 34); Hebrew \fqa jambs \ft or \fqa dividing wall\f* \rb faced the outer|הַחִ֣יצוֹנָ֔ה\rb* \rb court|לֶֽחָצֵר֙\rb*, \rb and its side pillars|אֵילוֹ\rb* \rb were decorated with palm trees|וְתִמֹרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb on each side|מִפּ֣וֹ\rb*\rb |וּמִפּ֑וֹ\rb*. \rb Eight|וּשְׁמֹנֶ֥ה\rb* \rb steps|מַעֲל֖וֹת\rb* \rb led up to it|מַעֲלוֹ׃\rb*.
\s1 Eight Tables for Sacrifices
\p \v 38 \rb There was a chamber|וְלִשְׁכָּ֣ה\rb* \rb with a doorway|וּפִתְחָ֔הּ\rb* \rb by the portico|בְּאֵילִ֖ים\rb*\f + \fr 40:38 \ft Hebrew \fqa at the jambs\f* \rb in each of the inner gateways|הַשְּׁעָרִ֑ים\rb*. \rb There|שָׁ֖ם\rb* \rb the burnt offering|הָעֹלָֽה׃\rb* \rb was to be washed|יָדִ֥יחוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb*. \v 39 \rb Inside the portico|וּבְאֻלָ֣ם\rb* \rb of the gateway|הַשַּׁ֗עַר\rb* \rb were two|שְׁנַ֤יִם\rb* \rb tables|שֻׁלְחָנוֹת֙\rb* \rb on each side|מִפּ֔וֹ\rb*,\rb |וּשְׁנַ֥יִם\rb*\rb |שֻׁלְחָנ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |מִפֹּ֑ה\rb* \rb on which|אֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb the burnt offerings|הָעוֹלָ֔ה\rb*, \rb sin offerings|וְהַחַטָּ֖את\rb*, \rb and guilt offerings|וְהָאָשָֽׁם׃\rb* \rb were to be slaughtered|לִשְׁח֤וֹט\rb*.
\p \v 40 \rb Outside|מִח֗וּצָה\rb*, \rb as one goes up|לָעוֹלֶה֙\rb* \rb to the entrance|לְפֶ֙תַח֙\rb* \rb of the north|הַצָּפ֔וֹנָה\rb* \rb gateway|הַשַּׁ֣עַר\rb*, \rb there were two|שְׁנַ֖יִם\rb* \rb tables|שֻׁלְחָנ֑וֹת\rb* \rb on|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb one side|הַכָּתֵ֣ף\rb* \rb and two|שְׁנַ֖יִם\rb* \rb more tables|שֻׁלְחָנֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb on|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the other|הָאַחֶ֗רֶת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb side|הַכָּתֵ֣ף\rb* \rb of the gate’s|הַשַּׁ֔עַר\rb* \rb portico|לְאֻלָ֣ם\rb*. \v 41 \rb So there were four|אַרְבָּעָ֨ה\rb* \rb tables|שֻׁלְחָנ֜וֹת\rb* \rb inside|מִפֹּ֗ה\rb* \rb the gateway|הַשָּׁ֑עַר\rb* \rb and four|וְאַרְבָּעָ֧ה\rb* \rb outside|מִפֹּ֖ה\rb* — \rb eight|שְׁמוֹנָ֥ה\rb* \rb tables|שֻׁלְחָנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb in all|אֲלֵיהֶ֥ם\rb* — \rb on which the sacrifices were to be slaughtered|יִשְׁחָֽטוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 42 \rb There were also four|וְאַרְבָּעָה֩\rb* \rb tables|שֻׁלְחָנ֨וֹת\rb* \rb of dressed stone|אַבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |גָזִ֗ית\rb* \rb for the burnt offering|לָעוֹלָ֜ה\rb*, \rb each a cubit|אַמָּ֨ה\rb* \rb and a|אַחַ֤ת\rb* \rb half|וָחֵ֙צִי֙\rb* \rb long|אֹרֶךְ֩\rb*, \rb a cubit|אַמָּ֤ה\rb* \rb and a|אַחַת֙\rb* \rb half|וָחֵ֔צִי\rb* \rb wide|וְרֹ֨חַב\rb*, \rb and a|אֶחָ֑ת\rb* \rb cubit|אַמָּ֣ה\rb* \rb high|וְגֹ֖בַהּ\rb*.\f + \fr 40:42 \ft The tables were approximately 2.6 feet in length and width, and 1.75 feet high (79.2 centimeters in length and width, and 53.3 centimeters high).\f* \rb On these|אֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb were placed|וְיַנִּ֤יחוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the utensils|הַכֵּלִים֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb used to slaughter|יִשְׁחֲט֧וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the burnt offerings|הָעוֹלָ֛ה\rb* \rb and the other sacrifices|וְהַזָּֽבַח׃\rb*.
\p \v 43 \rb The double-pronged hooks|וְהַֽשְׁפַתַּ֗יִם\rb*,\f + \fr 40:43 \ft Or \fqa shelves\f* \rb each a|אֶחָ֛ד\rb* \rb handbreadth long|טֹ֧פַח\rb*,\f + \fr 40:43 \fqa A handbreadth \ft is approximately 2.9 inches or 7.4 centimeters long.\f* \rb were fastened|מוּכָנִ֥ים\rb* \rb all around|סָבִ֣יב׀\rb*\rb |סָבִ֑יב\rb* \rb the inside of the room|בַּבַּ֖יִת\rb*, \rb and the flesh|בְּשַׂ֥ר\rb* \rb of the offering|הַקָּרְבָֽן׃\rb* \rb was to be placed on|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the tables|הַשֻּׁלְחָנ֖וֹת\rb*.
\s1 Chambers for Ministry
\p \v 44 \rb Outside|וּמִחוּצָה֩\rb* \rb the inner|הַפְּנִימִ֜י\rb* \rb gate|לַשַּׁ֨עַר\rb*, \rb within the inner|הַפְּנִימִי֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֗ר\rb* \rb court|בֶּחָצֵ֤ר\rb*, \rb were two chambers|לִֽשְׁכ֣וֹת\rb*,\f + \fr 40:44 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa within the inner court were chambers for the singers\f* \rb one beside|אֶל־\rb*\rb |כֶּ֙תֶף֙\rb* \rb the north|הַצָּפ֔וֹן\rb* \rb gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb and facing|וּפְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*\rb |דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb south|הַדָּר֑וֹם\rb*, \rb and another|אֶחָ֗ד\rb* \rb beside|אֶל־\rb*\rb |כֶּ֙תֶף֙\rb* \rb the south gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb*\f + \fr 40:44 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa the east gateway\f*\rb |הַקָּדִ֔ים\rb* \rb and facing|פְּנֵ֖י\rb*\rb |דֶּ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb north|הַצָּפֹֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 45 \rb Then the man said|וַיְדַבֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָ֑י\rb*: “\rb The|זֹ֣ה\rb* \rb chamber|הַלִּשְׁכָּ֗ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb faces|פָּנֶ֙יהָ֙\rb*\rb |דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb south|הַדָּר֔וֹם\rb* \rb is for the priests|לַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb who keep|שֹׁמְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb charge|מִשְׁמֶ֥רֶת\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבָּֽיִת׃\rb*, \v 46 \rb and the chamber|וְהַלִּשְׁכָּ֗ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb faces|פָּנֶ֙יהָ֙\rb*\rb |דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb north|הַצָּפ֔וֹן\rb* \rb is for the priests|לַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb* \rb who keep|שֹׁמְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb charge|מִשְׁמֶ֣רֶת\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb*. \rb These|הֵ֣מָּה\rb* \rb are the sons|בְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Zadok|צָד֗וֹק\rb*,\rb |מִבְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb the only Levites|לֵוִ֛י\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb who may approach|הַקְּרֵבִ֧ים\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb to minister before Him|לְשָׁרְתֽוֹ׃\rb*.”
\s1 The Inner Court
\p \v 47 \rb Next he measured|וַיָּ֨מָד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the court|הֶחָצֵ֜ר\rb*. \rb It was square|מְרֻבָּ֑עַת\rb*, \rb a hundred|מֵאָ֣ה\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֗ה\rb* \rb long|אֹ֣רֶךְ׀\rb* \rb and a hundred|מֵאָ֥ה\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֖ה\rb* \rb wide|וְרֹ֛חַב\rb*. \rb And the altar was|וְהַמִּזְבֵּ֖חַ\rb* \rb in front|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבָּֽיִת׃\rb*.
\p \v 48 \rb Then he brought me|וַיְבִאֵנִי֮\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the portico|אֻלָ֣ם\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּיִת֒\rb* \rb and measured|וַיָּ֙מָד֙\rb* \rb the side pillars|אֵ֣ל\rb* \rb of the portico|אֻלָ֔ם\rb* \rb to be five|חָמֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּוֹת֙\rb* \rb on each|מִפֹּ֔ה\rb* \rb side|מִפֹּ֑ה\rb*. \rb The width|וְרֹ֣חַב\rb* \rb of the gateway was fourteen cubits and its sidewalls were|הַשַּׁ֔עַר\rb* \rb three|שָׁלֹ֤שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּוֹת֙\rb* \rb on either side|מִפּ֔וֹ\rb*\rb |וְשָׁלֹ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |אַמּ֖וֹת\rb*\rb |מִפּֽוֹ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 40:48 \ft LXX; the gateway was approximately 24.5 feet or 7.5 meters wide, with sidewalls approximately 5.25 feet or 1.6 meters wide on either side. Hebrew \fqa The width of the gateway was three cubits on either side.\f* \v 49 \rb The portico|הָאֻלָ֞ם\rb* \rb was twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֗ה\rb* \rb wide|אֹ֣רֶךְ\rb*\f + \fr 40:49 \fqa 20 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 35 feet or 10.7 meters.\f* \rb and twelve|עַשְׁתֵּ֣י\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֣ה\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb deep|וְרֹ֙חַב֙\rb*,\f + \fr 40:49 \ft LXX; \fqa 12 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 21 feet or 6.4 meters; Hebrew \fqa eleven cubits deep\ft ; that is, approximately 19.25 feet or 5.9 meters.\f* \rb and ten steps|וּבַֽמַּעֲל֔וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb led up|יַעֲל֖וּ\rb* \rb to it|אֵלָ֑יו\rb*.\f + \fr 40:49 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa and steps led up to it \f* \rb There were columns|וְעַמֻּדִים֙\rb* \rb by|אֶל־\rb* \rb the side pillars|הָ֣אֵילִ֔ים\rb*, \rb one|אֶחָ֥ד\rb* \rb on each side|מִפֹּ֖ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶחָ֥ד\rb*\rb |מִפֹּֽה׃\rb*.
\c 41
\s1 Inside the Temple
\p \v 1 \rb Then the man brought me|וַיְבִיאֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the outer sanctuary|הַהֵיכָ֑ל\rb* \rb and measured|וַיָּ֣מָד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the side pillars|הָאֵילִ֗ים\rb* \rb to be six|שֵׁשׁ־\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֨וֹת\rb* \rb wide|רֹ֧חַב־\rb*\f + \fr 41:1 \fqa 6 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 10.5 feet or 3.2 meters; also in verses 3, 5, and 8.\f* \rb on each side|מִפּ֛וֹ\rb*\rb |וְשֵׁשׁ־\rb*\rb |אַמּֽוֹת־\rb*\rb |רֹ֥חַב\rb*\rb |מִפּ֖וֹ\rb*\rb |רֹ֥חַב\rb*\rb |הָאֹֽהֶל׃\rb*.\f + \fr 41:1 \ft One Hebrew manuscript and LXX; most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa on each side—the width of the tent\f* \v 2 \rb The width|וְרֹ֣חַב\rb* \rb of the entrance|הַפֶּתַח֮\rb* \rb was ten|עֶ֣שֶׂר\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּוֹת֒\rb*,\f + \fr 41:2 \fqa 10 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 17.5 feet or 5.3 meters.\f* \rb and the sides|וְכִתְפ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the entrance|הַפֶּ֔תַח\rb* \rb were five|חָמֵ֤שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּוֹת֙\rb*\f + \fr 41:2 \fqa 5 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 8.75 feet or 2.7 meters; also in verses 9, 11, and 12.\f* \rb on each|מִפּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb side|מִפּ֑וֹ\rb*. \rb He also measured|וַיָּ֤מָד\rb* \rb the length of the outer sanctuary|אָרְכּוֹ֙\rb* \rb to be forty|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֖וֹת\rb*, \rb and the width|וְרֹ֖חַב\rb* \rb to be twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אַמָּֽה׃\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֔ה\rb*.\f + \fr 41:2 \ft The outer sanctuary was approximately 70 feet long and 35 feet wide (21.3 meters long and 10.7 meters wide).\f*
\p \v 3 \rb And he went|וּבָ֣א\rb* \rb into the inner sanctuary|לִפְנִ֔ימָה\rb* \rb and measured|וַיָּ֥מָד\rb* \rb the side pillars|אֵֽיל־\rb* \rb at the entrance|הַפֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb to be two|שְׁתַּ֣יִם\rb* \rb cubits wide|אַמּ֑וֹת\rb*.\f + \fr 41:3 \fqa 2 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 3.5 feet or 1.1 meters.\f* \rb The entrance|וְהַפֶּ֙תַח֙\rb* \rb was six|שֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb cubits wide|אַמּ֔וֹת\rb*, \rb and the walls on each side|הַפֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb were seven|שֶׁ֥בַע\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb wide|וְרֹ֥חַב\rb*.\f + \fr 41:3 \fqa 7 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 12.25 feet or 3.7 meters.\f* \v 4 \rb Then he measured|וַיָּ֨מָד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the room adjacent to|אֶל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the inner sanctuary|הַֽהֵיכָ֑ל\rb*\f + \fr 41:4 \ft Or \fqa the length of the inner sanctuary\f* \rb to be twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֗ה\rb* \rb long|אָרְכּ֜וֹ\rb* \rb and twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֖ה\rb* \rb wide|וְרֹ֛חַב\rb*.\f + \fr 41:4 \ft The room was approximately 35 feet long and 35 feet wide (10.7 meters long and 10.7 meters wide).\f* \rb And he said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*, “\rb This|זֶ֖ה\rb* \rb is the Most Holy Place|קֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הַקֳּדָשִֽׁים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 41:4 \ft Or \fqa the Holy of Holies\f*”
\s1 Outside the Temple
\p \v 5 \rb Next he measured|וַיָּ֥מָד\rb* \rb the wall|קִֽיר־\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb to be six|שֵׁ֣שׁ\rb* \rb cubits thick|אַמּ֑וֹת\rb*, \rb and the width|וְרֹ֣חַב\rb* \rb of each|סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb side room|הַצֵּלָע֩\rb* \rb around|סָבִ֧יב׀\rb*\rb |סָבִ֛יב\rb* \rb the temple|לַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb was four|אַרְבַּ֨ע\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֜וֹת\rb*.\f + \fr 41:5 \fqa 4 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 7 feet or 2.1 meters.\f* \v 6 \rb The side rooms|וְהַצְּלָעוֹת֩\rb* \rb were arranged one|צֵלָ֨ע\rb* \rb above|אֶל־\rb* \rb another|צֵלָ֜ע\rb* \rb in three levels|שָׁל֧וֹשׁ\rb* \rb of thirty rooms each|וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֣ים\rb*.\rb |פְּעָמִ֗ים\rb* \rb There were ledges|וּ֠בָאוֹת\rb* \rb all around|סָבִ֥יב׀\rb*\rb |סָבִ֖יב\rb* \rb the wall|בַּקִּ֨יר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb of the temple|לַבַּ֧יִת\rb* \rb to serve as|לִהְי֣וֹת\rb* \rb supports|אֲחוּזִ֑ים\rb* \rb for the side rooms|לַצְּלָע֛וֹת\rb*, \rb so that the supports|אֲחוּזִ֖ים\rb* \rb would not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb be fastened into|יִהְי֥וּ\rb* \rb the wall|בְּקִ֥יר\rb* \rb of the temple itself|הַבָּֽיִת׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb The side rooms|לַצְּלָע֗וֹת\rb*\rb |כִּ֣י\rb* \rb surrounding|מֽוּסַב־\rb* \rb the temple|הַ֠בַּיִת\rb* \rb widened at each successive level|וְֽרָחֲבָ֡ה\rb*\rb |וְֽנָסְבָה֩\rb*\rb |לְמַ֨עְלָה\rb*,\rb |לְמַ֜עְלָה\rb* \rb because the structure surrounding|סָבִ֤יב׀\rb*\rb |סָבִיב֙\rb* \rb the temple|לַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb ascended|לְמַ֨עְלָה\rb* \rb by stages|לְמַ֜עְלָה\rb* \rb corresponding to|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֥ן\rb* \rb the narrowing of the temple wall|רֹֽחַב־\rb*\rb |לַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb as it rose upward|לְמָ֑עְלָה\rb*. \rb And so|וְכֵ֧ן\rb* \rb a stairway went up|יַעֲלֶ֥ה\rb* \rb from the lowest story|הַתַּחְתּוֹנָ֛ה\rb* \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the highest|הָעֶלְיוֹנָ֖ה\rb*, \rb through the middle one|לַתִּיכוֹנָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 8 \rb I saw|וְרָאִ֧יתִי\rb* \rb that the temple|לַבַּ֛יִת\rb* \rb had a raised base|גֹּ֖בַהּ\rb* \rb all|סָבִ֣יב׀\rb* \rb around it|סָבִ֑יב\rb*, \rb forming the foundation|מְיֻסְּדוֹת\rb* \rb of the side rooms|הַצְּלָעוֹת֙\rb*. \rb It was the full length of|מְל֣וֹ\rb* \rb a rod|הַקָּנֶ֔ה\rb*, \rb six|שֵׁ֥שׁ\rb* \rb long|אַצִּֽילָה׃\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֖וֹת\rb*. \v 9 \rb The outer|הַח֖וּץ\rb* \rb wall|הַקִּ֧יר\rb*\rb |אֲ‍ֽשֶׁר־\rb* \rb of the side rooms|לַצֵּלָ֛ע\rb* \rb was five|חָמֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֑וֹת\rb* \rb thick|רֹ֣חַב\rb*, \rb and|וַאֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb the open area|מֻנָּ֔ח\rb* \rb between|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb the side rooms|צְלָע֖וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb of the temple|לַבָּֽיִת׃\rb* \v 10 \rb |וּבֵ֨ין\rb* \rb and the outer chambers|הַלְּשָׁכ֜וֹת\rb* \rb was twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֛ה\rb* \rb wide|רֹ֣חַב\rb* \rb all around|סָבִ֥יב\rb*\rb |סָבִ֥יב׀\rb*\rb |סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb the temple|לַבַּ֖יִת\rb*. \v 11 \rb The side rooms|הַצֵּלָע֙\rb* \rb opened into this area|לַמֻּנָּ֔ח\rb*,\rb |פֶּ֤תַח\rb* \rb with one|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb entrance|וּפֶ֤תַח\rb* \rb on|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb the north|הַצָּפ֔וֹן\rb*\rb |וּפֶ֥תַח\rb* \rb and another|אֶחָ֖ד\rb* \rb on the south|לַדָּר֑וֹם\rb*. \rb The open area|מְק֣וֹם\rb*\rb |הַמֻּנָּ֔ח\rb* \rb was five|חָמֵ֥שׁ\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb wide|וְרֹ֙חַב֙\rb* \rb all|סָבִ֥יב׀\rb* \rb around|סָבִֽיב׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Now the building|וְהַבִּנְיָ֡ן\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb faced|אֶל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb the temple courtyard|הַגִּזְרָ֜ה\rb*\rb |פְּאַ֣ת\rb* \rb on|דֶּֽרֶךְ־\rb* \rb the west|הַיָּ֗ם\rb* \rb was seventy|שִׁבְעִ֣ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֔ה\rb* \rb wide|רֹ֚חַב\rb*,\f + \fr 41:12 \fqa 70 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 122.5 feet or 37.3 meters.\f* \rb and the wall|וְקִ֧יר\rb* \rb of the building|הַבִּנְיָ֛ן\rb* \rb was five|חָֽמֵשׁ־\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb thick|רֹ֖חַב\rb* \rb all|סָבִ֣יב׀\rb* \rb around|סָבִ֑יב\rb*, \rb with a length|וְאָרְכּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb of ninety|תִּשְׁעִ֥ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּֽה׃\rb*.\f + \fr 41:12 \fqa 90 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 157.5 feet or 48 meters.\f*
\p \v 13 \rb Then he measured|וּמָדַ֣ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the temple|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb to be a hundred|מֵאָ֣ה\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֑ה\rb* \rb long|אֹ֖רֶךְ\rb*,\f + \fr 41:13 \fqa 100 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 175 feet or 53.3 meters; similarly in verses 14 and 15.\f* \rb and the temple courtyard|וְהַגִּזְרָ֤ה\rb* \rb and the building|וְהַבִּנְיָה֙\rb* \rb with its walls|וְקִ֣ירוֹתֶ֔יהָ\rb* \rb were also a hundred|מֵאָ֥ה\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּֽה׃\rb* \rb long|אֹ֖רֶךְ\rb*. \v 14 \rb The width|וְרֹחַב֩\rb* \rb of the temple courtyard|וְהַגִּזְרָ֛ה\rb* \rb on the east|לַקָּדִ֖ים\rb*, \rb including the front|פְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֧יִת\rb*, \rb was a hundred|מֵאָ֥ה\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּֽה׃\rb*.
\s1 The Interior Structures
\p \v 15 \rb Next he measured|וּמָדַ֣ד\rb* \rb the length|אֹֽרֶךְ־\rb* \rb of the building|הַ֠בִּנְיָן\rb* \rb facing|אֶל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֨י\rb* \rb the temple courtyard|הַגִּזְרָ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the rear of the temple|אַחֲרֶ֧יהָ\rb*, \rb including its galleries|וְאַתּוּקֵיהָא\rb* \rb on each side|מִפּ֥וֹ\rb*;\rb |וּמִפּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb it was a hundred|מֵאָ֣ה\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֑ה\rb*. \rb The outer sanctuary|וְהַֽהֵיכָל֙\rb*, \rb the inner sanctuary|הַפְּנִימִ֔י\rb*, \rb and the porticoes|וְאֻֽלַמֵּ֖י\rb* \rb facing the court|הֶחָצֵֽר׃\rb*, \v 16 \rb as well as the thresholds|הַסִּפִּ֡ים\rb* \rb and the beveled|הָ֠אֲטֻמוֹת\rb* \rb windows|וְהַחַלּוֹנִ֣ים\rb* \rb and the galleries|וְהָאַתִּיקִ֤ים׀\rb* \rb all around|סָבִיב֙\rb* \rb with their three|לִשְׁלָשְׁתָּ֔ם\rb* \rb levels opposite|נֶ֧גֶד\rb* \rb the threshold|הַסַּ֛ף\rb*, \rb were overlaid with|שְׂחִ֥יף\rb* \rb wood|עֵ֖ץ\rb* \rb on all sides|סָבִ֣יב׀\rb*\rb |סָבִ֑יב\rb*. \rb They were paneled from the ground|וְהָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the windows|הַֽחַלֹּנ֔וֹת\rb*, \rb and the windows|וְהַֽחַלֹּנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb were covered|מְכֻסּֽוֹת׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb In the space above|עַל־\rb*\rb |מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the outside of the entrance|הַפֶּ֡תַח\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb* \rb the inner|הַפְּנִימִ֨י\rb* \rb sanctuary|הַבַּיִת֩\rb* \rb on|וְלַח֜וּץ\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the walls|הַקִּ֨יר\rb*, \rb spaced evenly|מִדּֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb around|סָבִ֧יב׀\rb*\rb |סָבִ֛יב\rb* \rb the inner and|בַּפְּנִימִ֥י\rb* \rb outer sanctuary|וּבַחִיצ֖וֹן\rb*, \v 18 \rb were alternating|וְתִֽמֹרָה֙\rb*\rb |בֵּין־\rb*\rb |כְּר֣וּב\rb* \rb carved|וְעָשׂ֥וּי\rb* \rb cherubim|כְּרוּבִ֖ים\rb* \rb and palm trees|וְתִֽמֹרִ֑ים\rb*. \rb Each cherub|לִכְר֔וּב\rb* \rb had two|וּשְׁנַ֥יִם\rb* \rb faces|פָּנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |לַכְּרֽוּב׃\rb*: \v 19 \rb the face|וּפְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of a man|אָדָ֤ם\rb* \rb was toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb the palm tree|הַתִּֽמֹרָה֙\rb* \rb on one side|מִפּ֔וֹ\rb*, \rb and the face|וּפְנֵֽי־\rb* \rb of a young lion|כְפִ֥יר\rb* \rb was toward|אֶל־\rb* \rb the palm tree|הַתִּֽמֹרָ֖ה\rb* \rb on the other side|מִפּ֑וֹ\rb*. \rb They were carved|עָשׂ֥וּי\rb* \rb all the way around|אֶל־\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |סָבִ֥יב׀\rb*\rb |סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb the temple|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb*. \v 20 \rb Cherubim|הַכְּרוּבִ֥ים\rb* \rb and palm trees|וְהַתִּֽמֹרִ֖ים\rb* \rb were carved|עֲשׂוּיִ֑ם\rb* \rb on the wall|וְקִ֖יר\rb* \rb of the outer sanctuary|הַׄהֵׄיׄכָֽׄלׄ׃\rb* \rb from the floor|מֵהָאָ֙רֶץ֙\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the space above|מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb the entrance|הַפֶּ֔תַח\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb The outer sanctuary|הַֽהֵיכָ֖ל\rb* \rb had a rectangular|רְבֻעָ֑ה\rb* \rb doorframe|מְזוּזַ֣ת\rb*, \rb and the doorframe|וּפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the sanctuary|הַקֹּ֔דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |הַמַּרְאֶ֖ה\rb* \rb was similar|כַּמַּרְאֶֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb There was an altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֡חַ\rb* \rb of wood|עֵ֣ץ\rb* \rb three|שָׁלוֹשׁ֩\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֨וֹת\rb* \rb high|גָּבֹ֜הַּ\rb* \rb and two|שְׁתַּֽיִם־\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֗וֹת\rb* \rb square|וְאָרְכּ֣וֹ\rb*.\f + \fr 41:22 \ft Or \fqa long\ft ; the altar was approximately 5.25 feet high and 3.5 feet square (1.6 meters high and 1.1 meters square)\f* \rb Its corners|וּמִקְצֹֽעוֹתָיו֙\rb*, \rb base|וְאָרְכּ֥וֹ\rb*, \rb and sides|וְקִֽירֹתָ֖יו\rb* \rb were of wood|עֵ֑ץ\rb*. \rb And the man told|וַיְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*, “\rb This|זֶ֚ה\rb* \rb is the table|הַשֻּׁלְחָ֔ן\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb is before|לִפְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb*.”
\p \v 23 \rb Both the outer sanctuary|לַֽהֵיכָ֖ל\rb* \rb and the inner sanctuary|וְלַקֹּֽדֶשׁ׃\rb* \rb had double|וּשְׁתַּ֧יִם\rb* \rb doors|דְּלָת֛וֹת\rb*, \v 24 \rb and each|וּשְׁתַּ֥יִם\rb* \rb door|דְּלָת֖וֹת\rb* \rb had two|שְׁ֚תַּיִם\rb* \rb swinging|מוּסַבּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb panels|לַדְּלָת֑וֹת\rb*. \rb There were two|שְׁ֚תַּיִם\rb* \rb panels|דְּלָת֔וֹת\rb* \rb for one|אֶחָ֔ת\rb* \rb door|לְדֶ֣לֶת\rb* \rb and two|וּשְׁתֵּ֥י\rb*\rb |דְלָת֖וֹת\rb* \rb for the other|לָאַחֶֽרֶת׃\rb*. \v 25 \rb Cherubim|כְּרוּבִ֣ים\rb* \rb and palm trees|וְתִֽמֹרִ֔ים\rb* \rb like those|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |עֲשׂוּיִ֖ם\rb* \rb on the walls|לַקִּיר֑וֹת\rb* \rb were carved|וַעֲשׂוּיָ֨ה\rb* \rb on|אֲלֵיהֶ֜ן\rb* \rb the doors|דַּלְת֤וֹת\rb* \rb of the outer sanctuary|הַֽהֵיכָל֙\rb*, \rb and there was a wooden|עֵ֛ץ\rb* \rb canopy|וְעָ֥ב\rb* \rb outside|מֵהַחֽוּץ׃\rb*, \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the front|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the portico|הָאוּלָ֖ם\rb*. \v 26 \rb There were beveled|אֲטֻמ֤וֹת\rb* \rb windows|וְחַלּוֹנִ֨ים\rb* \rb and palm trees|וְתִֽמֹרִים֙\rb*\rb |מִפּ֣וֹ\rb*\rb |וּמִפּ֔וֹ\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the sidewalls|כִּתְפ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the portico|הָֽאוּלָ֑ם\rb*. \rb The side rooms|וְצַלְע֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb also had canopies|וְהָעֻבִּֽים׃\rb*.
\c 42
\s1 Chambers for the Priests
\p \v 1 \rb Then the man led me out|וַיּוֹצִאֵ֗נִי\rb*\rb |הַדֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb*\rb |דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb northward|הַצָּפ֑וֹן\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the outer|הַחִ֣יצוֹנָ֔ה\rb* \rb court|הֶֽחָצֵר֙\rb*, \rb and he brought me|וַיְבִאֵ֣נִי\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the group of chambers|הַלִּשְׁכָּ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb opposite|נֶ֧גֶד\rb* \rb the temple courtyard|הַגִּזְרָ֛ה\rb*\rb |וַאֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb and|נֶ֥גֶד\rb* \rb the outer wall|הַבִּנְיָ֖ן\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the north side|הַצָּפֽוֹן׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb The building|אֹ֙רֶךְ֙\rb* \rb with the door|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb facing north|הַצָּפ֑וֹן\rb* \rb was a hundred|הַמֵּאָ֔ה\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb long|וְהָרֹ֖חַב\rb* \rb and fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֥ים\rb* \rb cubits wide|אַמּֽוֹת׃\rb*.\f + \fr 42:2 \ft The building was approximately 175 feet long and 87.5 feet wide (53.3 meters long and 26.7 meters wide).\f* \v 3 \rb Gallery|אַתִּ֥יק\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb faced|פְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb gallery|אַתִּ֖יק\rb* \rb in three levels|בַּשְּׁלִשִֽׁים׃\rb* \rb opposite|נֶ֣גֶד\rb* \rb the twenty cubits|הָֽעֶשְׂרִ֗ים\rb*\f + \fr 42:3 \fqa 20 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 35 feet or 10.7 meters.\f* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb belonged to the inner|הַפְּנִימִ֔י\rb* \rb court|לֶחָצֵ֣ר\rb* \rb and opposite|וְנֶ֣גֶד\rb* \rb the pavement|רִֽצְפָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb belonged to the outer|הַחִֽיצוֹנָ֑ה\rb* \rb court|לֶחָצֵ֣ר\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb In front|וְלִפְנֵ֨י\rb* \rb of the chambers|הַלְּשָׁכ֜וֹת\rb* \rb was an inner walkway|מַהֲלַךְ֩\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |הַפְּנִימִ֔ית\rb* \rb ten|עֶ֨שֶׂר\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb wide|רֹ֙חַב֙\rb* \rb and a hundred|אֶחָ֑ת\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֣ה\rb* \rb long|דֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb*.\f + \fr 42:4 \ft LXX. The walkway was approximately 17.5 feet wide and 175 feet long (5.3 meters wide and 53.3 meters long). Hebrew \fqa ten cubits wide and a cubit long.\f* \rb Their doors|וּפִתְחֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb were on the north|לַצָּפֽוֹן׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Now the upper|הָעֶלְיוֹנֹ֖ת\rb* \rb chambers|וְהַלְּשָׁכ֥וֹת\rb* \rb were smaller|קְצֻר֑וֹת\rb* \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the galleries|אַתִּיקִ֜ים\rb* \rb took more space|יוֹכְל֨וּ\rb* \rb from the chambers|מֵהֵ֗נָה\rb* \rb on the lower|מֵֽהַתַּחְתֹּנ֛וֹת\rb* \rb and middle floors|וּמֵהַתִּֽכֹנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb of the building|בִּנְיָֽן׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb For|כִּ֤י\rb* \rb they|הֵ֔נָּה\rb* \rb were arranged in three stories|מְשֻׁלָּשׁוֹת֙\rb*, \rb and unlike|כְּעַמּוּדֵ֖י\rb* \rb the courts|הַחֲצֵר֑וֹת\rb*, \rb they had|לָהֶן֙\rb* \rb no|וְאֵ֤ין\rb* \rb pillars|עַמּוּדִ֔ים\rb*. \rb So|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb the upper chambers were set back further|נֶאֱצַ֗ל\rb* \rb than the lower|מֵהַתַּחְתּוֹנ֛וֹת\rb* \rb and middle floors|וּמֵהַתִּֽיכֹנ֖וֹת\rb*. \v 7 \rb An outer|לַחוּץ֙\rb* \rb wall|וְגָדֵ֤ר\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb front|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the chambers|הַלְּשָׁכ֑וֹת\rb* \rb was|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֥ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּֽה׃\rb* \rb long|אָרְכּ֖וֹ\rb* \rb and ran parallel to|לְעֻמַּ֣ת\rb* \rb the chambers|הַלְּשָׁכ֔וֹת\rb* \rb and|דֶּ֛רֶךְ\rb* \rb the outer|הַחִֽצוֹנָ֖ה\rb* \rb court|הֶחָצֵ֥ר\rb*. \v 8 \rb For|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the chambers|הַלְּשָׁכ֗וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֛ר\rb* \rb on the outer|הַחִֽצוֹנָ֖ה\rb* \rb court|לֶחָצֵ֥ר\rb* \rb were fifty|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֑ה\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb long|אֹ֣רֶךְ\rb*, \rb while those facing|עַל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the temple|הַהֵיכָ֖ל\rb* \rb were a hundred|מֵאָ֥ה\rb* \rb cubits long|אַמָּֽה׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb And below|וּמִתַּחֲתָה\rb* \rb these|הָאֵ֑לֶּה\rb* \rb chambers was|לְּשָׁכוֹת\rb* \rb the entrance|הַמָּבוֹא\rb* \rb on the east side|מֵֽהַקָּדִ֔ים\rb* \rb as one enters|בְּבֹא֣וֹ\rb* \rb them|לָהֵ֔נָּה\rb* \rb from the outer|הַחִצֹנָֽה׃\rb* \rb court|מֵֽהֶחָצֵ֖ר\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb On the|דֶּ֧רֶךְ\rb* \rb south side|הַקָּדִ֛ים\rb*\f + \fr 42:10 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa east side\f* \rb along the length|בְּרֹ֣חַב׀\rb* \rb of the wall|גֶּ֣דֶר\rb* \rb of the outer court|הֶחָצֵ֗ר\rb* \rb were chambers|לְשָׁכֽוֹת׃\rb* \rb adjoining|פְּנֵ֧י\rb* \rb the courtyard|הַגִּזְרָ֛ה\rb* \rb and|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb opposite|פְּנֵ֥י\rb* \rb the building|הַבִּנְיָ֖ן\rb*, \v 11 \rb with a passageway|וְדֶ֙רֶךְ֙\rb* \rb in front of them|לִפְנֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*,\rb |כְּמַרְאֵ֣ה\rb* \rb just like the chambers|הַלְּשָׁכ֗וֹת\rb* \rb that were|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb on|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb the north|הַצָּפ֔וֹן\rb*. \rb They had the same length|כְּאָרְכָּ֖ן\rb*\rb |כֵּ֣ן\rb* \rb and width|רָחְבָּ֑ן\rb*, \rb with similar|וְכֹל֙\rb* \rb exits|מוֹצָ֣אֵיהֶ֔ן\rb* \rb and dimensions|וּכְמִשְׁפְּטֵיהֶ֖ן\rb*\rb |וּכְפִתְחֵיהֶֽן׃\rb*. \v 12 \rb And corresponding to the doors|וּכְפִתְחֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the chambers|הַלְּשָׁכ֗וֹת\rb* \rb that were|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb facing|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb south|הַדָּר֔וֹם\rb*, \rb there was a door|פֶּ֖תַח\rb* \rb in front|בְּרֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of the walkway|דָּ֑רֶךְ\rb*\rb |דֶּ֗רֶךְ\rb* \rb that was parallel|בִּפְנֵי֙\rb* \rb to the wall|הַגְּדֶ֣רֶת\rb* \rb extending|הֲגִינָ֔ה\rb*\rb |דֶּ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb eastward|הַקָּדִ֖ים\rb*\rb |בְּבוֹאָֽן׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Then the man said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֗י\rb*, “\rb The north|הַצָּפ֜וֹן\rb* \rb and south|הַדָּרוֹם֮\rb* \rb chambers|לִֽשְׁכ֨וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb facing|אֶל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the temple courtyard|הַגִּזְרָה֒\rb*\rb |הֵ֣נָּה׀\rb* \rb are the holy|הַקֹּ֗דֶשׁ\rb* \rb chambers|לִֽשְׁכ֣וֹת\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֛ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb approach|קְרוֹבִ֥ים\rb* \rb the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb will eat|יֹאכְלוּ־\rb* \rb the most holy offerings|קָדְשֵׁ֣י\rb*\rb |הַקֳּדָשִׁ֑ים\rb*. \rb There|שָׁ֞ם\rb* \rb they will place|יַנִּ֣יחוּ׀\rb* \rb the most holy offerings|קָדְשֵׁ֣י\rb*\rb |הַקֳּדָשִׁ֗ים\rb*— \rb the grain offerings|וְהַמִּנְחָה֙\rb*, \rb the sin offerings|וְהַחַטָּ֣את\rb*, \rb and the guilt offerings|וְהָאָשָׁ֔ם\rb*— \rb for|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb the place|הַמָּק֖וֹם\rb* \rb is holy|קָדֹֽשׁ׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb Once the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֗ים\rb* \rb have entered|בְּבֹאָ֣ם\rb* \rb the holy area|מֵהַקֹּ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb*, \rb they must not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb go out|יֵצְא֤וּ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the outer|הַחִיצוֹנָ֔ה\rb*\rb |וְשָׁ֞ם\rb* \rb court|הֶחָצֵ֣ר\rb* \rb until they have left behind|יַנִּ֧יחוּ\rb* \rb the garments|בִגְדֵיהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb in which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they minister|יְשָׁרְת֥וּ\rb*, \rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb these|הֵ֑נָּה\rb* \rb are holy|קֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*. \rb They are to put on|יִלְבְּשׁוּ\rb* \rb other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb clothes|בְּגָדִ֣ים\rb* \rb before they approach|וְקָרְב֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the places that are|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb for the people|לָעָֽם׃\rb*.”
\s1 The Outer Measurements
\p \v 15 \rb Now when the man had finished|וְכִלָּ֗ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb measuring|מִדּוֹת֙\rb* \rb the interior|הַפְּנִימִ֔י\rb* \rb of the temple area|הַבַּ֣יִת\rb*, \rb he led me out|וְהוֹצִיאַ֙נִי֙\rb* \rb by|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb the gate|הַשַּׁ֔עַר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb faced|פָּנָ֖יו\rb*\rb |דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb east|הַקָּדִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and he measured the area|וּמְדָד֖וֹ\rb* \rb all|סָבִ֥יב׀\rb* \rb around|סָבִֽיב׃\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \v 16 \rb With a measuring|הַמִּדָּ֑ה\rb* \rb rod|בִּקְנֵ֣ה\rb* \rb he measured|מָדַ֛ד\rb* \rb the east|הַקָּדִ֖ים\rb* \rb side|ר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb to be five|חֲמֵשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred|אֵמוֹת\rb* \rb cubits|קָנִ֛ים\rb* \rb long|סָבִֽיב׃\rb*.\f + \fr 42:16 \ft See LXX; \fqa five hundred cubits \ft from verse 17 LXX and implied in verses 16, 18, 19, and 20 is approximately 875 feet or 266.7 meters in length. Hebrew \fqa five hundred reeds, with the measuring reed round about\ft , that is approximately 5,250 feet or 1,600 meters; similarly in verses 17, 18, 19, and 20.\f*
\li1 \v 17 \rb He measured|מָדַ֖ד\rb* \rb the north|הַצָּפ֑וֹן\rb* \rb side|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb to be five|חֲמֵשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֥וֹת\rb* \rb cubits|קָנִ֛ים\rb* \rb long|הַמִּדָּ֖ה\rb*\rb |סָבִֽיב׃\rb*\rb |בִּקְנֵ֥ה\rb*.
\li1 \v 18 \rb |אֵ֛ת\rb* \rb He measured|מָדָ֑ד\rb* \rb the south|הַדָּר֖וֹם\rb* \rb side|ר֥וּחַ\rb* \rb to be five|חֲמֵשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֥וֹת\rb* \rb cubits|קָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb long|הַמִּדָּֽה׃\rb*.
\li1 \v 19 \rb And he came around|סָבַ֖ב\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb and measured|מָדַ֛ד\rb* \rb the west|הַיָּ֑ם\rb* \rb side|ר֣וּחַ\rb* \rb to be five|חֲמֵשׁ־\rb* \rb hundred|מֵא֥וֹת\rb* \rb cubits|קָנִ֖ים\rb* \rb long|הַמִּדָּֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb So he measured|מְדָד֗וֹ\rb* \rb the area on all four|לְאַרְבַּ֨ע\rb* \rb sides|רוּח֜וֹת\rb*. \rb It had a wall|ח֤וֹמָה\rb* \rb all|סָבִ֣יב׀\rb* \rb around|סָבִ֔יב\rb*, \rb five|חֲמֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb hundred cubits|מֵא֔וֹת\rb* \rb long|אֹ֚רֶךְ\rb* \rb and five|חֲמֵ֣שׁ\rb* \rb hundred cubits|מֵא֑וֹת\rb* \rb wide|וְרֹ֖חַב\rb*, \rb to separate|לְהַבְדִּ֕יל\rb*\rb |בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb the holy|הַקֹּ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb from the common|לְחֹֽל׃\rb*.
\c 43
\s1 The Glory of the LORD Returns to the Temple
\p \v 1 \rb Then the man brought me|וַיּוֹלִכֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb back to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the gate|הַשָּׁ֑עַר\rb*\rb |שַׁ֕עַר\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb faces|פֹּנֶ֖ה\rb*\rb |דֶּ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb east|הַקָּדִֽים׃\rb*, \v 2 \rb and I saw|וְהִנֵּ֗ה\rb* \rb the glory|כְּבוֹד֙\rb* \rb of the God|אֱלֹהֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb coming|בָּ֖א\rb* \rb from|מִדֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb the east|הַקָּדִ֑ים\rb*. \rb His voice|וְקוֹל֗וֹ\rb* \rb was like the roar|כְּקוֹל֙\rb* \rb of many|רַבִּ֔ים\rb* \rb waters|מַ֣יִם\rb*, \rb and the earth|וְהָאָ֖רֶץ\rb* \rb shone|הֵאִ֥ירָה\rb* \rb with His glory|מִכְּבֹדֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb The vision|וּכְמַרְאֵ֨ה\rb* \rb I saw|רָאִ֗יתִי\rb* \rb was like the vision|הַמַּרְאֶ֜ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |כַּמַּרְאֶ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb I had seen|רָאִ֙יתִי֙\rb* \rb when He came|בְּבֹאִי֙\rb*\f + \fr 43:3 \ft Some Hebrew manuscripts and Vulgate; most Hebrew manuscripts \fqa when I came\f* \rb to destroy|לְשַׁחֵ֣ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb and like the visions|וּמַרְא֕וֹת\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I had seen|רָאִ֖יתִי\rb* \rb by|אֶל־\rb* \rb the River|נְהַר־\rb* \rb Kebar|כְּבָ֑ר\rb*. \rb I fell|וָאֶפֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb facedown|אֶל־\rb*\rb |פָּנָֽי׃\rb*, \v 4 \rb and the glory|וּכְב֥וֹד\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb entered|בָּ֣א\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the temple|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb* \rb through|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb the gate|שַׁ֔עַר\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb facing|פָּנָ֖יו\rb*\rb |דֶּ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb east|הַקָּדִֽים׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb Then the Spirit|ר֔וּחַ\rb* \rb lifted me up|וַתִּשָּׂאֵ֣נִי\rb* \rb and brought me|וַתְּבִיאֵ֕נִי\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the inner|הַפְּנִימִ֑י\rb*\rb |וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb court|הֶֽחָצֵ֖ר\rb*, \rb and the glory|כְבוֹד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb* \rb filled|מָלֵ֥א\rb* \rb the temple|הַבָּֽיִת׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 \rb While the man|וְאִ֕ישׁ\rb* \rb was|הָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb standing|עֹמֵ֖ד\rb* \rb beside me|אֶצְלִֽי׃\rb*, \rb I heard|וָאֶשְׁמַ֛ע\rb* \rb someone speaking|מִדַּבֵּ֥ר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb from inside the temple|מֵהַבָּ֑יִת\rb*, \v 7 \rb and He said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֗י\rb*, “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָם֙\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this is the place|מְק֣וֹם\rb* \rb of My throne|כִּסְאִ֗י\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the place|מְקוֹם֙\rb* \rb for the soles|כַּפּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of My feet|רַגְלַ֔י\rb*, \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb I will dwell|אֶשְׁכָּן־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֛ם\rb* \rb among|בְּת֥וֹךְ\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb* \rb forever|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*\rb |לְעוֹלָ֑ם\rb*. \rb The house|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִ֠שְׂרָאֵל\rb* \rb will never|וְלֹ֣א\rb* \rb again|ע֣וֹד\rb* \rb defile|יְטַמְּא֣וּ\rb* \rb My holy|קָדְשִׁ֞י\rb* \rb name|שֵׁ֣ם\rb* — \rb neither they|הֵ֤מָּה\rb* \rb nor their kings|וּמַלְכֵיהֶם֙\rb* — \rb by their prostitution|בִּזְנוּתָ֔ם\rb* \rb and by the funeral offerings|וּבְפִגְרֵ֥י\rb*\f + \fr 43:7 \ft Or \fqa the monuments\ft ; also in verse 9 \f* \rb for their kings|מַלְכֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb at their deaths|בָּמוֹתָֽם׃\rb*.\f + \fr 43:7 \ft Or \fqa for their kings on their high places\f* \v 8 \rb When they placed|בְּתִתָּ֨ם\rb* \rb their threshold|סִפָּ֜ם\rb* \rb next to|אֶת־\rb* \rb My threshold|סִפִּ֗י\rb* \rb and their doorposts|וּמְזֽוּזָתָם֙\rb* \rb beside|אֵ֣צֶל\rb* \rb My doorposts|מְזוּזָתִ֔י\rb*, \rb with only a wall|וְהַקִּ֖יר\rb* \rb between Me and them|בֵּינִ֣י\rb*,\rb |וּבֵֽינֵיהֶ֑ם\rb* \rb they defiled|וְטִמְּא֣וּ׀\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My holy|קָדְשִׁ֗י\rb* \rb name|שֵׁ֣ם\rb* \rb by the abominations|בְּתֽוֹעֲבוֹתָם֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb they committed|עָשׂ֔וּ\rb*. \rb Therefore I have consumed|וָאֲכַ֥ל\rb* \rb them|אֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb in My anger|בְּאַפִּֽי׃\rb*. \v 9 \rb Now|עַתָּ֞ה\rb* \rb let them remove|יְרַחֲק֧וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb far from Me|מִמֶּ֑נִּי\rb* \rb their prostitution|זְנוּתָ֛ם\rb* \rb and the funeral offerings|וּפִגְרֵ֥י\rb* \rb for their kings|מַלְכֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb and I will dwell|וְשָׁכַנְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb among them|בְתוֹכָ֖ם\rb* \rb forever|לְעוֹלָֽם׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb As for you|אַתָּ֣ה\rb*, \rb son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֗ם\rb*, \rb describe|הַגֵּ֤ד\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the temple|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb to the people|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb so that they may be ashamed|וְיִכָּלְמ֖וּ\rb* \rb of their iniquities|מֵעֲוֺנֽוֹתֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb Let them measure|וּמָדְד֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the plan|תָּכְנִֽית׃\rb*, \v 11 \rb and if|וְאִֽם־\rb* \rb they are ashamed|נִכְלְמ֞וּ\rb*\f + \fr 43:11 \ft Hebrew; LXX and Vulgate \fqa and they will be ashamed\f* \rb of all|מִכֹּ֣ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they have done|עָשׂ֗וּ\rb*, \rb then make known|הוֹדַ֣ע\rb* \rb to them|אוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb the design|צוּרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֡יִת\rb*— \rb its arrangement|וּתְכוּנָת֡וֹ\rb* \rb and its exits|וּמוֹצָאָ֡יו\rb* \rb and entrances|וּמוֹבָאָ֣יו\rb*— \rb its whole|וְֽכָל־\rb* \rb design|צֽוּרֹתָ֡ו\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֣ת\rb* \rb along with all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its statutes|חֻקֹּתָיו֩\rb*, \rb forms|צוּרֹתָי\rb*, \rb and|וְכָל־\rb* \rb laws|תּוֹרֹתוֹ\rb*. \rb Write it down|וּכְתֹ֖ב\rb* \rb in their sight|לְעֵֽינֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb so that they may keep|וְיִשְׁמְר֞וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb its complete|כָּל־\rb* \rb design|צוּרָת֛וֹ\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb its statutes|חֻקֹּתָ֖יו\rb* \rb and may carry them out|וְעָשׂ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אוֹתָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb This|זֹ֖את\rb* \rb is the law|תּוֹרַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb*: \rb All|כָּל־\rb* \rb its surrounding|סָבִ֤יב׀\rb*\rb |סָבִיב֙\rb* \rb territory|גְּבֻל֞וֹ\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb top|רֹ֣אשׁ\rb* \rb of the mountain|הָ֠הָר\rb* \rb will be most holy|קֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |קָדָשִׁ֔ים\rb*. \rb Yes|הִנֵּה־\rb*, \rb this|זֹ֖את\rb* \rb is the law|תּוֹרַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבָּֽיִת׃\rb*.
\s1 The Altar of Sacrifice
\p \v 13 \rb These|וְאֵ֨לֶּה\rb* \rb are the measurements|מִדּ֤וֹת\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb* \rb in long cubits|בָּֽאַמּ֔וֹת\rb*\f + \fr 43:13 \ft The \fqa long cubit\ft , about 21 inches or 53.3 centimeters, is the basic unit for linear measurement throughout Ezekiel 40–48. \f* (\rb a cubit|אַמָּ֥ה\rb*\rb |אַמָּ֖ה\rb* \rb and a handbreadth|וָטֹ֑פַח\rb*): \rb Its gutter|וְחֵ֨יק\rb* \rb shall be a cubit deep|הָאַמָּ֜ה\rb* \rb and a cubit|וְאַמָּה־\rb* \rb wide|רֹ֗חַב\rb*, \rb with a rim|וּגְבוּלָ֨הּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb of one|הָאֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb span|זֶ֣רֶת\rb*\f + \fr 43:13 \fqa One span \ft is approximately 9 inches or 22.9 centimeters.\f* \rb around|סָבִיב֙\rb* \rb its edge|שְׂפָתָ֤הּ\rb*.
\p \rb And this is|וְזֶ֖ה\rb* \rb the height|גַּ֥ב\rb* \rb of the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb*: \v 14 \rb The space from the gutter|וּמֵחֵ֨יק\rb* \rb on the ground|הָאָ֜רֶץ\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the lower|הַתַּחְתּוֹנָה֙\rb* \rb ledge|הָעֲזָרָ֤ה\rb* \rb shall be two|שְׁתַּ֣יִם\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֔וֹת\rb*, \rb and the ledge one|אֶחָ֑ת\rb* \rb cubit|אַמָּ֣ה\rb* \rb wide|וְרֹ֖חַב\rb*.\f + \fr 43:14 \ft The space was to be approximately 3.5 feet (1.1 meters), and the ledge was to be approximately 1.75 feet wide (53.3 centimeters wide).\f* \rb The space from the smaller|הַקְּטַנָּ֜ה\rb* \rb ledge|וּמֵהֳעֲזָרָ֨ה\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the larger|הַגְּדוֹלָה֙\rb* \rb ledge|הָעֲזָרָ֤ה\rb* \rb shall be four|אַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb cubits|אַמּ֔וֹת\rb*, \rb and the ledge one cubit|הָאַמָּֽה׃\rb* \rb wide|וְרֹ֖חַב\rb*.\f + \fr 43:14 \ft The space was to be approximately 7 feet (2.1 meters), and the ledge was to be approximately 1.75 feet wide (53.3 centimeters wide).\f*
\p \v 15 \rb The altar hearth|וְהַֽהַרְאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb shall be four|אַרְבַּ֣ע\rb* \rb cubits high|אַמּ֑וֹת\rb*, \rb and four|אַרְבַּֽע׃\rb* \rb horns|הַקְּרָנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb shall project upward|וּלְמַ֔עְלָה\rb* \rb from the hearth|וּמֵהָאֲרִאֵ֣יל\rb*. \v 16 \rb The altar hearth shall be|וְהָאֲרִאֵיל\rb* \rb square|רָב֕וּעַ\rb* \rb at|אֶ֖ל\rb* \rb its four|אַרְבַּ֥עַת\rb* \rb corners|רְבָעָֽיו׃\rb*, \rb twelve cubits|שְׁתֵּ֤ים\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵה֙\rb* \rb long|אֹ֔רֶךְ\rb* \rb and twelve cubits|בִּשְׁתֵּ֥ים\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֖ה\rb* \rb wide|רֹ֑חַב\rb*.\f + \fr 43:16 \fqa 12 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 21 feet or 6.4 meters.\f* \v 17 \rb The ledge|וְהָעֲזָרָ֞ה\rb* \rb shall also be square|אֶ֖ל\rb*\rb |אַרְבַּ֣עַת\rb*\rb |רְבָעֶ֑יהָ\rb*, \rb fourteen cubits|אַרְבַּ֧ע\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵ֣ה\rb* \rb long|אֹ֗רֶךְ\rb* \rb and fourteen cubits|בְּאַרְבַּ֤ע\rb*\rb |עֶשְׂרֵה֙\rb* \rb wide|רֹ֔חַב\rb*,\f + \fr 43:17 \fqa 14 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 24.5 feet or 7.5 meters.\f* \rb with a rim|וְהַגְּבוּל\rb* \rb of half|חֲצִ֣י\rb* \rb a cubit|הָאַמָּ֗ה\rb*\f + \fr 43:17 \fqa A half cubit \ft is approximately 10.5 inches or 26.7 centimeters.\f* \rb and a gutter|וְהַֽחֵיק־\rb* \rb of a cubit|אַמָּה֙\rb* \rb all around|סָבִ֨יב\rb* \rb it|אוֹתָ֜הּ\rb*\rb |סָבִ֔יב\rb*. \rb The steps of the altar|וּמַעֲלֹתֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb shall face|פְּנ֥וֹת\rb* \rb east|קָדִֽים׃\rb*.”
\p \v 18 \rb Then He said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֗י\rb*: “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָם֙\rb*, \rb this is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: ‘\rb These|אֵ֚לֶּה\rb* \rb are the statutes|חֻקּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb for the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb on the day|בְּי֖וֹם\rb* \rb it is constructed|הֵעָֽשׂוֹת֑וֹ\rb*, \rb so that burnt offerings|עוֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb may be sacrificed|לְהַעֲל֤וֹת\rb* \rb on it|עָלָיו֙\rb* \rb and blood|דָּֽם׃\rb* \rb may be splattered|וְלִזְרֹ֥ק\rb* \rb on it|עָלָ֖יו\rb*: \v 19 \rb You are to give|וְנָתַתָּ֣ה\rb* \rb a young|בֶּן־\rb* \rb bull|פַּ֥ר\rb* \rb from the herd|בָּקָ֖ר\rb* \rb as a sin offering|לְחַטָּֽאת׃\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Levitical|הַלְוִיִּ֡ם\rb* \rb priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֣ים\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb are of|הֵם֩\rb* \rb the family|מִזֶּ֨רַע\rb* \rb of Zadok|צָד֜וֹק\rb*, \rb who approach|הַקְּרֹבִ֣ים\rb* \rb Me|אֵלַ֗י\rb* \rb to minister before Me|לְשָֽׁרְתֵ֑נִי\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֛ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֖ה\rb*. \v 20 \rb You are to take|וְלָקַחְתָּ֣\rb* \rb some of its blood|מִדָּמ֗וֹ\rb* \rb and put it|וְנָ֨תַתָּ֜ה\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the four|אַרְבַּ֤ע\rb* \rb horns of the altar|קַרְנֹתָיו֙\rb*, \rb on|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the four|אַרְבַּע֙\rb* \rb corners|פִּנּ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the ledge|הָעֲזָרָ֔ה\rb*,\rb |וְאֶֽל־\rb* \rb and all around|סָבִ֑יב\rb* \rb the rim|הַגְּב֖וּל\rb*; \rb thus you will cleanse|וְחִטֵּאתָ֥\rb*\rb |אוֹת֖וֹ\rb* \rb the altar and make atonement for it|וְכִפַּרְתָּֽהוּ׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb Then you are to take away|וְלָ֣קַחְתָּ֔\rb*\rb |אֵ֖ת\rb* \rb the bull|הַפָּ֣ר\rb* \rb for the sin offering|הַֽחַטָּ֑את\rb* \rb and burn it|וּשְׂרָפוֹ֙\rb* \rb in the appointed part|בְּמִפְקַ֣ד\rb* \rb of the temple area|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb outside|מִח֖וּץ\rb* \rb the sanctuary|לַמִּקְדָּֽשׁ׃\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb On the second|הַשֵּׁנִ֔י\rb* \rb day|וּבַיּוֹם֙\rb* \rb you are to present|תַּקְרִ֛יב\rb* \rb an unblemished|תָּמִ֖ים\rb* \rb male goat|שְׂעִיר־\rb*\rb |עִזִּ֥ים\rb* \rb as a sin offering|לְחַטָּ֑את\rb*,\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb and the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb is to be cleansed|וְחִטְּאוּ֙\rb* \rb as it was|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb*\rb |חִטְּא֖וּ\rb* \rb with the bull|בַּפָּֽר׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb When you have finished|בְּכַלּוֹתְךָ֖\rb* \rb the purification|מֵֽחַטֵּ֑א\rb*, \rb you are to present|תַּקְרִיב֙\rb* \rb a young|בֶּן־\rb*,\rb |בָּקָ֣ר\rb* \rb unblemished|תָּמִ֔ים\rb* \rb bull|פַּ֣ר\rb* \rb and an unblemished|תָּמִֽים׃\rb* \rb ram|וְאַ֥יִל\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the flock|הַצֹּ֖אן\rb*. \v 24 \rb You must present them|וְהִקְרַבְתָּ֖ם\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*; \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֤ים\rb* \rb are to sprinkle|וְהִשְׁלִ֨יכוּ\rb* \rb salt|מֶ֔לַח\rb* \rb on them|עֲלֵיהֶם֙\rb* \rb and sacrifice|וְהֶעֱל֥וּ\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֛ם\rb* \rb as a burnt offering|עֹלָ֖ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb For seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb you are to provide|תַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb a male goat|שְׂעִיר־\rb* \rb daily|לַיּ֑וֹם\rb* \rb for a sin offering|חַטָּ֖את\rb*; \rb you are also to provide|יַעֲשֽׂוּ׃\rb* \rb a young bull|וּפַ֧ר\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb*\rb |בָּקָ֛ר\rb* \rb and a ram|וְאַ֥יִל\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the flock|הַצֹּ֖אן\rb*, \rb both unblemished|תְּמִימִ֥ים\rb*. \v 26 \rb For seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֗ים\rb* \rb the priests are to make atonement|יְכַפְּרוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֔חַ\rb* \rb and cleanse it|וְטִֽהֲר֖וּ\rb*;\rb |אֹת֑וֹ\rb* \rb so they shall consecrate|וּמִלְא֖וּ\rb* \rb it|יָדוֹ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 43:26 \ft Hebrew \fqa fill its hand\f* \v 27 \rb At the end|וִֽיכַלּ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb of these days|הַיָּמִ֑יםס\rb*,\rb |וְהָיָה֩\rb* \rb from the eighth|הַשְּׁמִינִ֜י\rb* \rb day|בַיּ֨וֹם\rb* \rb on|וָהָ֗לְאָה\rb*, \rb the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֤ים\rb* \rb are to present|יַעֲשׂ֨וּ\rb* \rb your burnt offerings|עוֹלֽוֹתֵיכֶם֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and peace offerings|שַׁלְמֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb the altar|הַמִּזְבֵּ֙חַ֙\rb*.\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb Then I will accept you|וְרָצִ֣אתִי\rb*,\rb |אֶתְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהֹוִֽה׃ס\rb*.’”
\c 44
\s1 The East Gate Assigned to the Prince
\p \v 1 \rb The man then brought me back|וַיָּ֣שֶׁב\rb*\rb |אֹתִ֗י\rb* \rb to|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb the outer|הַֽחִיצ֔וֹן\rb* \rb gate|שַׁ֤עַר\rb* \rb of the sanctuary|הַמִּקְדָּשׁ֙\rb* \rb that faced|הַפֹּנֶ֖ה\rb* \rb east|קָדִ֑ים\rb*, \rb but it|וְה֖וּא\rb* \rb was shut|סָגֽוּר׃\rb*. \v 2 \rb And the LORD|יְהוָ֗ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֜י\rb*, “\rb This|הַזֶּה֩\rb* \rb gate|הַשַּׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb is to remain|יִהְיֶ֜ה\rb* \rb shut|סָג֨וּר\rb*. \rb It shall not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb be opened|יִפָּתֵ֗חַ\rb*, \rb and no|לֹא־\rb* \rb man|וְאִישׁ֙\rb* \rb shall enter|יָ֣בֹא\rb* \rb through it|ב֔וֹ\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֛י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֥ה\rb*, \rb the God|אֱלֹהֵֽי־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb has entered|בָּ֣א\rb* \rb through it|ב֑וֹ\rb*. \rb Therefore it will remain|וְהָיָ֖ה\rb* \rb shut|סָגֽוּר׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb |אֶֽת־\rb* \rb Only the prince|הַנָּשִׂ֗יא\rb*\rb |נָ֥שִׂיא\rb* \rb himself|ה֛וּא\rb* \rb may sit|יֵֽשֶׁב־\rb* \rb inside the gateway|בּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb to eat|לֶאֱכָול־\rb*\rb |לֶ֖חֶם\rb* \rb in the presence of|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb He must enter|יָב֔וֹא\rb* \rb by way|מִדֶּ֨רֶךְ\rb* \rb of the portico|אֻלָ֤ם\rb* \rb of the gateway|הַשַּׁ֙עַר֙\rb* \rb and go out|יֵצֵֽא׃\rb* \rb the same way|וּמִדַּרְכּ֖וֹ\rb*.”
\p \v 4 \rb Then the man brought me|וַיְבִיאֵ֜נִי\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the front|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּיִת֒\rb* \rb by way|דֶּֽרֶךְ־\rb* \rb of the north|הַצָּפוֹן֮\rb* \rb gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb*. \rb I looked|וָאֵ֕רֶא\rb* \rb and saw|וְהִנֵּ֛ה\rb* \rb the glory|כְבוֹד־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb filling|מָלֵ֥א\rb* \rb His|יְהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb temple|בֵּ֣ית\rb*, \rb and I fell|וָאֶפֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb facedown|אֶל־\rb*\rb |פָּנָֽי׃\rb*. \v 5 \rb The LORD|יְהֹוָ֗ה\rb* \rb said|וַיֹּ֨אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֜י\rb*: “\rb Son|בֶּן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֡ם\rb*, \rb pay attention|שִׂ֣ים\rb*\rb |לִבְּךָ֩\rb*; \rb look carefully|וּרְאֵ֨ה\rb* \rb with your eyes|בְעֵינֶ֜יךָ\rb* \rb and listen closely|שְּׁמָ֗ע\rb*\rb |אֵ֣ת\rb* \rb with your ears|וּבְאָזְנֶ֣יךָ\rb* \rb to everything|כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I|אֲנִי֙\rb* \rb tell|מְדַבֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb you|אֹתָ֔ךְ\rb* \rb concerning all|לְכָל־\rb* \rb the statutes|חֻקּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb and|וּלְכָל־\rb* \rb laws|תּוֹרֹתוֹ\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּית־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*. \rb Take careful note|וְשַׂמְתָּ֤\rb*\rb |לִבְּךָ֙\rb* \rb of the entrance|לִמְב֣וֹא\rb* \rb to the temple|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb*, \rb along with all|בְּכֹ֖ל\rb* \rb the exits|מוֹצָאֵ֥י\rb* \rb of the sanctuary|הַמִּקְדָּֽשׁ׃\rb*.
\s1 Reproof of the Levites
\p \v 6 \rb Tell|וְאָמַרְתָּ֤\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the rebellious|מֶ֙רִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb* \rb that this is what|כֹּ֥ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֑ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֖ר\rb*: ‘\rb I have had enough|רַב־\rb* \rb of all|מִֽכָּל־\rb* \rb your abominations|תּוֹעֲבֽוֹתֵיכֶ֖ם\rb*, \rb O house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 7 \rb In addition|אֶ֖ל\rb* \rb to all|כָּל־\rb* \rb your other abominations|תּוֹעֲבוֹתֵיכֶֽם׃\rb*, \rb you brought in|בַּהֲבִיאֲכֶ֣ם\rb* \rb foreigners|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |נֵכָ֗ר\rb* \rb uncircumcised|עַרְלֵי־\rb* \rb in both heart|לֵב֙\rb*\rb |וְעַרְלֵ֣י\rb* \rb and flesh|בָשָׂ֔ר\rb* \rb to occupy|לִהְי֥וֹת\rb* \rb My sanctuary|בְּמִקְדָּשִׁ֖י\rb*; \rb you defiled|לְחַלְּל֣וֹ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My temple|בֵּיתִ֑י\rb* \rb when you offered|בְּהַקְרִֽיבְכֶ֤ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My food|לַחְמִי֙\rb*— \rb the fat|חֵ֣לֶב\rb* \rb and the blood|וָדָ֔ם\rb*; \rb you broke|וַיָּפֵ֙רוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My covenant|בְּרִיתִ֔י\rb*. \v 8 \rb And you have not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb kept|שְׁמַרְתֶּ֖ם\rb* \rb charge|מִשְׁמֶ֣רֶת\rb* \rb of My holy things|קָדָשָׁ֑י\rb*, \rb but have appointed|וַתְּשִׂימ֗וּן\rb* \rb others to keep|לְשֹׁמְרֵ֧י\rb* \rb charge|מִשְׁמַרְתִּ֛י\rb* \rb of My sanctuary|בְּמִקְדָּשִׁ֖י\rb* \rb for you|לָכֶֽם׃\rb*.’
\p \v 9 \rb This is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִה֒\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֮\rb*: \rb No|כָּל־\rb* \rb foreigner|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |נֵכָ֗ר\rb* \rb uncircumcised|עֶ֤רֶל\rb* \rb in heart|לֵב֙\rb*\rb |וְעֶ֣רֶל\rb* \rb and flesh|בָּשָׂ֔ר\rb*\rb |לֹ֥א\rb* \rb may enter|יָב֖וֹא\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb My sanctuary|מִקְדָּשִׁ֑י\rb* —\rb |לְכָל־\rb* \rb not even a foreigner|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |נֵכָ֔ר\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֕ר\rb* \rb lives among|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the Israelites|בְּנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Surely|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb* \rb the Levites|הַלְוִיִּ֗ם\rb* \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb wandered away|רָֽחֲקוּ֙\rb* \rb from Me|מֵֽעָלַ֔י\rb* \rb when Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb went astray|בִּתְע֤וֹת\rb*, \rb and who|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb wandered|תָּע֣וּ\rb* \rb away from Me|מֵֽעָלַ֔י\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb their idols|גִּלּֽוּלֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb will bear the consequences|וְנָשְׂא֖וּ\rb* \rb of their iniquity|עֲוֺנָֽם׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb Yet they shall be|וְהָי֤וּ\rb* \rb ministers|מְשָׁ֣רְתִ֔ים\rb* \rb in My sanctuary|בְמִקְדָּשִׁי֙\rb*, \rb having charge|פְּקֻדּוֹת֙\rb* \rb of|אֶל־\rb* \rb the gates|שַׁעֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb* \rb and ministering|וּֽמְשָׁרְתִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb there|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb*. \rb They|הֵ֠מָּה\rb* \rb shall slaughter|יִשְׁחֲט֨וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the burnt offerings|הָעֹלָ֤ה\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and other sacrifices|הַזֶּ֙בַח֙\rb* \rb for the people|לָעָ֔ם\rb*\rb |וְהֵ֛מָּה\rb* \rb and stand|יַעַמְד֥וּ\rb* \rb before them|לִפְנֵיהֶ֖ם\rb* \rb to minister to them|לְשָֽׁרְתָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Because|יַ֗עַן\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb they ministered|יְשָׁרְת֤וּ\rb*\rb |אוֹתָם֙\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb their idols|גִלּֽוּלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and became|וְהָי֥וּ\rb* \rb a stumbling block|לְמִכְשׁ֣וֹל\rb* \rb of iniquity|עָוֺ֑ן\rb* \rb to the house|לְבֵֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*, \rb therefore|עַל־\rb*\rb |כֵּן֩\rb* \rb I swore with an uplifted|נָשָׂ֨אתִי\rb* \rb hand|יָדִ֜י\rb* \rb concerning them|עֲלֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb that they would bear the consequences|וְנָשְׂא֖וּ\rb* \rb of their iniquity|עֲוֺנָֽם׃\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻם֙\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb*. \v 13 \rb They must not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb approach|יִגְּשׁ֤וּ\rb* \rb Me|אֵלַי֙\rb* \rb to serve Me as priests|לְכַהֵ֣ן\rb* \rb or come near|וְלָגֶ֙שֶׁת֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb of My holy things|קָ֣דָשַׁ֔י\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb or the most holy things|קָדְשֵׁ֖י\rb*\rb |הַקְּדָשִׁ֑ים\rb*. \rb They will bear|וְנָֽשְׂאוּ֙\rb* \rb the shame|כְּלִמָּתָ֔ם\rb* \rb of the abominations|וְתוֹעֲבוֹתָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb they have committed|עָשֽׂוּ׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb Yet I will appoint|וְנָתַתִּ֣י\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֔ם\rb* \rb to keep|שֹׁמְרֵ֖י\rb* \rb charge|מִשְׁמֶ֣רֶת\rb* \rb of all|לְכֹל֙\rb* \rb the work|עֲבֹ֣דָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb for the temple|הַבָּ֑יִת\rb* \rb and everything|וּלְכֹ֛ל\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb to be done|יֵעָשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb in it|בּֽוֹ׃פ\rb*.
\s1 The Duties of the Priests
\p \v 15 \rb But the Levitical|הַלְוִיִּ֜ם\rb* \rb priests|וְהַכֹּהֲנִ֨ים\rb*, \rb who are descended|בְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb from Zadok|צָד֗וֹק\rb* \rb and who|אֲשֶׁ֨ר\rb* \rb kept|שָׁמְר֜וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb charge|מִשְׁמֶ֤רֶת\rb* \rb of My sanctuary|מִקְדָּשִׁי֙\rb* \rb when the Israelites|בְּנֵֽי־\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb* \rb went astray|בִּתְע֤וֹת\rb* \rb from Me|מֵֽעָלַ֔י\rb*,\rb |הֵ֛מָּה\rb* \rb are to approach|יִקְרְב֥וּ\rb* \rb Me|אֵלַ֖י\rb* \rb to minister before Me|לְשָֽׁרְתֵ֑נִי\rb*. \rb They will stand|וְעָמְד֣וּ\rb* \rb before Me|לְפָנַ֗י\rb* \rb to offer|לְהַקְרִ֥יב\rb* \rb Me|לִי֙\rb* \rb fat|חֵ֣לֶב\rb* \rb and blood|וָדָ֔ם\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*. \v 16 \rb They alone|הֵ֜מָּה\rb* \rb shall enter|יָבֹ֣אוּ\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb My sanctuary|מִקְדָּשִׁ֗י\rb*\rb |וְהֵ֛מָּה\rb* \rb and draw near|יִקְרְב֥וּ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb My table|שֻׁלְחָנִ֖י\rb* \rb to minister before Me|לְשָׁרְתֵ֑נִי\rb*. \rb They will keep|וְשָׁמְר֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb My charge|מִשְׁמַרְתִּֽי׃\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb When they enter|בְּבוֹאָם֙\rb*\rb |אֶֽל־\rb* \rb the gates|שַׁעֲרֵי֙\rb* \rb of the inner|הַפְּנִימִ֔ית\rb* \rb court|הֶחָצֵ֣ר\rb*, \rb they are to wear|יִלְבָּ֑שׁוּ\rb* \rb linen|פִשְׁתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb garments|בִּגְדֵ֥י\rb*; \rb they must not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb wear|יַעֲלֶ֤ה\rb* \rb anything made of wool|צֶ֔מֶר\rb* \rb when they minister|בְּשָֽׁרְתָ֗ם\rb* \rb at the gates|בְּשַׁעֲרֵ֛י\rb* \rb of the inner|הַפְּנִימִ֖ית\rb* \rb court|הֶחָצֵ֥ר\rb* \rb or inside the temple|וָבָֽיְתָה׃\rb*. \v 18 \rb They are to wear linen|פִשְׁתִּים֙\rb*\rb |יִהְי֣וּ\rb* \rb turbans|פַּאֲרֵ֤י\rb* \rb on|עַל־\rb* \rb their heads|רֹאשָׁ֔ם\rb* \rb and linen|פִשְׁתִּ֔ים\rb*\rb |יִהְי֖וּ\rb* \rb undergarments|וּמִכְנְסֵ֣י\rb* \rb around|עַל־\rb* \rb their waists|מָתְנֵיהֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb They must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb wear|יַחְגְּר֖וּ\rb* \rb anything that makes them perspire|בַּיָּֽזַע׃\rb*.
\p \v 19 \rb When they go out|וּ֠בְצֵאתָם\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the outer|הַחִיצוֹנָ֜ה\rb* \rb court|הֶחָצֵ֨ר\rb*, \rb to|אֶל־\rb*\rb |הֶחָצֵ֣ר\rb*\rb |הַחִיצוֹנָה֮\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the people|הָעָם֒\rb*, \rb they are to take off|יִפְשְׁט֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the garments|בִּגְדֵיהֶ֗ם\rb* \rb in which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb they|הֵ֙מָּה֙\rb* \rb have ministered|מְשָׁרְתִ֣ם\rb*, \rb leave|וְהִנִּ֥יחוּ\rb* \rb them|אוֹתָ֖ם\rb* \rb in the holy|הַקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb chambers|בְּלִֽשְׁכֹ֣ת\rb*, \rb and dress|וְלָֽבְשׁוּ֙\rb* \rb in other|אֲחֵרִ֔ים\rb* \rb clothes|בְּגָדִ֣ים\rb* \rb so that they do not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb transmit holiness|יְקַדְּשׁ֥וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the people|הָעָ֖ם\rb* \rb with their garments|בְּבִגְדֵיהֶֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb They must not|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb shave|יְגַלֵּ֔חוּ\rb* \rb their heads|וְרֹאשָׁם֙\rb* \rb or let their hair|וּפֶ֖רַע\rb*\rb |לֹ֣א\rb* \rb grow long|יְשַׁלֵּ֑חוּ\rb*, \rb but must carefully trim|כָּס֥וֹם\rb*\rb |יִכְסְמ֖וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb their hair|רָאשֵׁיהֶֽם׃\rb*. \v 21 \rb No|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb priest|כֹּהֵ֑ן\rb* \rb may drink|יִשְׁתּ֖וּ\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb* \rb wine|וְיַ֥יִן\rb* \rb before he enters|בְּבוֹאָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the inner|הַפְּנִימִֽית׃\rb* \rb court|הֶחָצֵ֥ר\rb*. \v 22 \rb And they shall not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb marry|יִקְח֥וּ\rb*\rb |לְנָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb a widow|וְאַלְמָנָה֙\rb* \rb or a divorced woman|וּגְרוּשָׁ֔ה\rb*, \rb but|אִם־\rb* \rb must marry|יִקָּֽחוּ׃\rb* \rb a virgin|בְּתוּלֹ֗ת\rb* \rb of the descendants|מִזֶּ֙רַע֙\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*,\rb |וְהָֽאַלְמָנָה֙\rb* \rb or a widow|אַלְמָנָ֔ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb*\rb |תִּֽהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb of a priest|מִכֹּהֵ֖ן\rb*. \v 23 \rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb They are to teach|יוֹר֔וּ\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֣י\rb* \rb the difference between|בֵּ֥ין\rb* \rb the holy|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb and the common|לְחֹ֑ל\rb* \rb and show them how to discern|יוֹדִעֻֽם׃\rb* \rb between|וּבֵין־\rb* \rb the clean|לְטָה֖וֹר\rb* \rb and the unclean|טָמֵ֥א\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb In|וְעַל־\rb* \rb any dispute|רִ֗יב\rb*, \rb they|הֵ֚מָּה\rb* \rb shall officiate|יַעַמְד֣וּ\rb* \rb as judges|לִשְׁפֹּט\rb* \rb and judge|וְשָׁפְטֻהוּ\rb* \rb according to My ordinances|בְּמִשְׁפָּטַ֖י\rb*. \rb They must keep|יִשְׁמֹ֔רוּ\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb My laws|תּוֹרֹתַ֤י\rb* \rb and|וְאֶת־\rb* \rb statutes|חֻקֹּתַי֙\rb* \rb regarding all|בְּכָל־\rb* \rb My appointed feasts|מוֹעֲדַ֣י\rb*, \rb and they must keep My Sabbaths|שַׁבְּתוֹתַ֖י\rb* \rb holy|יְקַדֵּֽשׁוּ׃\rb*.
\p \v 25 \rb A priest must not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb defile himself|לְטָמְאָ֑ה\rb* \rb by going|יָב֖וֹא\rb* \rb near|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb a dead|מֵ֣ת\rb* \rb person|אָדָ֔ם\rb*. \rb However|כִּ֣י\rb*\rb |אִם־\rb*, \rb for a father|לְאָ֡ב\rb*, \rb a mother|וּ֠לְאֵם\rb*, \rb a son|וּלְבֵ֨ן\rb*, \rb a daughter|וּלְבַ֜ת\rb*, \rb a brother|לְאָ֗ח\rb*,\rb |אֲשֶֽׁר־\rb* \rb or an unmarried|לֹא־\rb*\rb |הָיְתָ֥ה\rb*\rb |לְאִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb sister|וּלְאָח֛וֹת\rb*, \rb he may do so|יִטַּמָּֽאוּ׃\rb*, \v 26 \rb and after|וְאַחֲרֵ֖י\rb* \rb he is cleansed|טָֽהֳרָת֑וֹ\rb*, \rb he must count|יִסְפְּרוּ־\rb* \rb off seven|שִׁבְעַ֥ת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb for himself|לֽוֹ׃\rb*. \v 27 \rb And on the day|וּבְיוֹם֩\rb* \rb he goes|בֹּא֨וֹ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the sanctuary|הַקֹּ֜דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the inner|הַפְּנִימִית֙\rb* \rb court|הֶחָצֵ֤ר\rb*, \rb to minister|לְשָׁרֵ֣ת\rb* \rb in the sanctuary|בַּקֹּ֔דֶשׁ\rb*, \rb he must present|יַקְרִ֖יב\rb* \rb his sin offering|חַטָּאת֑וֹ\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb In regard to|וְהָיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb their|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb inheritance|לְֽנַחֲלָ֔ה\rb*, \rb I am|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb their inheritance|נַֽחֲלָתָ֑ם\rb*. \rb You are to give|תִתְּנ֤וּ\rb* \rb them|לָהֶם֙\rb* \rb no|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb possession|וַאֲחֻזָּ֗ה\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*, \rb for I am|אֲנִ֖י\rb* \rb their possession|אֲחֻזָּתָֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 29 \rb They|הֵ֖מָּה\rb* \rb shall eat|יֹֽאכְל֑וּם\rb* \rb the grain offerings|הַמִּנְחָה֙\rb*, \rb the sin offerings|וְהַחַטָּ֣את\rb*, \rb and the guilt offerings|וְהָאָשָׁ֔ם\rb*. \rb Everything|וְכָל־\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb devoted|חֵ֥רֶם\rb* \rb to the LORD|יִהְיֶֽה׃\rb* \rb will belong to them|לָהֶ֥ם\rb*. \v 30 \rb The best|וְרֵאשִׁית֩\rb* \rb of all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the firstfruits|בִּכּ֨וּרֵי\rb*\rb |כֹ֜ל\rb* \rb and of every|וְכָל־\rb* \rb contribution|תְּר֣וּמַת\rb*\rb |כֹּ֗ל\rb* \rb from all|מִכֹּל֙\rb* \rb your offerings|תְּרוּמ֣וֹתֵיכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb will belong to|יִֽהְיֶ֑ה\rb* \rb the priests|לַכֹּהֲנִ֖ים\rb*. \rb You are to give|תִּתְּנ֣וּ\rb* \rb your first|וְרֵאשִׁ֤ית\rb* \rb batch of dough|עֲרִסֽוֹתֵיכֶם֙\rb* \rb to the priest|לַכֹּהֵ֔ן\rb*, \rb so that a blessing|בְּרָכָ֖ה\rb* \rb may rest|לְהָנִ֥יחַ\rb* \rb upon|אֶל־\rb* \rb your homes|בֵּיתֶֽךָ׃\rb*. \v 31 \rb The priests|הַכֹּהֲנִֽים׃פ\rb* \rb may not|לֹ֥א\rb* \rb eat|יֹאכְל֖וּ\rb* \rb any|כָּל־\rb* \rb bird|הָע֖וֹף\rb*\rb |וּמִן־\rb* \rb or animal|הַבְּהֵמָ֑ה\rb* \rb found dead|נְבֵלָה֙\rb* \rb or torn by wild beasts|וּטְרֵפָ֔ה\rb*\rb |מִן־\rb*.[’’]
\c 45
\s1 Consecration of the Land
\p \v 1 “\rb When you divide the land|הָאָ֜רֶץ\rb* \rb by lot|וּבְהַפִּֽילְכֶ֨ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb as an inheritance|בְּנַחֲלָ֗ה\rb*, \rb you are to set aside|תָּרִימוּ֩\rb* \rb a portion|תְרוּמָ֨ה\rb* \rb for the LORD|לַיהוָ֥ה׀\rb*, \rb a holy|קֹדֶשׁ֮\rb* \rb portion of|מִן־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָרֶץ֒\rb* \rb 25,000 cubits|חֲמִשָּׁ֨ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֙לֶף֙\rb*\rb |אֹ֔רֶךְ\rb* \rb long|אֹ֗רֶךְ\rb* \rb and 20,000 cubits|עֲשָׂ֣רָה\rb*\rb |אָ֑לֶף\rb* \rb wide|וְרֹ֖חַב\rb*.\f + \fr 45:1 \ft LXX; the holy portion was to be approximately 8.3 miles long and 6.6 miles wide (13.3 kilometers long and 10.7 kilometers wide). Hebrew \fqa 25,000 cubits long and 10,000 wide\ft . See also verses 3 and 5 and \ref Ezekiel 48:9|EZK 48:9\ref*.\f* \rb This|ה֥וּא\rb* \rb entire|בְכָל־\rb* \rb tract of land|גְּבוּלָ֖הּ\rb*\rb |סָבִֽיב׃\rb* \rb will be holy|קֹדֶשׁ־\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb Within this area|מִזֶּה֙\rb* \rb there is to be|יִהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb a section for|אֶל־\rb* \rb the sanctuary|הַקֹּ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb 500 cubits|חֲמֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֛וֹת\rb* \rb square|מְרֻבָּ֣ע\rb*,\f + \fr 45:2 \fqa 500 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 875 feet or 266.7 meters.\f* \rb with 50|וַחֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb* \rb cubits|אַמָּ֔ה\rb*\f + \fr 45:2 \fqa 50 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 87.5 feet or 26.7 meters.\f* \rb around it|סָבִ֑יב\rb* \rb for open land|מִגְרָ֥שׁ\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb From|וּמִן־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּאת֙\rb* \rb holy portion|הַמִּדָּ֤ה\rb*, \rb you are to measure off|תָּמ֔וֹד\rb* \rb a length|אֹ֗רֶךְ\rb* \rb of 25,000 cubits|חֲמֵשׁ\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶ֔לֶף\rb* \rb and a width|וְרֹ֖חַב\rb* \rb of 10,000 cubits|עֲשֶׂ֣רֶת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֑ים\rb*,\f + \fr 45:3 \ft The portion was to be approximately 8.3 miles long and 3.3 miles wide (13.3 kilometers long and 5.3 kilometers wide); similarly in verse 5.\f* \rb and in it|וּבֽוֹ־\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb the sanctuary|הַמִּקְדָּ֖שׁ\rb*, \rb the Most|קָדָשִֽׁים׃\rb* \rb Holy Place|קֹ֥דֶשׁ\rb*.\f + \fr 45:3 \ft Or \fqa the Holy of Holies\f* \v 4 \rb It will be|יִֽהְיֶ֔ה\rb* \rb a holy portion|קֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb the land|הָאָ֜רֶץ\rb*\rb |ה֗וּא\rb* \rb to be used by the priests|לַכֹּ֨הֲנִ֜ים\rb* \rb who minister|מְשָׁרְתֵ֤י\rb* \rb in the sanctuary|הַמִּקְדָּשׁ֙\rb*, \rb who draw near|הַקְּרֵבִ֖ים\rb* \rb to minister before|לְשָׁרֵ֣ת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָ֑ה\rb*. \rb It will be|וְהָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb a place|מָקוֹם֙\rb* \rb for their|לָהֶ֤ם\rb* \rb houses|לְבָ֣תִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb as well as a holy area|וּמִקְדָּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb for the sanctuary|לַמִּקְדָּֽשׁ׃\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb An adjacent area 25,000 cubits|וַחֲמִשָּׁ֨ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֙לֶף֙\rb* \rb long|אֹ֔רֶךְ\rb* \rb and 10,000 cubits|וַעֲשֶׂ֥רֶת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb* \rb wide|רֹ֑חַב\rb* \rb shall belong|יִהְיֶה\rb* \rb to the Levites|לַלְוִיִּם֩\rb* \rb who minister|מְשָׁרְתֵ֨י\rb* \rb in the temple|הַבַּ֧יִת\rb*;\rb |לָהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb it will be their possession|לַאֲחֻזָּ֖ה\rb* \rb for towns in which to live|עֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |לְשָׁכֹֽת׃\rb*.\f + \fr 45:5 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa their possession, twenty chambers\f*
\p \v 6 \rb As the property|וַאֲחֻזַּ֨ת\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֜יר\rb*, \rb you are to set aside|תִּתְּנ֗וּ\rb* \rb an area 5,000 cubits|חֲמֵ֤שֶׁת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִים֙\rb* \rb wide|רֹ֔חַב\rb* \rb and 25,000 cubits|חֲמִשָּׁ֤ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶ֔לֶף\rb* \rb long|וְאֹ֗רֶךְ\rb*,\f + \fr 45:6 \ft The property of the city was to be approximately 1.7 miles wide and 8.3 miles long (2.7 kilometers wide and 13.3 kilometers long).\f* \rb adjacent to|לְעֻמַּ֖ת\rb* \rb the holy|הַקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb* \rb district|תְּרוּמַ֣ת\rb*. \rb It will belong to|יִהְיֶֽה׃\rb* \rb the whole|לְכָל־\rb* \rb house|בֵּ֥ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb*.
\s1 The Prince’s Portion
\p \v 7 \rb Now the prince|וְלַנָּשִׂ֡יא\rb* \rb will have the area|מִזֶּ֣ה\rb* \rb bordering|פְּנֵ֤י\rb* \rb each side of the area formed by|וּמִזֶּה֩\rb*\rb |לִתְרוּמַ֨ת\rb*\rb |וְלַאֲחֻזַּ֣ת\rb*\rb |הָעִ֗יר\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the holy|הַקֹּ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb* \rb district|תְרֽוּמַת־\rb*\rb |וְאֶל־\rb*\rb |פְּנֵי֙\rb* \rb and the property|אֲחֻזַּ֣ת\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb*, \rb extending westward|יָ֣ם\rb* \rb from the western|יָ֔מָּה\rb* \rb side|מִפְּאַת־\rb* \rb and eastward|קָדִ֑ימָה\rb* \rb from the eastern|קֵ֖דְמָה\rb* \rb side|וּמִפְּאַת־\rb*, \rb running lengthwise|וְאֹ֗רֶךְ\rb* \rb from the western|יָ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb boundary|מִגְּב֥וּל\rb* \rb to the eastern|קָדִֽימָה׃\rb* \rb boundary|גְּב֥וּל\rb* \rb and parallel to|לְעֻמּוֹת֙\rb* \rb one|אַחַ֣ד\rb* \rb of the tribal portions|הַחֲלָקִ֔ים\rb*. \v 8 \rb This land|לָאָ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb will be|יִֽהְיֶה־\rb* \rb his|לּ֥וֹ\rb* \rb possession|לַֽאֲחֻזָּ֖ה\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*.
\p \rb And My princes|נְשִׂיאַי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will no|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb longer|ע֤וֹד\rb* \rb oppress|יוֹנ֨וּ\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֔י\rb*, \rb but will give|יִתְּנ֥וּ\rb* \rb the rest of the land|וְהָאָ֛רֶץ\rb* \rb to the house|לְבֵֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֖ל\rb* \rb according to their tribes|לְשִׁבְטֵיהֶֽם׃ס\rb*. \v 9 \rb For this is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֞ר\rb*: ‘\rb Enough|רַב־\rb*, \rb O princes|נְשִׂיאֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*! \rb Cease|הָסִ֔ירוּ\rb* \rb your violence|חָמָ֤ס\rb* \rb and oppression|וָשֹׁד֙\rb*, \rb and do|עֲשׂ֑וּ\rb* \rb what is just|וּמִשְׁפָּ֥ט\rb* \rb and right|וּצְדָקָ֖ה\rb*. \rb Stop|הָרִ֤ימוּ\rb* \rb dispossessing|גְרֻשֹֽׁתֵיכֶם֙\rb*\rb |מֵעַ֣ל\rb* \rb My people|עַמִּ֔י\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*.’
\s1 Honest Scales
\r (\ref Deuteronomy 25:13–16|DEU 25:13-16\ref*; \ref Proverbs 11:1–3|PRO 11:1-3\ref*)
\p \v 10 \rb You must use|יְהִ֥י\rb* \rb honest|צֶ֧דֶק\rb* \rb scales|מֹֽאזְנֵי־\rb*, \rb a just|צֶ֛דֶק\rb* \rb ephah|וְאֵֽיפַת־\rb*,\f + \fr 45:10 \fqa An ephah \ft is a dry measure of approximately 20 dry quarts or 22 liters.\f* \rb and a just|צֶ֖דֶק\rb* \rb bath|וּבַת־\rb*.\f + \fr 45:10 \fqa A bath \ft was a liquid measure of approximately 5.8 gallons or 22 liters.\f*
\p \v 11 \rb The ephah|הָאֵיפָ֣ה\rb* \rb and the bath|וְהַבַּ֗ת\rb* \rb shall be|יִֽהְיֶ֔ה\rb* \rb the same|אֶחָד֙\rb* \rb quantity|תֹּ֤כֶן\rb* \rb so that the bath|הַבָּ֑ת\rb* \rb will contain|לָשֵׂ֕את\rb* \rb a tenth|מַעְשַׂ֥ר\rb* \rb of a homer|הַחֹ֖מֶר\rb*, \rb and the ephah|הָֽאֵיפָ֔ה\rb* \rb a tenth|וַעֲשִׂירִ֤ת\rb* \rb of a homer|הַחֹ֙מֶר֙\rb*;\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb the homer|הַחֹ֖מֶר\rb* \rb will be|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb the standard measure for both|מַתְכֻּנְתּֽוֹ׃\rb*.\f + \fr 45:11 \fqa A homer \ft was a dry measure of approximately 6.24 bushels or 220 liters; also in verses 13 and 14.\f*
\p \v 12 \rb The shekel|וְהַשֶּׁ֖קֶל\rb* \rb will consist of twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb* \rb gerahs|גֵּרָ֑ה\rb*.\f + \fr 45:12 \fqa 20 gerahs \ft is equivalent to one shekel (approximately 0.4 ounces or 11.4 grams).\f* \rb Twenty|עֶשְׂרִ֨ים\rb* \rb shekels|שְׁקָלִ֜ים\rb* \rb plus twenty-five|וְעֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |חֲמִשָּׁ֧ה\rb* \rb shekels|שְׁקָלִ֗ים\rb* \rb plus fifteen|עֲשָׂרָ֤ה\rb*\rb |וַחֲמִשָּׁה֙\rb* \rb shekels|שֶׁ֔קֶל\rb* \rb will equal|יִֽהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb one mina|הַמָּנֶ֖ה\rb*.\f + \fr 45:12 \ft That is, 60 shekels total; elsewhere, the common mina was 50 shekels. Sixty shekels weighed approximately 1.5 pounds or 683.8 grams.\f*
\s1 Offerings and Feasts
\p \v 13 \rb This|זֹ֥את\rb* \rb is the contribution|הַתְּרוּמָ֖ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you are to offer|תָּרִ֑ימוּ\rb*: \rb a sixth|שִׁשִּׁ֤ית\rb* \rb of an ephah|הָֽאֵיפָה֙\rb* \rb from each homer|מֵחֹ֣מֶר\rb* \rb of wheat|הַֽחִטִּ֔ים\rb*, \rb and a sixth|וְשִׁשִּׁיתֶם֙\rb* \rb of an ephah|הָֽאֵיפָ֔ה\rb* \rb from each homer|מֵחֹ֖מֶר\rb* \rb of barley|הַשְּׂעֹרִֽים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 45:13 \ft That is, a sixtieth of the harvest of wheat and of barley; \fqa a sixth of an ephah \ft was approximately 3.3 dry quarts or 3.7 liters.\f* \v 14 \rb The prescribed portion|וְחֹ֨ק\rb* \rb of oil|הַשֶּׁ֜מֶן\rb*, \rb measured by the bath|הַבַּ֣ת\rb*\rb |הַשֶּׁ֗מֶן\rb*, \rb is a tenth|מַעְשַׂ֤ר\rb* \rb of a bath|הַבַּת֙\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb each cor|הַכֹּ֔ר\rb*\f + \fr 45:14 \ft That is, one percent of one’s oil; \fqa a tenth of a bath \ft was approximately 2.3 quarts or 2.2 liters.\f* (\rb a cor consists of ten|עֲשֶׂ֥רֶת\rb* \rb baths|הַבַּתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb or one homer|חֹ֑מֶר\rb*, \rb since|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb ten|עֲשֶׂ֥רֶת\rb* \rb baths|הַבַּתִּ֖ים\rb* \rb are equivalent to a homer|חֹֽמֶר׃\rb*). \v 15 \rb And|מִן־\rb* \rb one|אַחַ֨ת\rb* \rb sheep shall be given|וְשֶׂה־\rb* \rb from each flock|הַצֹּ֤אן\rb* \rb of|מִן־\rb* \rb two hundred|הַמָּאתַ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb from the well-watered pastures|מִמַּשְׁקֵ֣ה\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*. \rb These are for the grain offerings|לְמִנְחָ֖ה\rb*, \rb burnt offerings|וּלְעוֹלָ֣ה\rb*, \rb and peace offerings|וְלִשְׁלָמִ֑ים\rb*, \rb to make atonement|לְכַפֵּ֣ר\rb* \rb for the people|עֲלֵיהֶ֔ם\rb*, \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 16 \rb All|כֹּ֚ל\rb* \rb the people|הָעָ֣ם\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb must participate|יִהְי֖וּ\rb* \rb in|אֶל־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֑את\rb* \rb contribution|הַתְּרוּמָ֣ה\rb* \rb for the prince|לַנָּשִׂ֖יא\rb* \rb in Israel|בְּיִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb And|וְעַֽל־\rb* \rb it shall be|יִהְיֶ֗ה\rb* \rb the prince’s part|הַנָּשִׂ֣יא\rb* \rb to provide the burnt offerings|הָעוֹל֣וֹת\rb*, \rb grain offerings|וְהַמִּנְחָה֮\rb*, \rb and drink offerings|וְהַנֵּסֶךְ֒\rb* \rb for the feasts|בַּחַגִּ֤ים\rb*, \rb New Moons|וּבֶחֳדָשִׁים֙\rb*, \rb and Sabbaths|וּבַשַּׁבָּת֔וֹת\rb*— \rb for all|בְּכָֽל־\rb* \rb the appointed feasts|מוֹעֲדֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the house|בֵּ֣ית\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*. \rb He|הֽוּא־\rb* \rb will provide|יַעֲשֶׂ֞ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sin offerings|הַחַטָּ֣את\rb*,\f + \fr 45:17 \ft Or \fqa purification offerings\ft ; also in verses 19, 22, 23, and 25\f*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb grain offerings|הַמִּנְחָ֗ה\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb burnt offerings|הָֽעוֹלָה֙\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and peace offerings|הַשְּׁלָמִ֔ים\rb* \rb to make atonement|לְכַפֵּ֖ר\rb* \rb for|בְּעַ֥ד\rb* \rb the house|בֵּֽית־\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb This is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִה֒\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֮\rb*: ‘\rb On the first day|בְּאֶחָ֣ד\rb*\rb |לַחֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the first month|בָּֽרִאשׁוֹן֙\rb* \rb you are to take|תִּקַּ֥ח\rb* \rb a young bull|פַּר־\rb*\rb |בֶּן־\rb*\rb |בָּקָ֖ר\rb* \rb without blemish|תָּמִ֑ים\rb* \rb and purify|וְחִטֵּאתָ֖\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the sanctuary|הַמִּקְדָּֽשׁ׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb And the priest|הַכֹּהֵ֜ן\rb* \rb is to take|וְלָקַ֨ח\rb* \rb some of the blood|מִדַּ֣ם\rb* \rb from the sin offering|הַחַטָּ֗את\rb* \rb and put it|וְנָתַן֙\rb* \rb on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the doorposts|מְזוּזַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֔יִת\rb*, \rb on|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the four|אַרְבַּ֛ע\rb* \rb corners|פִּנּ֥וֹת\rb* \rb of the ledge|הָעֲזָרָ֖ה\rb* \rb of the altar|לַמִּזְבֵּ֑חַ\rb*, \rb and on|וְעַ֨ל־\rb* \rb the gateposts|מְזוּזַ֔ת\rb*\rb |שַׁ֖עַר\rb* \rb of the inner|הַפְּנִימִֽית׃\rb* \rb court|הֶחָצֵ֥ר\rb*. \v 20 \rb You must do|תַּֽעֲשֶׂה֙\rb* \rb the same thing|וְכֵ֤ן\rb* \rb on the seventh|בְּשִׁבְעָ֣ה\rb* \rb day of the month|בַחֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb for anyone|מֵאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb who strays unintentionally|שֹׁגֶ֖ה\rb* \rb or in ignorance|וּמִפֶּ֑תִי\rb*. \rb In this way you will make atonement|וְכִפַּרְתֶּ֖ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for the temple|הַבָּֽיִת׃\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb On the fourteenth|בְּאַרְבָּעָ֨ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֥ר\rb* \rb day|יוֹם֙\rb*\rb |לַחֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb of the first month|בָּ֠רִאשׁוֹן\rb* \rb you are to observe|יִהְיֶ֥ה\rb* \rb the Passover|הַפָּ֑סַח\rb*, \rb a feast|חָ֕ג\rb* \rb of seven|שְׁבֻע֣וֹת\rb* \rb days|יָמִ֔ים\rb*, \rb during which unleavened bread|מַצּ֖וֹת\rb* \rb shall be eaten|יֵאָכֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb On that|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb day|בַּיּ֣וֹם\rb* \rb the prince|הַנָּשִׂיא֙\rb* \rb shall provide|וְעָשָׂ֤ה\rb* \rb a bull|פַּ֖ר\rb* \rb as a sin offering|חַטָּֽאת׃\rb* \rb for himself|בַּעֲד֕וֹ\rb* \rb and for|וּבְעַ֖ד\rb* \rb all|כָּל־\rb* \rb the people|עַ֣ם\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*. \v 23 \rb Each day|לַיּֽוֹם׃\rb* \rb during the seven|וְשִׁבְעַ֨ת\rb* \rb days|יְמֵֽי־\rb* \rb of the feast|הֶחָ֜ג\rb*, \rb he shall provide|יַעֲשֶׂ֧ה\rb* \rb seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb bulls|פָּ֠רִים\rb* \rb and seven|וְשִׁבְעַ֨ת\rb* \rb rams|אֵילִ֤ים\rb* \rb without blemish|תְּמִימִם֙\rb* \rb as a burnt offering|עוֹלָ֣ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֗ה\rb*\rb |לַיּ֔וֹם\rb*\rb |שִׁבְעַ֖ת\rb*\rb |הַיָּמִ֑ים\rb*, \rb along with a male goat|שְׂעִ֥יר\rb*\rb |עִזִּ֖ים\rb* \rb for a sin offering|וְחַטָּ֕את\rb*. \v 24 \rb He shall also provide|יַֽעֲשֶׂ֑ה\rb* \rb as a grain offering|וּמִנְחָ֗ה\rb* \rb an ephah|אֵיפָ֥ה\rb* \rb for each bull|לַפָּ֛ר\rb* \rb and an ephah|וְאֵיפָ֥ה\rb* \rb for each ram|לָאַ֖יִל\rb*, \rb along with a hin|הִ֥ין\rb* \rb of olive oil|וְשֶׁ֖מֶן\rb* \rb for each ephah of grain|לָאֵיפָֽה׃\rb*.\f + \fr 45:24 \ft Literally \fqa a hin of oil for each ephah\ft ; that is, approximately 0.97 gallons or 3.67 liters of oil for each ephah of grain\f* \v 25 \rb During the seven|שִׁבְעַ֣ת\rb* \rb days|הַיָּמִ֑ים\rb* \rb of the feast|בֶּחָ֔ג\rb* \rb that begins on the fifteenth|בַּחֲמִשָּׁה֩\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֨ר\rb* \rb day|י֤וֹם\rb* \rb of the seventh|בַּשְּׁבִיעִ֡י\rb* \rb month|לַחֹ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb*,\f + \fr 45:25 \ft That is, Sukkot, the autumn feast of pilgrimage to Jerusalem; also translated as \fqa the Feast of Booths \ft or \fqa the Feast of Shelters \ft and originally called \fqa the Feast of Ingathering\ft (see \ref Exodus 23:16|EXO 23:16\ref* and Exodus 34:22).\f* \rb he is to make the same provision|יַעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |כָאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb for sin offerings|כַּֽחַטָּאת֙\rb*, \rb burnt offerings|כָּעֹלָ֔ה\rb*, \rb grain offerings|וְכַמִּנְחָ֖ה\rb*, \rb and oil|וְכַשָּֽׁמֶן׃ס\rb*.’[’’]
\c 46
\s1 The Prince’s Offerings
\p \v 1 “\rb This is what|כֹּֽה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִה֒\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֮\rb*: ‘\rb The gate|שַׁ֜עַר\rb* \rb of the inner|הַפְּנִימִית֙\rb* \rb court|הֶחָצֵ֤ר\rb* \rb that faces|הַפֹּנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb east|קָדִ֔ים\rb* \rb must be|יִהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb kept shut|סָג֔וּר\rb* \rb during the six|שֵׁ֖שֶׁת\rb* \rb days|יְמֵ֣י\rb* \rb of work|הַֽמַּעֲשֶׂ֑ה\rb*, \rb but on the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּת֙\rb* \rb day|וּבְי֤וֹם\rb* \rb and|יִפָּתֵֽחַ׃\rb* \rb on the day|וּבְי֥וֹם\rb* \rb of the New Moon|הַחֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb it shall be opened|יִפָּתֵ֔חַ\rb*. \v 2 \rb The prince|הַנָּשִׂ֡יא\rb* \rb is to enter|וּבָ֣א\rb* \rb from the outside|מִח֗וּץ\rb* \rb through|דֶּרֶךְ֩\rb* \rb the portico|אוּלָ֨ם\rb* \rb of the gateway|הַשַּׁ֜עַר\rb* \rb and stand|וְעָמַד֙\rb* \rb by|עַל־\rb* \rb the gatepost|מְזוּזַ֣ת\rb*\rb |הַשַּׁ֔עַר\rb*, \rb while the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֗ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb sacrifice|וְעָשׂ֣וּ\rb* \rb his burnt offerings|עֽוֹלָתוֹ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and peace offerings|שְׁלָמָ֔יו\rb*. \rb He is to bow in worship|וְהִֽשְׁתַּחֲוָ֛ה\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the threshold|מִפְתַּ֥ן\rb* \rb of the gate|הַשַּׁ֖עַר\rb* \rb and then depart|וְיָצָ֑א\rb*, \rb but the gate|וְהַשַּׁ֥עַר\rb* \rb must not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb be shut|יִסָּגֵ֖ר\rb* \rb until|עַד־\rb* \rb evening|הָעָֽרֶב׃\rb*. \v 3 \rb On the Sabbaths|בַּשַּׁבָּת֖וֹת\rb* \rb and New Moons|וּבֶחֳדָשִׁ֑ים\rb* \rb the people|עַם־\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֗רֶץ\rb* \rb are also to bow in worship|וְהִשְׁתַּחֲו֣וּ\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֖י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָֽה׃\rb* \rb at the entrance|פֶּ֚תַח\rb* \rb to that|הַה֔וּא\rb* \rb gateway|הַשַּׁ֣עַר\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb The burnt offering|וְהָ֣עֹלָ֔ה\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the prince|הַנָּשִׂ֖יא\rb* \rb presents|יַקְרִ֥ב\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb on the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּ֗ת\rb* \rb day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb* \rb shall be six|שִׁשָּׁ֧ה\rb* \rb unblemished|תְּמִימִ֖ם\rb* \rb male lambs|כְבָשִׂ֛ים\rb* \rb and an unblemished|תָּמִֽים׃\rb* \rb ram|וְאַ֥יִל\rb*. \v 5 \rb The grain offering|וּמִנְחָה֙\rb* \rb with the ram|לָאַ֔יִל\rb* \rb shall be one ephah|אֵיפָ֣ה\rb*,\f + \fr 46:5 \fqa An ephah \ft is approximately 20 dry quarts or 22 liters (probably about 38.3 pounds or 17.4 kilograms of grain); also in verses 7 and 11.\f* \rb and the grain offering|מִנְחָ֖ה\rb* \rb with the lambs|וְלַכְּבָשִׂ֥ים\rb* \rb shall be|מַתַּ֣ת\rb* \rb as much as he is able|יָד֑וֹ\rb*, \rb along with a hin|הִ֥ין\rb* \rb of oil|וְשֶׁ֖מֶן\rb* \rb per ephah|לָאֵיפָֽה׃\rb*. \v 6 \rb On the day|וּבְי֣וֹם\rb* \rb of the New Moon|הַחֹ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb he shall offer|יִהְיֽוּ׃\rb* \rb a young|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |בָּקָ֖ר\rb*, \rb unblemished|תְּמִימִ֑ם\rb* \rb bull|פַּ֥ר\rb*, \rb six|וְשֵׁ֧שֶׁת\rb* \rb lambs|כְּבָשִׂ֛ם\rb*, \rb and a ram|וָאַ֖יִל\rb* \rb without blemish|תְּמִימִ֥ם\rb*. \v 7 \rb He is to provide|יַעֲשֶׂ֣ה\rb* \rb a grain offering|מִנְחָ֔ה\rb* \rb of an ephah|וְאֵיפָ֨ה\rb* \rb with the bull|לַפָּ֜ר\rb*, \rb an ephah|וְאֵיפָ֤ה\rb* \rb with the ram|לָאַ֙יִל֙\rb*, \rb and as much|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb as he is able|תַּשִּׂ֖יג\rb*\rb |יָד֑וֹ\rb* \rb with the lambs|וְלַ֨כְּבָשִׂ֔ים\rb*, \rb along with a hin|הִ֥ין\rb* \rb of oil|וְשֶׁ֖מֶן\rb* \rb per ephah|לָאֵיפָֽה׃\rb*. \v 8 \rb When the prince|הַנָּשִׂ֑יא\rb* \rb enters|וּבְב֖וֹא\rb*, \rb he shall go in|יָב֔וֹא\rb* \rb through|דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb the portico|אוּלָ֤ם\rb* \rb of the gateway|הַשַּׁ֙עַר֙\rb*, \rb and he shall go out|יֵצֵֽא׃\rb* \rb the same way|וּבְדַרְכּ֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb When the people|עַם־\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֜רֶץ\rb* \rb come|וּבְב֨וֹא\rb* \rb before|לִפְנֵ֣י\rb* \rb the LORD|יְהוָה֮\rb* \rb at the appointed feasts|בַּמּֽוֹעֲדִים֒\rb*, \rb whoever enters|הַבָּ֡א\rb* \rb by|דֶּרֶךְ־\rb* \rb the north|צָפ֜וֹן\rb* \rb gate|שַׁ֨עַר\rb* \rb to worship|לְהִֽשְׁתַּחֲוֺ֗ת\rb* \rb must go out|יֵצֵא֙\rb* \rb by|דֶּרֶךְ־\rb* \rb the south|נֶ֔גֶב\rb* \rb gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb*, \rb and whoever enters|וְהַבָּא֙\rb* \rb by|דֶּרֶךְ־\rb* \rb the south|נֶ֔גֶב\rb* \rb gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb must go out|יֵצֵ֖א\rb* \rb by|דֶּרֶךְ־\rb* \rb the north|צָפ֑וֹנָה\rb* \rb gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb*. \rb No one|לֹ֣א\rb* \rb is to return|יָשׁ֗וּב\rb* \rb through|דֶּ֤רֶךְ\rb* \rb the gate|הַשַּׁ֙עַר֙\rb* \rb by which|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb he entered|בָּ֣א\rb*\rb |ב֔וֹ\rb*, \rb but|כִּ֥י\rb* \rb each must go out|יֵצְאוּ׃\rb* \rb by the opposite gate|נִכְח֖וֹ\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb When the people enter|בְּבוֹאָם֙\rb*, \rb the prince|וְֽהַנָּשִׂ֑יא\rb* \rb shall go in|יָב֔וֹא\rb* \rb with them|בְּתוֹכָ֤ם\rb*, \rb and when they leave|וּבְצֵאתָ֖ם\rb*, \rb he shall leave|יֵצֵֽאוּ׃\rb*. \v 11 \rb At the festivals|וּבַחַגִּ֣ים\rb* \rb and appointed feasts|וּבַמּוֹעֲדִ֗ים\rb*, \rb the grain offering|הַמִּנְחָה֙\rb* \rb shall be|תִּהְיֶ֤ה\rb* \rb an ephah|אֵיפָ֤ה\rb* \rb with a bull|לַפָּר֙\rb*, \rb an ephah|וְאֵיפָ֣ה\rb* \rb with a ram|לָאַ֔יִל\rb*, \rb and as much as one is able|יָד֑וֹ\rb* \rb to give|מַתַּ֣ת\rb* \rb with the lambs|וְלַכְּבָשִׂ֖ים\rb*, \rb along with a hin|הִ֥ין\rb* \rb of oil|וְשֶׁ֖מֶן\rb* \rb per ephah|לָאֵיפָֽה׃ס\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb When|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb the prince|הַנָּשִׂ֨יא\rb* \rb makes|יַעֲשֶׂה֩\rb* \rb a freewill offering|נְדָבָ֜ה\rb*\rb |נְדָבָ֣ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָה֒\rb*, \rb whether a burnt offering|עוֹלָ֣ה\rb* \rb or|אֽוֹ־\rb* \rb a peace offering|שְׁלָמִים֮\rb*, \rb the gate|הַשַּׁ֙עַר֙\rb* \rb facing|הַפֹּנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb east|קָדִ֔ים\rb* \rb must be opened|וּפָ֣תַֽח\rb* \rb for him|ל֗וֹ\rb*.\rb |אֶת\rb* \rb He is to offer|וְעָשָׂ֤ה\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb his burnt offering|עֹֽלָתוֹ֙\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb or peace offering|שְׁלָמָ֔יו\rb* \rb just as|כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb he does|יַעֲשֶׂ֖ה\rb* \rb on the Sabbath|הַשַּׁבָּ֑ת\rb* \rb day|בְּי֣וֹם\rb*. \rb Then he shall go out|וְיָצָ֛א\rb*, \rb and the gate|הַשַּׁ֖עַר\rb* \rb must be closed|וְסָגַ֥ר\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb after|אַחֲרֵ֥י\rb* \rb he goes out|צֵאתֽוֹ׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb And you shall provide|תַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb* \rb an unblemished|תָּמִ֗ים\rb* \rb year-old|בֶּן־\rb*\rb |שְׁנָת֜וֹ\rb* \rb lamb|וְכֶ֨בֶשׂ\rb* \rb as a daily|לַיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb burnt offering|עוֹלָ֛ה\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהֹוָ֑ה\rb*; \rb you are to offer it|תַּעֲשֶׂ֥ה\rb*\rb |אֹתֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb every morning|בַּבֹּ֥קֶר\rb*\rb |בַּבֹּ֖קֶר\rb*. \v 14 \rb You are also to provide|תַעֲשֶׂ֨ה\rb* \rb with it|עָלָ֜יו\rb* \rb every morning|בַּבֹּ֤קֶר\rb* \rb a grain offering|וּמִנְחָה֩\rb*\rb |בַּבֹּ֙קֶר֙\rb* \rb of a sixth|שִׁשִּׁ֣ית\rb* \rb of an ephah|הָֽאֵיפָ֔ה\rb*\f + \fr 46:14 \fqa A sixth of an ephah \ft is approximately 3.3 dry quarts or 3.7 liters (probably about 4.2 pounds or 1.9 kilograms of flour).\f* \rb with a third|שְׁלִישִׁ֥ית\rb* \rb of a hin|הַהִ֖ין\rb* \rb of oil|וְשֶׁ֛מֶן\rb*\f + \fr 46:14 \ft Or \fqa a third of a hin of olive oil\ft ; that is, approximately 1.3 quarts or 1.2 liters\f* \rb to moisten|לָרֹ֣ס\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the fine flour|הַסֹּ֑לֶת\rb*— \rb a grain offering|מִנְחָה֙\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֔ה\rb*. \rb This is a permanent|עוֹלָ֖ם\rb*\rb |תָּמִֽיד׃\rb* \rb statute|חֻקּ֥וֹת\rb*. \v 15 \rb Thus they shall provide|וְעָשׂוּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the lamb|הַכֶּ֧בֶשׂ\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb the grain offering|הַמִּנְחָ֛ה\rb*,\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the oil|הַשֶּׁ֖מֶן\rb* \rb every morning|בַּבֹּ֣קֶר\rb*\rb |בַּבֹּ֑קֶר\rb* \rb as a regular|תָּמִֽיד׃פ\rb* \rb burnt offering|עוֹלַ֖ת\rb*.’
\p \v 16 \rb This is what|כֹּה־\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהֹוִ֗ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַ֞ר\rb*: ‘\rb If|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the prince|הַנָּשִׂ֤יא\rb* \rb gives|יִתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb a gift|מַתָּנָה֙\rb* \rb to any|לְאִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb of his sons|מִבָּנָ֔יו\rb* \rb as an inheritance|נַחֲלָת֥וֹ\rb*, \rb it|הִ֖יא\rb* \rb will belong to his descendants|לְבָנָ֣יו\rb*. \rb It will become|תִּֽהְיֶ֑ה\rb* \rb their property|אֲחֻזָּתָ֥ם\rb*\rb |הִ֖יא\rb* \rb by inheritance|בְּנַחֲלָֽה׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb But if|וְכִֽי־\rb* \rb he gives|יִתֵּ֨ן\rb* \rb a gift|מַתָּנָ֜ה\rb* \rb from his inheritance|מִנַּחֲלָת֗וֹ\rb* \rb to one|לְאַחַד֙\rb* \rb of his servants|מֵֽעֲבָדָ֔יו\rb*, \rb it will belong to|וְהָ֤יְתָה\rb* \rb that servant until|עַד־\rb* \rb the year|שְׁנַ֣ת\rb* \rb of freedom|הַדְּר֔וֹר\rb*; \rb then it will revert|וְשָׁבַ֖ת\rb* \rb to the prince|לַנָּשִׂ֑יא\rb*. \rb His inheritance|נַחֲלָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb belongs only|אַ֚ךְ\rb* \rb to his sons|בָּנָ֖יו\rb*; \rb it shall be|תִּהְיֶֽה׃\rb* \rb theirs|לָהֶ֥ם\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb The prince|הַנָּשִׂ֜יא\rb* \rb must not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb take|יִקַּ֨ח\rb* \rb any of the inheritance|מִנַּחֲלַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the people|הָעָ֗ם\rb* \rb by evicting them|לְהֽוֹנֹתָם֙\rb* \rb from their property|מֵאֲחֻזָּתָ֔ם\rb*. \rb He is to provide an inheritance|יַנְחִ֣ל\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb for his sons|בָּנָ֑יו\rb* \rb from his own property|מֵאֲחֻזָּת֖וֹ\rb*, \rb so that|לְמַ֙עַן֙\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb none|לֹֽא־\rb*\rb |אִ֖ישׁ\rb* \rb of My people|עַמִּ֔י\rb* \rb will be displaced|יָפֻ֣צוּ\rb* \rb from his property|מֵאֲחֻזָּתֽוֹ׃\rb*.’”
\s1 The Courts for Boiling and Baking
\p \v 19 \rb Then the man brought me|וַיְבִיאֵ֣נִי\rb* \rb through the entrance|בַמָּבוֹא֮\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb at|עַל־\rb* \rb the side|כֶּ֣תֶף\rb* \rb of the gate|הַשַּׁעַר֒\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the holy|הַקֹּ֙דֶשׁ֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb chambers|הַלִּשְׁכ֤וֹת\rb* \rb facing|הַפֹּנ֖וֹת\rb* \rb north|צָפ֑וֹנָה\rb*, \rb which belonged to the priests|הַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb*, \rb and he showed me|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb a place|מָק֔וֹם\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֣ם\rb* \rb at the far western|יָֽמָּה׃ס\rb* \rb end|בַּיַּרְכֹתִם\rb* \v 20 \rb and said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֔י\rb*, “\rb This|זֶ֣ה\rb* \rb is the place|הַמָּק֗וֹם\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb the priests|הַכֹּ֣הֲנִ֔ים\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb shall boil|יְבַשְּׁלוּ־\rb*\rb |שָׁם֙\rb* \rb the guilt offering|הָאָשָׁ֖ם\rb*\rb |וְאֶת־\rb* \rb and the sin offering|הַחַטָּ֑את\rb*, \rb and where|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb they shall bake|יֹאפוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the grain offering|הַמִּנְחָ֔ה\rb*, \rb so that they do not|לְבִלְתִּ֥י\rb* \rb bring them|הוֹצִ֛יא\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the outer|הַחִֽיצוֹנָ֖ה\rb* \rb court|הֶחָצֵ֥ר\rb* \rb and transmit holiness|לְקַדֵּ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb to the people|הָעָֽם׃\rb*.”
\p \v 21 \rb Then he brought me|וַיּוֹצִיאֵ֗נִי\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the outer|הַחִ֣יצֹנָ֔ה\rb* \rb court|הֶֽחָצֵר֙\rb* \rb and led me around to|וַיַּ֣עֲבִירֵ֔נִי\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb its|הֶחָצֵ֑ר\rb* \rb four|אַרְבַּ֖עַת\rb* \rb corners|מִקְצוֹעֵ֣י\rb*, \rb and I saw|וְהִנֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb a separate court|חָצֵר֙\rb* \rb in each of its|הֶחָצֵ֔ר\rb*\rb |חָצֵ֖ר\rb*\rb |בְּמִקְצֹ֥עַ\rb*\rb |הֶחָצֵֽר׃\rb* \rb corners|בְּמִקְצֹ֣עַ\rb*. \v 22 \rb In the four|בְּאַרְבַּ֜עַת\rb* \rb corners|מִקְצֹע֤וֹת\rb* \rb of the outer court|הֶֽחָצֵר֙\rb* \rb there were enclosed|קְטֻר֔וֹת\rb* \rb courts|חֲצֵר֣וֹת\rb*, \rb each forty cubits|אַרְבָּעִ֣ים\rb* \rb long|אֹ֔רֶךְ\rb* \rb and thirty cubits|וּשְׁלֹשִׁ֖ים\rb* \rb wide|רֹ֑חַב\rb*.\f + \fr 46:22 \ft The enclosed courts were approximately 70 feet long and 52.5 feet wide (21.3 meters long and 16 meters wide).\f* \rb Each of the four|לְאַרְבַּעְתָּ֖ם\rb* \rb corner areas|מְׄהֻׄקְׄצָׄעֽׄוֹׄתׄ׃\rb* \rb had the same|אַחַ֔ת\rb* \rb dimensions|מִדָּ֣ה\rb*. \v 23 \rb Around|סָבִ֖יב\rb* \rb the inside|סָבִ֥יב\rb* \rb of each|בָּהֶ֛ם\rb* \rb of the four courts|לְאַרְבַּעְתָּ֑ם\rb* \rb was a row of masonry|וְט֨וּר\rb* \rb with ovens|וּמְבַשְּׁל֣וֹת\rb* \rb built|עָשׂ֔וּי\rb* \rb at the base of|מִתַּ֥חַת\rb* \rb the walls|הַטִּיר֖וֹת\rb* \rb on all sides|סָבִֽיב׃\rb*.
\p \v 24 \rb And he said|וַיֹּ֖אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלָ֑י\rb*, “\rb These|אֵ֚לֶּה\rb* \rb are the kitchens|בֵּ֣ית\rb*\rb |הַֽמְבַשְּׁלִ֔ים\rb* \rb where|אֲשֶׁ֧ר\rb* \rb those who minister|מְשָׁרְתֵ֥י\rb* \rb at the temple|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb will cook|יְבַשְּׁלוּ־\rb*\rb |שָׁ֛ם\rb* \rb the sacrifices|זֶ֥בַח\rb* \rb offered by the people|הָעָֽם׃\rb*.”
\c 47
\s1 Waters from under the Temple
\p \v 1 \rb Then the man brought me back|וַיְשִׁבֵנִי֮\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the entrance|פֶּ֣תַח\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּיִת֒\rb*, \rb and I saw|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb water|מַ֣יִם\rb* \rb flowing|יֹצְאִ֗ים\rb* \rb from under|מִתַּ֨חַת\rb* \rb the threshold|מִפְתַּ֤ן\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֙יִת֙\rb* \rb toward the east|קָדִ֔ימָה\rb* (\rb for|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the temple|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb* \rb faced|פְנֵ֥י\rb* \rb east|קָדִ֑ים\rb*). \rb The water|וְהַמַּ֣יִם\rb* \rb was coming down|יֹרְדִ֗ים\rb* \rb from under|מִתַּ֜חַת\rb* \rb the south|הַיְמָנִ֔ית\rb* \rb side|מִכֶּ֤תֶף\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֙יִת֙\rb*, \rb south|מִנֶּ֖גֶב\rb* \rb of the altar|לַמִּזְבֵּֽחַ׃\rb*.
\p \v 2 \rb Next he brought me out|וַיּוֹצִאֵנִי֮\rb* \rb through|דֶּֽרֶךְ־\rb* \rb the north|צָפוֹנָה֒\rb* \rb gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb and led me around|וַיְסִבֵּ֙נִי֙\rb*\rb |דֶּ֣רֶךְ\rb* \rb the outside|ח֔וּץ\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the outer|הַח֔וּץ\rb*\rb |דֶּ֖רֶךְ\rb* \rb gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb facing|הַפּוֹנֶ֣ה\rb* \rb east|קָדִ֑ים\rb*, \rb and there I saw|וְהִנֵּה־\rb* \rb the water|מַ֣יִם\rb* \rb trickling out|מְפַכִּ֔ים\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the south|הַיְמָנִֽית׃\rb* \rb side|הַכָּתֵ֖ף\rb*.
\p \v 3 \rb As the man|הָאִ֥ישׁ\rb* \rb went|בְּצֵאת־\rb* \rb eastward|קָדִ֖ים\rb* \rb with a measuring line|וְקָ֣ו\rb* \rb in his hand|בְּיָד֑וֹ\rb*, \rb he measured off|וַיָּ֤מָד\rb* \rb a thousand|אֶ֙לֶף֙\rb* \rb cubits|בָּֽאַמָּ֔ה\rb*\f + \fr 47:3 \fqa 1,000 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 1,750 feet or 533.4 meters.\f* \rb and led me through|וַיַּעֲבִרֵ֥נִי\rb*\rb |מֵ֥י\rb* \rb ankle-deep|אָפְסָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb water|בַמַּ֖יִם\rb*.
\p \v 4 \rb Then he measured off|וַיָּ֣מָד\rb* \rb a thousand cubits|אֶ֔לֶף\rb* \rb and led me through|וַיַּעֲבִרֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb knee-deep|בִּרְכָּ֑יִם\rb* \rb water|בַמַּ֖יִם\rb*\rb |מַ֣יִם\rb*.
\p \rb Again he measured|וַיָּ֣מָד\rb* \rb a thousand cubits|אֶ֔לֶף\rb* \rb and led me through|וַיַּעֲבִרֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb waist-deep|מָתְנָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb water|מֵ֥י\rb*.
\p \v 5 \rb Once again he measured off|וַיָּ֣מָד\rb* \rb a thousand cubits|אֶ֔לֶף\rb*, \rb but now it was a river|נַ֕חַל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb I could|אוּכַ֖ל\rb* \rb not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb cross|לַעֲבֹ֑ר\rb*, \rb because|כִּֽי־\rb* \rb the water|הַמַּ֙יִם֙\rb* \rb had risen|גָא֤וּ\rb* \rb and|מֵ֣י\rb* \rb was deep enough for swimming|שָׂ֔חוּ\rb* — \rb a river|נַ֖חַל\rb* \rb that|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb could not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb be crossed on foot|יֵעָבֵֽר׃\rb*.
\p \v 6 “\rb Son|בֶן־\rb* \rb of man|אָדָ֑ם\rb*, \rb do you see this|הֲרָאִ֣יתָ\rb*?” \rb he asked|וַיֹּ֥אמֶר\rb*\rb |אֵלַ֖י\rb*. \rb Then he led me|וַיּוֹלִכֵ֥נִי\rb* \rb back|וַיְשִׁבֵ֖נִי\rb* \rb to the bank|שְׂפַ֥ת\rb* \rb of the river|הַנָּֽחַל׃\rb*.
\p \v 7 \rb When I arrived|בְּשׁוּבֵ֕נִי\rb*, \rb I saw|וְהִנֵּה֙\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb a great|מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb number of|רַ֣ב\rb* \rb trees|עֵ֖ץ\rb* \rb along both|מִזֶּ֖ה\rb*\rb |וּמִזֶּֽה׃\rb* \rb banks|שְׂפַ֣ת\rb* \rb of the river|הַנַּ֔חַל\rb*. \v 8 \rb And he said|וַיֹּ֣אמֶר\rb* \rb to me|אֵלַ֗י\rb*, “\rb This|הָאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb water|הַמַּ֤יִם\rb* \rb flows out|יוֹצְאִ֗ים\rb* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the eastern|הַקַּדְמוֹנָ֔ה\rb* \rb region|הַגְּלִילָה֙\rb* \rb and goes down|וְיָרְד֖וּ\rb* \rb into|עַל־\rb* \rb the Arabah|הָֽעֲרָבָ֑ה\rb*. \rb When it empties|וּבָ֣אוּ\rb* \rb into|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Dead Sea|הַיָּ֔מָּה\rb*,\f + \fr 47:8 \ft Literally \fqa the Sea\f*\rb |הַיָּ֥מָּה\rb*\rb |הַמּֽוּצָאִ֖ים\rb* \rb the water there|הַמָּֽיִם׃\rb* \rb becomes fresh|וְנִרְפְּאוּ\rb*.\f + \fr 47:8 \ft Hebrew \fqa is healed\ft ; similarly in verses 9 and 11\f* \v 9 \rb Wherever|אֶ֣ל\rb*\rb |כָּל־\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר֩\rb* \rb the river|נַחֲלַ֙יִם֙\rb*\rb |שָׁ֤ם\rb* \rb flows|יָב֨וֹא\rb*, \rb there will be|וְהָיָ֣ה\rb*\rb |כָל־\rb*\rb |אֲ‍ֽשֶׁר־\rb* \rb swarms|יִשְׁרֹ֡ץ\rb* \rb of living|נֶ֣פֶשׁ\rb* \rb creatures|חַיָּ֣ה׀\rb*\rb |יִֽחְיֶ֔ה\rb* \rb and|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb a great number of|רַבָּ֣ה\rb*\rb |מְאֹ֑ד\rb* \rb fish|הַדָּגָ֖ה\rb*, \rb because|כִּי֩\rb*\rb |הָאֵ֗לֶּה\rb* \rb it|הַמַּ֣יִם\rb* \rb flows|בָ֨אוּ\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֜מָּה\rb* \rb and makes the waters fresh|וְיֵרָֽפְאוּ֙\rb*; \rb so wherever|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb the river|הַנָּֽחַל׃\rb* \rb flows|יָ֥בוֹא\rb*, \rb everything|כֹּ֛ל\rb*\rb |שָׁ֖מָּה\rb* \rb will flourish|וָחָ֔י\rb*.
\p \v 10 \rb Fishermen|דַּוָּגִ֗ים\rb* \rb will stand|יַעַמְדוּ\rb* \rb by the shore|עָלָ֜יו\rb*; \rb from En-gedi|גֶּ֙דִי֙\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb*\rb |עֵ֣ין\rb* \rb En-eglaim|עֶגְלַ֔יִם\rb* \rb they will|יִהְי֑וּ\rb* \rb spread|מִשְׁט֥וֹחַ\rb* \rb their nets|לַֽחֲרָמִ֖ים\rb* \rb to catch fish|דְגָתָ֔ם\rb* \rb of many|רַבָּ֥ה\rb*\rb |מְאֹֽד׃\rb* \rb kinds|לְמִינָה֙\rb*,\rb |תִּהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb like the fish|כִּדְגַ֛ת\rb* \rb of the Great|הַגָּד֖וֹל\rb* \rb Sea|הַיָּ֥ם\rb*.\f + \fr 47:10 \ft That is, the Mediterranean Sea; also in verses 15, 19, and 20\f*
\p \v 11 \rb But the swamps|בִּצֹּאתוֹ\rb* \rb and marshes|וּגְבָאָ֛יו\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb become fresh|יֵרָפְא֖וּ\rb*; \rb they will be left|נִתָּֽנוּ׃\rb* \rb for salt|לְמֶ֥לַח\rb*.
\p \v 12 \rb Along|וְעַל־\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb both|מִזֶּ֣ה׀\rb*\rb |וּמִזֶּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb banks|שְׂפָת֣וֹ\rb* \rb of the river|הַנַּ֣חַל\rb*, \rb fruit|מַ֠אֲכָל\rb* \rb trees|עֵֽץ־\rb* \rb of all kinds|כָּל־\rb* \rb will grow|יַעֲלֶ֣ה\rb*. \rb Their leaves|עָלֵ֜הוּ\rb* \rb will not|לֹא־\rb* \rb wither|יִבּ֨וֹל\rb*, \rb and their fruit|פִּרְי֗וֹ\rb* \rb will not|וְלֹֽא־\rb* \rb fail|יִתֹּ֣ם\rb*. \rb Each month|לָֽחֳדָשָׁיו֙\rb* \rb they will bear fruit|יְבַכֵּ֔ר\rb*, \rb because|כִּ֣י\rb* \rb the water|מֵימָ֔יו\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the sanctuary|הַמִּקְדָּ֖שׁ\rb* \rb flows to them|יֽוֹצְאִ֑ים\rb*.\rb |הֵ֣מָּה\rb* \rb Their fruit|פִרְיוֹ֙\rb* \rb will be used|וְהָיוּ\rb* \rb for food|לְמַֽאֲכָ֔ל\rb* \rb and their leaves|וְעָלֵ֖הוּ\rb* \rb for healing|לִתְרוּפָֽה׃ס\rb*.”
\s1 The Borders of the Land
\p \v 13 \rb This is what|כֹּ֤ה\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֣י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִ֔ה\rb* \rb says|אָמַר֙\rb*: “\rb These are|גֵּ֤ה\rb* \rb the boundaries|גְבוּל֙\rb* \rb by which|אֲשֶׁ֣ר\rb* \rb you are to divide the land|הָאָ֔רֶץ\rb* \rb as an inheritance|תִּתְנַחֲל֣וּ\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb among the twelve|לִשְׁנֵ֥י\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb* \rb tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*; \rb Joseph|יוֹסֵ֖ף\rb* \rb shall receive two portions|חֲבָלִֽים׃\rb*.\f + \fr 47:13 \ft Since Levi had no portion, Joseph’s sons Ephraim and Manasseh received land as two tribes.\f* \v 14 \rb You are to divide|וּנְחַלְתֶּ֤ם\rb* \rb it|אוֹתָהּ֙\rb* \rb equally|אִ֣ישׁ\rb* \rb among them|כְּאָחִ֔יו\rb*. \rb Because|אֲשֶׁ֤ר\rb* \rb I swore with an uplifted|נָשָׂ֙אתִי֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb hand|יָדִ֔י\rb* \rb to give|לְתִתָּ֖הּ\rb* \rb it to your forefathers|לַאֲבֹֽתֵיכֶ֑ם\rb*, \rb this|הַזֹּ֛את\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֧רֶץ\rb* \rb will fall|וְנָ֨פְלָ֜ה\rb* \rb to you|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb as an inheritance|בְּנַחֲלָֽה׃\rb*.
\p \v 15 \rb This|וְזֶ֖ה\rb* \rb shall be the boundary|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb On the north|צָפ֜וֹנָה\rb* \rb side|לִפְאַ֨ת\rb* \rb it will extend from|מִן־\rb* \rb the Great|הַגָּד֛וֹל\rb* \rb Sea|הַיָּ֧ם\rb* \rb by way|הַדֶּ֥רֶךְ\rb* \rb of Hethlon|חֶתְלֹ֖ן\rb* \rb through Lebo-hamath|לְב֥וֹא\rb* \rb to Zedad|צְדָֽדָה׃\rb*, \v 16 \rb |חֲמָ֤ת׀\rb* \rb Berothah|בֵּר֙וֹתָה֙\rb*, \rb and Sibraim|סִבְרַ֔יִם\rb*\f + \fr 47:16 \ft LXX; MT \fqa \fv 15\fv*...through Lebo to Zedad, \fv 16\fv*Hamath, Berothah, and Sibraim\f* \rb (which|אֲשֶׁר֙\rb* \rb is on|בֵּין־\rb* \rb the border between|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb Damascus|דַּמֶּ֔שֶׂק\rb*\rb |וּבֵ֖ין\rb* \rb and|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb Hamath|חֲמָ֑ת\rb*),\rb |חָצֵר֙\rb* \rb as far as Hazer-hatticon|הַתִּיכ֔וֹן\rb*, \rb which|אֲשֶׁ֖ר\rb* \rb is on|אֶל־\rb* \rb the border|גְּב֥וּל\rb* \rb of Hauran|חַוְרָֽן׃\rb*. \v 17 \rb So the border|גְב֜וּל\rb* \rb will run|וְהָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb from|מִן־\rb* \rb the Sea|הַיָּ֗ם\rb*\rb |חֲצַ֤ר\rb* \rb to Hazar-enan|עֵינוֹן֙\rb*, \rb along the northern|צָפ֖וֹנָה\rb* \rb border|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb of Damascus|דַּמֶּ֔שֶׂק\rb*, \rb with the territory|וּגְב֣וּל\rb* \rb of Hamath|חֲמָ֑ת\rb*\rb |וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb to the north|וְצָפ֥וֹן׀\rb*. \rb This will be the northern|צָפֽוֹן׃\rb* \rb boundary|פְּאַ֥ת\rb*.
\li1 \v 18 \rb On the east|קָדִ֡ים\rb* \rb side|וּפְאַ֣ת\rb* \rb the border|מִגְּב֛וּל\rb* \rb will run between|מִבֵּ֣ין\rb* \rb Hauran|חַוְרָ֣ן\rb* \rb and|וּמִבֵּין־\rb* \rb Damascus|דַּמֶּשֶׂק֩\rb*, \rb along the Jordan|הַיַּרְדֵּ֔ן\rb* \rb between|וּמִבֵּ֨ין\rb* \rb Gilead|הַגִּלְעָ֜ד\rb*\rb |וּמִבֵּ֨ין\rb* \rb and the land|אֶ֤רֶץ\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵל֙\rb*, \rb to|עַל־\rb* \rb the Eastern|הַקַּדְמוֹנִ֖י\rb* \rb Sea|הַיָּ֥ם\rb* \rb and|וְאֵ֖ת\rb* \rb as far as Tamar|תָּמֹ֑דּוּ\rb*.\f + \fr 47:18 \ft See Syriac; that is, \fqa of Israel, to the Dead Sea and as far as Tamar\ft ; Hebrew \fqa of Israel. And along the Eastern Sea you are to measure.\f* \rb This will be the eastern|קָדִֽימָה׃\rb* \rb boundary|פְּאַ֥ת\rb*.
\li1 \v 19 \rb On the south|נֶ֣גֶב\rb*\rb |תֵּימָ֔נָה\rb* \rb side|וּפְאַת֙\rb* \rb it will run from Tamar|מִתָּמָ֗ר\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the waters|מֵי֙\rb* \rb of Meribath-kadesh|מְרִיב֣וֹת\rb*\rb |קָדֵ֔שׁ\rb*, \rb and along the Brook of Egypt|נַחֲלָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 47:19 \ft Hebrew does not include \fqa of Egypt\ft .\f* \rb to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the Great|הַגָּד֑וֹל\rb* \rb Sea|הַיָּ֣ם\rb*.\rb |וְאֵ֥ת\rb*\rb |תֵּימָ֖נָה\rb* \rb This will be the southern|נֶֽגְבָּה׃\rb* \rb boundary|פְּאַת־\rb*.
\li1 \v 20 \rb And on the west|יָם֙\rb* \rb side|וּפְאַת־\rb*, \rb the Great|הַגָּד֔וֹל\rb* \rb Sea|הַיָּ֣ם\rb* \rb will be the boundary|מִגְּב֕וּל\rb* \rb up to|עַד־\rb* \rb a point opposite|נֹ֖כַח\rb* \rb Lebo-hamath|לְב֣וֹא\rb*\rb |חֲמָ֑ת\rb*. \rb This|זֹ֖את\rb* \rb will be the western|יָֽם׃\rb* \rb boundary|פְּאַת־\rb*.
\p \v 21 \rb You are to divide|וְחִלַּקְתֶּ֞ם\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb this|הַזֹּ֛את\rb* \rb land|הָאָ֧רֶץ\rb* \rb among yourselves|לָכֶ֖ם\rb* \rb according to the tribes|לְשִׁבְטֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 22 \rb |וְהָיָ֗ה\rb* \rb You shall allot|תַּפִּ֣לוּ\rb* \rb it|אוֹתָהּ֮\rb* \rb as an inheritance|בְּנַחֲלָה֒\rb* \rb for yourselves|לָכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb and for the foreigners|וּלְהַגֵּרִים֙\rb* \rb who dwell|הַגָּרִ֣ים\rb* \rb among you|בְּתוֹכְכֶ֔ם\rb* \rb and who|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb have|הוֹלִ֥דוּ\rb* \rb children|בָנִ֖ים\rb*\rb |בְּתֽוֹכְכֶ֑ם\rb*. \rb You are to treat them|וְהָי֣וּ\rb*\rb |לָכֶ֗ם\rb* \rb as native-born|כְּאֶזְרָח֙\rb* \rb Israelites|בִּבְנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*; \rb along with you|אִתְּכֶם֙\rb*, \rb they shall be allotted|יִפְּל֣וּ\rb* \rb an inheritance|בְנַחֲלָ֔ה\rb* \rb among|בְּת֖וֹךְ\rb* \rb the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*. \v 23 \rb |וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb In whatever|אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb tribe|בַשֵּׁ֔בֶט\rb* \rb a foreigner|הַגֵּ֖ר\rb*\rb |אִתּ֑וֹ\rb* \rb dwells|גָּ֥ר\rb*, \rb you are to assign|תִּתְּנ֣וּ\rb* \rb his inheritance|נַחֲלָת֔וֹ\rb* \rb there|שָׁ֚ם\rb*,” \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃ס\rb*.
\c 48
\s1 The Portions for the Tribes
\p \v 1 “\rb Now these|וְאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb are the names|שְׁמ֣וֹת\rb* \rb of the tribes|הַשְּׁבָטִ֑ים\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb At the northern|צָפ֡וֹנָה\rb* \rb frontier|מִקְצֵ֣ה\rb*, \rb Dan|דָּ֥ן\rb* \rb will have one portion|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb bordering|אֶל־\rb*\rb |יַ֣ד\rb* \rb the road|דֶּֽרֶךְ־\rb* \rb of Hethlon|חֶתְלֹ֣ן׀\rb*\rb |לְֽבוֹא־\rb* \rb to Lebo-hamath|חֲמָ֡ת\rb*\rb |חֲצַ֣ר\rb* \rb and running on to Hazar-enan|עֵינָן֩\rb* \rb on the border|גְּב֨וּל\rb* \rb of Damascus|דַּמֶּ֤שֶׂק\rb* \rb with Hamath|חֲמָ֔ת\rb*\rb |אֶל־\rb*\rb |יַ֣ד\rb* \rb to the north|צָפ֙וֹנָה֙\rb*, \rb and extending from the east|קָדִ֛ים\rb* \rb side|פְאַת־\rb* \rb to the west side|הַיָּ֖ם\rb*.
\li1 \v 2 \rb Asher|אָשֵׁ֥ר\rb* \rb will have one portion|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb bordering|וְעַ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the territory|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb of Dan|דָּ֗ן\rb* \rb from east|קָדִ֛ים\rb*\rb |מִפְּאַ֥ת\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb*\rb |פְּאַת־\rb* \rb west|יָ֖מָּה\rb*.
\li1 \v 3 \rb Naphtali|נַפְתָּלִ֥י\rb* \rb will have one portion|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb bordering|וְעַ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the territory|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb of Asher|אָשֵׁ֗ר\rb* \rb from east|קָדִ֛ימָה\rb*\rb |מִפְּאַ֥ת\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb*\rb |פְּאַת־\rb* \rb west|יָ֖מָּה\rb*.
\li1 \v 4 \rb Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֥ה\rb* \rb will have one portion|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb bordering|וְעַ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the territory|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb of Naphtali|נַפְתָּלִ֗י\rb* \rb from east|קָדִ֛מָה\rb*\rb |מִפְּאַ֥ת\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb*\rb |פְּאַת־\rb* \rb west|יָ֖מָּה\rb*.
\li1 \v 5 \rb Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֥יִם\rb* \rb will have one portion|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb bordering|וְעַ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the territory|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb of Manasseh|מְנַשֶּׁ֗ה\rb* \rb from east|קָדִ֛מָה\rb*\rb |מִפְּאַ֥ת\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb*\rb |פְּאַת־\rb* \rb west|יָ֖מָּה\rb*.
\li1 \v 6 \rb Reuben|רְאוּבֵ֥ן\rb* \rb will have one portion|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb bordering|וְעַ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the territory|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb of Ephraim|אֶפְרַ֗יִם\rb* \rb from east|קָדִ֛ים\rb*\rb |מִפְּאַ֥ת\rb* \rb to|וְעַד־\rb*\rb |פְּאַת־\rb* \rb west|יָ֖מָּה\rb*.
\li1 \v 7 \rb Judah|יְהוּדָ֥ה\rb* \rb will have one portion|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb bordering|וְעַ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the territory|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb of Reuben|רְאוּבֵ֗ן\rb* \rb from east|קָדִ֛ים\rb*\rb |מִפְּאַ֥ת\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb*\rb |פְּאַת־\rb* \rb west|יָ֖מָּה\rb*.
\s1 The Portions for the Priests and Levites
\p \v 8 \rb Bordering|וְעַל֙\rb* \rb the territory|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֔ה\rb*, \rb from east|קָדִ֖ים\rb*\rb |מִפְּאַ֥ת\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb west|יָ֑מָּה\rb*, \rb will be|תִּהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb the portion|הַתְּרוּמָ֣ה\rb*\rb |אֲ‍ֽשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you are to set apart|תָּרִ֡ימוּ\rb*. \rb It will be 25,000 cubits|חֲמִשָּׁה֩\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֨ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֜לֶף\rb* \rb wide|רֹ֗חַב\rb*,\f + \fr 48:8 \fqa 25,000 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 8.3 miles or 13.3 kilometers; also in verses 9, 10, 13, 15, 20, and 21.\f* \rb and the length|וְאֹ֜רֶךְ\rb* \rb of a|כְּאַחַ֤ד\rb* \rb tribal portion|הַחֲלָקִים֙\rb* \rb from|מִפְּאַ֤ת\rb* \rb east|קָדִ֙ימָה֙\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb*\rb |פְּאַת־\rb* \rb west|יָ֔מָּה\rb*. \rb In the center|בְּתוֹכֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb the sanctuary|הַמִּקְדָּ֖שׁ\rb*.
\p \v 9 \rb The special portion|הַתְּרוּמָ֕ה\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb you set apart|תָּרִ֖ימוּ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַֽיהוָ֑ה\rb* \rb shall be 25,000 cubits|חֲמִשָּׁ֤ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶ֔לֶף\rb* \rb long|אֹ֗רֶךְ\rb* \rb and 10,000 cubits|עֲשֶׂ֥רֶת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִֽים׃\rb* \rb wide|וְרֹ֖חַב\rb*.\f + \fr 48:9 \fqa 10,000 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 3.3 miles or 5.3 kilometers; also in verses 10, 13, and 18.\f*
\p \v 10 \rb This will be|וּ֠לְאֵ֜לֶּה\rb* \rb the holy|הַקֹּדֶשׁ֮\rb* \rb portion|תְרֽוּמַת־\rb* \rb for the priests|לַכֹּֽהֲנִים֒\rb*. \rb It will be|תִּהְיֶ֣ה\rb* \rb 25,000 cubits long|חֲמִשָּׁ֧ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֣ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֗לֶף\rb* \rb on the north side|צָפ֜וֹנָה\rb*, \rb 10,000 cubits|עֲשֶׂ֣רֶת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֔ים\rb* \rb wide|רֹ֚חַב\rb* \rb on the west side|וְיָ֙מָּה֙\rb*, \rb 10,000 cubits|עֲשֶׂ֣רֶת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֔ים\rb* \rb wide|רֹ֚חַב\rb* \rb on the east side|וְקָדִ֗ימָה\rb*, \rb and 25,000 cubits|חֲמִשָּׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אָ֑לֶף\rb* \rb long|אֹ֕רֶךְ\rb* \rb on the south side|וְנֶ֕גְבָּה\rb*. \rb In the center|בְּתוֹכֽוֹ׃\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיָ֥ה\rb* \rb the sanctuary|מִקְדַּשׁ־\rb* \rb of the LORD|יְהוָ֖ה\rb*. \v 11 \rb It will be for the consecrated|הַֽמְקֻדָּשׁ֙\rb* \rb priests|לַכֹּהֲנִ֤ים\rb*, \rb the descendants|מִבְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Zadok|צָד֔וֹק\rb*, \rb who|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb kept|שָׁמְר֖וּ\rb* \rb My charge|מִשְׁמַרְתִּ֑י\rb* \rb and did not|לֹֽא־\rb* \rb go astray|תָע֗וּ\rb* \rb as the Levites|הַלְוִיִּֽם׃ס\rb* \rb did|תָּע֖וּ\rb* \rb when the Israelites|בְּנֵ֣י\rb*\rb |יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*\rb |כַּאֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb went astray|בִּתְעוֹת֙\rb*. \v 12 \rb It will be|וְהָיְתָ֨ה\rb* \rb a special portion|תְּרוּמִיָּ֛ה\rb* \rb for them|לָהֶ֧ם\rb* \rb set apart|מִתְּרוּמַ֥ת\rb* \rb from the land|הָאָ֖רֶץ\rb*, \rb a most holy portion|קֹ֣דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |קָדָשִׁ֑ים\rb*\f + \fr 48:12 \ft Or \fqa a Most Holy Place\f* \rb adjacent to|אֶל־\rb* \rb the territory|גְּב֖וּל\rb* \rb of the Levites|הַלְוִיִּֽם׃\rb*.
\p \v 13 \rb Bordering|לְעֻמַּת֙\rb* \rb the territory|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb of the priests|הַכֹּהֲנִ֔ים\rb*, \rb the Levites|וְהַלְוִיִּ֗ם\rb* \rb shall have an area 25,000|חֲמִשָּׁ֨ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֙לֶף֙\rb* \rb cubits long|אֹ֔רֶךְ\rb* \rb and 10,000 cubits|עֲשֶׂ֣רֶת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֑ים\rb* \rb wide|וְרֹ֖חַב\rb*. \rb The whole|כָּל־\rb* \rb length|אֹ֗רֶךְ\rb* \rb will be 25,000 cubits|חֲמִשָּׁ֤ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶ֔לֶף\rb*, \rb and the width|וְרֹ֖חַב\rb* \rb 10,000 cubits|עֲשֶׂ֥רֶת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִֽים׃\rb*. \v 14 \rb They must not|וְלֹא־\rb* \rb sell|יִמְכְּר֣וּ\rb* \rb or exchange|יָמֵ֛ר\rb* \rb any of it|מִמֶּ֗נּוּ\rb*, \rb and they must|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb not|וְלֹ֥א\rb* \rb transfer|יַעֲבוּר\rb* \rb this best part|רֵאשִׁ֣ית\rb* \rb of the land|הָאָ֑רֶץ\rb*, \rb for|כִּי־\rb* \rb it is holy|קֹ֖דֶשׁ\rb* \rb to the LORD|לַיהוָֽה׃\rb*.
\s1 The Common Portion
\p \v 15 \rb The remaining area|הַנּוֹתָ֣ר\rb*, \rb 5,000 cubits|וַחֲמֵ֨שֶׁת\rb*\f + \fr 48:15 \fqa 5,000 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 1.7 miles or 2.7 kilometers.\f*\rb |אֲלָפִ֜ים\rb* \rb wide|בָּרֹ֗חַב\rb* \rb and 25,000 cubits long|חֲמִשָּׁ֤ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶ֔לֶף\rb*, \rb will be for common use|חֹֽל־\rb* \rb by the city|לָעִ֔יר\rb*, \rb for houses|לְמוֹשָׁ֖ב\rb*, \rb and for pastureland|וּלְמִגְרָ֑שׁ\rb*. \rb The city|הָעִ֖יר\rb* \rb will be|וְהָיְתָ֥ה\rb* \rb in the center of it|בְּתוֹכֹה׃\rb* \v 16 \rb and will have these|וְאֵלֶּה֮\rb* \rb measurements|מִדּוֹתֶיהָ֒\rb*: \rb 4,500 cubits|חֲמֵ֤שׁ\rb*\f + \fr 48:16 \fqa 4,500 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 1.5 miles or 2.4 kilometers; also in verses 30, 32, 33, and 34.\f*\rb |מֵאוֹת֙\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבַּ֣עַת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֔ים\rb* \rb on the north|צָפ֗וֹן\rb* \rb side|פְּאַ֣ת\rb*, \rb 4,500 cubits|חֲמֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבַּ֣עַת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֑ים\rb* \rb on the south|נֶ֕גֶב\rb* \rb side|וּפְאַת־\rb*, \rb 4,500 cubits|חֲמֵ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵאוֹת֙\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבַּ֣עַת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֔ים\rb* \rb on the east|קָדִ֗ים\rb* \rb side|וּמִפְּאַ֣ת\rb*, \rb and 4,500 cubits|חֲמֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֖וֹת\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבַּ֥עַת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִֽים׃\rb* \rb on the west|יָ֕מָּה\rb* \rb side|וּפְאַת־\rb*.
\p \v 17 \rb The pastureland|מִגְרָשׁ֮\rb* \rb of the city|לָעִיר֒\rb* \rb will extend|וְהָיָ֣ה\rb* \rb 250 cubits|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb*\f + \fr 48:17 \fqa 250 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 437.5 feet or 133.4 meters.\f*\rb |וּמָאתַ֔יִם\rb* \rb to the north|צָפ֙וֹנָה֙\rb*, \rb 250 cubits|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |וּמָאתָ֑יִם\rb* \rb to the south|וְנֶ֖גְבָּה\rb*, \rb 250 cubits|חֲמִשִּׁ֣ים\rb*\rb |וּמָאתַ֔יִם\rb* \rb to the east|וְקָדִ֙ימָה֙\rb*, \rb and 250 cubits|חֲמִשִּׁ֥ים\rb*\rb |וּמָאתָֽיִם׃\rb* \rb to the west|וְיָ֖מָּה\rb*.
\p \v 18 \rb The remainder|וְהַנּוֹתָ֨ר\rb* \rb of the length|בָּאֹ֜רֶךְ\rb* \rb bordering|לְעֻמַּ֣ת׀\rb* \rb the holy|הַקֹּ֗דֶשׁ\rb* \rb portion|תְּרוּמַ֣ת\rb* \rb and running|וְהָיָ֕ה\rb* \rb adjacent to|לְעֻמַּ֖ת\rb* \rb it|הַקֹּ֑דֶשׁ\rb*\rb |תְּרוּמַ֣ת\rb* \rb will be 10,000 cubits|עֲשֶׂ֨רֶת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֤ים\rb* \rb on the east side|קָדִ֙ימָה֙\rb* \rb and 10,000 cubits|וַעֲשֶׂ֤רֶת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִים֙\rb* \rb on the west side|יָ֔מָּה\rb*. \rb Its produce|תְבוּאָתֹה\rb* \rb will supply|וְהָיְתָ֤ה\rb* \rb food|לְלֶ֔חֶם\rb* \rb for the workers|לְעֹבְדֵ֖י\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִֽיר׃\rb*. \v 19 \rb The workers|וְהָעֹבֵ֖ד\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb* \rb who cultivate it|יַעַבְד֕וּהוּ\rb* \rb will come from all|מִכֹּ֖ל\rb* \rb the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֥י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵֽל׃\rb*.
\p \v 20 \rb The entire|כָּל־\rb* \rb portion|הַתְּרוּמָ֗ה\rb* \rb will be a square|רְבִיעִ֗ית\rb*, \rb 25,000 cubits|חֲמִשָּׁ֤ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִים֙\rb*\rb |אֶ֔לֶף\rb* \rb by 25,000 cubits|בַּחֲמִשָּׁ֥ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֖ים\rb*\rb |אָ֑לֶף\rb*. \rb You are to set apart|תָּרִ֙ימוּ֙\rb*\rb |אֶת־\rb* \rb the holy|הַקֹּ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb portion|תְּרוּמַ֣ת\rb*, \rb along with|אֶל־\rb* \rb the city|הָעִֽיר׃\rb* \rb property|אֲחֻזַּ֖ת\rb*.
\s1 The Portion for the Prince
\p \v 21 \rb The remaining area|וְהַנּוֹתָ֣ר\rb* \rb on both sides|מִזֶּ֣ה׀\rb*\rb |וּמִזֶּ֣ה׀\rb* \rb of the holy|הַקֹּ֣דֶשׁ\rb* \rb portion|לִתְרֽוּמַת־\rb* \rb and of the property|וְלַאֲחֻזַּ֪ת\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֟יר\rb* \rb will belong to the prince|לַנָּשִׂ֣יא\rb*. \rb He|לַנָּשִׂ֑יא\rb* \rb will own the land adjacent to|לְעֻמַּ֥ת\rb* \rb the tribal portions|חֲלָקִ֖ים\rb*,\rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb extending eastward|פְּנֵ֣י\rb* \rb from the 25,000 cubits|חֲמִשָּׁה֩\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֨ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֥לֶף׀\rb* \rb of the holy district|תְּרוּמָה֮\rb* \rb toward|עַד־\rb* \rb the eastern|קָדִימָה֒\rb* \rb border|גְּב֣וּל\rb*, \rb and westward|וְיָ֗מָּה\rb*\rb |פְּ֠נֵי\rb* \rb from the 25,000 cubits|חֲמִשָּׁ֨ה\rb*\rb |וְעֶשְׂרִ֥ים\rb*\rb |אֶ֙לֶף֙\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb to the western|יָ֔מָּה\rb* \rb border|גְּב֣וּל\rb*. \rb And in the center of them|בְּתוֹכֹה׃\rb* \rb will be|וְהָֽיְתָה֙\rb* \rb the holy|הַקֹּ֔דֶשׁ\rb* \rb portion|תְּרוּמַ֣ת\rb* \rb and the sanctuary|וּמִקְדַּ֥שׁ\rb* \rb of the temple|הַבַּ֖יִת\rb*.
\p \v 22 \rb So the Levitical|הַלְוִיִּם֙\rb* \rb property|וּמֵאֲחֻזַּ֤ת\rb* \rb and the city|הָעִ֔יר\rb* \rb property|וּמֵאֲחֻזַּ֣ת\rb* \rb will lie in the center|בְּת֛וֹךְ\rb* \rb of the area|אֲשֶׁ֥ר\rb* \rb belonging|יִֽהְיֶ֑ה\rb* \rb to the prince|לַנָּשִׂ֖יא\rb*— \rb the area between|בֵּ֣ין׀\rb* \rb the borders|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָ֗ה\rb* \rb and|וּבֵין֙\rb*\rb |גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִ֔ן\rb*\rb |יִהְיֶֽה׃\rb*\rb |לַנָּשִׂ֖יא\rb*.
\s1 The Portions for the Remaining Tribes
\p \v 23 \rb As for the rest|וְיֶ֖תֶר\rb* \rb of the tribes|הַשְּׁבָטִ֑ים\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִ֥ן\rb* \rb will have one portion|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb extending from the east|קָדִ֛ימָה\rb* \rb side|מִפְּאַ֥ת\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb* \rb the|פְּאַת־\rb* \rb west side|יָ֖מָּה\rb*.
\li1 \v 24 \rb Simeon|שִׁמְע֥וֹן\rb* \rb will have one portion|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb bordering|וְעַ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the territory|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb of Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִ֗ן\rb* \rb from east|קָדִ֛ימָה\rb*\rb |מִפְּאַ֥ת\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb*\rb |פְּאַת־\rb* \rb west|יָ֖מָּה\rb*.
\li1 \v 25 \rb Issachar|יִשָׂשכָ֥ר\rb* \rb will have one portion|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb bordering|וְעַ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the territory|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb of Simeon|שִׁמְע֗וֹן\rb* \rb from east|קָדִ֛ימָה\rb*\rb |מִפְּאַ֥ת\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb*\rb |פְּאַת־\rb* \rb west|יָ֖מָּה\rb*.
\li1 \v 26 \rb Zebulun|זְבוּלֻ֥ן\rb* \rb will have one portion|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb bordering|וְעַ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the territory|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb of Issachar|יִשָׂשכָ֗ר\rb* \rb from east|קָדִ֛ימָה\rb*\rb |מִפְּאַ֥ת\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb*\rb |פְּאַת־\rb* \rb west|יָ֖מָּה\rb*.
\li1 \v 27 \rb And Gad|גָּ֥ד\rb* \rb will have one portion|אֶחָֽד׃\rb* \rb bordering|וְעַ֣ל׀\rb* \rb the territory|גְּב֣וּל\rb* \rb of Zebulun|זְבוּלֻ֗ן\rb* \rb from east|קָדִ֛מָה\rb*\rb |מִפְּאַ֥ת\rb* \rb to|עַד־\rb*\rb |פְּאַת־\rb* \rb west|יָ֖מָּה\rb*.
\p \v 28 \rb |אֶל־\rb* \rb The southern|נֶ֣גֶב\rb*\rb |תֵּימָ֑נָה\rb* \rb border|גְב֜וּל\rb* \rb of Gad|גָּ֔ד\rb* \rb will run|וְהָיָ֨ה\rb* \rb from Tamar|מִתָּמָ֗ר\rb* \rb to the waters|מֵ֚י\rb* \rb of Meribath-kadesh|מְרִיבַ֣ת\rb*\rb |קָדֵ֔שׁ\rb*, \rb then along the Brook of Egypt|נַחֲלָ֖ה\rb*\f + \fr 48:28 \ft Hebrew does not include \fqa of Egypt\ft .\f* \rb and out to|עַל־\rb* \rb the Great|הַגָּדֽוֹל׃\rb* \rb Sea|הַיָּ֥ם\rb*.\f + \fr 48:28 \ft That is, the Mediterranean Sea\f* \v 29 \rb This|זֹ֥את\rb* \rb is the land|הָאָ֛רֶץ\rb*\rb |אֲשֶׁר־\rb* \rb you are to allot|תַּפִּ֥ילוּ\rb* \rb as an inheritance|מִֽנַּחֲלָ֖ה\rb* \rb to the tribes|לְשִׁבְטֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֑ל\rb*, \rb and these|וְאֵ֙לֶּה֙\rb* \rb will be their portions|מַחְלְקוֹתָ֔ם\rb*,” \rb declares|נְאֻ֖ם\rb* \rb the Lord|אֲדֹנָ֥י\rb* \rb GOD|יְהוִֽה׃פ\rb*.
\s1 The City Gates and Dimensions
\p \v 30 “\rb These|וְאֵ֖לֶּה\rb* \rb will be the exits|תּוֹצְאֹ֣ת\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֑יר\rb*:
\b 
\li1 \rb Beginning on the north|צָפ֔וֹן\rb* \rb side|מִפְּאַ֣ת\rb*, \rb which will be|מִדָּֽה׃\rb* \rb 4,500 cubits long|חֲמֵ֥שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֛וֹת\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבַּ֥עַת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֖ים\rb*, \v 31 \rb the gates|וְשַׁעֲרֵ֣י\rb* \rb of the city|הָעִ֗יר\rb*\rb |עַל־\rb* \rb will be named|שְׁמוֹת֙\rb* \rb after the tribes|שִׁבְטֵ֣י\rb* \rb of Israel|יִשְׂרָאֵ֔ל\rb*. \rb On the north side|צָפ֑וֹנָה\rb* \rb there will be three|שְׁלוֹשָׁ֖ה\rb* \rb gates|שְׁעָרִ֥ים\rb*: \rb the gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb of Reuben|רְאוּבֵ֞ן\rb*, \rb the gate|שַׁ֤עַר\rb* \rb of Judah|יְהוּדָה֙\rb*,\rb |אֶחָ֔ד\rb* \rb and the gate|שַׁ֥עַר\rb* \rb of Levi|לֵוִ֖י\rb*.
\li1 \v 32 \rb On|וְאֶל־\rb* \rb the east|קָדִ֗ימָה\rb* \rb side|פְּאַ֣ת\rb*, \rb which will be 4,500 cubits long|חֲמֵ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵאוֹת֙\rb*,\rb |וְאַרְבַּ֣עַת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֔ים\rb* \rb there will be three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֑ה\rb* \rb gates|וּשְׁעָרִ֖ים\rb*: \rb the gate|וְשַׁ֨עַר\rb* \rb of Joseph|יוֹסֵ֜ף\rb*, \rb the gate|שַׁ֤עַר\rb* \rb of Benjamin|בִּנְיָמִן֙\rb*, \rb and the gate|שַׁ֥עַר\rb* \rb of Dan|דָּ֖ן\rb*.
\li1 \v 33 \rb On the south|נֶ֗גְבָּה\rb* \rb side|וּפְאַת־\rb*, \rb which will be|מִדָּ֔ה\rb* \rb 4,500 cubits long|חֲמֵ֨שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵא֜וֹת\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבַּ֤עַת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִים֙\rb*, \rb there will be three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֑ה\rb* \rb gates|וּשְׁעָרִ֖ים\rb*: \rb the gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb of Simeon|שִׁמְע֞וֹן\rb*, \rb the gate|שַׁ֤עַר\rb* \rb of Issachar|יִשָּׂשכָר֙\rb*, \rb and the gate|שַׁ֥עַר\rb* \rb of Zebulun|זְבוּלֻ֖ן\rb*.
\li1 \v 34 \rb And on the west|יָ֗מָּה\rb* \rb side|פְּאַת־\rb*, \rb which will be 4,500 cubits long|חֲמֵ֤שׁ\rb*\rb |מֵאוֹת֙\rb*\rb |וְאַרְבַּ֣עַת\rb*\rb |אֲלָפִ֔ים\rb*, \rb there will be three|שְׁלֹשָׁ֑ה\rb* \rb gates|שַֽׁעֲרֵיהֶ֖ם\rb*: \rb the gate|שַׁ֣עַר\rb* \rb of Gad|גָּ֞ד\rb*, \rb the gate|שַׁ֤עַר\rb* \rb of Asher|אָשֵׁר֙\rb*, \rb and the gate|שַׁ֥עַר\rb* \rb of Naphtali|נַפְתָּלִ֖י\rb*.
\p \v 35 \rb The perimeter|סָבִ֕יב\rb* \rb of the city will be 18,000 cubits|שְׁמֹנָ֥ה\rb*\rb |עָשָׂ֖ר\rb*\rb |אָ֑לֶף\rb*,\f + \fr 48:35 \fqa 18,000 (long) cubits \ft is approximately 6 miles or 9.6 kilometers.\f* \rb and from that day on|מִיּ֖וֹם\rb* \rb the name|וְשֵׁם־\rb* \rb of the city will be|הָעִ֥יר\rb*:
\pc \rb THE LORD|יְהוָ֥ה׀\rb* \rb IS THERE|שָֽׁמָּה׃\rb*.\f + \fr 48:35 \ft Hebrew \fqa YHWH Shammah\f*”
